{"id":"xpo-5894eb","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-3a6251ab-2e32-47ce-8d35-aa01394a0854","text":"## Implementation\n\nAdded hash-based routing to the web app. No dependencies, ~40 lines of code.\n\n### Routes\n- `#/issues` — Issue list (backlog)\n- `#/issues/:id` — Issue detail page\n- `#/board` — Board view\n- `#/dashboard` — Dashboard\n- `#/dependencies` — Dependencies\n\n### How it works\n- `parseHash()` reads the current URL hash and returns `{ view, issueId }`\n- `setHash()` writes the hash without triggering a page reload\n- A `useEffect` syncs state → hash whenever `view` or `selectedIssueId` changes\n- A `hashchange` listener syncs hash → state for browser back/forward\n- Initial state is parsed from the hash on mount, so direct links work\n\n### Files changed\n- `web/src/App.tsx` — added routing logic (parseHash, setHash, useEffect listeners, initial state from hash)"},"created_at":"2026-05-19T07:23:18.215634Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
