{"id":"xpo-533f00","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-573788cb-af2b-41ad-9b1e-5d6bf9388ff9","text":"## Implementation\n\nAdded sub-issue hierarchy to the backlog view.\n\n### How it works\n- Issues with `parent_id` are nested visually under their parent in the backlog\n- A `childrenByParent` map is built once from all issues and passed down\n- Each status group renders top-level issues first, with an `IssueTree` component recursing into children\n- Parent rows show a collapse/expand chevron and a circular progress indicator (`3/5` sub-issues done)\n- Child rows are indented 24px per depth level with a subtle tree-branch connector icon\n- Leaf rows at depth 0 keep the drag-handle dots on hover\n\n### Visual details\n- Sub-issue progress: tiny ring SVG that fills based on completion percentage, green when 100%\n- Tree connectors: L-shaped line for child rows\n- Collapse state is per-parent, defaults to expanded\n\n### Test data\n- Set `xpo-274e84`, `xpo-8e74b1`, `xpo-e1ee26` as children of `xpo-477ca3` (Command palette epic)\n\n### Files changed\n- `web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx` — rewrote StatusGroup to use IssueTree, added SubProgress component"},"created_at":"2026-05-19T07:30:45.615797Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
