{"id":"xpo-49c21a","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"sort_order":"a0t"},"created_at":"2026-05-19T16:05:40.631523Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-8faf44","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"sort_order":"a0x"},"created_at":"2026-05-19T16:05:50.041585Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-7392c6","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Set default label for create issue dialog to \"Feature\"","description":"When creating new issues with the \"c\" shortcut, we focus the title input field, but cannot quickly create the issue because the label is required and not set. Getting there requires multiple shift+tab to move backwards in focus list. We should set a default to feature and let people use the same shortcuts (\"l\" for label, \"s\" for status, \"e\" for estimate) to quickly open the relevant popovers. CMD+Enter should hit \"Create issue\" button","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-19T16:14:23.717598Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-7392c6","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"sort_order":"Zz"},"created_at":"2026-05-19T16:14:26.341195Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-7392c6","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-05-19T16:15:06.271431Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-7392c6","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-642e186c-b4a3-4cba-a3b6-4c275f56e671","text":"## Summary\n\n- Default label is now `feature` (pre-selected when dialog opens)\n- `Cmd+Enter` / `Ctrl+Enter` submits the form from anywhere in the modal (title, description, or dropdown focused)\n- After creation, label resets to `feature` instead of empty\n\n### Files changed\n- `web/src/App.tsx`: `NewIssueModal` default state and keydown handler"},"created_at":"2026-05-19T16:15:58.51072Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-7392c6","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-05-19T16:15:58.538239Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-5520eb","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Don't open multiple browser windows","description":"When running `beats board` we start the server and open the page in a browser window. That behaviour is great. However, we create a new window each time we run beats board. Could we instead reuse/reload the existing window if already open?","labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-05-19T16:18:11.629886Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-7710bb","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Allow to change labels, status, estimate from issue overview","description":"The UI renders all meta as \"clickable\" tags.\n- hovering over a status shows a popover with a \"time in status\" info\n- clicking on a status allows to quickly change/set a new status on the issue via a popover\n- clicking on a label opens a popover that let's user select labels\n- clicking on an estimate opens a popover that let's user select an estimate\nthe popovers are reused / same style as the ones on the issue details view.\n\nAlso, the estimate is rendered as a \"tag\" or \"badge\" with a triangle icon in front of the estimate number","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-19T16:20:48.640914Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-5520eb","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"sort_order":"Zz"},"created_at":"2026-05-19T16:20:54.90517Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-7710bb","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"sort_order":"ZzV"},"created_at":"2026-05-19T16:20:57.236092Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-5520eb","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-05-19T19:19:52.06096Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-5520eb","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-eee42276-a9e4-47b7-839d-23827c2d381c","text":"## Summary\n\nOn macOS, `beats board` now reuses an existing browser tab instead of opening a new one each time.\n\n### How it works\n- Uses AppleScript via `osascript` to search for an existing tab whose URL starts with `http://localhost:{port}`\n- Checks Chrome first, then Safari\n- If found: activates the window, switches to the tab, and reloads it\n- If not found: falls back to `open url` (opens a new tab as before)\n- Linux and Windows behavior unchanged (`xdg-open` / `rundll32`)\n\n### Files changed\n- `cmd/beats/board.go`: Added `reloadExistingTab()` function, refactored `openBrowser()` to try reuse first"},"created_at":"2026-05-19T19:23:28.75058Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-5520eb","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-05-19T19:23:28.782515Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-5520eb","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-82919645-1c40-4889-864d-24bf69bfb1c9","text":"Reverted — AppleScript approach triggers macOS security/automation permission pop-ups for each browser, which is worse than the extra tab. Restored original `open url` behavior."},"created_at":"2026-05-19T22:10:25.517272Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-5520eb","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-05-19T22:10:25.543359Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-7ec710","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"A better way to ingest data programatically by agents","description":"Right now, agents call the `beats create` and `beats update` cli interfaces passing long command line arguments like description or comments with implementation details. We should find a better way so that agents can interact with the system in a more direct / agent-native way.\n\nOptions include:\n- MCP\n- Claude skills\n\nWe should research more to see if additional ways viable and select the best option","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-20T04:46:54.219756Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-7ec710","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"sort_order":"Zz"},"created_at":"2026-05-20T04:47:05.535726Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
