{"id":"xpo-c7b7c6","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Cycles: time-boxed iteration tracking","description":"## Overview\n\nAdd support for **Cycles** — fixed-cadence, time-boxed iterations (inspired by other trackers). Cycles provide a planning lens over existing issues without heavy ceremony.\n\n## Design Principles\n\n- **Convention over enforcement** — cycles are a planning tool, not a gate\n- **Computed rollover** — no background daemon or manual rollover command needed\n- **Minimal writes** — an issue stores the cycle it was *originally assigned to*; rollover is derived at read time\n\n## Core Rules\n\n1. User configures cadence once: duration (1w/2w/3w/4w) + start day\n2. Cycles are **computed from config + current date**, not stored as discrete records (e.g., `2026-W21`)\n3. Issues get a `CycleID` field (the cycle they were first assigned to)\n4. **Done issues** stay attributed to their original cycle → gives you cycle history\n5. **Not-done issues** in a past cycle are computed as belonging to the current cycle → automatic rollover, zero writes\n6. The gap between original `CycleID` and actual completion date reveals planning slip\n\n## Scope\n\n- Data model: add `CycleID` to issue payloads\n- Config: cycle cadence settings in `.beats/config.toml`\n- CLI: `beats cycle` commands + `--cycle` flag on existing commands\n- Web UI: cycle views in the board\n- Projection: computed rollover logic","labels":["epic"]},"created_at":"2026-05-20T16:38:28.148479Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-ffe8df","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Cycle config: cadence settings in config.toml","description":"## Goal\n\nAdd cycle configuration to `.beats/config.toml` so users can define their iteration cadence once.\n\n## Fields\n\n- `cycle_duration` — one of `1w`, `2w`, `3w`, `4w`\n- `cycle_start_day` — day of the week (e.g., `monday`)\n- `cycle_start_date` — optional anchor date for the first cycle (defaults to nearest past start day)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Add cycle config fields to `internal/config/config.go`\n- [ ] Parse and validate cycle config when loading `.beats/config.toml`\n- [ ] Expose a function to compute the current cycle ID (e.g., `2026-W21`) from config + current date\n- [ ] Expose a function to compute cycle boundaries (start/end dates) for any cycle ID\n- [ ] Unit tests for cycle computation, edge cases (year boundaries, DST, etc.)","parent_id":"xpo-c7b7c6","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-20T16:38:53.255104Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-11e95c","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Data model: add CycleID field to issues","description":"## Goal\n\nAdd a `CycleID` string field to the issue model so issues can be assigned to a cycle.\n\n## Changes\n\n- [ ] Add `CycleID` to `CreatePayload`, `UpdatePayload`, and `Issue` in `internal/model/types.go`\n- [ ] Update projection logic in `internal/beats/projection.go` to populate `CycleID` from events\n- [ ] Ensure backward compatibility — existing issues without a `CycleID` are unaffected\n\n## Notes\n\n- `CycleID` is a string like `2026-W21` derived from the cycle config\n- This is the cycle the issue was **originally assigned to** (not rewritten on rollover)","parent_id":"xpo-c7b7c6","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-20T16:38:54.692652Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-f7f968","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Computed rollover logic in projection","description":"## Goal\n\nImplement the core rollover computation: issues with a past `CycleID` that are not done are treated as belonging to the current cycle at read time.\n\n## Rules\n\n1. If `issue.CycleID` is set and `issue.Status == DONE` → issue stays in its original cycle\n2. If `issue.CycleID` is set and `issue.Status != DONE` and cycle is in the past → issue is **computed** as belonging to the current cycle\n3. If `issue.CycleID` is empty → issue is uncycled (not in any cycle)\n\n## Changes\n\n- [ ] Add helper: `EffectiveCycleID(issue, config) string` that applies the rules above\n- [ ] Integrate into projection/filtering so `beats ls --cycle current` uses effective cycle\n- [ ] Add a `OriginalCycleID` or similar accessor so history is still available\n- [ ] Unit tests for rollover across multiple cycle boundaries","parent_id":"xpo-c7b7c6","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-20T16:46:47.460479Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-c70ad2","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"CLI: beats cycle commands","description":"## Goal\n\nAdd CLI commands for working with cycles.\n\n## Commands\n\n- `beats cycle init --duration 2w --start monday` — configure cadence (writes to config.toml)\n- `beats cycle` / `beats cycle current` — show current cycle info + its issues\n- `beats cycle next` — show next cycle + its issues\n- `beats cycle history` — list past cycles with completion stats (done/total)\n\n## Flags on existing commands\n\n- `beats ls --cycle current|next|\u003ccycle-id\u003e` — filter issues by effective cycle\n- `beats add --cycle current|next` — assign new issue to a cycle\n- `beats update \u003cid\u003e --cycle current|next|none` — assign/unassign cycle\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `beats cycle init` writes config\n- [ ] `beats cycle` displays current cycle with boundaries and issue list\n- [ ] `--cycle` filter works on `beats ls`\n- [ ] `--cycle` flag works on `beats add` and `beats update`\n- [ ] Shell completions for cycle values","parent_id":"xpo-c7b7c6","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-20T16:46:49.137737Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-e20298","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Web UI: cycle views in board","description":"## Goal\n\nAdd cycle awareness to the web board UI.\n\n## Changes\n\n- [ ] Cycle selector/filter in the board header (current / next / history)\n- [ ] Show cycle boundaries (dates) in the UI\n- [ ] Visual indicator for rolled-over issues (originally from a past cycle)\n- [ ] Cycle summary stats: total issues, completed, points, scope change\n\n## Dependencies\n\nDepends on the CLI/data model work being complete first.","parent_id":"xpo-c7b7c6","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-20T16:48:24.37344Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
