{"id":"xpo-d85818","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Cross-group drag and drop in backlog","description":"## Description\n\nSupport dragging issues between status groups in the backlog view.\n\n## Behavior\n\n1. **Default drag (no modifier):** Dragging over a different status group highlights the entire group with an accent border. Dropping assigns the new status and sorts the issue to the bottom of that group.\n\n2. **CMD+drag (modifier held):** Allows precise positioning between issues in any group, showing the accent indicator line at the drop edge. Dropping assigns the new status AND places the issue at the specific position.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Same-group drag behavior remains unchanged (reorder only, no modifier needed)\n- Visual feedback is key: group highlight vs. edge indicator line makes the two modes distinct","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-21T05:12:55.711359Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-d85818","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T05:12:59.332549Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-d85818","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-0f260159-607e-42f9-8357-350b92d8b9a3","text":"## Changes\n\n### Default drag (cross-group)\n- Dragging an issue over a different status group highlights the entire group (accent tint on header + rows)\n- Dropping assigns the new status and sorts the issue to the bottom of the target group\n\n### CMD+drag (cross-group precise positioning)\n- Holding CMD while dragging over a different group shows the edge indicator line between issues\n- Dropping assigns the new status AND positions the issue at the specific location\n\n### Implementation details\n- Added `dropGroupStatus` state to track which group is highlighted as a drop target\n- Separated \"draggable\" (source) from \"drop target\" (receiver) — all top-level issue rows accept drops when a drag is active\n- Group headers also act as drop targets for cross-group moves\n- Same-group reordering behavior is unchanged (no modifier needed)\n- Visual feedback: group header gets accent border + rows get subtle accent tint for group-level drops"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T05:15:19.730274Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-d85818","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a3"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T05:16:14.931114Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-d85818","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","sort_order":"Zz"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T05:16:36.294875Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-d85818","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a3"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T05:42:18.185564Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-d85818","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","sort_order":"Zz"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T05:42:24.011696Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-d85818","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a0V"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T05:49:38.29898Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-d85818","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","sort_order":"Zz"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T05:49:42.180595Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-d85818","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-d2195ef4-e089-4040-9388-e829aaf3bec1","text":"## Changes\n\n### Cross-group drag and drop\n- **Default drag** over a different status group highlights the entire group with an accent ring border. Dropping assigns the new status and sorts the issue to the bottom.\n- **CMD+drag** over a different group shows the precise edge indicator line. Dropping assigns the new status AND places the issue at the specific position.\n\n### Key implementation details\n- Restructured rendering: each status group is wrapped in a container div so the ring border can surround the entire section (header + issues).\n- Drop logic extracted into shared `performDrop` function called from both `handleDrop` (native drop event) and `handleDragEnd` (always fires). This works around macOS browsers blocking the native `drop` event when CMD is held.\n- `dropHandledRef` flag prevents double execution when both events fire.\n- State refs (`dropIndicatorRef`, `dropGroupStatusRef`) updated synchronously via custom setters to avoid stale closure issues with React batching.\n- `effectAllowed: 'all'` and `dropEffect: 'move'` set on the dataTransfer to allow modifier-key drags."},"created_at":"2026-05-21T05:51:00.452242Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-d85818","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T05:52:38.598783Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
