{"id":"xpo-c7b7c6","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"BACKLOG","sort_order":"a4"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T09:50:05.920912Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-f2947b","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-dc1886d0-e35a-4dd6-9a15-af09f8ed5c36","text":"## Changes\n\n### All Issues tab (flat + breadcrumbs)\n- Child issues with a different status from parent render as standalone top-level rows\n- Prefixed with breadcrumb: `Parent Title \u003e Child Title` (muted parent name + chevron)\n- Same-status children still nest normally under their parent\n\n### Active/Backlog tabs (tree with ghost parents)\n- When children exist in a status group but their parent doesn't, a ghost parent row appears at 50% opacity with muted title\n- Ghost parents are always expanded and not draggable\n- Children nest under the ghost parent normally\n\n### Tab adjustments\n- Active tab: PLANNED + DOING + BLOCKED\n- Backlog tab: BACKLOG only\n\n### Implementation\n- Extended `RowItem` type with optional `parentBreadcrumb` and `isGhostParent` fields\n- Split row-building logic in `rows` useMemo by tab type (`isAllTab`)\n- Ghost parents collected by finding children whose parent ID is not in the current status group\n- Breadcrumbs resolved by looking up parent title from the full issues list"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T09:50:16.294304Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
