{"id":"xpo-974810","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-e6ddf1e3-b71e-4a59-8f18-13f3fa0b0546","text":"## Implementation Plan\n\n### Problem\nThe web UI constrains label selection to predefined options in two places:\n1. **Create modal** (`App.tsx`) — hardcoded `InlineDropdown` with only 4 options (bug, feature, epic, improvement)\n2. **Issue detail labels popover** (`IssueDetail.tsx`) — shows builtin labels + labels from existing issues, but no text input to create new ones\n\nThe backend already accepts any label string — no changes needed there.\n\n### Solution\nAdd a combo-box style input (filter + create) to both places, matching the GitHub/standard label picker pattern:\n\n1. **Labels popover in issue detail**: Add a search input at the top. As user types, filter existing labels. If typed text doesn't match any existing label, show a \"Create 'xyz'\" option that adds it immediately.\n\n2. **Create modal**: Replace the fixed `InlineDropdown` with a similar combo-box — show all known labels (builtin + from issues), allow filtering, and allow typing a new label on the fly.\n\n### Files to modify\n- `web/src/components/IssueDetail/IssueDetail.tsx` — labels popover\n- `web/src/App.tsx` — create modal label selector\n- Possibly extract a shared `LabelPicker` component"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T10:17:48.204832Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-974810","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T10:17:52.21603Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-49579f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Issues index tab is lost on detail view","description":"Selecting a different index view tab like Active or Backlog, then navigating to an issue detail view from that list and then either using browser back button or pressing the Esc key to go back to the overview, the selected view is lost and reverts back to All Issues","labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-05-21T10:19:42.465661Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-49579f","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T10:19:51.428092Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-49579f","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"labels":["bug","UX"]},"created_at":"2026-05-21T10:23:58.838667Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-974810","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-4b71a511-f3b0-4fde-a462-1d3dff2e0458","text":"## Changes Summary\n\n### Modified files\n- `web/src/App.tsx` — Replaced hardcoded `InlineDropdown` with a combo-box label picker in the create modal\n- `web/src/components/IssueDetail/IssueDetail.tsx` — Added search/filter input and \"Create\" option to the labels popover\n\n### What changed\n\n**Create modal (`NewIssueModal`):**\n- Removed hardcoded `LABEL_OPTIONS` (was limited to 4 labels: bug, feature, epic, improvement)\n- Added a combo-box label picker that shows all known labels (builtin + from existing issues)\n- Includes a search input to filter labels as you type\n- Shows a \"Create \u003clabel\u003e\" option when the typed text doesn't match any existing label\n- Full keyboard support: arrow keys to navigate, Enter to select, Escape to close\n- Uses `LabelBadge` component for consistent label rendering\n\n**Issue detail labels popover:**\n- Added a search/filter input at the top of the popover\n- Labels are filtered as the user types\n- When typed text doesn't match any existing label, a \"Create \u003clabel\u003e\" option appears\n- Full keyboard support on the input (ArrowUp/Down, Enter, Escape)\n- Shows \"No matching labels\" when filter has no results and text matches an existing label exactly\n\n### No backend changes needed\nThe Go backend already accepts arbitrary label strings — the limitation was purely in the web UI."},"created_at":"2026-05-21T10:24:38.575786Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-4cd67d","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Configurable labels and colors via config file","description":"## Problem\n\nLabels and their colors are currently hardcoded in the frontend:\n- `BUILTIN_LABELS` in `constants.ts` defines the known label set\n- `LABEL_COLORS` in `Badge.tsx` maps only 4 labels to colors, everything else is gray\n- The frontend scans all issues to discover custom labels — no label registry exists\n\n## Solution\n\nAdd a `labels` section to `.beats/config.yaml` that maps label names to hex colors:\n\n```yaml\nlabels:\n  bug: \"#eb5757\"\n  feature: \"#b36cd9\"\n  epic: \"#5e6ad2\"\n  improvement: \"#4da6e8\"\n  UX: \"#e8a64d\"\n  refactor: \"#6bc9a0\"\n```\n\nThis provides a label registry (no scanning issues) and customizable colors in one shot.\n\n## Files to modify\n\n1. `internal/config/config.go` — Add `Labels map[string]string` field\n2. `internal/server/handlers.go` — Expose labels in `/api/config` response\n3. `web/src/api/client.ts` — Update `fetchConfig` return type\n4. `web/src/components/ui/Badge.tsx` — Use config colors instead of hardcoded `LABEL_COLORS`\n5. `web/src/App.tsx` + `web/src/components/IssueDetail/IssueDetail.tsx` — Use config labels as known label set\n6. `.beats/config.yaml` — Add default labels section","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-21T10:55:38.47751Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-4cd67d","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T10:55:41.531987Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-4cd67d","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-2dd2520b-fa28-46fe-952b-40ae4ce3dc2e","text":"## Changes Summary\n\n### Backend\n- **`internal/config/config.go`**: Added `Labels map[string]string` field to the `Config` struct\n- **`internal/server/handlers.go`**: Exposed `labels` in the `/api/config` response\n- **`.beats/config.yaml`**: Added default labels section with colors for bug, feature, epic, improvement, UI, and refactor\n\n### Frontend\n- **`web/src/components/ui/Badge.tsx`**: Added `LabelColorsContext` (React Context) so `LabelBadge` reads config colors without prop drilling. Falls back to hardcoded `LABEL_COLORS`, then to `var(--color-text-muted)`\n- **`web/src/components/ui/index.ts`**: Exported `LabelColorsContext`\n- **`web/src/api/client.ts`**: Updated `fetchConfig` return type to include `labels: Record\u003cstring, string\u003e`\n- **`web/src/App.tsx`**: Fetches config labels, wraps app in `LabelColorsContext.Provider`, passes `configLabels` to `NewIssueModal` and `IssueDetail` for the known label list\n- **`web/src/components/IssueDetail/IssueDetail.tsx`**: Uses config label names as primary source for `allKnownLabels` (falls back to `BUILTIN_LABELS` when config has none)\n\n### How it works\n1. Labels are defined in `.beats/config.yaml` as `labels: { name: \"#hexcolor\" }`\n2. The Go server exposes them via `/api/config`\n3. The frontend uses them as the known label set (replacing hardcoded `BUILTIN_LABELS`) and for rendering colors (via React Context, replacing hardcoded `LABEL_COLORS`)\n4. Custom labels from issues are still discovered and shown alongside config labels\n5. If no labels are configured, falls back to the built-in defaults"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T11:06:17.544607Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-974810","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T11:06:31.900438Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-4cd67d","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-16ee95e5-1b84-4f64-b28b-39e224cea323","text":"## Redesign Complete\n\nSimplified the labels feature based on clearer design principles:\n\n1. **Labels are free-form strings on issues** — no registry, no `BUILTIN_LABELS`\n2. **Config maps names to colors** — purely cosmetic, `.beats/config.yaml`\n3. **Known labels = discovered from issues** — `allKnownLabels` derives from `issues.flatMap()` only\n\n### What was removed\n- `BUILTIN_LABELS` constant from `constants.ts`\n- `LABEL_COLORS` hardcoded map from `Badge.tsx`\n- `--color-label-*` CSS variables from `index.css`\n- `configLabelNames` memo (was used as label registry)\n\n### What was fixed\n- `allKnownLabels` in App.tsx, IssueDetail.tsx, Backlog.tsx — now derived from issues only\n- Optimistic state update — after creating a label color mapping, `configLabels` updates immediately via `onConfigLabelsChange` callback\n- Color picker skip — if config already has a color for a label, the picker is skipped\n- Dependencies.tsx — replaced stale `var(--color-label-epic)` with `var(--color-accent-primary)`\n- Default labels in `setup.go` init template — new projects ship with color mappings for bug, feature, epic, improvement"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T15:01:55.908321Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-4cd67d","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T16:22:20.355719Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-49579f","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"sort_order":"Zy"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T19:35:57.036247Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-49579f","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T19:36:29.13985Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-49579f","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-1ceaca8e-26c7-48ff-b8c4-ca770147bb4d","text":"## Fix\n\nThe `activeTab` state was local to the `Backlog` component. When navigating to an issue detail, `Backlog` unmounted and lost the tab selection. On return, it remounted with the default `'all'` tab.\n\n**Fix:** Lifted `activeTab` state to `App.tsx` and passed it as a prop (`activeTab` + `onTabChange`). The tab now persists across issue detail navigation.\n\n### Files changed\n- `web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx` — exported `Tab` type, replaced local state with props\n- `web/src/App.tsx` — owns `backlogTab` state, passes to `Backlog`"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T19:38:18.018573Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-49579f","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T19:38:18.09721Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
