{"id":"xpo-6178dc","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"The ability to save searches and filters as a custom view, available as a tab besides the built-in views of All Issues, Aactive, and Backlog.\n\nThis requires filters and searching to be implemented first.\n\nFilter options should be by:\n\n- Status\n- Creator\n- Assignee\n- Priority\n- Estimate\n- Labels\n\nView options (display options) should include:\n\n- Grouping (by status"},"created_at":"2026-05-22T05:36:35.993136Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-6178dc","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"The ability to save searches and filters as a custom view, available as a tab besides the built-in views of All Issues, Aactive, and Backlog.\n\nThis requires filters and searching to be implemented first.\n\nFilter options should be by:\n\n- Status\n- Creator\n- Assignee\n- Priority\n- Estimate\n- Labels\n\nView options (display options) should include:\n\n- Grouping (by status, priority, label, assignee)\n- Sub-Grouping"},"created_at":"2026-05-22T05:36:56.332171Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-6178dc","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"The ability to save searches and filters as a custom view, available as a tab besides the built-in views of All Issues, Aactive, and Backlog.\n\nThis requires filters and searching to be implemented first.\n\nFilter options should be by:\n\n- Status\n- Creator\n- Assignee\n- Priority\n- Estimate\n- Labels\n\nView options (display options) should include:\n\n- Grouping (by status, priority, label, assignee, ...)\n- Sub-Grouping (by status, priority, label, assignee,...)\n- Ordering of completed by recency regardless of other sort set\n- Toggle for turning the nesting of sub-issues on and off\n- Toggle for turning the display of empty groups on and off\n- Customization of which data fields are shown (id, status, priority, cycle, estimate, labels, timestamps, ...)"},"created_at":"2026-05-22T05:38:44.486306Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-2094f2","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Ability to define relationships (depends on, blocks, ...)","description":"We should have a way in the user interface to define issue relationships. A \"Relates to\" button that let's use first pick the relationship type from a select menu, and a combobox that allows us to search for issues.","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-22T05:40:18.558198Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-19f91b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Support the concept of Assignee","description":"We should have a new optional data field on issues for \"assignee\" describing the person (identified by name/email) that is assigned to work on that issue.","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-22T05:41:02.165808Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-19f91b","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"parent_id":"xpo-c7b7c6","sort_order":"a5"},"created_at":"2026-05-22T05:41:14.380435Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-1115c8","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Improved delta writing on issues.db","description":"When making changes in the Web UI, we should have a concept of the last snapshot (from git) of the issues.db and all data that was appended after that snapshot (uncommitted). \n\nWhen modifying issues in the UI, we shall not blindly append a new row for each trivial/atomic action but instead be smart and collapse the changes into a minimal set of lines. \n\nThis also means that actions like adding a label and removing that label will not generate 2 entries that effectively cancel each other out, or that updating a comment text 3-4 times with additional information only appends a single update line with the final text instead of multiple updates.","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-22T05:44:26.465862Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-1115c8","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-05-22T05:44:29.696306Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-1115c8","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"sort_order":"Zy"},"created_at":"2026-05-22T05:44:33.218241Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-1115c8","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-05-22T05:45:47.081618Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-1115c8","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-f94c07c6-34aa-4645-81e3-c15cefcd545e","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented smart delta collapsing for uncommitted events in `issues.db`.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Snapshot boundary**: `committedLineCount()` uses `git show HEAD:.beats/issues.db` to determine how many lines are committed. Everything after that line is uncommitted.\n2. **Event collapsing**: When a new UPDATE event arrives for an issue that already has an uncommitted UPDATE, the payloads are merged (field-by-field) instead of appending a new line. Same for COMMENT events with the same comment ID.\n3. **Atomic rewrite**: The uncommitted tail is rewritten via a temp file + rename for crash safety. Committed lines are never touched.\n\n### What collapses\n- Multiple status changes on the same issue → single UPDATE with final status\n- Adding then removing a label → single UPDATE with final labels array  \n- Editing a comment multiple times → single COMMENT event with final text\n- Setting estimate, priority, sort_order, etc. → merged into one UPDATE\n\n### What doesn't collapse\n- CREATE events (always new)\n- DELETE events (always new)\n- Different issues (each issue has its own collapsible UPDATE)\n- CLI commands (`Collapse: false` by default, only web UI sets it)\n\n### Files changed\n- `internal/storage/collapse.go` (new): `AppendEventCollapsed`, `committedLineCount`, merge helpers, `rewriteFile`\n- `internal/beats/client.go`: Added `Collapse` field and `appendEvent()` method\n- `internal/beats/update.go`, `add.go`, `comment.go`, `delete.go`: Use `c.appendEvent()` instead of `storage.AppendEvent()`\n- `internal/server/handlers.go`: Sets `client.Collapse = true` for web UI requests"},"created_at":"2026-05-22T05:56:42.850081Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-1115c8","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-05-22T05:56:42.875721Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-1115c8","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-fe4858e3-6e6f-413c-99c3-416834321919","text":"## Fix: Preserve committed lines byte-for-byte during event collapsing\n\nThe bug was in `rewriteFile()` in `internal/storage/collapse.go` — it re-marshaled committed events through `json.Marshal`, which changed field ordering and whitespace, causing the entire file to show as modified in git diffs.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Replaced `committedLineCount()` with `readCommittedBytes()` — reads the raw bytes from `git show HEAD:.beats/issues.db` instead of just counting lines\n- Added `countLines()` helper to derive the line count from the raw bytes (used to split events into committed vs uncommitted)\n- Changed `rewriteFile()` signature to accept `[]byte` for committed portion — writes them verbatim, only JSON-serializes the uncommitted events\n\nNow only the uncommitted tail of `issues.db` appears in git diffs."},"created_at":"2026-05-22T06:04:30.864998Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
