{"id":"xpo-57dec9","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Currently there is a label select dropdown on the top left side that let's us pick from and set multiple labels. Ideally we could split this into two distinct dropdowns:\n\n- One on the left-hand side that allows to set built-in labels (such as Bug, Feature, Epic, ...) and only allow a single option to be set.\n- Another one on the far right side next to the Estimate dropdown that let's us set any number of custom labels.","labels":["feature"],"title":"Split Labels in Create new issue dialog"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T06:44:59.706732879Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-57dec9","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T06:45:05.01864672Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-9aff89","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Currently, only one instance of `beats board` can be running at any time as it grabs port 8080. We frequently have the requirement to run Beats boards for multiple projects simultaneously and it is cumbersome to navigate to the running instance and terminate it before starting a new instance in another terminal when switching from one project to another.\n\nIt would be great if the first beats instances could register something like \"a proxy\" upon start and additional instances could detect that their default port `8080` is already taken, pick a different port but register themselves with the proxy. In turn the other projects become available in the proxy instances sidebar so the user can easily switch to them.","labels":["feature"],"title":"Ability to start multiple instances of Beats Board in different projects"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T06:48:18.00020306Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-9aff89","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T06:48:24.888764601Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-42f277","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Similarly to the problem we had earlier in xpo-2165bd with the collapse icon, the status icon is also a small click target and we do not have a cursor or hover highlight indication that we are currently on that target.","labels":["bug"],"title":"Click target for status is too small in issue overview"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T06:49:53.896034614Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
