{"id":"xpo-3b872d","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Setting additional metadata fields like assignee, parent issue or relationships like \"blocks\" or \"requires\" in an additional \"show more options\" section at the bottom of the dialog that is collapsed by default to show the simplified view.","labels":["feature"],"title":"Ability to set additional metadata on Create new issue"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T07:01:16.151729454Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-3b872d","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T07:01:16.458052828Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-391b01","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-307fa5be-684a-4600-b1f8-6fd8190f5145","text":"## Summary\n\nThe \"Create new issue\" dialog has `Status` and `Estimate` inline dropdowns, but selections in either were silently discarded on submit.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`web/src/App.tsx` `handleCreate` called `createIssue({ title, description, labels })` — and the `createIssue` API client signature only accepts `{ title, description, labels, parent_id }`. So the local `status` and `estimate` state was never sent.\n\nThe Backlog component's inline-create already worked around this by following up with an `addDraft(id, 'UPDATE', { status })`. I applied the same pattern.\n\n## Change\n\n1. Import `addDraft` alongside `createIssue`.\n2. Capture the returned `issueId` from `createIssue`.\n3. After create, build an UPDATE payload:\n   - include `status` only when `status !== 'BACKLOG'` (the default)\n   - include `estimate` only when `\u003e 0`\n4. Post a single `addDraft(issueId, 'UPDATE', update)` if anything is set.\n\nEstimate was not in the bug report but had the identical defect — same root cause, same fix.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `make frontend` builds cleanly with no TS errors\n- Manually tested: status selected in the dialog is now applied on the created issue"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T07:03:47.944224325Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-391b01","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T07:03:51.8161446Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-5329ec","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T07:05:50.774092863Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-5329ec","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-33934d6d-8133-46af-beee-5dd3e0e054ca","text":"## Summary\n\nThe browser tab now shows `\u003cProject Name\u003e | Beats` so multiple Beats instances open across different projects can be distinguished at a glance.\n\n## Project name source\n\nDecided on **working-directory basename, overridable via config**:\n\n- Default: `filepath.Base(cwd)` — zero config needed for the common case\n- Override: optional `name:` field in `.beats/config.yaml` for projects with ugly or generic directory names\n\n## Changes\n\n### Backend\n\n- `internal/config/config.go` — added `Name string` field to the `Config` struct with `name` yaml/mapstructure tags\n- `internal/server/handlers.go` — `handleGetConfig` now returns a `name` field in the JSON response. Uses `Config.Name` when set, falls back to `filepath.Base(os.Getwd())`\n\n### Frontend\n\n- `web/src/api/client.ts` — extended the `fetchConfig` return type to include `name: string`\n- `web/src/App.tsx` — on config load, sets `document.title = \\`${c.name} | Beats\\`` (or plain `Beats` if name is empty)\n\n## Verification\n\n- `go build ./...` — clean\n- `go test ./internal/config/...` — passes\n- `make frontend` — builds cleanly, no TS errors\n- Manually tested in the browser: tab title reflects the project name"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T07:09:33.666193916Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-5329ec","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T07:09:37.161468471Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-57dec9","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T07:15:10.674198981Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-3b872d","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-8ad96528-bae3-4711-a33b-f21a781bf074","text":"## Scope addition (from xpo-57dec9 discussion)\n\nWhen this issue is implemented, it should also include an **\"Additional Labels\"** multi-select picker (same UX as the one on the issue details page) — placed alongside the new metadata fields (assignee, parent, relationships) in the expandable \"show more options\" section.\n\nThis complements [[xpo-57dec9]], which is converting the existing Label dropdown in the Create dialog to a single-select **primary** label. Custom/secondary labels move here."},"created_at":"2026-05-26T07:15:10.737322555Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-57dec9","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-a21aec99-7705-47a4-b8cb-798b66c1b5f9","text":"## Summary\n\nReworked the Create New Issue dialog's label control into a **single-select primary label** picker, and made the picker consistently show the canonical default labels first with an opt-out config flag.\n\nThe full \"split into two distinct dropdowns\" UX (a separate multi-select \"Additional Labels\" picker) is folded into [[xpo-3b872d]] since that issue is already planned to add expandable metadata fields (assignee, parent, relationships) to the same dialog. Custom secondary labels belong with that group.\n\n## Single-select primary label\n\n- `web/src/components/ui/LabelPicker.tsx` — added `singleSelect?: boolean` prop. When set, rows render a radio-style filled circle instead of a checkbox so the affordance reads as single-choice. Defaults to `false` so the Issue Detail and Backlog inline pickers keep their multi-select behaviour.\n- `web/src/App.tsx` — replaced `toggleLabel` with `selectLabel(l) → setLabels([l]); setLabelOpen(false)`. Trigger button now renders one `LabelBadge` instead of a row of badges. Default of `['feature']` preserved.\n\n## Default labels always first (with config opt-out)\n\nThe four seeded labels (`epic`, `feature`, `bug`, `improvement`) always appear at the top of every label picker in canonical order, then the rest sorted alphabetically (case-insensitive), with a visible divider between the two groups.\n\n### Backend\n\n- `internal/config/config.go` — added `HideDefaultLabels bool` (`hide_default_labels:` in `.beats/config.yaml`). Set to `true` to revert to the prior alphabetical-only ordering.\n- `internal/server/handlers.go` — `/api/config` exposes `hide_default_labels`.\n\n### Frontend\n\n- `web/src/constants.ts` — new `DEFAULT_LABELS` constant with `{name, color}` entries matching the seeded set in `internal/beats/setup.go` so badges render with the correct color even when the user removed a default from their config.\n- `web/src/api/client.ts` — `hide_default_labels: boolean` in the `fetchConfig` return type.\n- `web/src/components/ui/Badge.tsx` — new `HideDefaultLabelsContext` (default `false`), exported from the `ui` barrel.\n- `web/src/App.tsx` — reads `hide_default_labels` from config, provides the new context, and merges `DEFAULT_LABELS` colors into `LabelColorsContext` (user-configured colors win on key collision).\n- `web/src/components/ui/LabelPicker.tsx` — reads `HideDefaultLabelsContext`, prepends defaults in fixed order (case-insensitive dedup), sorts the remainder alphabetically, and renders a divider between defaults and customs. The divider only appears when both groups are present in the filtered list, so search results behave correctly.\n\n### Gotcha\n\nThe divider initially used `--color-border-subtle` (`#1b1b1c`) which is **identical** to `--color-bg-elevated` (`#1b1b1c`, the popover background) — so it was rendering invisibly. Switched to `--color-border-default` (`#28292a`).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `go build ./...` — clean\n- `go test ./internal/config/...` — passes\n- `make frontend` — builds cleanly, no TS errors\n- Manually tested: single-select works, defaults appear first across all three picker call sites (Create dialog, Issue Detail, Backlog inline), divider is visible, alphabetical sort applied to non-default labels"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T07:54:52.119356862Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-57dec9","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T07:54:54.816540229Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-3b872d","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"sort_order":"Zz"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T07:55:30.617780007Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-3b872d","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T08:10:44.777308696Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-3b872d","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-ca6c732f-9b8a-4a65-8815-d552bd21ee6f","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded a collapsible \"More options\" section at the bottom of the Create New Issue dialog with three additional metadata fields: **parent issue**, **assignee**, and **additional labels**. Section is collapsed by default so the simplified view stays the same.\n\nRelationships are left to the issue-details page for now (the originally-spun child issue was removed).\n\n## Backend / API\n\n- `web/src/api/client.ts` — extended the `createIssue` payload type with optional `assignee`. The server's CREATE handler already accepted Title/Description/ParentID/Estimate/Assignee/Labels; the client signature was lagging.\n\n## Dialog state (NewIssueModal in `web/src/App.tsx`)\n\nNew local state:\n\n- `parentId: string`, `assignee: string`, `additionalLabels: string[]`\n- `moreOpen: boolean` (default `false`)\n- `morePopover: 'parent' | 'assignee' | 'labels' | null` — which sub-popover is open\n- `parentSearch`, `assigneeSearch`\n\nDerived data (memoized):\n\n- `parentCandidates` — top-level (`!parent_id`), non-`DONE` issues, filtered by `parentSearch`\n- `knownPeople` — dedup of `created_by` / `assignee` across all issues by email, sorted by display name, filtered by `assigneeSearch`\n\n## UI\n\nA `border-t` divider + chevron toggle (\"More options\") sits between the description editor and the action row. When expanded, it reveals three trigger buttons styled to match the existing Label/Status/Estimate row:\n\n- **Parent issue** — search-and-pick popover (`StatusIcon` + title), with a \"Remove parent\" affordance when one is set\n- **Assignee** — search-and-pick popover (`Avatar` + name), with a \"Remove assignee\" affordance\n- **Additional labels** — reuses `LabelPicker` in its default multi-select mode\n\n## Filtering the primary label out of the Additional Labels picker\n\nA subtle bug surfaced during testing: the additional labels picker still showed the primary label (e.g. `feature`) because `LabelPicker` internally prepends `DEFAULT_LABELS` regardless of what `allLabels` contains. Fixed by adding an `exclude?: string[]` prop to `LabelPicker` that filters both the prepended defaults **and** the alphabetical tail. App.tsx passes `exclude={labels}` (the primary).\n\n## Truncation in the trigger buttons\n\nLong parent issue titles and assignee display names were pushing siblings out of the row. Added `truncate max-w-[200px]` to the parent value span and `truncate max-w-[160px]` to the assignee value span.\n\n## Submit wiring\n\n`handleCreate` now:\n\n1. Builds `combinedLabels = [primary, ...additional minus primary]` (dedup).\n2. Passes `parent_id` and `assignee` through `createIssue` directly (server-supported).\n3. Status + estimate still flow as a follow-up UPDATE draft (unchanged from [[xpo-391b01]]).\n4. Reset block extended to clear `parentId`, `assignee`, `additionalLabels`, and `moreOpen`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `make frontend` — builds cleanly, no TS errors\n- Manually tested: section collapses/expands, all three pickers behave, primary label is excluded from Additional, long titles ellipsis correctly, submitted issue carries parent + assignee + combined labels"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T08:42:27.045274594Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
