{"id":"xpo-237dd6","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-5012bfdf-0d9c-47ad-a5c2-7d5f268045f9","text":"## Summary\n\nPromoted the Dashboard to first-class navigation and made it the default landing view, plus centered the page content.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `web/src/components/Layout/Layout.tsx` — moved `dashboard` from `SECONDARY_NAV` to **first** position in `PRIMARY_NAV` (above Issues and Board). Renamed the label from `Analytics` to `Dashboard` for clarity. Used the existing bar-chart icon.\n- `web/src/App.tsx` — `parseHash` fallback changed from `'backlog'` to `'dashboard'` so opening the app with no hash route lands on the Dashboard.\n- `web/src/components/Dashboard/Dashboard.tsx` — wrapped the scrollable content area in `\u003cdiv className=\"max-w-6xl mx-auto p-6 space-y-6\"\u003e` so the page is horizontally centered on wide screens (was left-hugging). Width bumped from 5xl → 6xl (1152px) per a follow-up tweak.\n\n## Polish notes captured alongside\n\nWhile doing this I also applied a visual polish pass agreed in chat: monochrome stat numbers, aligned metric card layouts, uppercase tracking-wider section headers, ProgressRing repositioned and de-saturated, monochrome distribution bars."},"created_at":"2026-05-26T12:02:36.745336555Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-d23f3e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Replace the current top metric row with a **Pulse** strip that answers \"how is the project doing right now?\" at a glance. Stats only for v1 — clicking through to filtered views comes later.\n\n## Cards (single row, 4 columns)\n\n### 1. Velocity\n- Headline: points completed in the last 7d.\n- Sparkline: last **8 weeks** of weekly buckets (points completed per week).\n- **No-estimate issues count as 1 point** (decision: keeps small/grooming work visible in velocity).\n- Data source: walk the event log, bucket `status = DONE` transition events by week.\n\n### 2. Throughput\n- Headline: count of issues completed in the last 7d.\n- Sub: delta vs prior 7d (e.g. `+12%` or `-3`).\n- Counts all DONE transitions regardless of estimate.\n\n### 3. WIP\n- Headline: count of issues currently in DOING.\n- Sub: subset that's been in DOING \u003e **5d** (stale threshold), called out in warning color if \u003e 0.\n- Stale check: look up the event that last moved the issue into DOING; if older than 5d, count as stale.\n\n### 4. Blockers\n- Headline: count of issues currently in BLOCKED.\n- Sub: age (days) of the **oldest** blocker.\n- Age: timestamp of the event that moved it into BLOCKED.\n\n## Backend\n\nLikely needs a new `/api/metrics` endpoint that walks the event log on the server and returns precomputed metrics (much cheaper than shipping the full event log to the browser).\n\n## Visual style\n\nMatch the existing metric card style from [[xpo-237dd6]]: uppercase tracking-wider header, large monochrome number, muted sub. The sparkline should be monochrome (`text-secondary` stroke) matching the distribution bars.\n\n## Rolling window decisions\n\n- Throughput / velocity window: **7d** rolling.\n- Sparkline buckets: **8 weeks**.\n- Staleness threshold: **5d**.\n- Cycle/sprint concept is deferred — once it lands we revisit these as configurable per-cycle.","labels":["feature"],"title":"Dashboard Phase 1: Pulse row (velocity, throughput, WIP, blockers)"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T12:04:41.559726367Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-70c971","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Two cards that answer **\"what should I look at right now?\"** and **\"is the team balanced?\"**.\n\n## Attention card\n\nA single card with up to 5 rows surfacing the most actionable issues. Sorted by urgency.\n\nRow sources (whichever match — caps total at 5):\n1. Oldest blocker — `title — blocked Nd`\n2. Stale in progress — `title — no movement Nd` (\u003e 5d, matching [[Phase 1 staleness threshold]])\n3. High priority not started — `title` (priority ≤ 2, status = BACKLOG or PLANNED)\n\nClick row → opens the issue detail view.\n\n## Workload table\n\nPer-person row, sorted by in-progress count desc:\n\n| Avatar | Name | In Progress | Open Points | Blocked | Last completed |\n\n- **In Progress**: count of issues in DOING + BLOCKED assigned to this person.\n- **Open Points**: sum of estimates on all non-DONE assigned issues (no-estimate = 1, matching Phase 1).\n- **Blocked**: count of BLOCKED.\n- **Last completed**: date of most recent DONE transition for this person, or \"never\".\n\nImbalance is visible at a glance (someone with 0 in progress vs someone with 8).","labels":["feature"],"title":"Dashboard Phase 2: Attention card + Workload table"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T12:04:41.581579275Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-90adb3","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"One row per active epic (parent issues with sub-issues, non-DONE status). Answers **\"how are our big initiatives tracking?\"**.\n\n## Row layout\n\n| Title | Children done/total | Points done/total | Progress bar | Stale indicator |\n\n- **Title**: clickable, opens the epic.\n- **Counts**: `done/total` for both issue count and story points (using the no-estimate=1 convention).\n- **Progress bar**: monochrome (`text-secondary`), proportional to points-done %.\n- **Stale indicator**: small badge if no child issue has had a status transition in \u003e 5d (matches Phase 1 staleness threshold).\n\n## Sort order\n\nBy **remaining points desc** (biggest active epic first). Done epics drop off the list.\n\n## Empty state\n\nIf no epics exist: \"No epics yet — create one with the `epic` label.\"","labels":["feature"],"title":"Dashboard Phase 3: Epic progress section"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T12:04:41.602316258Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-155c47","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Move the current label/assignee/priority distribution cards (from [[xpo-49c21a]], [[xpo-12c9f8]], [[xpo-0be7ab]]) into a single **\"Composition\"** section near the bottom of the Dashboard, **collapsed by default**.\n\n## Why\n\nAfter Phases 1–3 land, the top of the Dashboard tells the *stories* (pulse, attention, epics, workload). The distribution cards are useful for *exploration*, not insight. They belong as an on-demand drawer, not in the primary visual hierarchy.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Section header with chevron toggle (matches the \"More options\" pattern from [[xpo-3b872d]]).\n- When expanded, renders the three `DistributionSection` cards in the existing single-row layout.\n- State persists to localStorage so a user who opens it once doesn't have to expand again.\n\n## Also revisit\n\n- The current Status Distribution row (5 small cards) — also a candidate for demotion if Phase 1 Pulse covers status health adequately.","labels":["feature"],"title":"Dashboard Phase 4: Demote composition cards to collapsible section"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T12:04:41.6232625Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
