{"id":"xpo-d23f3e","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-ddf9e7d2-118c-4b9c-9bcc-b8454bb5e7cb","text":"## Summary\n\nReplaced the old top metric row (Overall Progress / Active Work / Pipeline) with the new **Pulse** row of four story-led cards — velocity, throughput, WIP, blockers — backed by a new `/api/metrics` endpoint that walks the event log server-side.\n\n## Backend\n\n`internal/server/metrics.go` (new):\n\n- `computePulseMetrics(issues, now)` — single pass over projected issues. For each issue, `latestStatusTimestamps()` walks `issue.Events` once and returns timestamps of the most recent UPDATE events that set status to DONE / DOING / BLOCKED. Auto-progressed parents (no explicit status event) correctly return nil and are excluded from velocity/throughput.\n- **Velocity**: `last_7d_points` + `weekly_buckets` (8 Monday-aligned weekly buckets, oldest → newest). No-estimate issues count as **1 point** per the agreed convention.\n- **Throughput**: `last_7d` count + signed absolute `delta` vs prior 7d (chose count delta over % — clearer at small N).\n- **WIP**: count in DOING + `stale` subset where the move-to-DOING event is older than the `stale_threshold_days` (5d, defined in package constant for easy tuning).\n- **Blockers**: count in BLOCKED + age of the oldest blocker in days.\n\n`internal/server/router.go` — registered `GET /api/metrics`.\n\nThe endpoint reuses `s.GetProjectedIssues()` so it includes pending unsaved events. Metrics reflect what the user sees in the UI.\n\n## Frontend\n\n`web/src/api/client.ts` — `PulseMetrics` type + `fetchMetrics()`.\n\n`web/src/components/Dashboard/Dashboard.tsx`:\n\n- Fetches metrics on mount, polls every 30s, refreshes on `window.focus` and whenever the issues prop changes.\n- **Replaced** the entire old top metric row with the Pulse row (`grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4`).\n- New `PulseCard` and `Sparkline` helper components.\n- Sparkline: 8 monochrome bars (`text-secondary` fill), max-normalized so the relative shape is visible. 1px minimum height so zero-weeks still register visually instead of disappearing.\n- Throughput delta colored green for positive, warning for negative, muted at zero. Sign prefix on positive (`+3` vs `-2`).\n- WIP stale subset surfaced in warning color with a clock icon. Always hidden when zero (no \"all fresh\" noise).\n- Blockers oldest-age surfaced in error color, hidden when zero.\n- Loading state: `—` placeholder per card while the first fetch is in flight.\n\n## Cut\n\n- Old \"Overall Progress\" ring — replaced by velocity/throughput which are more actionable.\n- Old \"Active Work\" card — replaced by WIP with the stale callout.\n- Old \"Pipeline\" card — redundant with Status Distribution row below.\n- Unused `ProgressRing` import + `completionRate` variable.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `go build ./...` — clean\n- `go test ./internal/...` — passes\n- `make frontend` — builds cleanly\n- Manually tested: metrics populate, sparkline renders, polling refreshes, delta colors correct, stale + oldest-blocker callouts appear/hide based on data"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T12:22:47.804012708Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
