{"id":"xpo-70c971","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-1f449a8f-deea-4dac-9d72-e6eb409188b8","text":"## Summary\n\nExtended `/api/metrics` with two new payload sections (`attention` and `workload`), added two Dashboard cards rendering them side-by-side below the Pulse row.\n\n## Backend (`internal/server/metrics.go`)\n\nSame endpoint, new fields. Computed during the single pass over projected issues.\n\n- **`attention[]`** — up to 5 items, gathered into three candidate lists, then concatenated in severity order: blockers (sorted by age desc) → stale WIP (by age desc) → high-priority not-started (priority 1 before 2). Each item carries `issue_id`, `title`, `kind` (`blocker` | `stale_wip` | `high_priority`), `age_days` for the first two, `priority` for the third.\n- **`workload[]`** — `map[assignee]*workAccum` accumulator. Skips issues without an assignee. **InProgress** = DOING + BLOCKED count. **OpenPoints** = sum of `max(estimate, 1)` on non-DONE issues (no-estimate = 1 convention from [[xpo-d23f3e]]). **Blocked** = subset count. **LastCompleted** = max DONE-transition timestamp from `latestStatusTimestamps()` across this person's currently-DONE issues, formatted `YYYY-MM-DD`. Sorted stable: `InProgress` desc, then `OpenPoints` desc as tiebreaker.\n\n## Frontend\n\n`web/src/api/client.ts` — added `AttentionItem` and `WorkloadEntry` types and extended `PulseMetrics`.\n\n`web/src/App.tsx` — wired `onIssueClick={handleIssueClick}` through to `\u003cDashboard\u003e`. Click on a Needs Attention row opens that issue.\n\n`web/src/components/Dashboard/Dashboard.tsx`:\n\n- New section below Pulse: `grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2` with Workload on the left, Needs Attention on the right.\n- **Workload table**: column header row + per-person rows (Avatar + name | WIP | Pts | Blocked). Compact `grid-cols-[1fr_auto_auto_auto]` layout. Blocked column colored error when \u003e 0, muted otherwise. `last_completed` exposed as a `title` tooltip on hover instead of a dedicated column — saves horizontal space while still being discoverable.\n- **Needs Attention card**: each row = small uppercase pill badge (`BLOCKED` red / `STALE` warning / `URGENT` or `HIGH` neutral) + truncated title + days-old on the right. Click → `onIssueClick(issue)`. New `AttentionBadge` and `attentionMeta` helpers.\n\n## Stability + empty states\n\n- Both cards have `min-h-[220px]` so they don't collapse when empty.\n- Pulse cards have `min-h-[128px]` so the row holds steady regardless of conditional secondary callouts.\n- DistributionSection (label/assignee/priority breakdowns) also got `min-h-[160px]` + centered empty states.\n- All empty states use `flex-1 flex items-center justify-center` to vertically and horizontally center the message in the card's reserved space.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `go build ./...` — clean\n- `make frontend` — builds cleanly\n- Manually tested: attention surfaces blockers and stale items correctly, workload table sorts by WIP, clicking attention row opens issue, empty states center properly"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T12:35:44.706914286Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
