{"id":"xpo-90adb3","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-456311b7-3e02-4582-98e6-58cd80e21d55","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded an **Active Epics** section to the Dashboard with one row per epic, surfacing children done/total, points done/total, a progress bar with %, and a stale badge when warranted.\n\n## Backend (`internal/server/metrics.go`)\n\n- New `epicProgress` payload type and `computeEpicProgress(issues, now)` function (separate pass after the main Pulse pass).\n- **Epic definition**: issue with the `epic` label (case-insensitive via `strings.EqualFold`), at least one immediate child, and status in PLANNED / DOING / BLOCKED. BACKLOG epics are queued (not started) and excluded. DONE epics are completed and excluded.\n- **Counts**: `children_done` (DONE children) / `children_total`, `points_done` / `points_total` using the no-estimate=1 convention from [[xpo-d23f3e]].\n- **Sort**: `points_remaining` desc, with title as tiebreaker — biggest active initiative first.\n\n## Stale rule (took two iterations to land)\n\nInitial spec was \"no child status transition in \u003e 5d\". Two refinements based on feedback:\n\n1. **Transitions *to* BACKLOG don't count** — moving a child back into the queue isn't \"activity\" in the work-happening sense. Children sitting in BACKLOG with no non-BACKLOG transition contribute nothing to the freshness signal.\n2. **BACKLOG epics shouldn't appear at all** — the section is \"Active Epics\". An epic whose own status is BACKLOG is queued, not active, so it's excluded entirely (not just unmarked-stale).\n\nFinal rule: epic is stale if at least one child has ever transitioned to a non-BACKLOG status AND the most recent such transition was more than `staleWipDays` (5d) ago. Brand-new epics with no non-BACKLOG transitions yet get the benefit of the doubt (no stale badge).\n\n## Frontend\n\n`web/src/api/client.ts` — added `EpicProgress` type, extended `PulseMetrics`.\n\n`web/src/components/Dashboard/Dashboard.tsx` — new section between Workload/Attention and Status Distribution. Row layout: `grid-cols-[auto_1fr_auto_auto_120px_auto]`:\n\n| CopyableId | Title (truncated, click → open issue) | Children done/total | Points done/total | Progress bar with % | Stale badge or aligned placeholder |\n\n- Monochrome progress bar (`text-secondary`), consistent with the rest of the Dashboard.\n- Stale badge uses the warning color treatment matching the Needs Attention `STALE` pill.\n- When not stale, a fixed-width placeholder keeps the column aligned across rows.\n- Empty state centered: \"No epics yet — create one with the `epic` label.\"\n\n## Verification\n\n- `go build ./...` — clean\n- `make frontend` — builds cleanly\n- Manually tested with a mix of active/backlog/done epics; only the actively-worked ones surface, stale flags fire only when work has truly stalled"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T12:59:34.370842229Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
