{"id":"xpo-155c47","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-683ff128-1493-4dbf-9566-62fed9f30597","text":"## Summary\n\nDemoted the four exploration cards (status distribution + label/assignee/priority breakdowns) into a single collapsible **\"Composition\"** section at the bottom of the Dashboard, **collapsed by default** with state persisted to localStorage.\n\n## Why\n\nAfter Phases 1–3, the top of the Dashboard tells the *stories*: Pulse (velocity/throughput/WIP/blockers), Workload, Needs Attention, Active Epics. The distribution cards are useful for *exploration* but should be on-demand, not in the primary visual hierarchy.\n\nThe status distribution row was also demoted (the spec mentioned this as a candidate — Pulse now covers DOING/BLOCKED actively, so the 5-card status row is exploration, not insight).\n\n## Implementation (`web/src/components/Dashboard/Dashboard.tsx`)\n\n- New state `compositionOpen` initialized from `localStorage.getItem('exponential-dashboard-composition-open')` (`'1'` → expanded).\n- `toggleComposition()` read-modify-writes both state and localStorage on each click.\n- Section header uses the muted uppercase tracking-wider style with a chevron that rotates 90° when expanded — same affordance as the \"More options\" pattern from [[xpo-3b872d]].\n- When expanded, renders two subsections inside a `space-y-6` container:\n  1. **By status** — 5-card status row\n  2. **By label / By assignee / By priority** — single-row breakdowns\n- Subsection headers tightened to \"By X\" form since they're now nested under the \"Composition\" parent.\n\n## Final Dashboard flow\n\n1. **Pulse row** — Velocity, Throughput, WIP, Blockers\n2. **Workload + Needs Attention**\n3. **Active Epics**\n4. **Composition** (collapsed by default)\n\n## Verification\n\n- `make frontend` — builds cleanly\n- Toggle expands/collapses; reload preserves the state correctly via localStorage"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T13:02:05.69685286Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-155c47","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T13:02:10.30402034Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-5b11b2","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Goal\n\nApply visual polish to the Dashboard to bring it into line with the visual language already established by the Issues view: dark, minimal, monochrome, with color used sparingly.\n\n## Issues observed\n\n- Flat information hierarchy: every section uses the same  label treatment, so nothing reads as primary.\n- Wasted vertical space:  /  /  minimums make sparse cards feel cavernous.\n- Type-scale gap: KPI numbers (28px) vs labels (~10px uppercase) is too wide.\n- Zero-state KPIs ( in WIP/Blockers) visually compete with non-zero numbers.\n- Sparkline floats orphaned beside the Velocity number with no anchor.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Section headers across the Dashboard:  mixed-case (match Issues view: ).\n- PulseCard labels: mixed-case , drop uppercase.\n- Move sparkline below the Velocity number.\n- Mute zero-state KPI numbers (use  color when value is 0).\n- Shrink card min-heights so empty/sparse cards do not reserve large blocks.\n- Increase outer section spacing slightly ( → ) for breathing room.\n- Composition collapsible header: same new section-header treatment.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- No new metrics, no functional changes.\n- Keep uppercase microlabels only where canonical: Workload column headers (), AttentionBadge pills ( /  / ), Active Epics  indicator.","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"xpo-4faf3d","title":"Dashboard: visual polish — hierarchy, type scale, breathing room"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T13:27:20.23175691Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-5b11b2","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## Goal\n\nApply visual polish to the Dashboard to match the visual language already established by the Issues view: dark, minimal, monochrome, with color used sparingly.\n\n## Issues observed\n\n- **Flat information hierarchy** — every section uses the same  label treatment, so nothing reads as primary.\n- **Wasted vertical space** —  /  /  minimums make sparse cards feel cavernous.\n- **Type-scale gap** — KPI numbers (~28px) vs labels (~10px uppercase) is too wide; nothing carries section-heading weight.\n- **Zero-state KPIs** —  in WIP/Blockers visually competes with non-zero numbers like .\n- **Sparkline orphaned** — floats beside the Velocity number with no anchor.\n\n## Changes\n\n1. Section headers across the Dashboard: replace  with  mixed-case (match Issues view: ).\n2.  labels: mixed-case , drop uppercase.\n3. Move the velocity sparkline below the number so each KPI reads top-to-bottom.\n4. Mute zero-state KPI numbers — use  color when value is 0.\n5. Shrink card min-heights so empty/sparse cards do not reserve large blocks.\n6. Increase outer section spacing slightly ( → ) for breathing room.\n7. Composition collapsible header: same new section-header treatment.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- No new metrics, no functional changes.\n- Keep uppercase microlabels only where canonical:\n  - Workload column headers ()\n  - AttentionBadge pills ( /  / )\n  - Active Epics  indicator","status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T13:33:59.435371005Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-5b11b2","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"Harmonize the Dashboard's visual treatment with the polished Issues view. Currently the Dashboard reads as a slide deck of detached cards while Issues reads as one connected document. The plan below brings them into the same visual language.\n\n## Concrete changes\n\n### 1. Drop the centered `max-w-6xl` — go full-width\nIssues uses the full panel width. The centered column is the single biggest reason the Dashboard reads as a different page. Use consistent `px-6` left/right padding, no max width.\n\n### 2. De-card the list sections\n- **Keep** Pulse as tile cards (KPIs read well as discrete cards).\n- **Drop** the `\u003cCard variant=\"elevated\"\u003e` wrapper from Workload, Needs Attention, Active Epics, and Recent Activity. They become inline lists under a section header. Section dividers do the visual separation, not card borders.\n\n### 3. New section-header treatment, matching Issues' group headers\nReplace the current `text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-muted` section labels with the Issues-style group header:\n\n- `flex items-center gap-2 px-5 h-11 border-b border-subtle`\n- Small left icon\n- `text-sm font-medium text-primary` plain-case name (e.g., `Workload`)\n- Muted count on the right where applicable (e.g., `Active Epics 4`, `Recent Activity 30`)\n- Hover affordance + chevron toggle to collapse, mirroring the Backlog group pattern\n\n### 4. Top header bar should match Issues' chrome\nCurrently it's just `\u003cspan\u003eDashboard\u003c/span\u003e` in an 11px-tall row. Match Issues exactly: same height, same `border-b`, same typography. Add right-side meta (e.g., `Updated Xm ago` or issue count) so the rhythm matches.\n\n### 5. Tighten breathing room\nDrop inter-section spacing from `space-y-6` (24px) to `space-y-0` and let the section borders carry the separation. Section internals stay at `py-3`. The page becomes a continuous list of titled sections, like Issues' status groups.\n\n### 6. Pulse tiles: tone down\n- `min-h-[128px]` → `min-h-[112px]`\n- Padding `p-4` → `p-3.5`\n\nLess visual weight per tile so the row reads as a strip, not four blocks.\n\n### 7. Composition toggle: just another collapsible section\nWith the new section-header pattern from #3, the Composition section already has the toggle affordance built in. Drop the bespoke chevron + `border-t` treatment so it becomes uniform with every other section.\n\n## What to keep\n\n- Pulse cards themselves (tile pattern works for KPIs).\n- All current monochrome bars, status icons, attention pills — already polished.\n- The action icons in Recent Activity (from [[xpo-8faf44]]).\n- The empty-state centering pattern.\n\n## Phasing (single PR, suggested order)\n\n1. Header bar + remove centering — cheapest, biggest perceived shift.\n2. New `\u003cSection\u003e` helper component (title + icon + count + collapsible).\n3. De-card the four list sections, replacing `\u003cCard\u003e` with the new section pattern.\n4. Composition section uses the same pattern.\n5. Pulse tile tightening + final spacing pass.\n\n## Why\n\nThe Issues view's polish comes from inline rows over cards, section headers with weight and count, full-width layout, and tight density. The Dashboard currently has none of those four things. Adopting them is purely visual — no metric logic changes — but should make the two views feel like one app."},"created_at":"2026-05-26T13:38:43.48164007Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
