{"id":"xpo-ab8ef1","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-c1c938c0-51d0-4be5-b51c-89040bc7d62d","text":"## Summary\n\nThe \"Needs Attention\" section landed as part of [[xpo-70c971]] (Dashboard Phase 2), and stale-issue detection is split between that section and the WIP card in [[xpo-d23f3e]] (Phase 1). Closing this out and documenting what shipped vs. the original spec.\n\n## What landed\n\nThe **Needs Attention** section surfaces up to 5 actionable issues, sourced (in severity order) from three candidate lists, each with a distinct colored pill badge:\n\n1. **`BLOCKED`** — every issue currently in BLOCKED status, sorted by age desc. The oldest blocker's age is also called out in the Pulse \"Blockers\" card.\n2. **`STALE`** — issues in DOING whose move-to-DOING event is older than 5 days, sorted by age desc.\n3. **`URGENT`** / **`HIGH`** — priority ≤ 2 with status BACKLOG or PLANNED.\n\nEach row: badge + truncated title + age-days, click → open issue detail.\n\n## Differences from original spec\n\n| Original | What landed | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| Stale DOING \u003e 7d | Stale DOING \u003e 5d | Aligned with the Pulse WIP staleness threshold so the two cards tell the same story. |\n| Blocked \u003e 3d | All blockers surfaced, sorted by age desc | Surfaces more, not less — the oldest blocker is always #1, and the Blockers Pulse card adds `oldest Nd` callout for emphasis. |\n| Aging backlog \u003e 30d | Not implemented | Backlog age isn't tracked in Pulse, and surfacing aging-backlog items risks overlap with the High-priority-not-started source. Worth a follow-up if it proves missing. |\n| (n/a) | **High-priority not started** added | Surfaces Urgent (P1) and High (P2) issues sitting in BACKLOG/PLANNED — caught by team-lead review during the design conversation. |\n\n## Visibility behavior\n\nThe whole section auto-hides when there's nothing surfaced (no blockers, stale WIP, or high-priority backlog items). When calm, the eye flows directly from Pulse to Workload without a vestigial \"Nothing urgent\" placeholder.\n\n## Future follow-up (not blocking)\n\nIf \"aging backlog \u003e 30d\" turns out to matter, it'd be a one-source addition to `computePulseMetrics` in `internal/server/metrics.go` — walk events, check creation timestamp, no status transitions, status still BACKLOG. New attention kind `aging_backlog`."},"created_at":"2026-05-26T15:05:14.185344674Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
