{"id":"xpo-a79a91","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-674d7782-e9fe-4480-a6f4-3739e0236d6d","text":"## Summary\n\nBuilt as one of three cards in a new **Trends** section on the Dashboard, alongside [[xpo-52bad2]] and [[xpo-6958d5]].\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Backend (`internal/server/metrics.go`)\n\n- Extended `/api/metrics` with a `trends` block (new `trendsBlock` type).\n- New `weeklyTrend` payload: `week_start`, `created`, `completed` per week.\n- Reuses the existing 8-week Monday-aligned bucket window from the Pulse velocity sparkline. Single pass over issues: `CreatedAt` increments the `created` count for that week's bucket; the latest move-to-DONE timestamp increments `completed` for its bucket.\n\n### Frontend (`web/src/components/Dashboard/Dashboard.tsx`)\n\n- New `TrendChart` SVG component renders 8 weekly pairs of bars side-by-side.\n  - Created bar in `text-muted` (gray)\n  - Completed bar in `accent-primary` (blue)\n  - 6px wide bars, 2px inner gap within a week-group, 6px gap between groups, 56px chart height. Min 1px height so empty weeks still register.\n- Card includes a small inline legend (`■ created   ■ completed`) in the header row.\n- `last 8 weeks` caption anchored to the card bottom via `flex flex-col` + `mt-auto` so the baseline aligns with the sibling cards.\n\n## Departures from original spec\n\n- **Bars instead of lines** — paired bars per week read better in the compact card width than two overlapping polylines, especially when the two series diverge sharply.\n- **Issue counts, not points** — Velocity (points) is already covered by the Pulse sparkline. This card tracks pure throughput in/out, which the spec called for as \"created vs completed\".\n\n## Verification\n\n`make frontend` builds cleanly. Manually checked: weeks render in chronological order (oldest left, newest right), bar heights scale to the max of either series across the window, legend dots match bar colors."},"created_at":"2026-05-26T15:27:04.912583853Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-52bad2","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-489e3cb7-e943-4595-87d8-3fb11ab7d0df","text":"## Summary\n\nBuilt as one of three cards in a new **Trends** section on the Dashboard, alongside [[xpo-a79a91]] and [[xpo-6958d5]].\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Backend (`internal/server/metrics.go`)\n\n- Extended the `trends` block in `/api/metrics` with:\n  - `median_triage_mins int` — median triage time in minutes\n  - `triaged_count int` — number of issues that contributed to the median\n\n- **Triage time definition**: `CreatedAt → first UPDATE event that sets status to anything other than BACKLOG` (i.e. first move into PLANNED, DOING, BLOCKED, or DONE). Issues that never left BACKLOG don't contribute.\n- Computed in the existing single pass over issues; durations accumulated in a slice, then sorted at the end and indexed at `len/2`.\n\n### Frontend (`web/src/components/Dashboard/Dashboard.tsx`)\n\n- New `formatTriage(mins)` helper renders adaptive units:\n  - `\u003c60m` → `Xm`\n  - `\u003c24h` → `Xh`\n  - `\u003c10d` → `X.Yd` (one decimal)\n  - `≥10d` → `Xd` (rounded)\n- Card layout: header at top, big monochrome headline number, `across N triaged issues` (or `no triaged issues yet` when empty) anchored to the bottom via `flex flex-col` + `mt-auto` so the baseline aligns with the sibling cards.\n\n## Verification\n\n`make frontend` builds cleanly. Tested with the current project: median renders as `17m` across 79 triaged issues."},"created_at":"2026-05-26T15:27:04.965123919Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-6958d5","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-238b0451-cf28-4009-9b67-e392ab43ebdf","text":"## Summary\n\nBuilt as one of three cards in a new **Trends** section on the Dashboard, alongside [[xpo-a79a91]] and [[xpo-52bad2]].\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Backend (`internal/server/metrics.go`)\n\n- Extended the `trends` block in `/api/metrics` with a `bug_age` payload — six buckets covering the lifecycle of open bugs:\n  - `under_24h`, `under_48h`, `under_5d`, `under_14d`, `under_1mo`, `over_1mo`\n- **Selection**: non-DONE issues with the `bug` label (case-insensitive via `strings.EqualFold`, mirroring the existing `hasEpicLabel` pattern). New `hasBugLabel` helper.\n- **Bucketing**: `now - issue.CreatedAt`, fall-through switch ordered youngest → oldest so each issue lands in exactly one bucket.\n\n### Frontend (`web/src/components/Dashboard/Dashboard.tsx`)\n\n- Vertical bar chart, time on the X axis, count on Y.\n- 6 buckets along the X axis (`\u003c24h`, `\u003c48h`, `\u003c5d`, `\u003c14d`, `\u003c1mo`, `\u003e1mo`).\n- 12px wide bars (`w-3 rounded-t-sm`) centered in flex cells so labels stay evenly spaced.\n- 48px tall chart area, bars proportional to the max bucket count, 2px minimum height when count \u003e 0.\n- Severity-graded colors: fresh (`\u003c24h`, `\u003c48h`) in `text-secondary`, mid-age (`\u003c5d`, `\u003c14d`) in `warning`, stale (`\u003c1mo`, `\u003e1mo`) in `error`.\n- Count appears as a small tabular number above each non-zero bar.\n- Chart+labels block anchored to the bottom of the card via `flex flex-col` + `mt-auto` so the bucket labels' baseline aligns with the sibling cards' bottom captions.\n- Empty state: `0` + `no open bugs` when total is 0 across all buckets.\n\n## Initial design and iteration\n\nFirst pass was horizontal rows (label + bar + count) with three coarse buckets (`\u003c7d`, `7-30d`, `\u003e30d`). User asked for finer-grained buckets and a flipped orientation — vertical bars with time on X axis. Then asked for narrower bars (`w-full` → `w-3`), and finally for the baseline alignment with the other Trends cards. Final design landed after all three.\n\n## Verification\n\n`make frontend` builds cleanly. Tested with the current project: empty state renders correctly when there are no open bug-labeled issues; bars render proportionally when bugs exist."},"created_at":"2026-05-26T15:27:05.00594179Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
