{"id":"xpo-725327","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Problem\n\nAgents currently pass long markdown descriptions and comments via the `--desc` flag and `beats comment \u003cid\u003e \"\u003ctext\u003e\"` positional argument. Multi-line markdown with backticks, quotes, `$`, and other shell metacharacters frequently breaks under shell escaping, leading to malformed content or aborted commands.\n\n## Proposal\n\nSupport reading description/comment body from stdin or a file:\n\n- `beats add --desc-stdin \"Title\"` — read description from stdin\n- `beats add --desc-file path.md \"Title\"` — read description from file\n- `beats comment \u003cid\u003e --stdin` — read comment body from stdin\n- `beats comment \u003cid\u003e --file path.md` — read comment body from file\n- `beats update \u003cid\u003e --desc-stdin` / `--desc-file` — same for updates\n\nThe existing `--desc \"string\"` and positional comment forms remain for short, single-line text.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `--desc-stdin` / `--desc-file` work for `beats add` and `beats update`\n- [ ] `--stdin` / `--file` work for `beats comment`\n- [ ] Mutually exclusive with the inline string form (error if both passed)\n- [ ] Trailing newline trimmed; otherwise content preserved verbatim\n- [ ] Tests cover multi-line markdown with backticks, quotes, `$`, and `!`\n\n## Rationale\n\nShort-term fix for the shell-escaping pain described in [[xpo-7ec710]]. Works with any agent transport (CLI today, also useful for humans piping from editors). Does not block the longer-term MCP work.","labels":["feature","CLI"],"title":"Add stdin/file input for description and comment text"},"created_at":"2026-05-27T06:03:18.980772577Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-5b37e3","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Problem\n\nAgents interact with beats through the CLI, which means every description, comment, or update is squeezed through shell arguments. This causes recurring escaping breakage (see [[xpo-7ec710]]) and makes integration with Claude Code, Cursor, and other MCP-capable agents clunkier than it needs to be.\n\n## Proposal\n\nAdd a `beats mcp` subcommand that runs an MCP server (stdio transport for local use; HTTP/SSE later if needed) exposing the core operations as structured tools:\n\n- `beats_list` — list issues with filters\n- `beats_show` — fetch an issue with comments and history\n- `beats_add` — create an issue (title, description, labels, parent, story points)\n- `beats_update` — patch fields on an existing issue\n- `beats_comment` — add a comment\n- `beats_start` / `beats_done` / `beats_planned` / `beats_blocked` — status transitions\n- `beats_link` — add dependencies/relationships\n- `beats_history` — audit trail\n\nArguments are passed as JSON via MCP, so shell escaping disappears entirely.\n\n## Scope decisions to make\n\n- **Transport:** stdio first (per-project local server); HTTP later only if multi-user use cases emerge\n- **Identity:** how the MCP server records \"who\" did the action — env var, config field, or client-supplied?\n- **Distribution:** ship as a subcommand of the existing `beats` binary, no separate process or package\n- **Library reuse:** tools should call the same internal Go functions the CLI uses, not shell out to itself\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `beats mcp` starts an MCP server over stdio\n- [ ] All core read/write operations exposed as tools with JSONSchema params\n- [ ] Example client config snippet documented for Claude Code (`.mcp.json`) and Cursor\n- [ ] Agent identity is recorded on writes\n- [ ] Integration test exercises a full create → comment → done flow over MCP\n\n## Rationale\n\nMCP is the agent-native answer to [[xpo-7ec710]]. Skills don't solve the problem (they still call the CLI underneath), and stdin support is only a stopgap. This unlocks structured access for any MCP-capable agent.\n\n## Possible breakdown\n\nMay warrant promotion to an epic with sub-issues for:\n\n1. MCP server scaffolding + stdio transport\n2. Read-operation tool surface\n3. Write-operation tool surface\n4. Identity/auth handling\n5. Documentation and example client config","labels":["feature","CLI","Backend"],"title":"Expose beats as an MCP server for agent-native access"},"created_at":"2026-05-27T06:03:39.415261281Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
