{"id":"xpo-725327","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-05-27T06:55:59.029801776Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-725327","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-d6ff6b84-fbb4-4bc5-b7b0-dfe65a614037","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented the two-mode stdin/JSON input design end-to-end across `add`, `update`, and `comment`. All five planned phases landed in a single PR-worth of changes.\n\n## What changed\n\n### Phase 1 — Payload unification\n\n- Added `Status string` to `model.CreatePayload` so callers can set the initial status at creation time (default remains `BACKLOG`).\n- Dropped the redundant `beats.AddOptions` struct. `Client.AddIssue` now takes `model.CreatePayload` directly.\n- `Client.AddIssue` auto-fills `Dependency.SourceID` with the newly generated issue ID so callers don't need to know the ID up front.\n- Updated `internal/beats/projection.go` to honor the new `Status` field on CREATE events.\n- Simplified `internal/server/handlers.go` — the previous awkward `CreatePayload`→`AddOptions` translation is now a single call.\n\n### Phase 2 — Plain-text stdin + `-` opt-in\n\n- New helper file `cmd/beats/stdin.go` with three functions: `isStdinPiped()`, `readAllStdin()` (trims trailing newlines, preserves everything else), `readStdinExplicit()` (errors instead of hanging when stdin is a TTY).\n- `beats add \"title\"` now reads description from stdin when piped (and `--desc` not passed).\n- `beats add --desc - \"title\"` and `beats update \u003cid\u003e --desc -` opt in explicitly.\n- `beats update \u003cid\u003e` reads description from stdin when piped and no flags set.\n- `beats comment \u003cid\u003e -` opts in explicitly to stdin.\n\n### Phase 3 — Structured `--json` mode\n\n- New file `cmd/beats/json_input.go` defines `addJSONInput`, `updateJSONInput`, `commentJSONInput` with agent-friendly JSON field names (`parent`, `story_points`, `links`) that convert to the internal model types.\n- `decodeStrict` uses `DisallowUnknownFields` so typos surface as errors instead of being silently dropped.\n- Status enum is validated against the five known values.\n- Link types are normalized via the existing `normalizeDependencyKind` helper.\n- Both flag-path and JSON-path funnel through the same `Client.AddIssue` / `Client.UpdateIssue` / `Client.AddComment` functions — no duplicated business logic. This is the load-bearing piece for [[xpo-5b37e3]].\n\n### Phase 4 — Tests\n\n- `cmd/beats/json_input_test.go` covers strict decoding, status validation, link conversion, partial update patches, and a full multi-line markdown round-trip (backticks, quotes, `$vars`, code blocks).\n- Added three tests in `internal/beats/beats_test.go`: `AddIssue` with `Status` set, default status, auto-filled `SourceID` on dependencies.\n\n### Phase 5 — Verification\n\n- `go build ./...` clean, `go test ./...` green, `go vet ./...` clean.\n- Manual smoke tests in a temporary `.beats` workspace covered all 6 transports (plain stdin / `-` / `--json` × add / update / comment) plus error paths (unknown JSON fields, missing required title, invalid status, `-` with a TTY).\n- End-to-end check: a JSON payload containing `##` headings, backticks, `\"quotes\"`, `$env_vars`, `!bangs`, `\u0026 \u003c \u003e`, and triple-backtick code blocks round-trips byte-perfect into the event log.\n\n## Usage cheat sheet\n\n```bash\n# Plain stdin (auto-detect, no flags)\necho \"body\" | beats add \"Title\"\ncat desc.md  | beats update xpo-abc123\necho \"comment\" | beats comment xpo-abc123\n\n# Explicit `-` opt-in\nbeats add --desc - \"Title\" \u003c desc.md\nbeats update xpo-abc123 --desc - \u003c desc.md\nbeats comment xpo-abc123 - \u003c body.md\n\n# Structured JSON payload\nbeats add --json \u003c payload.json\nbeats update xpo-abc123 --json \u003c patch.json\nbeats comment xpo-abc123 --json \u003c comment.json\n```\n\n## Usage note (worth flagging)\n\nThe ticket spec showed `beats add --json -` with a trailing `-`. In practice cobra parses that `-` as a positional argument, which collides with `update`'s `ExactArgs(1)`. The working form is just `--json` (no trailing `-`); stdin is implied by the flag, and the source is whatever the shell pipes in (`\u003c file` or `|`). Behavior is correct end-to-end, just a minor docs nit relative to the ticket prose.\n\n## Architectural note for xpo-5b37e3\n\n`Client.AddIssue(model.CreatePayload)`, `Client.UpdateIssue(id, model.UpdatePayload, action)`, and `Client.AddComment(id, text)` are now the single entry points for issue mutations. Flag-path and JSON-path in the CLI both call them. The MCP server in [[xpo-5b37e3]] should adapt its tools to these same functions — JSONSchema for each tool can be derived from the input structs in `cmd/beats/json_input.go` (or the internal `CreatePayload`/`UpdatePayload` directly)."},"created_at":"2026-05-27T07:23:53.81504297Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-725327","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-05-27T07:24:32.156630211Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-5b37e3","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-05-27T07:33:18.678006591Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-5b37e3","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-b2f60075-2840-441b-9047-e3ffae371415","text":"## Summary\n\nMCP server is fully wired and tested. `beats mcp` launches a stdio MCP server with the full 7-tool surface, all funnelling through the same `internal/beats` Client methods the CLI uses (delivering on the architectural promise from [[xpo-725327]]).\n\n## What changed\n\n### Phase 1 — Shared inputs package\n\n- Created `internal/inputs/` and moved `AddInput` / `UpdateInput` / `CommentInput` / `LinkInput` / `DecodeStrict` / `ValidateStatus` / `LinksToDependencies` / `UpdatePayloadEmpty` out of `cmd/beats/json_input.go`.\n- Promoted `normalizeDependencyKind` (formerly local to `cmd/beats/link.go`) to `model.NormalizeDependencyKind` so both the CLI and MCP transports use a single normalizer.\n- Updated CLI `add`/`update`/`comment` and `link` commands to call into the shared types — zero behavioural change on the CLI side.\n\n### Phase 2 — Server scaffolding\n\n- New `internal/mcpserver/` package with `Run(ctx, cfg)` using the official `github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk` v1.6.1 over stdio.\n- Identity resolution in [internal/mcpserver/identity.go](internal/mcpserver/identity.go): `BEATS_AGENT_IDENTITY` env var → MCP `clientInfo` from the session → configured beats user. Recorded as `Client.UserOverride` so MCP writes don't mutate user config.\n- New `beats mcp` cobra subcommand in [cmd/beats/mcp.go](cmd/beats/mcp.go); `SilenceUsage: true` keeps clean stdin-close shutdowns from spewing help text.\n\n### Phase 3 — Tool surface\n\nSeven tools, all thin adapters over `Client` methods:\n\n| Tool | Wraps |\n|---|---|\n| `beats_list` | `Client.ListIssues` |\n| `beats_show` | `Client.GetIssue` (+ comments / optional events) |\n| `beats_history` | `Client.GetIssue` → event slice |\n| `beats_add` | `Client.AddIssue` via `inputs.AddInput.ToCreatePayload` |\n| `beats_update` | `Client.UpdateIssue` via `inputs.UpdateInput.ToUpdatePayload` |\n| `beats_comment` | `Client.AddComment` |\n| `beats_link` | `Client.UpdateIssue` with appended `Dependencies` |\n\nStatus shortcuts (`beats_start`/`beats_done`/…) intentionally dropped — agents transition via `beats_update` with `status: \"DOING\"` etc. Single, tight surface.\n\nEach tool has a typed input and output struct; JSONSchemas are generated by the SDK from `json:` and `jsonschema:` struct tags, so tool docs flow straight from the type definitions.\n\n### Phase 4 — Tests\n\n`internal/mcpserver/tools_test.go` (12 cases) exercises every handler directly with a real `Client` against a tempdir `.beats/issues.db` — covers add+show+update+comment+list+link+history, status transitions, validation errors, dependency auto-fill, and env-var vs config-default identity precedence.\n\n`internal/mcpserver/integration_test.go` wires a real MCP client to a real MCP server using `mcp.NewInMemoryTransports`, then calls `beats_add` followed by `beats_show` and asserts the markdown body round-trips byte-perfect. A second test verifies `tools/list` exposes all 7 expected tools.\n\n### Phase 5 — Docs\n\nAdded an \"MCP (Model Context Protocol) server\" section to `README.md` covering the `beats mcp` command, the tool catalogue, example `.mcp.json` for Claude Code (both basic and with `BEATS_AGENT_IDENTITY` env override), and the identity-resolution precedence.\n\n### Phase 6 — Verification\n\n- `go test ./...` clean, including the new in-memory end-to-end tests.\n- `go vet ./...` clean.\n- Stdio smoke test: piping a real MCP `initialize` + `tools/list` sequence into `beats mcp` returns a well-formed handshake response and the full tool catalogue with derived JSONSchemas. Exit code 0 on clean stdin close.\n\n## Architectural recap\n\nThe architectural promise from xpo-725327 holds: there is exactly one path for issue mutations — `Client.AddIssue` / `UpdateIssue` / `AddComment`. The CLI's flag path, the CLI's `--json` path, and now the MCP server's tool handlers all converge on those same functions. Adding a future transport (HTTP, gRPC, whatever) means writing a new adapter, not duplicating business logic.\n\n## Try it locally\n\n```bash\n# In any xpo-tracked project:\ncat \u003e .mcp.json \u003c\u003cJSON\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"beats\": {\n      \"command\": \"beats\",\n      \"args\": [\"mcp\"],\n      \"env\": { \"BEATS_AGENT_IDENTITY\": \"Claude Code \u003cagent@nicspc.local\u003e\" }\n    }\n  }\n}\nJSON\n# Restart Claude Code; agent now has structured beats tool calls.\n```"},"created_at":"2026-05-27T07:58:49.533040753Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-5b37e3","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-9d017ac4-4477-46fd-b677-ed5dada8f9ba","text":"Added a 'Setup for Claude Code' subsection to the README MCP block covering the three install paths: project-local `.mcp.json`, `claude mcp add` CLI, and manual user-level edit of `~/.claude/settings.json`."},"created_at":"2026-05-27T08:00:12.80604528Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
