{"id":"xpo-93b04d","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Dragging a sub-issue and dropping it on a different status causes the sub-issue to lose its parent link. We expect that link to stay intact.","labels":["bug"],"title":"Sub-Issue loses parent link"},"created_at":"2026-05-27T11:35:15.854412885Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-93b04d","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-05-27T11:35:16.096354032Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-93b04d","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-ce2833ae-ef40-43b9-b22b-ae3c9dec20ee","text":"## Investigation — Root cause\n\nThe frontend **explicitly clears** `parent_id` whenever a sub-issue is dropped on a different status column. This is intentional code, not an accidental omission.\n\n### The offending line\n\n[`web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx:556-564`](web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx#L556-L564) (inside `performDrop`):\n\n```typescript\nfor (const id of batchIds) {\n  const issue = issues.find((i) =\u003e i.id === id);\n  const update: Record\u003cstring, unknown\u003e = { status: groupTarget };\n  if (id === droppedId) {\n    update.sort_order = newKey;\n    if (issue?.parent_id) update.parent_id = \"\";  // ← bug: strips parent on cross-status drop\n  }\n  await addDraft(id, \"UPDATE\", update);\n}\n```\n\nWhen the dragged row has a `parent_id`, the cross-group handler sends `parent_id: \"\"` along with the new `status`. The backend faithfully applies that update and the sub-issue is unparented.\n\n### Why the backend accepts it\n\n`UpdatePayload.ParentID` is declared as `*string` with `omitempty` in [`internal/model/types.go:53-64`](internal/model/types.go#L53-L64). An incoming JSON `\"parent_id\": \"\"` deserializes to a **non-nil pointer to the empty string**, which `omitempty` does not strip on the way in (it only affects marshaling). The update layer treats a non-nil pointer as \"user wants to set this field,\" so the existing parent gets overwritten.\n\nSo the backend behavior is consistent with its contract — the issue is purely on the frontend, which should never send `parent_id` in this code path.\n\n### Suggested fix\n\nRemove [Backlog.tsx:561](web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx#L561). A status change should not touch parenthood. The sub-issue moving to a different status column is correct behavior and does not imply it should leave its epic.\n\nIf there was an original motivation for unparenting on status change (e.g. \"DONE sub-issues shouldn't roll up under their epic\"), that belongs in the rendering/grouping layer, not as a destructive mutation of `parent_id`.\n\n### Suggested test\n\nAdd a frontend unit test that simulates a cross-status drop of a sub-issue and asserts the `addDraft` call payload contains `{ status: \u003cnew\u003e }` but **does not** include `parent_id`. A complementary backend test could assert that `UpdatePayload` with a non-nil `parent_id: \"\"` is rejected (or treated as \"clear parent\") — whichever semantics we decide on — to lock down the contract."},"created_at":"2026-05-27T11:38:26.16042254Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-93b04d","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-a2b8cb6b-230b-497a-8176-6bbbdf20d21e","text":"## Update — refined diagnosis with two drag modes\n\nAfter re-reading the DnD code, there are actually **two intended modes** for cross-status drops, distinguished by a modifier key:\n\n### Mode A — plain drop on a status column\nCursor hovers a status group header (no modifier). The hover handler at [Backlog.tsx:488](web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx#L488) sets `dropGroupStatus` and clears the row indicator, and the drop falls into the `groupTarget` branch at [Backlog.tsx:539-567](web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx#L539-L567).\n\n**Intended behaviour:** change status, **preserve `parent_id`**. The sub-issue stays parented to its epic; it just moves to a different status column.\n\n**Actual behaviour:** [Backlog.tsx:561](web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx#L561) explicitly wipes `parent_id`. This is the bug.\n\n### Mode B — `CMD`-held drop (precise slot)\nWith `metaKey` held, the cross-group early-return is skipped ([Backlog.tsx:488](web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx#L488)) and the drop falls into the `indicatorTarget` branch at [Backlog.tsx:569-622](web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx#L569-L622), which uses the precise row under the cursor:\n\n- Dropping **between two children of an epic** → re-parents to that epic ([line 582](web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx#L582))\n- Dropping **between two top-level issues** → un-parents ([line 599](web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx#L599))\n\n**This branch is already correct** — re-parenting follows the drop target.\n\n### Fix\n\nSingle-line change in Mode A: remove [Backlog.tsx:561](web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx#L561).\n\n```diff\n       for (const id of batchIds) {\n         const issue = issues.find((i) =\u003e i.id === id);\n         const update: Record\u003cstring, unknown\u003e = { status: groupTarget };\n         if (id === droppedId) {\n           update.sort_order = newKey;\n-          if (issue?.parent_id) update.parent_id = \"\";\n         }\n         await addDraft(id, \"UPDATE\", update);\n       }\n```\n\nMode B is left as-is — its `parent_id = \"\"` at [line 599](web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx#L599) is correct because that path only runs when the user explicitly drops on a top-level slot.\n\n### Side observation (not in scope for this bug)\n\nThe \"precise slot\" modifier is `metaKey` only. On Linux/Windows that's the Super/Windows key, not Ctrl. Users on those platforms can't trigger Mode B currently. Worth filing as a separate small UX bug — should probably also accept `ctrlKey` (matching the pattern in [App.tsx:101](web/src/App.tsx#L101) which checks both).\n\n### Tests\n\n- Frontend: simulate a cross-group drop of a sub-issue with no modifier; assert the resulting `addDraft` payload is `{ status, sort_order }` only — `parent_id` is absent.\n- Frontend: simulate the same drop with `metaKey: true` on a target row between top-level issues; assert `parent_id: \"\"` IS present (Mode B un-parenting works).\n- Frontend: simulate `metaKey: true` drop between children of an epic; assert `parent_id` is set to that epic's id."},"created_at":"2026-05-27T11:48:09.373024219Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-895c22","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"relates_to","source_id":"xpo-895c22","target_id":"xpo-93b04d"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nThe \"precise slot\" cross-status drag-and-drop in the backlog only triggers when the user holds `metaKey` (Cmd on macOS, Super/Windows key on Linux/Windows). As a result, Linux and Windows users cannot reach this mode with their natural `Ctrl` chord.\n\n## Affected code\n\n- [web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx:488](web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx#L488)\n- [web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx:978](web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx#L978)\n\nBoth checks look like:\n\n```typescript\nif (isCrossGroup \u0026\u0026 !e.metaKey) {\n  // fall into group-target mode (column drop)\n}\n```\n\n`ctrlKey` is not consulted, so on Linux/Windows the user can never bypass the group-target branch via the standard `Ctrl` modifier.\n\n## Expected behaviour\n\nThe precise-slot mode should activate on `metaKey || ctrlKey`, matching the convention already used elsewhere in the app:\n\n- [web/src/App.tsx:101](web/src/App.tsx#L101) (`Cmd/Ctrl+K` palette)\n- [web/src/App.tsx:439](web/src/App.tsx#L439) (`Cmd/Ctrl+Enter` to create)\n- [web/src/components/MarkdownEditor.tsx:77](web/src/components/MarkdownEditor.tsx#L77)\n- [web/src/components/IssueDetail/IssueDetail.tsx:244](web/src/components/IssueDetail/IssueDetail.tsx#L244), [1602](web/src/components/IssueDetail/IssueDetail.tsx#L1602)\n\n## Proposed fix\n\nReplace `!e.metaKey` with `!(e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey)` at the two call sites above. No backend changes required.\n\n## How this was discovered\n\nFound while investigating [xpo-93b04d](#) — the cross-status DnD bug where sub-issues lost their parent link. The two issues share the same code path but are independent.","labels":["bug","WebApp","UX"],"title":"Precise-slot DnD modifier not available on Linux/Windows (metaKey only)"},"created_at":"2026-05-27T11:49:39.839010512Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
