{"id":"xpo-b75e16","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"The [README.md](http://README.md) is currently a collection of random thoughts more so than a proper documentation and instructions file. We need to rewrite the README to give a brief one-liner overview of what beats is and who it is for, followed by a Quickstart Guide, Installation instructions, Usage, Agentic Usage, etc.","labels":["improvement"],"title":"Improved documentation"},"created_at":"2026-05-27T11:52:10.60906939Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-b75e16","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"labels":["improvement","Documentation"],"status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-05-27T11:52:27.079351935Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-93b04d","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-12dadbd6-3cab-4509-beb4-985b71d6240f","text":"## Fix applied — walkthrough\n\n### Change\n\nRemoved [Backlog.tsx:561](web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx#L561) (the line that wiped `parent_id` on cross-status drops). Also dropped the now-unused `const issue = issues.find(...)` inside the same loop since the conditional was its only reader.\n\nFinal state of the cross-group branch in `performDrop`:\n\n```typescript\nfor (const id of batchIds) {\n  const update: Record\u003cstring, unknown\u003e = { status: groupTarget };\n  if (id === droppedId) {\n    update.sort_order = newKey;\n  }\n  await addDraft(id, \"UPDATE\", update);\n}\n```\n\nMode A (drop on status column, no modifier) now sends `{ status, sort_order }` only — parent link is preserved. Mode B (`metaKey` + precise slot) is untouched.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `make test` → all Go tests pass.\n- `bun run build` (`tsc -b \u0026\u0026 vite build`) → clean, type-checks.\n- `bunx eslint src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx` → 0 errors. The 4 warnings present are all pre-existing `react-hooks/exhaustive-deps` on lines I did not touch (445, 516, 657, 684).\n\n### Follow-up filed\n\n- [xpo-895c22](#) — \"Precise-slot DnD modifier not available on Linux/Windows (metaKey only)\". Linked via `relates_to`.\n\n### Not done in this PR\n\n- Automated test for the regression. The DnD path in `performDrop` is not currently covered by unit tests; adding one would need a test harness for the backlog's drag state machine. Recommend filing as a separate task if we want to lock down the contract.\n\nReady for review."},"created_at":"2026-05-27T11:54:48.019418439Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
