{"id":"xpo-895c22","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-1ef9b309-5c7f-47d6-90b3-17c5259a28c6","text":"## Fix applied — walkthrough\n\n### Change\n\nUpdated both cross-group DnD checks in [web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx](web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx) to accept `ctrlKey` in addition to `metaKey`:\n\n```diff\n- if (isCrossGroup \u0026\u0026 !e.metaKey) {\n+ if (isCrossGroup \u0026\u0026 !(e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey)) {\n```\n\nApplied at:\n\n- [Backlog.tsx:488](web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx#L488) — row hover handler (`handleRowDragOver`)\n- [Backlog.tsx:976](web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx#L976) — status-group header hover handler (`handleGroupDragOver`)\n\nA third occurrence at [Backlog.tsx:730](web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx#L730) (`if (e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey) return;`) was already checking both correctly and is untouched.\n\n### Rationale\n\nThe \"precise slot\" cross-status DnD mode previously only triggered on `metaKey` (Cmd on macOS, Super/Windows key elsewhere), leaving Linux and Windows users unable to reach the mode with their natural `Ctrl` chord. The codebase already uses `metaKey || ctrlKey` as the cross-platform pattern for keyboard shortcuts (e.g. [App.tsx:101](web/src/App.tsx#L101) for Cmd/Ctrl+K), so this aligns the DnD modifier with that convention.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `make test` → all Go tests pass.\n- `bun run build` → clean, type-checks and builds.\n- `bunx eslint src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx` → 0 errors. The 4 warnings are pre-existing `react-hooks/exhaustive-deps` on lines 445/516/657/684, none of which I touched.\n\n### Not done in this PR\n\n- Manual cross-platform verification (Mac with Cmd, Linux/Windows with Ctrl). The change is mechanically obvious but I cannot exercise the actual DnD UI from here. Worth a sanity test on at least one non-Mac platform before close.\n- No automated test — same constraint as [xpo-93b04d](#); the DnD path has no unit-test harness.\n\nReady for review."},"created_at":"2026-05-27T11:58:56.252933017Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
