{"id":"xpo-6178dc","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a2V"},"created_at":"2026-05-27T16:40:35.686445282Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-d918bd","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"blocks","source_id":"xpo-d918bd","target_id":"xpo-e1ee26"}],"description":"## Why\n\nThe Backlog drag-and-drop in [web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx](web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx) uses native HTML5 DnD. Switching to [@dnd-kit](https://dndkit.com/) buys three things and unblocks a fourth:\n\n1. **Accessibility** — keyboard navigation (space to pick up, arrows to move, space/enter to drop) and screen-reader announcements out of the box. Native HTML5 DnD has effectively zero keyboard story.\n2. **Touch/mobile** — works on touchscreens via pointer events. Native HTML5 DnD on mobile browsers is broken without polyfills.\n3. **Reduced complexity** — the `~600 LOC` of state machine in `Backlog.tsx` (drag indicator, group target, nest target, batch moves, manual `dragenter`/`dragleave` counters, drop position math) exists largely because native DnD is so quirky. With `@dnd-kit/core` + `@dnd-kit/sortable` most of that goes away; the library handles position math and collision detection.\n4. **Unblocks [xpo-e1ee26](#)** — Board view DnD. We want a single consistent pattern in the codebase. Doing Board on top of dnd-kit while Backlog is still native would lock in two patterns; migrating Backlog first gives the Board work a stable, modern foundation.\n\n## Scope\n\nReplace the native HTML5 DnD machinery in `Backlog.tsx` with `@dnd-kit/core` + `@dnd-kit/sortable`. Preserve **all** existing behaviors:\n\n- **Cross-status drops on a column** → status change, **parent link preserved** (regression-tested via [xpo-93b04d](#) — explicitly do not strip `parent_id`).\n- **Within-column reorder** → uses the existing fractional-key `generateKeyBetween` sort_order mechanism.\n- **`Alt`-drag onto another issue** → nest as sub-issue ([xpo-f28d0f](#)).\n- **`Cmd`/`Ctrl`-drag** → precise-slot mode that bypasses the column-level target and uses the row indicator position ([xpo-895c22](#)).\n- **Batch moves** — same-status children of a dragged issue move with it.\n- **Optimistic updates** via the existing `addDraft` flow.\n\nAdd on top:\n\n- **Keyboard DnD** — `Tab` to focus, `Space` to pick up, arrows to navigate, `Space` to drop, `Esc` to cancel.\n- **Custom drag overlay** — render the dragged card with our styles instead of the browser ghost.\n- **Screen-reader announcements** via `DragOverlay` + `Announcement` props.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Board view DnD ([xpo-e1ee26](#) — done next, on top of this).\n- Performance optimization beyond what dnd-kit gives for free.\n- Touch UX polish (basic touch should work; refinements can be filed separately).\n\n## Risks\n\n- **High** — this is a rewrite of working production code that has had multiple bug-fixes. The semantic regressions to avoid are concrete: parent stripping ([xpo-93b04d](#)) and Linux/Windows modifier handling ([xpo-895c22](#)).\n- **Mitigation** — write a manual test plan covering every interaction matrix (with/without `Alt`, with/without `Cmd`/`Ctrl`, same-status vs cross-status, top-level vs child rows) and walk through it before merge.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] All existing Backlog DnD interactions work identically to current behavior across the matrix above.\n- [ ] Keyboard DnD works end-to-end without a mouse.\n- [ ] Drag overlay uses project styling (no browser-painted ghost).\n- [ ] `Backlog.tsx` state-machine LOC measurably reduced (target: cut the DnD-specific code in half).\n- [ ] `@dnd-kit/core` and `@dnd-kit/sortable` added to `web/package.json`; native `draggable`, `onDragStart`, `onDragOver`, `onDrop`, `onDragEnd` attributes removed from Backlog code paths.\n- [ ] `bun run build` and `bun run lint` clean; existing test suite green.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n```bash\nbun add @dnd-kit/core @dnd-kit/sortable @dnd-kit/utilities\n```\n\nCombined gzipped weight is ~30-50 KB — acceptable for an in-app tracker.\n\n## Suggested approach\n\n1. Add the deps, scaffold a parallel `\u003cBacklogV2\u003e` behind a feature flag or sibling export.\n2. Port one interaction at a time: within-column sort → cross-status drop → `Alt`-nest → `Cmd`/`Ctrl` precise-slot → batch-move.\n3. Once parity is reached, swap the export and delete the native-DnD code in one commit.\n4. Add keyboard + screen-reader announcements as a follow-on commit.","labels":["feature","WebApp","refactor"],"status":"PLANNED","title":"Migrate Backlog drag-and-drop from native HTML5 to @dnd-kit"},"created_at":"2026-05-27T12:50:56.2889912Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
