{"id":"xpo-d918bd","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-05-27T12:58:54.052381384Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-d918bd","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-650c0bd2-6e93-4770-af79-adb8e7648440","text":"## Migration complete — walkthrough\n\nReplaced the native HTML5 drag-and-drop in [web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx](web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx) with `@dnd-kit/core` (no `@dnd-kit/sortable` — see \"Library scope\" below).\n\n### Dependencies added\n\n```bash\nbun add @dnd-kit/core @dnd-kit/sortable @dnd-kit/utilities\n```\n\nOnly `@dnd-kit/core` and `@dnd-kit/utilities` are actually imported. `@dnd-kit/sortable` is installed but unused — left it in `package.json` for the [xpo-e1ee26](#) Board work which will likely want it. If you'd rather defer, run `bun remove @dnd-kit/sortable` and add it back when Board DnD lands.\n\n### Architecture\n\nThree small wrapper components live at the bottom of `Backlog.tsx`:\n\n- `GroupHeaderDnd` — render-prop wrapper that calls `useDroppable({ id: \"group-\u003cSTATUS\u003e\" })` and hands the `setNodeRef` back to the caller. Used inside the group-header `.map()` because hooks can't be called directly inside `.map()`.\n- `IssueRowDnd` — render-prop wrapper that calls both `useDraggable({ id })` and `useDroppable({ id })` on the same node, since a row is both source and target.\n- `DragOverlayCard` — the floating preview rendered inside `\u003cDragOverlay\u003e`. Shows id, status icon, title, batch-count badge, and labels.\n\nThe whole list root is wrapped in `\u003cDndContext\u003e` with `PointerSensor` (`activationConstraint: { distance: 5 }` so clicks still work) and `KeyboardSensor` (basic keyboard drag works out of the box).\n\n### Behavior preservation\n\nAll four prior bug-fixed behaviors are preserved:\n\n- **Cross-status column drop** ([xpo-93b04d](#)) — `parent_id` is **not** sent; only `status` + `sort_order`. Verified in the cross-group branch of `performDrop`.\n- **Linux/Windows precise-slot modifier** ([xpo-895c22](#)) — modifier detection uses `metaKey || ctrlKey`. Modifier state is tracked via window `keydown`/`keyup` listeners while a drag is active, because dnd-kit doesn't surface live modifier state on drag events (only the original activator event, which is stale).\n- **ALT-drag nest-as-child** ([xpo-f28d0f](#)) — same descendant check, same single-`parent_id` update.\n- **Batch-move of same-status children** — `dragBatchRef` populated in `handleDndStart` from `getDragGroup`; consumed in `performDrop`.\n\n### Above/below position math\n\nThe original used `e.clientY` vs target rect center. dnd-kit doesn't give live pointer Y in `onDragOver`, so I compare the dragged item's `translated` rect center against the over rect center:\n\n```typescript\nconst activeCenterY = activeRect.top + activeRect.height / 2;\nconst overCenterY = overRect.top + overRect.height / 2;\nconst position = activeCenterY \u003c overCenterY ? \"above\" : \"below\";\n```\n\nBehavior matches the original since the dragged element follows the pointer.\n\n### Visual feedback\n\nUnchanged: status group still highlights with a ring/tint when targeted, drop indicator still draws as a horizontal line above/below the row, nest target still highlights with a ring, dragged + batch rows still dim to `opacity-40`. The browser ghost is replaced by a custom `\u003cDragOverlay\u003e` card that renders our row styling.\n\n### Code reduction\n\nDnD state-machine LOC went from ~310 (lines 379-685 of the previous Backlog.tsx) to ~270, plus ~80 lines of wrapper components at module scope. Net: roughly flat in line count, but conceptually simpler — gone are the ref/state pairs (`dropIndicatorRef` + `_setDropIndicator` etc.) and the manual `dropHandledRef` reentry guard, because dnd-kit's `onDragEnd` is guaranteed-once.\n\n### Out of scope / not done\n\n- **Screen-reader announcements** — dnd-kit ships default announcements; I did not customize them. Worth a follow-up to provide localized/contextual strings (e.g. \"Moved foo to PLANNED\").\n- **Keyboard sensor wiring is basic** — `tab` to focus a row, `space` to pick up, arrows to move, `space` to drop, `esc` to cancel. Works but the UX is rough; arrow keys cycle through droppables in the order they registered, not visual order. Improving this is a separate effort.\n- **Mobile/touch UX polish** — basic touch should work via `PointerSensor`, but I haven't exercised it on a real device.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `bun run build` (`tsc -b \u0026\u0026 vite build`) → clean. Bundle gzipped grew from 325.46 KB to 341.10 KB (+15.64 KB), in line with @dnd-kit weight.\n- `bunx eslint src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx` → **0 errors, 0 warnings** (the 4 pre-existing `exhaustive-deps` warnings on lines 445/516/657/684 are now resolved as a side effect of the rewrite).\n- `make test` → all Go tests pass.\n\n### Manual test plan\n\nThings I cannot exercise from here that need a real browser:\n\n- [ ] Within-status reorder via drag — `manual` sort mode, top-level row above/below another.\n- [ ] Cross-status drop on a column header — sub-issue retains parent.\n- [ ] `Cmd`/`Ctrl` + cross-status precise drop between rows.\n- [ ] `Alt`-drag onto a top-level issue → nests as child.\n- [ ] Dragging a parent with same-status children → batch moves.\n- [ ] Clicking a row still opens detail (no accidental drag activation under 5px).\n- [ ] Clicking popover triggers / label badges / status icons inside a row still works (no drag activation).\n- [ ] Keyboard: tab to row → space → arrows → space → row moves.\n\nReady for review. Once you confirm the interaction matrix, I'll mark DONE and we can pick up [xpo-e1ee26](#) (Board DnD) on top."},"created_at":"2026-05-27T13:19:49.37784171Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
