{"id":"xpo-4bb55e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Problem\n\nDrag-and-drop sorting in the Backlog (and Board) is intermittently broken — issues sometimes don't land where expected.\n\n**Root cause:** New issues are created without a `sort_order`. The frontend patches over this with \"virtual keys\" generated on-the-fly from creation order (`getEffectiveKeys` in `sort.ts`). These virtual keys collide with real sort keys generated by `generateKeyBetween` during DnD, causing unstable ordering.\n\n**Key collision example:** Dragging an issue to the end produces `generateKeyBetween(\"a1\", null) = \"a2\"`, which is the same virtual key that `generateNKeysBetween` assigns to the 3rd item in any set of 3+ issues.\n\n## Fix\n\n1. **Assign `sort_order` at creation time** — compute a key that appends the issue at the bottom of its status group\n2. **Backfill existing issues** — migrate issues with empty `sort_order` so all issues have a real key\n3. **Remove virtual key fallback** — eliminate `getEffectiveKeys` and use `sort_order` directly, with a simple fallback for any edge case","labels":["bug"],"priority":1,"status":"PLANNED","title":"Fix sort_order: assign on creation, backfill existing, remove virtual key fallback"},"created_at":"2026-05-29T05:07:27.889500039Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-4bb55e","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-05-29T05:07:31.222982409Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-4bb55e","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-343efd2d-c253-4949-bea4-6e42eb2f110e","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed the intermittent DnD sorting bug caused by virtual sort key collisions.\n\n### Root cause\n\nNew issues were created without a `sort_order`. The frontend patched this with \"virtual keys\" generated on-the-fly from creation order (`getEffectiveKeys` in `sort.ts`). These virtual keys collided with real sort keys produced by `generateKeyBetween` during DnD — for example, dragging an issue to the end generated `\"a2\"`, which is the same virtual key assigned to the 3rd issue in any set of 3+ items. This caused unstable ordering.\n\n### Changes\n\n**Go: New `internal/sortorder` package**\n- Ported the fractional-indexing algorithm (compatible with the npm `fractional-indexing` v3 package)\n- `GenerateKeyBetween(a, b)` and `GenerateNKeysBetween(a, b, n)` with full test coverage\n\n**Go: Backfill in `internal/beats/projection.go`**\n- `backfillSortOrder()` runs after projection, assigning sort keys to all issues that lack one\n- Groups by status, finds the max existing key, generates sequential keys after it for unkeyed issues in creation-time order\n\n**Frontend: Sort key assignment at creation**\n- `computeAppendKey()` in `sort.ts` computes a sort_order that appends after all existing issues in a group\n- All creation sites (`Backlog` inline create, `NewIssueModal`, `SubIssuesTable`) now pass `sort_order` in the CREATE payload\n\n**Frontend: Removed virtual key fallback**\n- Deleted `getEffectiveKeys()` from `sort.ts`\n- All sorting and DnD handlers now use `issue.sort_order` directly — no more ephemeral virtual keys\n- Updated `Backlog.tsx` `performDrop`, `Board.tsx` `handleDragEnd`, `sortGroup`, and `sortIssuesWithinGroups`\n\n### Files changed\n\n- `internal/sortorder/sortorder.go` — new: fractional-indexing port\n- `internal/sortorder/sortorder_test.go` — new: tests\n- `internal/beats/projection.go` — backfill logic\n- `web/src/utils/sort.ts` — removed `getEffectiveKeys`, added `computeAppendKey`\n- `web/src/api/client.ts` — `sort_order` param on `createIssue`\n- `web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx` — creation + DnD updates\n- `web/src/components/Board/Board.tsx` — DnD updates\n- `web/src/components/NewIssueModal/NewIssueModal.tsx` — creation with sort_order\n- `web/src/components/IssueDetail/SubIssuesTable.tsx` — creation with sort_order"},"created_at":"2026-05-29T05:42:45.906326648Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
