{"id":"xpo-901ece","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"},"created_at":"2026-05-29T09:46:59.670039247Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-901ece","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-89e7f65d-8d0d-48a6-8cf0-58163fe0c256","text":"## Summary\n\nMade default labels configurable by establishing `.beats/config.yaml` as the single source of truth for label names and colors, with built-in defaults as a server-side fallback.\n\n### Backend changes\n\n- **`internal/config/config.go`**: Added `BuiltinLabels` and `BuiltinLabelOrder` exported variables — centralizes the 4 default labels (`bug`, `feature`, `epic`, `improvement`) with their colors in one place.\n- **`internal/beats/setup.go`**: `InitBeats()` now generates the labels section of `config.yaml` from `config.BuiltinLabels` instead of inline strings.\n- **`internal/server/handlers.go`**: The `/api/config` endpoint now returns a `default_labels` field containing the built-in label set, so the frontend doesn't need its own hard-coded copy.\n- **`internal/ui/styles.go`**: `LabelColor()` now checks a config-provided color map first (set via `SetLabelColors()`), falling back to a deterministic hash-based color from a palette. The old substring-matching heuristic (e.g., any label containing \"bug\" → red) is removed.\n- **`cmd/beats/main.go`**: Calls `ui.SetLabelColors(cfg.Labels)` after loading config so CLI output uses project-configured label colors.\n\n### Frontend changes\n\n- **`web/src/api/client.ts`**: `fetchConfig` return type updated to include `default_labels: Record\u003cstring, string\u003e`.\n- **`web/src/components/ui/Badge.tsx`**: Added `DefaultLabelsContext` to provide server-supplied default labels.\n- **`web/src/components/ui/index.ts`**: Barrel-exports `DefaultLabelsContext`.\n- **`web/src/App.tsx`**: Fetches `default_labels` from the server, stores in state, provides via `DefaultLabelsContext.Provider`. The `effectiveLabelColors` memo now uses server-provided defaults instead of the hard-coded constant.\n- **`web/src/components/ui/LabelPicker.tsx`**: Reads `DefaultLabelsContext` instead of importing `DEFAULT_LABELS` from constants.\n- **`web/src/constants.ts`**: Removed the `DEFAULT_LABELS` export entirely.\n\n### Tests\n\n- **`internal/ui/styles_test.go`**: Rewrote tests to cover: config-driven colors, case-insensitive fallback, hash-based fallback for unknown labels, and config precedence over defaults.\n\n### Rationale\n\nThe previous design had default labels defined in three independent places (Go `setup.go`, frontend `constants.ts`, CLI `styles.go`). This made customization impossible without code changes and risked the three copies drifting out of sync. Now the server is authoritative: `BuiltinLabels` is defined once in Go, served via API, and the frontend consumes it dynamically. Users can override any default by editing the `labels:` section in `.beats/config.yaml` — config always takes precedence."},"created_at":"2026-05-29T09:52:08.192482288Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-901ece","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-8f69d858-b5e6-48f4-acf5-e661b40b0179","text":"## Summary\n\nMade default labels configurable via a new `default_labels` list in `.beats/config.yaml`, separate from the `labels` color map.\n\n### Config structure\n\n```yaml\ndefault_labels:        # names — which labels are \"primary\" (shown at top of pickers)\n  - bug\n  - feature\n  - epic\n  - improvement\nlabels:                # color map for all labels (default or not)\n  bug: \"#eb5757\"\n  feature: \"#b36cd9\"\n  epic: \"#5e6ad2\"\n  improvement: \"#4da6e8\"\n```\n\nUsers control which labels are primary by editing `default_labels`. Any label can have a color in `labels` without being a default. Existing projects without `default_labels` fall back to the built-in set.\n\n### Backend\n\n- **`internal/config/config.go`**: Added `BuiltinLabels`, `BuiltinLabelOrder` as centralized defaults. Added `DefaultLabels []string` to `Config` struct with fallback to `BuiltinLabelOrder` in `LoadConfig()`.\n- **`internal/beats/setup.go`**: `InitBeats()` writes both `default_labels:` list and `labels:` color map from the centralized built-ins.\n- **`internal/server/handlers.go`**: `/api/config` returns `default_labels` from config (the name list), not the hard-coded built-in map.\n- **`internal/ui/styles.go`**: `LabelColor()` uses config colors via `SetLabelColors()`, falling back to deterministic hash-based palette colors. Old substring-matching heuristic removed.\n- **`cmd/beats/main.go`**: Calls `ui.SetLabelColors(cfg.Labels)` after loading config.\n\n### Frontend\n\n- **`web/src/api/client.ts`**: `fetchConfig` return type updated — `default_labels` is `string[]`.\n- **`web/src/components/ui/Badge.tsx`**: Added `DefaultLabelsContext` for server-supplied default label names.\n- **`web/src/App.tsx`**: Fetches `default_labels` from server, builds `{name, color}[]` by joining names with the `labels` color map, provides via `DefaultLabelsContext.Provider`.\n- **`web/src/components/ui/LabelPicker.tsx`**: Reads `DefaultLabelsContext` instead of hard-coded constant.\n- **`web/src/constants.ts`**: Removed `DEFAULT_LABELS`.\n\n### Tests\n\n- **`internal/ui/styles_test.go`**: Covers config-driven colors, case-insensitive fallback, hash-based fallback, and config precedence."},"created_at":"2026-05-29T11:57:06.389689001Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
