{"id":"xpo-0135c0","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"priority":1},"created_at":"2026-05-29T14:32:12.404707338Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-74111b","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-70b0989a-152a-438b-9bcc-14ff40c41408","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented a right-click context menu on issue rows in the backlog view with flyout sub-menus, keyboard shortcuts, and filter inputs.\n\n### New component: `web/src/components/ui/ContextMenu.tsx`\n\n- **Main menu** with icon, label, keyboard shortcut hint, and chevron for each action: Status (S), Priority (P), Assignee (A), Labels (L), Estimate (E), Delete (Ctrl+Backspace)\n- **Flyout sub-menus** pop out to the right on hover, aligned with the hovered item\n- **Filter inputs** as sub-menu headers — typing filters the option list (status, priority, estimate, assignee). Labels reuses the existing `LabelPicker` with its built-in search.\n- **Delete** action shows inline confirmation before acting\n- **Keyboard shortcuts** work when the menu is open; uses `stopImmediatePropagation()` in capture phase to prevent Backlog's global shortcuts from firing\n- **Escape** closes sub-menu first, then the full menu on second press\n- **Click-outside** closes the menu (armed via `requestAnimationFrame` to avoid race with the triggering right-click)\n\n### Backlog changes: `web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx`\n\n- Added `contextMenu` state tracking issue + cursor coordinates\n- Native DOM `contextmenu` event listener on the list container, delegating via `data-context-issue` attributes (avoids interference from dnd-kit's pointer sensor listeners)\n- Context menu's target issue row stays highlighted while the menu is open (`isContextTarget` feeds into `isRowFocused`)\n\n### Design decisions\n\n- **Native event listener** instead of React's `onContextMenu` — dnd-kit's `PointerSensor` listeners (spread via `useDraggable`) interfered with React synthetic contextmenu events. Delegating from the list container via data attributes works reliably.\n- **Flyout sub-menus** rather than replacing the main menu — matches a standard UX pattern, allows hovering directly from main item to sub-menu option.\n- **`items-start` flex layout** — main menu and flyout size independently; the flyout doesn't stretch the main menu height.\n- **Due date and Cycle** omitted — no underlying data model support yet. Can be added when those features land."},"created_at":"2026-05-29T15:17:50.537309354Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-74111b","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-05-29T15:17:50.673148762Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-b1b852","type":"CREATE","payload":{"assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","description":"## Problem\n\nThe web UI contains **300+ instances** of non-standard Tailwind spacing/sizing classes that fall off the 4px grid. Fractional values like `gap-2.5` (10px), `px-1.5` (6px), and `w-3.5` (14px) break the visual rhythm and make alignments inconsistent by a few pixels.\n\n## Plan\n\nRemediate in 3 phases:\n\n- [ ] **Phase 1** — Icon sizes: `w-3.5 h-3.5` → `w-4 h-4`, `w-2.5 h-2.5` → `w-3 h-3`, `w-1.5 h-1.5` → `w-2 h-2` (~80 instances)\n- [ ] **Phase 2** — Gaps, padding, and margins: `gap-1.5` → `gap-1`/`gap-2`, `px-2.5` → `px-2`/`px-3`, etc. (per-instance judgment)\n- [ ] **Phase 3** — Arbitrary bracket values: fix off-grid `h-[38px]`, `w-[110px]`, etc. and replace on-grid arbitraries with standard classes","labels":["epic","feature"],"status":"PLANNED","title":"Standardize Tailwind spacing to 4px grid"},"created_at":"2026-05-30T07:14:22.822856962Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-53f2bb","type":"CREATE","payload":{"assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","description":"## Scope\n\nMechanical replacement of fractional icon size classes across all components:\n\n- `w-3.5 h-3.5` (14px) → `w-4 h-4` (16px)\n- `w-2.5 h-2.5` (10px) → `w-3 h-3` (12px)\n- `w-1.5 h-1.5` (6px) → `w-2 h-2` (8px)\n\n## Affected files\n\nPropertySidebar.tsx, Labels.tsx, Backlog.tsx, BoardCard.tsx, NewIssueModal.tsx, ContextMenu.tsx, ActivityTimeline.tsx, Layout.tsx, LabelPicker.tsx, Button.tsx, InlineDropdown.tsx, SubIssuesTable.tsx, icons.tsx, DndComponents.tsx, Dashboard/ActivityFeed.tsx, Dashboard/DistributionSection.tsx, Dashboard/Section.tsx, PendingEventsPanel.tsx, PendingChanges.tsx, Progress.tsx","estimate":2,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"xpo-b1b852","status":"PLANNED","title":"Phase 1: Normalize icon sizes to 4px grid"},"created_at":"2026-05-30T07:14:34.393928115Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
