{"id":"xpo-0135c0","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"priority":0},"created_at":"2026-05-30T07:27:26.59350875Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-53f2bb","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-7f9b43f7-3b28-42a4-9680-6343b964555e","text":"## Summary\n\nReplaced all fractional icon/indicator size classes across **19 source files** to align with the 4px grid:\n\n| Before | px | After | px |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `w-3.5 h-3.5` | 14px | `w-4 h-4` | 16px |\n| `w-2.5 h-2.5` | 10px | `w-3 h-3` | 12px |\n| `w-1.5 h-1.5` | 6px | `w-2 h-2` | 8px |\n\n**Files changed:** `Backlog.tsx`, `BoardCard.tsx`, `ActivityFeed.tsx`, `DistributionSection.tsx`, `Section.tsx`, `ActivityTimeline.tsx`, `PropertySidebar.tsx`, `SubIssuesTable.tsx`, `icons.tsx`, `Labels.tsx`, `Layout.tsx`, `NewIssueModal.tsx`, `PendingEventsPanel.tsx`, `Badge.tsx`, `Button.tsx`, `ContextMenu.tsx`, `InlineDropdown.tsx`, `LabelPicker.tsx`, `Progress.tsx`\n\n**Verification:** TypeScript compilation and Vite production build pass cleanly. SVG path data (which contains `h-1.5` as an SVG command) was correctly left untouched by word-boundary matching.\n\n**Note for Phase 2:** `Progress.tsx` still has `h-0.5` (2px) for the `sm` size variant — left for Phase 2 since it's a padding/sizing concern, not an icon size."},"created_at":"2026-05-30T07:28:04.872651661Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-ca68a0","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Phase 2: Normalize gaps, padding, margins to 4px grid","description":"## Scope\n\nReplace all fractional gap, padding, margin, and space classes with the nearest 4px-grid-aligned value:\n\n- `*-0.5` (2px) → `*-1` (4px)\n- `*-1.5` (6px) → `*-2` (8px)\n- `*-2.5` (10px) → `*-3` (12px)\n- `*-3.5` (14px) → `*-4` (16px)\n\nApplies to: `gap-`, `px-`, `py-`, `p-`, `m-`, `mb-`, `space-y-`, `space-x-`","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"xpo-b1b852","estimate":3,"assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-30T07:30:14.259009123Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-ca68a0","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-05-30T07:30:16.595013605Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-ca68a0","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-9615da73-d0f1-4657-a546-9dbda36c9943","text":"## Summary\n\nReplaced all fractional gap, padding, margin, and space classes across **28 source files** (~140 instances) to align with the 4px grid:\n\n| Pattern | Before (px) | After (px) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `*-0.5` | 2px | `*-1` (4px) |\n| `*-1.5` | 6px | `*-2` (8px) |\n| `*-2.5` | 10px | `*-3` (12px) |\n| `*-3.5` | 14px | `*-4` (16px) |\n\nApplied to: `gap-`, `px-`, `py-`, `p-`, `mb-`, `mt-`, `space-y-`, `space-x-`, `h-` (progress bar), `-m-` (avatar overlap)\n\n**Verification:** TypeScript compilation and Vite production build pass. CSS bundle size dropped from 40.15 KB → 38.99 KB due to fewer unique utility classes.\n\n**Notable changes:**\n- Badge `sm` size: `px-1.5 py-0.5` → `px-2 py-1` — slightly taller badges\n- Avatar stacking overlap: `-m-0.5` → `-m-1` — slightly tighter overlap\n- Progress bar `sm`: `h-0.5` → `h-1` — 2px → 4px thin bar\n- Dropdown list items: `py-1.5` → `py-2` everywhere — consistent row height"},"created_at":"2026-05-30T07:38:37.123181944Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-037391","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Phase 3: Normalize arbitrary bracket values to 4px grid","description":"## Scope\n\nFix arbitrary bracket pixel values that are off the 4px grid, and replace on-grid arbitrary values with standard Tailwind classes where available.\n\nCategories:\n- Off-grid values (e.g. `h-[38px]`, `w-[110px]`, `border-[1.5px]`) → snap to 4px grid\n- On-grid values with standard equivalents (e.g. `h-[40px]` → `h-10`, `max-h-[240px]` → `max-h-60`) → use standard classes\n- CSS variable references (`bg-[var(--color-*)]`) → leave as-is (design tokens)","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"xpo-b1b852","estimate":2,"assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-30T08:00:01.457616357Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-037391","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-05-30T08:00:05.253446838Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-037391","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-0e68d440-f873-4a89-8e49-ac6a3b8fed97","text":"## Summary\n\nReplaced all arbitrary bracket pixel values across **17 source files**:\n\n### Off-grid → snapped to 4px grid\n| Before | After |\n|---|---|\n| `h-[38px]` (38px) | `h-10` (40px) |\n| `w-[110px]` (110px) | `w-28` (112px) |\n| `w-[18px] h-[18px]` (18px) | `w-5 h-5` (20px) |\n| `w-[245px]` (245px) | `w-62` (248px) |\n| `max-w-[150px]` (150px) | `max-w-38` (152px) |\n| `border-[1.5px]` | `border-2` (2px) |\n| `border-b-[1.5px]` | `border-b-2` (2px) |\n| `rounded-[3px]` | `rounded` (4px) |\n\n### On-grid arbitrary → standard Tailwind v4 classes\n`min-h-[112px]` → `min-h-28`, `min-h-[160px]` → `min-h-40`, `min-h-[40px]` → `min-h-10`, `h-[52px]` → `h-13`, `max-h-[240px]` → `max-h-60`, `max-h-[400px]` → `max-h-100`, `max-w-[320px]` → `max-w-80`, `max-w-[400px]` → `max-w-100`, `max-w-[560px]` → `max-w-140`, `max-w-[200px]` → `max-w-50`, `max-w-[160px]` → `max-w-40`, `max-w-[280px]` → `max-w-70`, `min-w-[140px]` → `min-w-35`, `min-w-[200px]` → `min-w-50`, `min-w-[220px]` → `min-w-55`, `min-w-[160px]` → `min-w-40`\n\n### Intentionally kept\n- `text-[10px]` — font size, not layout spacing (Tailwind's own text scale isn't 4px-aligned)\n- `h-[2px]` — drag-drop indicator line (visual affordance, not layout spacing)"},"created_at":"2026-05-30T08:05:04.323259839Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-b1b852","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-05-30T08:08:42.476866199Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-f014bb","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Continuous tree connector lines for child issues in backlog","description":"## Problem\n\nChild issues in the backlog show disconnected L-shaped SVG connectors that:\n1. Don't align with the parent's expand/collapse arrow\n2. Are not continuous between siblings (each child has its own isolated L)\n3. Don't visually group children under their parent\n\n## Solution\n\n- Add `treeGuides` metadata to each row in `useBacklogRows.ts` — an array of guide types (`pipe` │, `tee` ├, `corner` └, `blank`) computed during tree traversal\n- Render absolutely-positioned SVG tree lines in each row's padding area, aligned with the parent's arrow column\n- Remove the old standalone L-shape connector\n- Support multi-level nesting with vertical continuation lines at each ancestor level","status":"DOING","estimate":3,"assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-30T08:28:09.713109634Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-f014bb","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-3730fe2e-5a72-4b57-b668-677811e47333","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented continuous tree connector lines for child issues in the backlog view.\n\n### Data layer (`useBacklogRows.ts`)\n- Added `TreeGuide` type: `'pipe' | 'tee' | 'corner' | 'blank'`\n- Added `treeGuides: TreeGuide[]` field to issue row items\n- Computed during tree traversal in both `addTree` functions (all-tab and filtered-tab branches)\n- Each child receives inherited ancestor guides (tee/pipe → pipe, corner/blank → blank) plus its own guide (corner for last sibling, tee otherwise)\n\n### Rendering (`Backlog.tsx`)\n- Added `relative` to the row div for absolute positioning of tree guide SVGs\n- Each tree guide renders as an absolutely positioned SVG in the row's left padding area, aligned at `left: 20 + k*24` (matching the parent's expand arrow column center at x=8 within the SVG)\n- Guide shapes:\n  - **pipe** (│): full-height vertical line — ancestor still has siblings below\n  - **tee** (├): full-height vertical + horizontal branch — not last sibling\n  - **corner** (└): half-height vertical + horizontal branch — last sibling\n  - **blank**: no line — ancestor was last child\n- Removed the old disconnected L-shape SVG connector (`depth \u003e 0 ? ...` branch)\n- Simplified first-column to just: expand arrow (if hasChildren) or drag handle (otherwise)\n\n### Alignment\nThe tree guide vertical line at SVG x=8, positioned at absolute `20 + k*24 + 8 = 28 + k*24`, aligns exactly with the expand arrow center at depth k (paddingLeft `20 + k*24` + arrow center offset 8)."},"created_at":"2026-05-30T08:30:27.075838317Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-5b051b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Priority icon as first column, aligned with section StatusIcon","description":"## Requirements\n\n1. Replace drag handle with priority icon for non-parent issue rows\n2. Keep expand/collapse arrow for parent issues\n3. Add priority icon as a second element (after expand arrow) for parent rows\n4. Align priority icon column with the section header's StatusIcon column\n5. Show `--` when no priority is set\n\n## Layout\n\n**Section header:** `[▶ chevron] [gap] [◐ StatusIcon] ...`\n**Parent row:** `[▶ expand] [gap] [Priority icon] [gap] [ID] ...`\n**Non-parent row:** `[spacer] [gap] [Priority icon] [gap] [ID] ...`\n\nColumn B (priority/StatusIcon) aligns vertically across section headers and issue rows.","status":"DOING","estimate":2,"assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-05-30T09:01:42.863251266Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-5b051b","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-11a0f4f5-3c77-49c8-8139-4ac02436ed18","text":"## Summary\n\n### New component: `PriorityIcon` ([PriorityIcon.tsx](web/src/components/ui/PriorityIcon.tsx))\n- SVG bar-chart style icon: ascending bars for priority levels, `--` dashes for no priority\n- P1 Urgent (4 bars, red), P2 High (3 bars, orange), P3 Medium (2 bars, secondary), P4 Low (1 bar, muted), P0 None (double dash, muted)\n- Props: `priority`, `size`, `className` — same API pattern as `StatusIcon`\n\n### Backlog layout changes ([Backlog.tsx](web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx))\n\n**Section header:** changed `gap-2` → `gap-3`, wrapped chevron SVG in `w-4` container so column A width matches issue rows.\n\n**Issue rows:** new column order:\n1. **Column A** (chevron-aligned): expand arrow for parents, invisible `w-4` spacer for non-parents\n2. **Column B** (StatusIcon-aligned): `PriorityIcon` showing issue priority\n3. CopyableId → StatusIcon → title → ...\n\n**Removed:** old priority text display (`!!!`/`!!`/`!`) from the right side of the row — now redundant.\n\n**Inline-create row:** updated to match new column structure with spacer, PriorityIcon (none), empty ID spacer, and StatusIcon.\n\n### Column alignment\nSection header: `[20px pad] [w-4 chevron container] [12px gap] [StatusIcon]` → StatusIcon at 48px\nIssue row: `[20px pad] [16px expand/spacer] [12px gap] [PriorityIcon]` → PriorityIcon at 48px ✓"},"created_at":"2026-05-30T09:05:36.28332301Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.152 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
