{"id":"xpo-a5da9b","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-63c7d66f-560f-4d02-8dd5-73aa9db0087e","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded two GitHub Actions workflow files:\n\n- **`.github/workflows/test.yml`** — runs `go test ./...` and `go vet ./...` on every push/PR to `main`.\n- **`.github/workflows/build.yml`** — three-phase pipeline:\n  1. **frontend** — installs Bun, builds the Vite app, uploads `internal/server/static/` as an artifact. Runs on all pushes/PRs as a smoke test.\n  2. **binaries** — 6-target cross-compilation matrix (linux/darwin/windows × amd64/arm64). Only runs on `v*` tag pushes.\n  3. **release** — downloads all binaries and creates a GitHub Release with auto-generated notes. Only runs on `v*` tag pushes.\n\nAll actions are pinned to Node 24-native versions (`actions/checkout@v5`, `actions/setup-go@v6`, `actions/upload-artifact@v6`, `actions/download-artifact@v7`, `oven-sh/setup-bun@v2`, `softprops/action-gh-release@v3`).\n\n## Rationale\n\nCross-compilation is gated to tag pushes to avoid wasting CI minutes on every commit. The frontend build still runs on all pushes/PRs to catch build regressions early."},"created_at":"2026-06-01T05:33:21.109071149Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-a5da9b","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T05:33:23.885414816Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-c7b7c6","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## Overview\\n\\nAdd support for **Cycles** — fixed-cadence, time-boxed iterations (inspired by other trackers). Cycles provide a planning lens over existing issues without heavy ceremony.\\n\\n## Design Principles\\n\\n- **Convention over enforcement** — cycles are a planning tool, not a gate\\n- **Computed rollover** — no background daemon or manual rollover command needed\\n- **Minimal writes** — an issue stores the cycle it was *assigned to*; rollover is derived at read time\\n\\n## Core Rules\\n\\n1. User configures cadence once: duration (1w/2w/3w/4w) + start day\\n2. Cycles are **computed from config + current date**, not stored as discrete records (e.g., `2026-W21`)\\n3. Issues get a `CycleID` field — can be set to **any** cycle (past, current, or future)\\n4. **Done issues** stay attributed to their original cycle → gives you cycle history\\n5. **Not-done issues** with a **past** CycleID are computed as belonging to the current cycle → automatic rollover, zero writes\\n6. **Not-done issues** with a **current or future** CycleID stay where they are\\n7. The gap between original `CycleID` and actual completion date reveals planning slip\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n- Data model: add `CycleID` to issue payloads\\n- Config: cycle cadence settings in `.beats/config.toml`\\n- CLI: `beats cycle` commands + `--cycle` flag on existing commands\\n- Web UI: cycle views in the board\\n- Projection: computed rollover logic"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T05:57:32.644878937Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-ffe8df","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T05:59:33.455371903Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-ffe8df","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-92bb16c1-b53f-4cef-9ca0-e1da6e279a06","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded cycle configuration and computation logic:\n\n- **`internal/config/config.go`** — added `CycleConfig` struct with `enabled`, `duration` (1w/2w/3w/4w), `start_day`, and `anchor_date` fields. Validation runs during `LoadConfig()` when cycles are enabled.\n- **`internal/config/cycle.go`** — core cycle computation:\n  - `Cycle` struct with `ID` (start date as YYYY-MM-DD), `Number`, `Start`, `End`\n  - `CycleForDate(date)` — compute which cycle a date falls in\n  - `CycleForID(id)` — resolve a stored cycle ID to its boundaries\n  - `CurrentCycle()` — convenience for current cycle\n  - `IsPastCycle(id, now)` — check if a cycle ID is before the current one (used for rollover)\n  - `EnumerateCycles(now, past, future)` — list N past/future cycles around now (for UI pickers)\n  - `Contains()`, `IsBefore()` on `Cycle` for boundary checks\n- **`internal/config/cycle_test.go`** — 17 tests covering: 2-week and 1-week cadences, boundary containment, past/current/future detection, enumeration, year boundary crossover, validation of all config fields, and dates before the anchor.\n\n### Design decisions\n\n- **CycleID = start date (YYYY-MM-DD)**: self-describing and stable even if cadence config changes later. ISO week format (`2026-W21`) was considered but doesn't map cleanly to multi-week cadences.\n- **Anchor date**: optional — defaults to the most recent `start_day` relative to now. When set, gives deterministic cycle numbering across machines.\n- **Negative cycle numbers**: dates before the anchor get cycle number 0, -1, etc. — the math extends infinitely in both directions."},"created_at":"2026-06-01T06:01:11.464785075Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
