{"id":"xpo-f7f968","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T07:12:35.573191998Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-f7f968","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-2cad3466-8278-4725-95e0-aa65371adaf1","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented computed rollover logic:\n\n- **`internal/beats/projection.go`** — added `applyCycleRollover()` called from `ProjectIssuesWithConfig()` when cycles are enabled. Rules:\n  - Done issues → `EffectiveCycleID` = original `CycleID` (history preserved)\n  - Not-done issues with a past `CycleID` → `EffectiveCycleID` = current cycle (automatic rollover)\n  - Not-done issues with current/future `CycleID` → `EffectiveCycleID` = `CycleID` (unchanged)\n  - Uncycled issues → `EffectiveCycleID` remains empty\n- **`internal/model/types.go`** — added `EffectiveCycleID` field to `Issue` (derived state, never persisted)\n- **`internal/beats/list.go`** — added `CycleID` to `FilterOptions`; filters against `EffectiveCycleID` for rollover-aware listing\n- **MCP + HTTP responses** — both `issueSummary`/`showOut` and `IssueResponse` now include `effective_cycle_id`\n- **`internal/beats/cycle_test.go`** — 7 tests covering: done stays in original, not-done rolls forward, current/future unchanged, uncycled untouched, multi-boundary rollover, and mixed-issue batch\n\n### Design\n\nOriginal `CycleID` is never mutated — it's the historical record. `EffectiveCycleID` is computed at projection time and used for filtering/display. This means zero writes on rollover."},"created_at":"2026-06-01T07:14:31.220434046Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
