{"id":"xpo-c70ad2","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-68a09c2b-09da-4f1e-b7c5-a7ac4f3c77ab","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded CLI commands and flags for cycle management in `cmd/beats/cycle.go`:\n\n### New commands\n- **`beats cycle`** / **`beats cycle current`** — show current cycle info + its issues\n- **`beats cycle next`** — show next cycle + its issues\n- **`beats cycle \u003cYYYY-MM-DD\u003e`** — show a specific cycle by ID\n- **`beats cycle init --duration 2w --start monday [--anchor YYYY-MM-DD]`** — configure cadence (writes to `.beats/config.yaml`)\n- **`beats cycle history [-n 5]`** — list past cycles with done/total completion stats\n\n### New flags on existing commands\n- **`beats ls --cycle current|next|\u003cYYYY-MM-DD\u003e`** — filter issues by effective cycle\n- **`beats add --cycle current|next|\u003cYYYY-MM-DD\u003e`** — assign new issue to a cycle at creation\n- **`beats update \u003cid\u003e --cycle current|next|none|\u003cYYYY-MM-DD\u003e`** — assign/unassign cycle (`none` clears it)\n\n### Implementation details\n- `resolveCycleID()` helper resolves symbolic names (`current`, `next`, `none`) to actual cycle IDs\n- `writeCycleConfig()` writes the cycles section to `.beats/config.yaml` using yaml.Node manipulation (same pattern as `AddLabel`)\n- `printCycleWithIssues()` renders a cycle header with its issue list using existing `ui.RenderIssueList`\n- Cycle filter in `beats ls` uses `EffectiveCycleID` so rollover is transparently applied"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T07:38:08.778762382Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-c70ad2","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T07:38:11.213126344Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-e20298","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## Goal\\n\\nAdd full cycle support to the web UI, inspired by a standard cycles view.\\n\\n## Views\\n\\n### 1. Cycles overview page\\n- List of all past and upcoming cycles with completion stats (done/total, success %)\\n- Current cycle highlighted\\n- Click into a cycle to see its filtered backlog\\n\\n### 2. Cycle detail view\\n- Backlog view pre-filtered to that cycle's issues\\n- Stats aside showing: cycle number, date range, current/upcoming/past label, scope/started/completed counts\\n\\n### 3. Navigation\\n- \\\"Cycles\\\" entry in the main sidebar nav\\n- Nested \\\"Current\\\" and \\\"Upcoming\\\" shortcuts under Cycles\\n\\n### 4. Context menu\\n- \\\"Move to cycle\\\" option in issue context menus\\n- Sub-menu with: No cycle, Current, Upcoming, and recent/next cycles\\n\\n### 5. Issue details\\n- Cycle indicator in the issue details aside panel\\n\\n### 6. Backlog indicators\\n- Small cycle icon/badge on issue rows in the backlog view\\n\\n## Backend prerequisites\\n\\n- New API endpoint: `GET /api/cycles` returning cycle list with stats\\n- New API endpoint: `GET /api/cycles/:id` returning cycle detail with issues\\n- Extend issue list endpoint to support `?cycle=\u003cid\u003e` filter\""},"created_at":"2026-06-01T08:01:13.737867896Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-e20298","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T08:01:18.226099219Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-e20298","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-cb197a60-29ee-42c9-912e-086ef416dd7c","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented the Web UI cycle views across backend and frontend:\n\n### Backend\n- **`internal/server/server.go`** — fixed `GetProjectedIssues()` to use `ProjectIssuesWithConfig()` so cycle rollover is applied in the web UI\n- **`internal/server/router.go`** — added `GET /api/cycles` route\n- **`internal/server/handlers.go`** — added `handleGetCycles()` returning cycle list with stats (done/total per cycle, status labels); added cycle config to `GET /api/config` response\n\n### Frontend — Types \u0026 API\n- **`web/src/api/types.ts`** — added `cycle_id`, `effective_cycle_id` to `Issue`; added `Cycle` and `CyclesResponse` interfaces\n- **`web/src/api/client.ts`** — added `fetchCycles()`, updated `fetchConfig` return type with `cycles` field\n\n### Frontend — Routing \u0026 Navigation\n- **`web/src/App.tsx`** — added `'cycles'` to `View` type, route mappings, `cyclesEnabled` state from config, renders `\u003cCycles /\u003e` component\n- **`web/src/components/Layout/Layout.tsx`** — added `cyclesEnabled` prop, conditionally renders Cycles nav item with refresh icon after Board entry\n\n### Frontend — Cycles Component\n- **`web/src/components/Cycles/Cycles.tsx`** — full cycles page with:\n  - **Cycle list sidebar** — all past/upcoming cycles with progress bars, done/total counts, status badges (current/upcoming/past)\n  - **Cycle detail view** — issues grouped by status (DOING, PLANNED, BACKLOG, BLOCKED, DONE) with status icons\n  - **Stats sidebar** — cycle number, date range, progress bar, per-status breakdown\n  - **Empty state** — helpful message with `beats cycle init` instructions when cycles aren't configured\n\n### Frontend — Issue Detail\n- **`web/src/components/IssueDetail/PropertySidebar.tsx`** — added Cycle picker in the Properties card (after Assignee); shows current/upcoming cycles in a popover with \"No cycle\" option to remove assignment\n\n### What's not yet implemented (follow-up scope)\n- Context menu \"Move to cycle\" submenu\n- Cycle badge/icon on backlog issue rows\n- Burndown/progress chart in cycle detail (the line chart)"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T08:08:55.272223885Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-e20298","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T08:08:58.57462804Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-64f3aa","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add a \"Move to cycle\" option to the issue context menu (right-click) in the backlog and board views.\\n\\nThe submenu should show:\\n- No cycle\\n- Current cycle (with checkmark if assigned)\\n- Upcoming cycles\\n- Recent past cycles\\n\\nFollow the existing submenu pattern in `web/src/components/ui/ContextMenu.tsx`.","labels":["feature","WebApp"],"parent_id":"xpo-c7b7c6","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Context menu: Move to cycle submenu"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T08:16:56.247418266Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-dd51a6","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Show a small cycle indicator/badge on issue rows in the backlog view when an issue is assigned to a cycle.\\n\\nThe badge should be compact (e.g., a small icon + cycle number) and only appear when cycles are enabled and the issue has a `cycle_id`.","labels":["feature","WebApp"],"parent_id":"xpo-c7b7c6","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Backlog: cycle badge on issue rows"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T08:16:59.01952044Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-308a37","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add a burndown or progress chart to the cycle detail view, similar to a scope/started/completed line chart.\\n\\nThis would require tracking historical scope changes over time, which may need a new data structure or event-based computation. Consider computing from the event stream: for each day in the cycle, replay events to determine how many issues were in scope vs completed.","labels":["feature","WebApp"],"parent_id":"xpo-c7b7c6","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Cycle detail: burndown/progress chart"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T08:17:02.784528107Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-671546","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"The event collapse logic in `internal/storage/collapse.go` was missing `CycleID` in three places:\\n\\n1. `mergeUpdatePayloads` — didn't merge `CycleID` from incoming events\\n2. `projectCommittedState` — didn't apply `CycleID` from create/update events\\n3. `pruneNoopUpdates` — didn't compare `CycleID` against committed state, and the empty-check omitted `CycleID`, causing cycle-only updates to be pruned as no-ops\"","labels":["bug","Backend"],"parent_id":"xpo-c7b7c6","status":"PLANNED","title":"Bug: cycle assignment from issue details view doesn't persist"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T09:36:07.913763853Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-329c1c","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Cycle numbers in `EnumerateCycles` were computed relative to the anchor date, so cycles before the anchor got numbers 0, -1, -2, etc. Users expect sequential positive numbers (Cycle 1, 2, 3...).\\n\\nFix: renumber cycles sequentially starting from 1 in `EnumerateCycles` output.\"","labels":["bug","Backend"],"parent_id":"xpo-c7b7c6","status":"PLANNED","title":"Bug: cycle numbers display as negative or zero"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T09:36:10.37007233Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-671546","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T09:36:15.095622118Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-329c1c","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T09:36:15.661030796Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-671546","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-f7ef92f2-31bb-4dfc-b678-e6ea4350e246","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded `CycleID` handling to three functions in `internal/storage/collapse.go`:\n\n- **`mergeUpdatePayloads`** — now merges `CycleID` from incoming update events into existing collapsed events\n- **`projectCommittedState`** — now applies `CycleID` from both CREATE and UPDATE events when building committed state\n- **`pruneNoopUpdates`** — now compares `CycleID` against committed state (prune if unchanged), and includes `CycleID` in the empty-payload check (prevents cycle-only updates from being dropped as no-ops)\n\n### Root cause\n\nThe collapse logic was written before `CycleID` existed. Every other field on `UpdatePayload` had corresponding entries in all three functions. `CycleID` was added to the model but not threaded through the collapse layer."},"created_at":"2026-06-01T09:36:23.613206931Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-329c1c","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-a33f4daa-bef3-4a22-acee-9d982f6e0231","text":"## Summary\n\nChanged `EnumerateCycles` in `internal/config/cycle.go` to number cycles sequentially from 1 based on position in the output list, instead of using the raw offset-based number from `cycleForDateFromAnchor`.\n\nThe internal `cycleForDateFromAnchor` still uses offset-based numbering (needed for `CycleForID` and `IsPastCycle`), but the display-facing `EnumerateCycles` now always produces Cycle 1, 2, 3, ... regardless of anchor position."},"created_at":"2026-06-01T09:36:26.835087651Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
