{"id":"xpo-77d7cb","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Right now, we scan past commits and git authors to determine contributors (who can be assignees). Additionally, I'd like to make this configurable in `.beats/config.yaml` so team members can be described ahead of time and are available to be assigned to issues even when they haven't committed to the project yet.","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"a4","title":"Make contributors configurable"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T10:27:28.716163481Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-77d7cb","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T10:27:28.98333658Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-3c2135","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Right now we have a visibility problem: if another developer picks up an issue ticket and creates a new branch to work on it, then on their branch sets the issue to \"in progress\", the issue is for everyone else marked as open and may be picked again. We somehow need to sync state across upstream branches, using some smart mechanism, maybe refs or git remote ls or something to consolidate distributed state.","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"a5","title":"Recognized \"in progress\" from existence of upstream git branches in addition to issues.db"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T10:29:45.251339632Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-3c2135","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T10:29:45.39480573Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
