{"id":"xpo-77d7cb","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-bcefdd42-55e6-48a1-a2e5-e7dd81dfe08a","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded configurable `contributors` field to `.beats/config.yaml`. Team members listed here appear in the web UI assignee picker even if they haven't created or been assigned to any issues yet.\n\n**Backend:**\n- Added `Contributors []string` to `Config` struct in `internal/config/config.go` with `\"Name \u003cemail\u003e\"` format validation\n- Exposed `contributors` array in `GET /api/config` response via `internal/server/handlers.go`\n\n**Frontend:**\n- Added `contributors?: string[]` to `fetchConfig()` return type in `web/src/api/client.ts`\n- Threaded `contributors` state through `App.tsx` → `IssueDetail` → `PropertySidebar`\n- Merged configured contributors into the `knownPeople` memo in `PropertySidebar.tsx`, deduplicating by email with issue-derived people\n\n**Config format:**\n```yaml\ncontributors:\n  - \"Alice Example \u003calice@example.com\u003e\"\n  - \"Bob Test \u003cbob@test.com\u003e\"\n```\n\nInvalid format produces a clear error: `config: invalid contributors[0] format: expected 'Name \u003cemail\u003e', got \"bad\"`"},"created_at":"2026-06-01T15:51:58.053370062Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.158 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
