{"id":"xpo-8c2171","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-54693403-bb67-467a-a8e2-b04224745ce7","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented auto-unparent: when a parent issue is deleted, all children have their `ParentID` cleared automatically.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n- `internal/beats/delete.go` — after appending the DELETE event, `DeleteIssue` now iterates all issues in the projected state, finds children whose `ParentID` matches the deleted issue, and emits UPDATE events to clear their `ParentID`.\n- `internal/beats/beats_test.go` — added `TestDeleteParentUnparentsChildren` covering the case of deleting a parent with two children and verifying both are unparented.\n\n**Rationale:** This is the safe default — no silent data loss. The alternative (cascade-delete children) is a separate, more dangerous feature that should be offered as a user choice in the Web UI, tracked as follow-up work."},"created_at":"2026-06-08T07:58:15.173529044Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.161 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-8c2171","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-f7dfd3c7-b215-4102-b150-de0ab681f851","text":"## Cascade delete — implementation complete\n\n### Backend\n\n- `internal/model/types.go` — added `Cascade bool` to `DeletePayload`\n- `internal/beats/delete.go` — `DeleteIssue` now accepts a variadic `cascade` parameter. When true, children get DELETE events instead of unparent UPDATE events. The cascade reason references the parent ID for traceability.\n- `internal/server/handlers.go` — passes `p.Cascade` from the API request through to `DeleteIssue`\n- `internal/beats/beats_test.go` — added `TestDeleteParentCascadeDeletesChildren` verifying parent + both children are deleted while unrelated issues survive\n\n### Frontend\n\n- `web/src/components/IssueDetail/PropertySidebar.tsx` — when deleting an issue with children, shows a three-option dialog: \"Keep sub-issues\" (unparent), \"Delete sub-issues too\" (cascade), and \"Cancel\". Issues without children get the existing simple confirmation.\n- `web/src/components/ui/ContextMenu.tsx` — same logic for the right-click context menu and the Ctrl+Backspace keyboard shortcut.\n\n### Design rationale\n\n\"Keep sub-issues\" is the prominent (filled) button since it's the safer default. \"Delete sub-issues too\" uses an outlined style to signal the destructive choice. Both paths go through the same `addDraft` → `handleDraft` → `DeleteIssue` pipeline."},"created_at":"2026-06-08T08:13:37.059753978Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.161 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
