{"id":"xpo-51af4e","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"},"created_at":"2026-06-09T06:16:44.022573229Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.169 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-51af4e","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-6fd57f2e-d737-4c2d-9a19-c170da437b6a","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented change indicators for issues with matching remote branches. When a remote branch matches an issue ID, the system now computes and displays commit count, files changed, insertions, and deletions relative to the default branch.\n\n### Files changed\n\n**Model layer:**\n- `internal/model/types.go` — added `BranchStats` struct (`Branch`, `Commits`, `FilesChanged`, `Insertions`, `Deletions`) and `BranchStats *BranchStats` field on `Issue`\n\n**Git logic:**\n- `internal/beats/branches.go` — refactored `branchMatchesIssue` into `matchingBranch` (returns branch name instead of bool); added `computeBranchStats` (runs `git rev-list --count` and `git diff --shortstat`) and `parseShortstat` helper. `applyBranchInference` now sets `BranchStats` on all issues with matching branches regardless of status (not just inferred-DOING ones)\n\n**CLI display:**\n- `internal/ui/styles.go` — added `FormatBranchStats()` for compact `[3 commits, 7 files, +142 -38]` annotations\n- `internal/ui/list.go` — appends branch stats tag after issue title when space permits\n- `internal/ui/details.go` — shows Branch and Changes rows in the detail view with colored +/- indicators\n\n**API layers:**\n- `internal/mcpserver/tools.go` — added `BranchStats *model.BranchStats` to `issueSummary` and `showOut` structs, wired through `toSummary()` and `show()` handler\n- `internal/server/responses.go` — added `BranchStats *model.BranchStats` to `IssueResponse`, mapped in `issueToResponse()`\n\n**Web frontend:**\n- `web/src/api/types.ts` — added `BranchStats` interface and `branch_stats` field on `Issue`\n- `web/src/components/IssueDetail/PropertySidebar.tsx` — new \"Branch\" card showing branch name, commit count, files, and colored +/- stats\n- `web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx` — compact inline stats badge (`3c 7f +142-38`) on issue rows\n\n**Tests:**\n- `internal/beats/branches_test.go` — added `TestMatchingBranch` (3 cases), `TestParseShortstat` (4 cases including edge cases), `TestBranchStatsComputed` (integration test with real git repos verifying commit count, files changed, insertions, and branch name)\n\n### Design rationale\n\n- **Read-time computation** (no caching) — stats are derived from git at projection time, same pattern as the existing branch inference. Avoids stale data and keeps the event log clean.\n- **Stats for all matched branches, not just inferred-DOING** — an issue explicitly set to DOING still benefits from seeing its branch stats. The status inference and stats computation are decoupled.\n- **`parseShortstat` over `--numstat`** — simpler to parse, single line, and we only need totals not per-file breakdown.\n- **Three-dot diff for shortstat** (`main...branch`) — shows the symmetric difference, which is the right semantic for \"what changed on this branch\" regardless of whether main has advanced."},"created_at":"2026-06-09T06:24:14.531430171Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.169 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-51af4e","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-b8b39d2e-32f0-4d85-8729-848da4d28833","text":"## Final update\n\nRefined the UI based on review feedback:\n\n- **Backlog/list view**: Simplified to commit count badge with Lucide `GitCommitVertical` icon; full stats available via tooltip on hover\n- **Issue detail (PropertySidebar)**: Added HEAD SHA (12-char) badge with `GitCommitVertical` icon in a monospace pill\n- **CLI list**: Compact `⊙ 3` badge; CLI detail view shows SHA next to branch name\n- **Model**: Added `HeadSHA` field to `BranchStats`, computed via `git rev-parse`\n- **Dependency**: Installed `lucide-react` for consistent iconography (will also be used by xpo-adc4ed)"},"created_at":"2026-06-09T07:22:18.252328863Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.169 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-51af4e","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-09T07:22:18.329795642Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.169 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-4f6d6d","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Overview\n\nA local-first code review and merge workflow that treats the beats issue as the pull request. No remote forge required — review the full diff, leave comments, and merge cleanly, all from the terminal or web UI.\n\nThe issue already carries the PR metadata (title, description, comments, history, branch stats). This epic adds the missing pieces: a review view and a merge action.\n\n## Workflow\n\n```\nbeats start \u003cissue\u003e     # create branch, transition to DOING\n# ... work, commit ...\nbeats review [\u003cissue\u003e]  # unified review: stats, commits, diff\nbeats merge [\u003cissue\u003e]   # merge branch, close issue\n```\n\nWhen invoked with no argument, both commands infer the issue from the current branch name using the existing branch-matching logic.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n- **`review` and `merge` are separate commands** — review is read-only and safe to repeat; merge is the action.\n- **New `MERGE` event type** — records branch, base SHA, merge SHA, and strategy in the issue history.\n- **Diff goes through the user's pager** — respects `GIT_PAGER` / `core.pager`, so `delta`, `diff-so-fancy`, etc. work out of the box.\n- **Merge strategies**: merge commit (default), squash, fast-forward.\n\n## Out of Scope (v1)\n\n- Multi-reviewer approval gates\n- Inline diff comments (file-level comments via `beats comment` are sufficient)\n- Merge conflict resolution UI (bail to git on conflicts)","labels":["epic"],"status":"BACKLOG","title":"Local pull request workflow"},"created_at":"2026-06-09T07:37:01.439198659Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.169 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-148cee","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\n`beats review [issue-id]` shows a unified review screen for a branch's changes — everything needed to decide whether to merge, in one place.\n\nWhen invoked with no argument, infers the issue from the current git branch using the existing branch-matching logic.\n\n## CLI Output\n\n```\nxpo-51af4e  Fix login flow\n══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\norigin/xpo-51af4e/fix-login → main\n⊙ a1b2c3d4e5f6  3 commits, 7 files, +142 -38\n\nCommits\n───────\na1b2c3d  Fix token refresh race condition\n8f4e2a1  Add retry logic for expired sessions\nc7d9b3e  Update tests\n\nDescription\n───────────\n(rendered markdown from the issue description)\n\nFiles Changed (7)\n──────────────────\nM  internal/auth/token.go          +45 -12\nM  internal/auth/token_test.go     +38 -0\nM  internal/auth/session.go        +22 -8\n...\n\n── Full diff follows (piped through pager) ──\n```\n\n## Behaviour\n\n1. Resolve the issue (by argument or by current branch)\n2. Verify issue has a matching remote branch; error with helpful message if not\n3. Render the summary header: issue title, branch → base, head SHA, stats\n4. List individual commits (`git log --oneline base..branch`)\n5. Render the issue description (markdown via glamour)\n6. List files changed with per-file stats (`git diff --stat base...branch`)\n7. Pipe the full diff through the user's pager (`GIT_PAGER` / `core.pager` / `PAGER` / `less`)\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- Reuse `computeBranchStats` from the existing branch inference for stats\n- Add `listBranchCommits(branch, base string) []Commit` helper to get individual commits\n- Add `listFilesChanged(branch, base string) []FileStat` helper for per-file stats\n- The diff pipe should use `git diff base...branch` with color enabled when outputting to a terminal\n- The issue description rendering already exists in `ui.RenderIssueDetails`\n- Add `inferIssueFromBranch()` helper that gets the current branch name and matches it against issues\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `beats review \u003cid\u003e` shows the full review view\n- [ ] `beats review` (no arg) infers issue from current branch\n- [ ] Commits listed individually with short SHA + message\n- [ ] Files changed listed with per-file insertions/deletions\n- [ ] Full diff piped through user's pager\n- [ ] Issue description rendered as markdown\n- [ ] Error message when no matching branch found\n- [ ] Error message when issue not found","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","CLI"],"parent_id":"xpo-4f6d6d","status":"BACKLOG","title":"beats review: unified code review from the terminal"},"created_at":"2026-06-09T07:37:20.060232291Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.169 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-bbef03","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\n`beats merge [issue-id]` merges the issue's branch into the default branch and transitions the issue to DONE. Supports merge commit, squash, and fast-forward strategies.\n\nWhen invoked with no argument, infers the issue from the current git branch.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Resolve the issue (by argument or current branch)\n2. Verify issue has a matching remote branch\n3. Pre-flight checks:\n   - Working tree must be clean (abort with message if dirty)\n   - Warn if local branch is behind remote\n4. Show a compact summary (branch → base, commits, files, +/-)\n5. Prompt for merge strategy (or accept via flag):\n   - `--merge` — merge commit via `git merge --no-ff` (default)\n   - `--squash` — `git merge --squash`, single commit with issue title as message\n   - `--ff` — `git merge --ff-only`, fails if not possible\n6. Switch to default branch, run the merge\n7. Record a `MERGE` event on the issue\n8. Add a completion comment summarizing what was merged\n9. Transition issue to `DONE`\n10. Prompt to delete the branch (or `--delete-branch` / `--keep-branch` flags)\n\n## New Event Type\n\n```go\nEventTypeMerge EventType = \"MERGE\"\n\ntype MergePayload struct {\n    Branch   string `json:\"branch\"`\n    BaseSHA  string `json:\"base_sha\"`\n    MergeSHA string `json:\"merge_sha\"`\n    Strategy string `json:\"strategy\"` // \"merge\", \"squash\", \"ff\"\n}\n```\n\n## Error Handling\n\n- **Dirty working tree** → abort, tell user to commit or stash\n- **Merge conflicts** → abort the merge, tell user to resolve with git and re-run. Do not attempt to build a conflict resolution UI.\n- **FF-only requested but not possible** → abort, suggest `--merge` or `--squash`\n- **No matching branch** → error with helpful message\n- **Already on default branch with no issue branch** → error\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `beats merge \u003cid\u003e` merges branch and closes issue\n- [ ] `beats merge` (no arg) infers issue from current branch\n- [ ] `--merge`, `--squash`, `--ff` strategy flags\n- [ ] Pre-flight: dirty tree check, behind-remote warning\n- [ ] `MERGE` event recorded with branch, SHAs, strategy\n- [ ] Completion comment auto-generated\n- [ ] Issue transitions to DONE\n- [ ] Branch deletion prompt (with `--delete-branch` / `--keep-branch` flags)\n- [ ] Clean error messages for all failure modes\n- [ ] Projection handles new `MERGE` event type","estimate":8,"labels":["feature","CLI"],"parent_id":"xpo-4f6d6d","status":"BACKLOG","title":"beats merge: merge branch and close issue"},"created_at":"2026-06-09T07:37:29.174647149Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.169 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-10d444","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\nA \"Review\" view on the issue detail page in the web UI that shows the full branch diff with syntax highlighting, commit list, and file browser. Provides the same review experience as `beats review` but in the browser with richer rendering.\n\n## Layout\n\nThe review view is accessible from the issue detail page when a branch is detected. It shows:\n\n1. **Header** — branch → base, head SHA badge, stats summary\n2. **Commit list** — each commit with SHA, message, author, timestamp\n3. **Files changed** — collapsible tree with per-file +/- stats\n4. **Diff viewer** — syntax-highlighted, unified diff per file. Expandable/collapsible per file.\n\n## API Endpoints\n\nNew endpoints needed on the web server:\n\n- `GET /api/issues/:id/commits` — returns list of commits on the branch\n- `GET /api/issues/:id/diff` — returns the full unified diff (or per-file diffs)\n- `GET /api/issues/:id/files` — returns list of files changed with stats\n\nThese endpoints reuse the branch detection from projection and run the same git commands as the CLI.\n\n## Frontend\n\n- **Diff rendering** — use a lightweight diff viewer component. Evaluate `react-diff-viewer` or build a minimal one with Shiki for syntax highlighting.\n- **File tree** — collapsible sidebar or top-level list of changed files, click to jump to that file's diff.\n- **Merge button** — calls `POST /api/issues/:id/merge` with `{ strategy: \"merge\" | \"squash\" | \"ff\" }`. Shows confirmation dialog with strategy picker.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Review view accessible from issue detail when branch exists\n- [ ] Commit list with SHAs, messages, authors\n- [ ] File list with per-file stats\n- [ ] Syntax-highlighted unified diff per file\n- [ ] Files collapsible/expandable\n- [ ] Merge button with strategy picker\n- [ ] API endpoints for commits, diff, files\n- [ ] Graceful fallback when no branch detected","estimate":8,"labels":["feature","WebApp"],"parent_id":"xpo-4f6d6d","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Web UI: review view with diff viewer"},"created_at":"2026-06-09T07:37:47.056942519Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.169 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
