{"id":"xpo-8c6306","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\nAdd a `beats_merge` MCP tool that merges an issue's branch into the default branch, records a `MERGE` event, and transitions the issue to `DONE`. This enables AI agents to complete the full issue lifecycle without shelling out to the CLI.\n\n## Implementation\n\nReuse the existing `client.MergeIssue()` method from `internal/beats/merge.go`. The MCP tool should:\n\n1. Accept issue ID and optional strategy (`squash`, `merge`, `ff`)\n2. Pre-flight check: working tree must be clean\n3. Call `client.MergeIssue()` with the given options\n4. Return merge SHA and messages\n\n## MCP Tool Definition\n\n```go\nmcp.AddTool(s, \u0026mcp.Tool{\n    Name:        \"beats_merge\",\n    Description: \"Merge an issue's branch into the default branch, record a MERGE event, and close the issue.\",\n}, t.merge)\n```\n\n### Input\n\n- `id` (required) — Issue ID\n- `strategy` (optional, default `squash`) — `squash`, `merge`, or `ff`\n- `delete_branch` (optional, default `false`) — Delete branch after merge\n\n### Output\n\n- `id` — Issue ID\n- `merge_sha` — SHA of the merge commit\n- `messages` — Status messages\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `beats_merge` MCP tool registered in `internal/mcpserver/tools.go`\n\n- [ ] Accepts issue ID, strategy, delete_branch parameters\n\n- [ ] Pre-flight: rejects if working tree is dirty\n\n- [ ] Calls `client.MergeIssue()` and returns result\n\n- [ ] Works with local and remote branches"},"created_at":"2026-06-09T16:14:21.595341196Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-5fc0f1","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-9fe0734f-6c6c-4867-80fc-f200d5a6328c","text":"Superseded by the local PR workflow: `beats review` (CLI) and the MergeView (Web UI) both provide full diff viewing with per-file stats, commit lists, and syntax-colored diffs. Closing as obsolete."},"created_at":"2026-06-09T16:15:07.874188854Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.169 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
