{"id":"xpo-0c592b","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-11T14:04:28.218288644Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.170 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-0c592b","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-050be261-462e-4d82-b54f-5aa462030790","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded Server-Sent Events for real-time issue update notifications, replacing the 5-second polling pattern.\n\n### Backend: `internal/server/sse.go`\n- `SSEHub` — central broadcaster with channel-per-client pattern, thread-safe subscribe/unsubscribe\n- `Broadcast(SSEEvent)` sends `{type, issue_id}` to all connected clients; drops events for slow clients\n- `handleSSE` — `GET /api/events` handler: sets `text/event-stream` headers, streams typed events (`issue_created`, `issue_updated`, `issue_deleted`, `issue_merged`, `issue_commented`), sends `:keepalive` comments every 30s, cleans up on client disconnect\n\n### Backend: broadcast wiring\n- `server.go` — added `SSEHub *SSEHub` field and `broadcastEvent()` helper\n- `handlers.go` — `handleDraft` broadcasts after every successful CREATE/UPDATE/COMMENT/DELETE; `handleStartWork` and `handleMergeIssue` broadcast on completion\n- `router.go` — `GET /api/events` registered with auth middleware when hub is configured; in proxy mode, the proxy already forwards SSE streams transparently\n\n### Frontend: `web/src/hooks/useSSE.ts`\n- `useSSE` hook: opens `EventSource` to `/api/events`, listens for all event types, calls `onEvent` callback on each\n- Auto-reconnect on error with 5s delay\n- Falls back to 30s polling interval when SSE is disconnected\n- On successful SSE connection, clears the polling interval\n\n### Frontend: `web/src/App.tsx`\n- Replaced `setInterval(fetchData, 5000)` with `useSSE({ onEvent: fetchData, fallbackInterval: 30000 })`\n- SSE-driven: instant UI updates when another user changes an issue\n- Graceful degradation: if SSE never connects (local mode, old server), falls back to 30s polling\n\n### Initialization\n- `cmd/beats/serve.go` — creates `SSEHub` on server startup\n- `cmd/beats/board.go` — creates `SSEHub` for local board (multi-tab support)\n\n### Tests (6 new)\n\n| Test | Coverage |\n|---|---|\n| `TestSSEHub_BroadcastToClients` | Broadcast reaches multiple subscribers |\n| `TestSSEHub_UnsubscribeRemovesClient` | Client count drops after unsubscribe |\n| `TestSSEHub_BroadcastDropsSlowClient` | Slow client doesn't block broadcasts |\n| `TestHandleSSE_StreamsEvents` | Full integration: connect → broadcast → receive typed SSE event |\n| `TestHandleSSE_NoHub_Returns503` | Returns 503 when SSE not enabled |\n| `TestBroadcastEvent_NilHub` | No panic when hub is nil |\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [x] `GET /api/events` SSE endpoint with bearer auth\n- [x] Server broadcasts on every event append\n- [x] Hub pattern with client registration/cleanup\n- [x] Heartbeat keepalive every 30s\n- [x] `beats board` proxy forwards SSE stream in remote mode (standard HTTP proxy)\n- [x] Frontend `EventSource` connection with automatic reconnect\n- [x] UI refreshes on receiving update notifications\n- [x] Graceful degradation: if SSE disconnects, fall back to polling (30s)"},"created_at":"2026-06-11T14:09:27.69514714Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.170 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
