{"id":"xpo-7e6300","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"beats login: write remote URL to .beats/config.yaml","description":"## Problem\n\nAfter refactoring credential storage from `.beats/` to `~/.config/beats/credentials.yaml`, `beats login` no longer writes the `remote.url` to `.beats/config.yaml`. This means `LoadConfig()` gets an empty `Remote.URL`, so `ResolveRemote()` never looks up the token — the project is effectively disconnected from the remote.\n\n## Design\n\n`beats login [server-url]` should own writing both files. Behavior matrix:\n\n| URL arg? | `.beats/config.yaml` state | Behavior |\n|---|---|---|\n| yes | doesn't exist | create minimal config with `remote.url`, login |\n| yes | exists, is local project (has `prefix`/`version`) | warn + exit |\n| yes | exists, already has `remote.url` | warn (don't overwrite) + exit |\n| yes | exists, no `remote.url` | add `remote.url` section, login |\n| no | has `remote.url` | use that URL, login |\n| no | no config or no `remote.url` | error: no server URL |\n\n## Implementation\n\n- [ ] Add `SetRemoteURL(serverURL)` to `internal/config/` — upserts `remote.url` in `.beats/config.yaml` via `yaml.Node`\n- [ ] Add `ReadRemoteURL()` to read just the remote URL from existing config\n- [ ] Add `IsLocalProjectConfig()` to detect server-side configs (has `prefix`/`version`)\n- [ ] Update `login.go` — make URL arg optional, implement the behavior matrix\n- [ ] Tests","status":"PLANNED","estimate":3,"assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-06-12T06:43:23.020026723Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.175 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-7e6300","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-12T06:43:25.778434264Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.175 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-3c0b49","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"beats serve: structured request logging middleware","description":"## Summary\n\nAdd structured, parseable request logging to `beats serve` so operators have visibility into client activity, REST API access, and MCP actions.\n\n## Design\n\nImplement as HTTP middleware that wraps all handlers (REST + MCP), emitting one log line per request to stdout in a comma-separated format:\n\n```\ntimestamp,method,path,status,duration_ms,client\n2026-06-12T10:30:01Z,POST,/api/issues,201,12,alice \u003calice@example.com\u003e\n2026-06-12T10:30:02Z,POST,/mcp,200,45,bob \u003cbob@example.com\u003e\n```\n\nFields:\n- **timestamp** — ISO 8601 UTC\n- **method** — HTTP method\n- **path** — request path (no query string to avoid leaking sensitive params)\n- **status** — HTTP status code\n- **duration_ms** — wall-clock request duration in milliseconds\n- **client** — identity from JWT `sub` claim, or `anonymous` if unauthenticated\n\n## Notes\n\n- Middleware approach keeps handler code untouched\n- Client identity extracted from the JWT already on the request context\n- Consider a `--quiet` flag or log-level option later if noise becomes an issue","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"xpo-075586","estimate":2,"labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-06-12T07:28:07.352320652Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.175 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-3c0b49","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"},"created_at":"2026-06-12T07:30:25.878636454Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.175 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-3c0b49","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-3add588c-7cea-4d71-a4ea-0c99c3d28537","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded structured request logging middleware to `beats serve`.\n\n**New file:** `internal/server/logging.go` — `RequestLogger` wraps the HTTP handler and emits one CSV line per request to stdout:\n\n```\n2026-06-12T10:30:01Z,POST,/api/issues,201,12,Alice \u003calice@example.com\u003e\n```\n\nFields: `timestamp,method,path,status,duration_ms,client`\n\n- Uses a `statusRecorder` wrapper to capture the response status code\n- Extracts client identity from the request context (set by the auth middleware) — falls back to `anonymous` for unauthenticated endpoints\n- Wired in at `cmd/beats/serve.go` wrapping the entire mux, so all routes (REST, MCP, auth, healthz, static) are logged\n- 3 tests covering anonymous requests, authenticated requests, and implicit 200 status"},"created_at":"2026-06-12T07:32:26.939806594Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.175 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-6cb6e0","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Empty project onboarding: full-page empty states","description":"## Summary\n\nWhen a project has zero issues, the Dashboard, Backlog, and Board views should show friendly full-page empty states that guide new users toward their first action — instead of rendering empty tables and charts with zeroes.\n\n## Design\n\nEach view gets a tailored empty state:\n\n- **Dashboard** — \"Welcome to Beats\" hero with a brief description and a \"Create your first issue\" CTA button\n- **Backlog** — centered illustration + \"No issues yet\" message with CTA\n- **Board** — empty columns with a prompt in the center\n\nThe empty state should:\n- Only appear when `issues.length === 0`\n- Use the existing design system (CSS vars, Card component, etc.)\n- Include a CTA that triggers the NewIssueModal\n- Disappear permanently once the first issue exists","labels":["feature","WebApp"]},"created_at":"2026-06-12T09:17:45.708362868Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-7e6300","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-6e260c50-2711-4098-9c22-ae7ff24f746f","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed `beats login` to write both credential and project config files.\n\n### Changes\n\n**`internal/config/remote.go`** — three new helpers:\n- `ReadRemoteURL()` — reads `remote.url` from `.beats/config.yaml`\n- `IsLocalProjectConfig()` — detects server-side configs (has `prefix` field)\n- `SetRemoteURL()` — upserts `remote.url` and `version: 2` into `.beats/config.yaml`, creating the file if needed\n\n**`cmd/beats/login.go`** — reworked login flow:\n- URL argument is now optional (`cobra.MaximumNArgs(1)`)\n- `resolveServerURL()` — uses config's `remote.url` when no arg given\n- `writeProjectRemote()` — writes config only when needed, warns on mismatch\n- Pre-flight check blocks login from local project directories\n\n**`internal/config/remote_test.go`** — 10 new tests covering all helpers\n\n### Behavior matrix\n\n| URL arg | Config state | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| yes | no config | creates minimal config, logs in |\n| yes | local project (has prefix) | error before auth |\n| yes | has same remote URL | logs in, no config change |\n| yes | has different remote URL | logs in, warns |\n| no | has remote URL | uses it, logs in |\n| no | no config/remote | error |"},"created_at":"2026-06-12T09:19:30.532444427Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-3c0b49","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-49ea67a0-4166-4f36-b058-355a20c1f247","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded structured request logging middleware to `beats serve`.\n\n### Changes\n\n**`internal/server/logging.go`** — `RequestLogger` HTTP middleware:\n- Logs one line per request: `timestamp,method,path,status,duration_ms,client`\n- Extracts client identity from JWT bearer token (username portion before `@`)\n- `statusRecorder` implements `http.Flusher` to avoid breaking SSE streaming\n- `ConfigureLogging()` sets the `log` package to RFC3339 UTC for consistent timestamps\n\n**`cmd/beats/serve.go`** — wired in `ConfigureLogging()` and `RequestLogger()`\n\n**`internal/server/logging_test.go`** — 7 tests covering anonymous/authenticated requests, JWT parsing, status capture\n\n### Also fixed\n\n**`internal/server/handlers.go`** — 5 nil-slice-as-JSON bugs: `var x []T` serializes as `null`, not `[]`. Changed to `make([]T, 0)` in `handleGetIssues`, `handleGetCycles`, `handleCycleProgress`, `handleGetIssueHistory`, `handleMergeability`. This was causing a blank page crash on empty projects."},"created_at":"2026-06-12T09:19:47.690851456Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
