{"id":"xpo-46d0d2","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-67868b95-4161-4556-aca4-3e6f23170289","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented issue locking to prevent claim races on `beats start`.\n\n### Changes\n\n**`internal/beats/start.go`** — added three pre-flight guards before transitioning to DOING:\n1. **Status check** — rejects already-DOING issues with \"already in progress (assigned to X)\" error showing the current assignee\n2. **Branch check** — rejects if a local or remote branch already exists for the issue\n3. **Force override** — `force` parameter bypasses both guards, logs \"Force-claiming\" message\n\n**`internal/beats/git.go`** — added `RemoteBranchExists()` using `git ls-remote --exit-code --heads`\n\n**`cmd/beats/update.go`** — added `--force` flag to the `start` CLI command\n\n**`internal/mcpserver/tools.go`** — added `force` field to `startIn` schema, passed through to `StartWork`\n\n**`internal/server/handlers.go`** — `handleStartWork` now:\n- Accepts `?force=true` query parameter\n- Wraps the entire `StartWork` call inside `s.mu.Lock()` for atomic check-and-transition in server mode\n- Returns 409 Conflict (not 500) on rejection\n\n**`internal/beats/start_test.go`** — 4 new tests: DOING-rejected, DOING-force, existing-branch-rejected, existing-branch-force. Updated all existing tests for the new `force` parameter."},"created_at":"2026-06-12T11:03:11.423885891Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.175 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-46d0d2","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-f1b21c29-e520-4cbc-98b7-1a5a49ac0132","text":"## Additional fix: SSE polling regression\n\nWhile testing, discovered that the SSE implementation broke real-time updates for changes made outside the HTTP server (CLI, MCP tools). \n\n**Root cause:** `useSSE.ts` cleared the fallback polling interval on SSE connect. Since CLI/MCP changes write directly to `issues.db` and never trigger SSE broadcasts, those changes became invisible until the SSE connection dropped.\n\n**Fix:** `web/src/hooks/useSSE.ts` — `onopen` handler no longer clears the fallback polling. SSE gives instant updates for in-server changes; 30-second polling runs alongside to catch external changes."},"created_at":"2026-06-12T11:50:36.217462028Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.175 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
