{"id":"xpo-83b550","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Reusable Menu/SubMenu component with keyboard navigation","description":"## Summary\n\nCreate a canonical `Menu` and `SubMenu` component pair that solves portal rendering, positioning, outside-click dismissal, keyboard navigation, and focus management once — replacing the ad-hoc implementations scattered across the app.\n\n## Problem\n\nWe keep re-solving the same UX problems in multiple places:\n\n- **Filter menu** — portal, outside click, sub-menu positioning, keyboard nav, focus trapping in search inputs\n- **Sort menu** — portal, outside click, keyboard nav\n- **Label picker** — portal, outside click, keyboard nav, search\n- **Context menu** — portal, positioning, outside click\n- **Popover** — portal, positioning, outside click\n\nEach has its own bugs and inconsistencies. Every new menu feature re-invents the same patterns.\n\n## Design\n\n### `Menu` component\n\nA single top-level menu primitive that handles:\n\n- **Portal rendering** to `document.body`\n- **Positioning** relative to an anchor element (configurable: below, above, left, right, auto)\n- **Outside click** dismissal (tracks all nested sub-menus)\n- **Escape** to close (layered: deepest sub-menu first)\n- **Arrow key navigation** between items (up/down)\n- **Enter/Space** to select\n- **Focus management** — auto-focus on open, restore on close\n\n### `SubMenu` component\n\nNested within `Menu`, triggered by hovering/arrowing to a parent item:\n\n- **Positioning** relative to the parent row (auto left/right based on viewport)\n- **Arrow left/right** to enter/exit sub-menus\n- **Search input** support without trapping focus (Escape/arrow-right still exit)\n- **Highlight tracking** for keyboard-navigated items\n\n### `MenuItem` component\n\nIndividual menu rows with:\n\n- Icon, label, trailing content (count, badge, check, chevron)\n- Active/hover/focused states via CSS\n- Optional checkbox mode for multi-select\n\n### API sketch\n\n```tsx\n\u003cMenu anchorRef={btnRef} onClose={close}\u003e\n  \u003cMenuItem icon={\u003cStatusIcon /\u003e} label=\"Status\" submenu={\n    \u003cSubMenu searchable\u003e\n      \u003cMenuItem checkbox checked={...} label=\"Planned\" count={3} onClick={...} /\u003e\n      \u003cMenuItem checkbox checked={...} label=\"Doing\" count={2} onClick={...} /\u003e\n    \u003c/SubMenu\u003e\n  } /\u003e\n  \u003cMenuItem icon={\u003cPriorityIcon /\u003e} label=\"Priority\" submenu={...} /\u003e\n  \u003cMenuDivider /\u003e\n  \u003cMenuItem label=\"Clear all\" onClick={...} /\u003e\n\u003c/Menu\u003e\n```\n\n## Consumers to migrate\n\n- Filter menu (`FilterMenu.tsx`) — first adopter\n- Sort menu (inline in `Backlog.tsx`)\n- Label picker (`LabelPicker.tsx`)\n- Context menu (`ContextMenu.tsx`)\n- Status/estimate popovers in backlog rows\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `Menu`, `SubMenu`, `MenuItem`, `MenuDivider` components\n- [ ] Portal rendering with auto-positioning\n- [ ] Outside click dismissal across all nested levels\n- [ ] Full keyboard navigation (arrows, Enter, Escape, left/right for sub-menus)\n- [ ] Search input in sub-menus without focus trapping\n- [ ] Migrate filter menu as first consumer\n- [ ] Migrate at least one other consumer (sort menu or label picker)","status":"PLANNED","estimate":8,"labels":["improvement","WebApp"]},"created_at":"2026-06-13T07:21:40.202133638Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.175 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-7fcd0b","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-52d99020-c2eb-4e9a-b257-e0239f550fb2","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed keyboard focus not entering the filter popover when opened via `F` shortcut.\n\n### Changes\n\n**`web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx`** — added `showFilterMenuRef` guard so the backlog keyboard handler yields all keys (except `F` toggle) while the filter menu is open.\n\n**`web/src/components/Backlog/FilterMenu.tsx`** — rewrote keyboard handling:\n- First dimension auto-selected on open (visual highlight)\n- All navigation via document-level keydown listener (no div focus needed)\n- Up/Down navigates dimensions in the main menu\n- Left/Enter/Space enters the sub-menu, Right exits back\n- Up/Down navigates options within the sub-menu, Enter/Space toggles\n- Escape exits layered: sub-menu → main menu → closed\n- Search inputs in sub-menus (e.g. Labels) allow typing but still respond to Right and Escape to exit\n- Blur on exit prevents input from recapturing focus\n\n### Follow-up\n\nFiled xpo-83b550 to build a canonical reusable `Menu`/`SubMenu` component, replacing the ad-hoc implementations across filter menu, sort menu, label picker, and context menu."},"created_at":"2026-06-13T07:21:54.297963592Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.175 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
