{"id":"xpo-48524c","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"},"created_at":"2026-06-13T07:35:25.306254368Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.175 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-48524c","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-43cd29fb-af85-4999-9b27-7e24e10920f4","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed parent issue showing wrong status icon in \"Sub-issue of\" subtitle.\n\n### Root cause\n\nThe auto-progress and auto-complete logic in `internal/beats/projection.go` was overwriting the parent's status to match children's status but never setting `InferredStatus = true`. This caused the parent's StatusIcon to render as if the status was explicitly set, making it look identical to the child's status with no visual distinction.\n\n### Fix\n\n**`internal/beats/projection.go`** — set `parent.InferredStatus = true` in all three auto-progression paths:\n- Auto-complete parent (all children DONE → parent DONE)\n- Auto-progress parent from BACKLOG → PLANNED (child is PLANNED/DOING)\n- Auto-progress parent from PLANNED → DOING (child is DOING)\n\nNow the parent's StatusIcon renders with the dashed/faded inferred style, visually distinguishing it from explicitly-set statuses."},"created_at":"2026-06-13T07:39:16.883822321Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.175 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
