{"id":"xpo-7cd82d","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\n`beats inbox` shows events relevant to you since your last check — assignments, comments on your issues, status changes, merges. For developers working in the terminal who don't have the board open.\n\n## Design\n\n### CLI command\n\n```\n$ beats inbox\n  2m ago   alice assigned xpo-abc123 to you\n  5m ago   bob commented on xpo-def456 \"Looks good, one nit...\"\n  1h ago   alice merged xpo-ghi789 via squash\n  3h ago   carol changed xpo-abc123 status to BLOCKED\n\n3 new since last check. Run `beats inbox --clear` to mark as read.\n```\n\n### What's \"relevant to you\"\n\nEvents on issues where you are:\n- The assignee\n- The creator\n- A commenter (you've participated in the conversation)\n\nPlus all MERGE events (team-wide visibility).\n\n### Read tracking\n\nPer-user read state stored as `last_read` under the server key in `~/.config/beats/user.yaml` (see `xpo-0a9e5b`):\n\n```yaml\nservers:\n  beats.internal:\n    url: https://beats.internal\n    token: eyJhbG...\n    last_read: \"2026-06-15T10:30:00Z\"\n```\n\n`beats inbox` shows events after `last_read`. `beats inbox --clear` updates it to now.\n\n**Invariant:** read state is always per-user, never in `.beats/` — even in local mode, multiple developers and agents may pull the same event log and each needs their own read cursor.\n\n### Distributed mode\n\nIn distributed mode, the server has all events. `beats inbox` calls `GET /api/inbox` which filters events server-side based on the authenticated user's identity.\n\n### Local mode\n\nIn local mode, scan the event log and filter by the git user identity. Less useful (you're the only user) but still handy for tracking what your agents did while you were away.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `beats inbox` shows recent events relevant to the current user\n- [ ] Events filtered by assignee, creator, commenter, plus merges\n- [ ] Per-user `last_read` timestamp in `~/.config/beats/user.yaml`\n- [ ] `beats inbox --clear` marks all as read\n- [ ] Works in local mode (scan event log)\n- [ ] Works in distributed mode (server-side filtering)\n- [ ] Compact, readable terminal output"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T05:49:51.591504548Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
