{"id":"xpo-c35c55","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T05:53:42.179123829Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-c35c55","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-946879bd-c589-438c-b8f9-897fcbaa2ee6","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed sub-issues table ordering in `web/src/components/IssueDetail/SubIssuesTable.tsx`.\n\nThe `children` array was rendered in raw filter order (whatever the API returned). Now it's sorted with `sortIssuesWithinGroups(…, 'manual')` — the same function the backlog uses — which groups by status (BACKLOG → PLANNED → DOING → BLOCKED → DONE) and sorts within each group by `sort_order` (fractional indexing). DONE issues sort by most-recently-updated.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Imported `sortIssuesWithinGroups` from `../../utils/sort`\n- Wrapped the filtered children in `sortIssuesWithinGroups(…, 'manual')` inside the existing `useMemo`"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T05:55:21.669778361Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-b92fb0","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"relates_to","source_id":"xpo-b92fb0","target_id":"xpo-c35c55"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nCurrently `sort_order` is recomputed relative to the **destination status group's neighbors** when an issue is dragged between columns. This makes `sort_order` keys only meaningful within a status group — the global ordering is destroyed on every status transition.\n\nIndustry standard (Jira/LexoRank, GitHub Projects) is a **single global rank** that persists across status changes. Only Shortcut uses per-state positioning.\n\n## Current behavior\n\nWhen dragging issue X from PLANNED to DOING in `web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx` (lines 419-446):\n\n```typescript\nconst prev = withoutDragged[insertIdx - 1];  // prev in DOING group only\nconst next = withoutDragged[insertIdx];       // next in DOING group only\nupdate.sort_order = generateKeyBetween(\n  prev?.sort_order || null,\n  next?.sort_order || null,\n);\n```\n\nThe key is computed between DOING neighbors, losing X's position relative to issues in other groups.\n\n## Desired behavior\n\nWhen an issue moves between status groups, its `sort_order` should be computed relative to **all visible issues** (global order), not just the target group. The status changes, but the rank stays globally consistent.\n\nThis means:\n- Dragging within a group: recompute key between neighbors in the group (same as today)\n- Dragging between groups without a specific drop target: append to the target group but with a globally consistent key\n- Dragging between groups to a specific position: compute key between global neighbors at the drop point\n\n## Impact\n\nOnce sort order is globally consistent:\n- The sub-issues table (`SubIssuesTable.tsx`) can use simple `sortGroup('manual')` instead of `sortIssuesWithinGroups` — no need to group by status since the global order is meaningful\n- Any view that shows issues across statuses gets a sensible default order for free\n- Matches user expectations from Jira\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `sort_order` keys remain globally consistent when issues transition between status groups\n- [ ] Drag-and-drop within a status group continues to work as before\n- [ ] Drag-and-drop between status groups preserves global rank position\n- [ ] Sub-issues table can rely on global `sort_order` without status grouping","estimate":3,"labels":["bug"],"status":"BACKLOG","title":"Make sort_order globally consistent across status transitions"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T06:04:53.784140005Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-b92fb0","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\nCurrently `sort_order` is recomputed relative to the **destination status group's neighbors** when an issue is dragged between columns. This makes `sort_order` keys only meaningful within a status group — the global ordering is destroyed on every status transition.\n\nIndustry standard (Jira/LexoRank, GitHub Projects) is a **single global rank** that persists across status changes. Only Shortcut uses per-state positioning.\n\n## Current behavior\n\nWhen dragging issue X from PLANNED to DOING in `web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx` (lines 419-446):\n\n```typescript\nconst prev = withoutDragged[insertIdx - 1];  // prev in DOING group only\nconst next = withoutDragged[insertIdx];       // next in DOING group only\nupdate.sort_order = generateKeyBetween(\n  prev?.sort_order || null,\n  next?.sort_order || null,\n);\n```\n\nThe key is computed between DOING neighbors, losing X's position relative to issues in other groups.\n\n## Desired behavior\n\nWhen an issue moves between status groups, its `sort_order` should be computed relative to **all visible issues** (global order), not just the target group. The status changes, but the rank stays globally consistent.\n\nThis means:\n- Dragging within a group: recompute key between neighbors in the group (same as today)\n- Dragging between groups without a specific drop target: append to the target group but with a globally consistent key\n- Dragging between groups to a specific position: compute key between global neighbors at the drop point\n\n**Note:** DONE issues are intentionally sorted by recency of completion (`updated_at`) rather than manual rank — this is correct behavior and should be preserved. The global sort order fix applies to active statuses (BACKLOG, PLANNED, DOING, BLOCKED).\n\n## Impact\n\nOnce sort order is globally consistent, any view showing issues across active statuses gets a sensible default order. Matches user expectations from Jira.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `sort_order` keys remain globally consistent when issues transition between active status groups\n- [ ] Drag-and-drop within a status group continues to work as before\n- [ ] Drag-and-drop between status groups preserves global rank position\n- [ ] DONE issues continue to sort by recency (`updated_at`), not manual rank","sort_order":"Zw","status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T06:08:54.080041304Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
