{"id":"xpo-068b94","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"In dependency view, we show all dependencies. It would be nice if we could have a toggle to show/hide complete (default: hide) which is where both sides of the dependency are marked DONE.","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"b3g","title":"Ability to toggle hiding of completed dependencies"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T06:16:17.998349402Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-068b94","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T06:16:18.346657668Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-068b94","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T06:16:47.196755755Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-068b94","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-b99f8e80-0c15-41e3-a43b-0d7e31fd2fb6","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded a toggle to hide/show completed dependencies in the Dependencies view.\n\n**Changes:**\n- New reusable `Toggle` component (`web/src/components/ui/Toggle.tsx`) — iOS-style switch with `role=\"switch\"` and `aria-checked` accessibility, available in `sm`/`md` sizes, using project design tokens\n- `web/src/components/Dependencies/Dependencies.tsx` — dependencies where both source and target are DONE are hidden by default; a toggle in the header (\"Show completed (N)\") reveals them\n- Toggle state persisted in `localStorage` (`exponential-deps-show-completed`)\n- Toggle only appears when there are completed dependencies to show"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T06:23:25.601303095Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-068b94","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T06:23:25.744804883Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-40a164","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Migrate sort_order keys to globally consistent values (v2 → v3)","description":"## Summary\n\nWhen `xpo-b92fb0` changes drag-and-drop to maintain globally consistent `sort_order` keys, existing projects will have keys that are only meaningful within their status group. A one-time migration is needed to reindex all issues with fresh globally-consistent fractional keys.\n\n## Design\n\n### Trigger\n\nBump the config `version` field from `2` to `3`. On project load, if `version \u003c 3`:\n\n1. Walk all issues in current visual order (status group by status group, preserving within-group `sort_order`)\n2. Assign fresh globally-consistent fractional keys across all active issues\n3. DONE issues keep their keys (they sort by `updated_at`, not `sort_order`)\n4. Write updated keys to the event log\n5. Bump `version` to `3` in `.beats/config.yaml`\n\n### Touchpoints\n\n- [ ] `beats init` — new projects start at version `3` with global sort order from the start\n- [ ] Config loading (`internal/config/`) — detect version and trigger migration\n- [ ] Migration logic — reindex sort_order keys preserving visual order\n- [ ] Distributed mode — server must handle the migration on its copy of the data\n\n### Constraints\n\n- Migration must be **idempotent** — running it twice produces the same result\n- Visual order must be **preserved exactly** — users should not notice any change in their backlog after migration\n- Migration should be **automatic and silent** — no user action required\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Projects with `version: 2` are automatically migrated on first load\n- [ ] `beats init` creates projects at `version: 3`\n- [ ] Visual order in the backlog is identical before and after migration\n- [ ] Migration is idempotent\n- [ ] DONE issues are not reindexed","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":3,"dependencies":[{"source_id":"xpo-40a164","target_id":"xpo-b92fb0","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-06-15T06:50:22.61951836Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-a5a8f1","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"beats init/doctor: write and update .mcp.json","description":"## Summary\n\n`beats init` and `beats doctor` detect and configure agent instruction files (`AGENTS.md`, `.cursorrules`, etc.) but do not create or update `.mcp.json`. Currently `.mcp.json` setup is a manual step documented only in `beats mcp --help`.\n\nSince `.mcp.json` is what actually connects AI agents to the beats MCP server, it should be part of the automated setup flow.\n\n## Design\n\n### `beats init`\n\n- Check if `.mcp.json` exists at the project root\n- If it exists, check if it contains a `beats` MCP server entry\n- Report status (same pattern as agent file detection)\n\n### `beats doctor`\n\n- If `.mcp.json` is missing: offer to create it with the beats MCP server config\n- If `.mcp.json` exists but lacks a beats entry: offer to add one\n- If `.mcp.json` exists with a beats entry: report as configured\n\n### Content to write\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"beats\": {\n      \"command\": \"beats\",\n      \"args\": [\"mcp\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWhen appending to an existing `.mcp.json`, merge into the existing `mcpServers` object — don't overwrite other MCP server entries.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `beats init` detects and reports `.mcp.json` status\n- [ ] `beats doctor` offers to create `.mcp.json` if missing\n- [ ] `beats doctor` offers to add beats entry if `.mcp.json` exists without one\n- [ ] Existing `.mcp.json` content is preserved when adding the beats entry\n- [ ] Non-interactive mode prints instructions instead of prompting","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":3,"labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-06-15T07:03:15.734660815Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
