{"id":"xpo-a5a8f1","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-81caabb1-d544-4b26-b51c-3032e7f3293d","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded `.mcp.json` detection and setup to `beats init` and `beats doctor`.\n\n**New functions in `internal/beats/agents.go`:**\n- `DetectMCPConfig()` — checks if `.mcp.json` exists and contains a `beats` MCP server entry\n- `EnsureMCPConfig()` — creates or updates `.mcp.json` with a beats entry, preserving existing MCP server entries\n\n**`cmd/beats/init.go`:**\n- Reports `.mcp.json` status: configured (OK), exists but no beats entry (note), or missing (note)\n- Directs user to `beats doctor` for fixes\n\n**`cmd/beats/doctor.go`:**\n- If `.mcp.json` is missing: offers to create it with beats entry\n- If `.mcp.json` exists but lacks beats: offers to add the entry\n- If configured: reports OK\n- Non-interactive mode prints instructions\n\n**Tests in `internal/beats/agents_test.go`:**\n- `TestDetectMCPConfig_Missing`, `_ExistsWithoutBeats`, `_ExistsWithBeats`\n- `TestEnsureMCPConfig_CreatesNew`, `_PreservesExisting`"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T07:27:13.631146624Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
