{"id":"xpo-7f6ca6","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Backlog drag-and-drop is laggy during pointer move","description":"## Summary\n\nDragging issues in the backlog view is not smooth — the drag overlay lags behind the cursor. The `onDragMove` handler fires on every pointer move and may be doing too much work per frame.\n\n## Potential causes\n\n- `handleDndMove` runs `rows.findIndex(...)` on every move (O(n) with ~180 issues)\n- `handleDndMove` depends on `[rows, issues, expandedNodes, getRowStatusGroup]` — any state change during drag recreates the callback and triggers re-renders\n- Background SSE/polling refreshes during drag cause `issues` state to change, triggering re-renders of the entire DndContext\n- Large DOM with ~180 issue rows\n\n## Possible fixes\n\n- Debounce or throttle `handleDndMove`\n- Use refs instead of state for drag indicators to avoid re-renders\n- Pause SSE/polling refresh while a drag is active\n- Virtualize the issue list (only render visible rows)","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":3,"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-06-15T09:24:45.257471528Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-b92fb0","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-ef3c86d2-9719-48f4-9c91-c6d8d7e7ae37","text":"## Update: additional fix\n\nAdded sort_order sorting for siblings in the child reorder drag path (`Backlog.tsx` line 405-407). Without this, `generateKeyBetween` could receive unsorted prev/next keys and throw. Also added a guard for duplicate keys (prev === next) — generates after prev instead of crashing.\n\nAlso updated `SubIssuesTable.tsx` to use `sortGroup('manual')` instead of `sortIssuesWithinGroups` — sub-issues now display in natural global order without status grouping."},"created_at":"2026-06-15T09:24:54.36860678Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-40a164","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-9a372b99-f35e-4b0c-8fc7-b16fe6214538","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented v2→v3 migration for globally consistent sort_order keys.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n- `internal/version/version.go`: `DataModelVersion` bumped to 3\n- `internal/beats/setup.go`: `beats init` creates projects at version 3\n- `internal/beats/migrate.go`: `RunMigrations` handles v2→v3 via `migrateV2ToV3()`:\n  - `buildGlobalOrder()` walks issues in visual order (status group by status group, sorted by sort_order within each group)\n  - `GenerateNKeysBetween(\"\", \"\", N)` assigns fresh globally-unique keys in sequence\n  - Writes UPDATE events with new sort_order for each issue\n  - `UpdateConfigVersion(3)` bumps the config\n- `internal/beats/migrate_test.go`: Tests for `RunMigrations` (v3 up-to-date, old version errors), `buildGlobalOrder` (status ordering, within-group sorting, empty set)\n\nMigration ran successfully on this project — 179 issues, 179 unique keys, 0 duplicates."},"created_at":"2026-06-15T09:25:02.119916534Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-529e01","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Cache projected issues in memory instead of reprojecting on every API call","description":"## Summary\n\n`GetProjectedIssues()` in `internal/server/server.go` reads the entire `issues.db` from disk and reprojects all events on **every API call**. With 1200+ events this is significant unnecessary work — the projection result is deterministic for a given set of events.\n\n## Current behavior\n\n```go\nfunc (s *Server) GetProjectedIssues() (map[string]*model.Issue, error) {\n    events, err := storage.ReadEvents()  // reads entire file from disk\n    allEvents := append(events, s.pendingEvents...)\n    issues := beats.ProjectIssuesWithConfig(allEvents, s.Config)  // O(n) replay\n    return issues, nil\n}\n```\n\nCalled by: `handleGetIssues`, `handleGetIssue`, `handleGetActivity`, metrics, cycles, merge, start — nearly every read endpoint.\n\n## Desired behavior\n\nCache the projected state in the `Server` struct. Invalidate and recompute only when:\n- A new event is written (via `handleDraft`)\n- Pending events change (save/discard)\n- External file changes detected (polling watcher for CLI/MCP writes)\n\n## Design sketch\n\n```go\ntype Server struct {\n    mu             sync.RWMutex\n    cachedIssues   map[string]*model.Issue\n    cacheValid     bool\n    // ...\n}\n\nfunc (s *Server) GetProjectedIssues() (map[string]*model.Issue, error) {\n    s.mu.RLock()\n    if s.cacheValid {\n        issues := s.cachedIssues\n        s.mu.RUnlock()\n        return issues, nil\n    }\n    s.mu.RUnlock()\n    // reproject and cache...\n}\n\nfunc (s *Server) invalidateCache() {\n    s.mu.Lock()\n    s.cacheValid = false\n    s.mu.Unlock()\n}\n```\n\nCall `invalidateCache()` after `handleDraft` writes, after save/discard, and when the file watcher detects external changes.","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":3,"labels":["improvement"]},"created_at":"2026-06-15T09:25:57.505160167Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
