{"id":"xpo-7cd82d","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T11:38:45.612607818Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-7cd82d","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-eda8e96c-d559-43ce-9c4f-77a91c8c1a61","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented `beats inbox` — a personal notification feed for terminal users.\n\n### Filtering — `internal/beats/inbox.go`\n- `BuildInbox(events, issues, me, since)`: returns events (newest-first) on issues where the user is creator, current assignee, or a commenter, **plus all `MERGE` events** (team-wide). Excludes the user's own actions.\n- `isMeaningfulInboxEvent`: skips sort-order-only `UPDATE` events (drag-reorder / migration noise). Works for both typed and `map[string]interface{}` payloads — the existing `isMeaningfulActivityEvent` only handled maps, which is why this is a separate helper.\n- `FormatInboxItem`: per-type one-line sentences (\"assigned X to you\", \"changed X status to BLOCKED\", \"merged X via squash\", comment snippets).\n- `identityMatches`: email-aware with case-insensitive fallback (handles `Name \u003cemail\u003e` vs bare email vs name-only).\n\n### Read cursor — `internal/config/remote.go`\n- `GetInboxLastRead` / `SetInboxLastRead` route to `Servers[host].LastRead` (distributed) or `Projects[absBeatsPath].LastRead` (local). `UserConfig` gained a `Projects map[string]ProjectState`. Cursor is fully client-side in both modes; setting it preserves existing tokens.\n\n### Transport / server / CLI\n- `GetInbox(since)` added to the `Transport` interface — `LocalTransport` scans the event log; `RemoteTransport` calls `GET /api/inbox?since=…`.\n- `handleInbox` + `GET /api/inbox` route: resolves identity from the auth context (falls back to configured user when auth is off), filters server-side via the same `BuildInbox`.\n- `cmd/beats/inbox.go`: `beats inbox` (compact `go-humanize` timestamps) and `beats inbox --clear`.\n\n### Rationale\n- Read state lives in `user.yaml` (per `xpo-0a9e5b`), never in `.beats/`, so each developer/agent keeps an independent cursor even off a shared event log.\n- `BuildInbox` is shared by the local CLI path and the server handler, so local and distributed mode apply identical relevance rules.\n- Distributed correctness: `/api/user` returns the JWT identity (`user.Raw`), the same value `handleInbox` filters on, so \"to you\" rendering matches the server's filter.\n\n### Scope note\nThe sort-order-noise filter wasn't in the original spec but proved necessary — a smoke test against this repo's own log showed the raw feed flooded by migration/reorder updates, defeating the \"compact, readable\" criterion.\n\n### Tests\n- `BuildInbox`: relevance + merge, newest-first, since-cutoff, own-action exclusion, sort-order noise (typed + map payloads).\n- `FormatInboxItem` (incl. map payload), `identityMatches`.\n- Config cursor get/set for local + distributed, plus token-preservation.\n- Server: `GET /api/inbox` happy path + invalid `since` → 400.\n- `go vet ./...` clean; full `go test ./...` passes. Smoke-tested end-to-end (list → `--clear` writes cursor → \"No new activity\").\n\nAll 7 acceptance criteria met."},"created_at":"2026-06-15T11:59:43.105611291Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-7cd82d","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T11:59:45.779822495Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-f59c6b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Inbox participation filter misses users who made updates","description":"## Bug\n\n`BuildInbox` determines issue participation by checking only the **projected issue state**: creator, current assignee, and commenters (`internal/beats/inbox.go:60-74`). Users who interacted with an issue via UPDATE events (status transitions, title edits, label changes, etc.) are not counted as participants.\n\nThis means a user who actively managed an issue — e.g. moved it to PLANNED, edited its title — will not see inbox notifications for that issue unless they also happen to be the creator, assignee, or a commenter.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. Agent creates issue X\n2. User changes issue X status to PLANNED (an UPDATE event)\n3. Agent later marks issue X as DONE\n4. User runs `beats inbox` → \"No new activity\" (expected: DONE transition visible)\n\n## Fix\n\nWhen building the `participates` set, also scan the event log for any event created by `me`. If the user authored any event on an issue, they participate in it.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":1,"dependencies":[{"source_id":"xpo-f59c6b","target_id":"xpo-7cd82d","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-06-15T12:14:43.685804353Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-f59c6b","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T12:14:46.759090132Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-f59c6b","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-0e94e306-0845-4c55-bf52-cba5d092db08","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed `BuildInbox` in `internal/beats/inbox.go` to count event-log authorship as participation.\n\n**Root cause:** The participation set was built only from projected issue state (creator, assignee, commenters). Users who interacted via UPDATE events (status transitions, title edits, label changes) were not counted as participants, so subsequent events by others on those issues were silently filtered out.\n\n**Fix:** Added a second pass over the event log after the issue-state scan — any issue where `me` authored at least one event is now marked as participatory. This is a 5-line addition after the existing `for id, issue := range issues` loop.\n\n**Test:** Added `TestBuildInbox_UpdateCountsAsParticipation` — verifies that a user who only made an UPDATE (no create/comment/assignment) sees subsequent events by others on that issue. All 133 tests pass.\n\n**Verified end-to-end:** `beats inbox` now correctly surfaces the `xpo-7cd82d` DONE transition that was previously invisible."},"created_at":"2026-06-15T12:18:13.698997396Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
