{"id":"xpo-213d27","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-006f63aa-3332-48a3-b3f5-eddd52a6eb08","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented the WebUI Inbox — a personal notification feed in the browser.\n\n### Backend\n\n- `GET /api/inbox` — added `limit` query param (default 200) to cap event volume\n- `GET /api/inbox/status` — new endpoint returning `{last_read, unread}` for the current user\n- `POST /api/inbox/read` — new endpoint that advances the read cursor to now\n- Routes registered in `router.go` for local mode; proxy mode forwards to remote\n\n### Filtering\n\nTightened `BuildInbox` participation to **creator + current assignee only** (dropped commenter and update-author participation). This makes the inbox a focused \"things directed at you\" feed rather than a noisy \"things near you\" stream — distinct from the Overview activity feed.\n\n### Frontend\n\n- **Inbox component** (`web/src/components/Inbox/Inbox.tsx`):\n  - Tabbed interface: **New** (unread) and **Read** tabs with distinct empty states\n  - Events grouped by issue — one card per issue showing latest event + expandable \"+N more updates\"\n  - Centered column layout (`max-w-2xl`) with full-width cards\n  - Card layout: `[unread dot] [action icon] [issue ID link] [title] [timestamp]`, latest event summary, expandable detail for comments\n  - Deep linking: issue IDs are `\u003ca\u003e` tags with `href=\"#/issues/{id}\"` — proper links that also trigger in-app navigation\n  - \"Mark all as read\" button on New tab\n  - Load more pagination (20 groups per page)\n- **Sidebar**: Inbox nav item between Cycles and Labels with unread count badge\n- **Command palette**: Inbox added to navigation options\n- **SSE**: inbox data refetches on real-time events alongside issue data\n\n### Types\n\n- `InboxItem` and `InboxStatus` interfaces in `api/types.ts`\n- `fetchInbox()`, `fetchInboxStatus()`, `markInboxRead()` in `api/client.ts`\n\n### Tests\n\n- `TestBuildInbox_OnlyCreatorAndAssignee` — verifies tighter filter (commenters/updaters excluded)\n- All existing inbox tests pass with the narrower participation set\n- Full `go test ./...` green; frontend `tsc --noEmit` clean"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T13:25:38.611476591Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
