{"id":"xpo-3fe8c8","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T13:35:17.45249454Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-3fe8c8","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-ec53632a-0fcc-434d-8a3c-a2a4f25e2516","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented role-based permissions via config, enforced server-side in distributed mode.\n\n### Config schema — `internal/config/config.go`\n\nNew `PermissionsConfig` struct with `Roles` (role → capability list) and `Users` (email → role) maps. Added to `Config` as `Permissions` field. Config example:\n\n```yaml\npermissions:\n  roles:\n    admin: [\"*\"]\n    developer: [issue.read, issue.create, issue.update, issue.comment, issue.start, issue.merge, issue.link]\n    viewer: [issue.read, issue.comment]\n  users:\n    alice@team.dev: admin\n    bob@team.dev: developer\n    intern@team.dev: viewer\n```\n\nMethods: `RoleFor(email)`, `Capabilities(role)`, `HasCapability(email, cap)`, `Enabled()`. Wildcard `\"*\"` expands to `AllCapabilities`. When no permissions section exists, `HasCapability` returns true (open access, backwards compatible).\n\n### Server middleware — `internal/auth/middleware.go`\n\nNew `RequireCapability(pubKey, perms, capability, next)` wraps `RequireAuth` with a capability check. Returns 403 with `{\"error\":\"forbidden: requires X capability\"}` when denied.\n\n### Route wiring — `internal/server/router.go`\n\nNew `handleCap` helper alongside existing `handle`. Each endpoint annotated with its required capability:\n- `issue.read` — all GET endpoints (issues, history, config, metrics, activity, inbox, cycles)\n- `issue.create` — `POST /api/draft`\n- `issue.update` — save, discard, label management\n- `issue.merge` — `POST /api/issues/{id}/merge`\n- `issue.start` — `POST /api/issues/{id}/start`\n- `GET /api/user` stays on plain `handle` (always accessible after auth)\n\nOnly enforced when auth is enabled (`s.SigningKey != nil`); local mode is unaffected.\n\n### CLI — `cmd/beats/whoami.go`\n\nExtended with `printPermissions` — shows role name and capability list when permissions are configured.\n\n### Tests\n\n- `internal/config/permissions_test.go` — 7 tests: Enabled, RoleFor, Capabilities (wildcard + explicit), HasCapability (allowed/denied/unmapped/unconfigured), unknown role\n- `internal/auth/middleware_test.go` — 3 new tests: RequireCapability allowed (admin wildcard), denied (viewer), open access (no perms)\n- Full `go test ./...` passes\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- ✅ Config schema for roles and user-role mapping\n- ✅ Server middleware checks capabilities per endpoint\n- ✅ 403 response with clear message on denied operations\n- ✅ Default: full access when no permissions configured\n- ✅ `beats whoami` shows current user's role and capabilities\n- ⚠️ Admin lockout guard not implemented — validating \"at least one admin\" at config-load time would require knowing the full user list, which isn't available until auth keys are loaded. This could be a follow-up validation in `beats serve` startup."},"created_at":"2026-06-15T13:38:59.593144014Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
