{"id":"xpo-87e6fc","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\nThe `internal/beats` package is the core of the system — projections, status transitions, cascading automations, merge, delete, add, list filtering — and sits at 49.5% coverage. This is where the next data-integrity bug is hiding.\n\n## Critical gaps (data loss / corruption risk)\n\n### update.go — UpdateIssue() — NO TESTS\nThe most dangerous file. Handles status transitions with cascading side effects:\n- **Blocked-by dependency check** — no test that DOING is rejected when a blocker is incomplete\n- **Incomplete-children check** — no test that DONE is rejected when children aren't done\n- **Auto-close sub-issues** — cascading DONE propagation untested; partial failure mid-cascade leaves invalid state\n- **Auto-progress sub-issues** — three progression rules (BACKLOG→PLANNED, PLANNED→DOING) untested\n- **Multi-event append failures** — if event 2 of 3 fails, events 1 is already persisted\n\n### delete.go — DeleteIssue() — NO TESTS\n- **Cascade delete** — both `cascade=true` (delete children) and `cascade=false` (unparent children) paths untested\n- **Partial cascade failure** — if unparenting child 2 of 3 fails, children 1 is already orphaned\n\n### merge.go — MergeIssue() — PARTIAL\n- Only squash tested; **ff-only and --no-ff strategies untested**\n- **Merge conflict abort path** untested\n- **Branch deletion failures** (local + remote) untested\n- Event recording race: event appended before git merge — if git fails, event log and repo diverge\n\n### local_transport.go — resolveIssue()\n- **Prefix match** and **substring ambiguity** error paths untested — wrong ID resolution applies updates to the wrong issue\n\n### migrate.go — migrateV2ToV3()\n- **Partial migration failure** — if sort-order backfill fails mid-way, data model version is already bumped\n\n## High gaps (silent failures)\n\n### add.go — AddIssue() — NO TESTS\n- Event persistence failure silently swallowed\n- Default status assignment (BACKLOG fallback) untested\n- Dependency source-ID autofill untested\n\n### comment.go — AddComment() — NO TESTS\n- Issue resolution failure, event append error, git commit failure — all untested\n\n### projection.go — ProjectIssues()\n- Payload marshaling errors silently ignored\n- `backfillSortOrder()` failures silently return\n- `ProjectIssuesWithConfig()` automation rules + cycle rollover untested\n\n### list.go — FilterIssues()\n- `ParseTimeFilter` duration math (off-by-one in date calculations)\n- \"Mine\" filter identity matching edge cases\n\n## Medium gaps\n\n- **inbox.go** — `emailOf()`, `identityMatches()` edge cases with malformed identities\n- **user.go** — all three fallback paths (override → config → git) untested\n- **start.go** — force flag with existing remote branch, lock acquisition failures\n- **remote_transport.go** — HTTP error handling, timeout behavior\n- **gitlock.go** — timeout exceeded, lock file cleanup on crash\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] update.go: all 4 automation paths + dependency blocking + multi-event failure\n- [ ] delete.go: cascade true/false + partial failure\n- [ ] merge.go: all 3 strategies + conflict abort + branch cleanup\n- [ ] add.go: happy path + persistence failure + default status\n- [ ] comment.go: happy path + error cases\n- [ ] local_transport.go: resolveIssue ambiguity + prefix match\n- [ ] projection.go: payload error handling + backfill edge cases\n- [ ] Target: ≥80% coverage","estimate":8,"labels":["improvement"],"status":"PLANNED","title":"Test coverage: internal/beats (49.5%)"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T14:51:13.342026357Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-83ce0f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\nThe `internal/storage` package handles all reads and writes to the event log — the single source of truth for all issue data. At 39.9% coverage, most write paths and the entire archive system are untested. The bug we just fixed (collapse prune ignoring CreatePayload status) lived here.\n\n## Critical gaps (data loss / corruption risk)\n\n### storage.go — AppendEvent() — NO TESTS\nThe basic write operation. No test for:\n- File creation when `issues.db` doesn't exist\n- Append to existing file\n- JSON marshaling errors\n- Write failures (permissions, disk full)\n- Newline separator correctness\n\n### collapse.go — mergeUpdatePayloads()\n11 fields, only 2-3 tested indirectly. **Untested field merges:**\n- Description, ParentID, Estimate, Priority, Assignee, CycleID, Labels, Dependencies\n- Nil incoming values (should not overwrite existing)\n- CreatedAt timestamp update on merge\n- Multiple sequential merges\n\n### collapse.go — mergeCommentPayloads() — NO TESTS\n- Same-ID merge (should update text, return true)\n- Different-ID merge (should return false, leave existing unchanged)\n\n### collapse.go — pruneNoopUpdates()\nOnly tested indirectly via round-trip tests. **Per-field noop detection untested for:**\n- Description, ParentID, Estimate, Priority, Assignee, CycleID, Labels, Dependencies\n- Event with single field that's a noop (entire event should be dropped)\n- UPDATE on non-existent issue (should pass through)\n\n### collapse.go — rewriteFile() — NO TESTS\nAtomic file operation — the most dangerous untested function:\n- Temp file creation + write + flush + rename sequence\n- Empty committed bytes\n- Empty uncommitted list\n- JSON marshal error mid-write (cleanup path)\n- Flush failure (cleanup path)\n- Rename failure\n\n### archive.go — ArchiveEvents() — NO TESTS\nCore archive operation:\n- Backup creation (copyFile)\n- Append to archive.db\n- Rewrite issues.db with active events\n- **Partial failure scenarios** — backup succeeds but archive write fails\n\n### archive.go — copyFile() — NO TESTS\n\n## High gaps\n\n### collapse.go — readCommittedBytes()\n- Returns `(nil, nil)` on any git error — caller cannot distinguish \"no commits\" from \"git failure\"\n\n### collapse.go — projectCommittedState()\n- Not directly tested for individual field application\n- CREATE with all fields populated untested\n\n### read.go — ReadArchivedEvents() — NO TESTS\nIdentical to ReadEvents but for archive.db. Never tested.\n\n### collapse.go — strSlicesEqual() / depsEqual() — NO TESTS\nUsed for Labels and Dependencies comparison in prune logic. Order sensitivity not validated.\n\n## Medium gaps\n\n### read.go — ReadEvents()\n- Malformed JSON handling\n- Scanner errors (line too long)\n- Empty file\n\n### collapse.go — countLines()\n- Single event without trailing newline\n- Multiple trailing newlines\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] storage.go: AppendEvent happy path + error cases\n- [ ] collapse.go: mergeUpdatePayloads for all 11 fields individually\n- [ ] collapse.go: mergeCommentPayloads same-ID + different-ID\n- [ ] collapse.go: pruneNoopUpdates per-field coverage\n- [ ] collapse.go: rewriteFile atomic operation + failure cleanup\n- [ ] archive.go: ArchiveEvents full cycle + partial failure\n- [ ] read.go: ReadEvents + ReadArchivedEvents error cases\n- [ ] Target: ≥80% coverage","estimate":5,"labels":["improvement"],"status":"PLANNED","title":"Test coverage: internal/storage (39.9%)"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T14:51:37.489546087Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-7138f1","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\nThe `internal/server` package serves the REST API and manages the in-memory cache + pending events buffer. At 38.4% coverage, most state-mutating handlers and the entire metrics engine are untested.\n\n## Critical gaps (data loss / silent failures)\n\n### handlers.go — handleDraft() — PARTIAL\nOnly CREATE event type tested. **Missing:**\n- UPDATE event type — status changes, field updates, error handling\n- COMMENT event type — comment creation via draft\n- DELETE event type — issue deletion via draft\n- Error propagation from `client.UpdateIssue()`, `client.AddComment()`, `client.DeleteIssue()`\n\n### handlers.go — handleSave() — NO TESTS\nPersists pending events to disk. Untested:\n- Pending events → disk persistence cycle\n- Auto-commit behavior (git add + commit)\n- Commit message parameter handling\n- Error recovery when AppendEvent fails\n- Empty pending list (no-op case)\n\n### handlers.go — handleMergeIssue() — NO TESTS\n- Merge strategy selection (squash/merge/ff)\n- Working tree clean check\n- MergeOptions passing (commit_message, delete_branch)\n- Error response on merge failure\n\n### handlers.go — handleStartWork() — NO TESTS\n- Force parameter handling\n- Branch creation via client.StartWork()\n- Concurrent claim races (despite mutex)\n\n### metrics.go — computePulseMetrics() — NO TESTS\n465-line analytics function, completely untested:\n- **Velocity** — weekly/daily bucketing, points calculation, delta\n- **Throughput** — 7-day windows, issue counting\n- **WIP** — stale detection (5-day threshold), off-by-one risk\n- **Blockers** — age calculation, oldest tracking\n- **Flow** — cycle/lead time percentiles (p50/p75/p90), min/max\n- **Attention items** — blocker/stale/high-priority ranking, cap at 5\n- **Workload** — assignee aggregation, in-progress sorting\n- **Epics** — progress calculation, stale detection, child aggregation\n- **Trends** — bug age bucketing (24h/48h/5d/14d/1mo), triage time median\n\n## High gaps (should be tested)\n\n### handlers.go — label management\n- **handleAddLabel** — label creation, in-memory config update\n- **handleUpdateLabel** — rename across all issues, case sensitivity\n- **handleDeleteLabel** — removal from all issues\n\n### handlers.go — handleCycleProgress() — NO TESTS\nComplex event state machine: day-by-day scope/started/completed tracking, cycle ID filtering, end date clamping\n\n### handlers.go — inbox endpoints\n- **handleInboxStatus** — unread count calculation, lastRead config read\n- **handleInboxRead** — cursor persistence\n\n### server.go — cache concurrency\n- No test for multiple goroutines calling `GetProjectedIssues()` + `AddPendingEvent()` simultaneously\n- `refreshEventsLocked()` error handling untested\n- Rapid pending→disk→pending cycles (cache generation counter races)\n\n### router.go — capability enforcement\n- Routes use `handleCap()` but no tests verify a viewer is actually blocked from write endpoints\n\n## Medium gaps\n\n### handlers.go — read-only handlers\n- handleGetCycles — cycle enumeration, status classification\n- handleGetUser — authenticated vs fallback identity\n- handleListInstances — registry integration\n- resolveIssueBranch — branch resolution, BranchStats population\n- handleGetIssueCommits/Files/Diff — git integration\n- handleMergeability — blocker logic\n\n### sse.go\n- High-frequency broadcast saturation\n- Client reconnection scenarios\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] handleDraft: UPDATE, COMMENT, DELETE event types + error paths\n- [ ] handleSave: persistence cycle + auto-commit + error recovery\n- [ ] handleMergeIssue: all 3 strategies + error cases\n- [ ] handleStartWork: happy path + force + concurrent claims\n- [ ] computePulseMetrics: velocity, WIP, flow percentiles, attention items\n- [ ] Label handlers: add/update/delete with cascading issue updates\n- [ ] Cache concurrency: parallel read/write race tests\n- [ ] Capability enforcement: viewer blocked from write endpoints\n- [ ] Target: ≥70% coverage","estimate":8,"labels":["improvement"],"status":"PLANNED","title":"Test coverage: internal/server (38.4%)"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T14:52:06.774183365Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
