{"id":"xpo-e4397a","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"sort_order":"a9V"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T18:45:48.822175139Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-f6c313","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\nThe JS bundle is 1.5MB (471KB gzip) in a single chunk. Vite warns about it. For a tool that runs locally this isn't critical, but for distributed mode (served over the network) it matters, and it signals unnecessary weight.\n\n## Current state\n\nSingle chunk contains everything:\n- react-markdown + remark-gfm + remark-breaks (unified/micromark parser chain — likely ~300KB)\n- @dnd-kit/core + @dnd-kit/sortable (drag-and-drop)\n- @tiptap/* (rich text editor — StarterKit, React, TaskList, Markdown)\n- lucide-react (icon library)\n- fractional-indexing\n\n## Proposed changes\n\n### Code splitting via lazy routes\nHash routing already maps to distinct views. Lazy-load heavy views:\n```tsx\nconst Board = lazy(() =\u003e import('./components/Board/Board'));\nconst Dashboard = lazy(() =\u003e import('./components/Dashboard/Dashboard'));\nconst Inbox = lazy(() =\u003e import('./components/Inbox/Inbox'));\n```\nBoard pulls in dnd-kit, Dashboard pulls in chart code, Inbox pulls in react-markdown. Only the active view loads.\n\n### Manual chunks\nSplit vendor libraries into stable chunks that cache independently:\n```js\n// vite.config.ts\nmanualChunks: {\n  'markdown': ['react-markdown', 'remark-gfm', 'remark-breaks'],\n  'dnd': ['@dnd-kit/core', '@dnd-kit/sortable', '@dnd-kit/utilities'],\n  'editor': ['@tiptap/react', '@tiptap/starter-kit', 'tiptap-markdown'],\n}\n```\n\n### Tree shaking audit\n- `lucide-react` — verify only used icons are bundled (named imports should tree-shake, but check)\n- `@tiptap/starter-kit` — includes many extensions; if we only use a few, import individually\n\n### Target\n- Initial load under 200KB gzip\n- Largest vendor chunk under 300KB","estimate":3,"labels":["improvement","WebApp"],"status":"PLANNED","title":"Frontend bundle optimization — code splitting and tree shaking"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T18:49:57.248364813Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-72f7b8","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\nThe WebUI should be usable without a mouse. Basic a11y:\n\n- All interactive elements focusable via Tab\n- ARIA roles on custom widgets (Board columns, drag-and-drop, popovers)\n- Color contrast meets WCAG AA (check muted text against dark backgrounds)\n- Status icons have text alternatives (not just color)\n- Keyboard shortcuts documented (we have some — C for create, Cmd+K for palette — but no discoverable help)","estimate":5,"labels":["improvement","WebApp"],"status":"BACKLOG","title":"Accessibility audit — keyboard navigation and screen reader support"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T18:50:05.342788598Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-dc7fe5","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\nThe WebUI assumes a wide viewport (sidebar + content). On narrow screens or when browser is half-width, the layout breaks. For v1 release:\n\n- Sidebar collapses to icons-only below ~900px, hidden below ~600px\n- Board columns stack or horizontally scroll\n- Issue detail uses full width on narrow screens\n- Mobile-usable for quick triage (read-only is fine)","estimate":5,"labels":["improvement","WebApp"],"status":"BACKLOG","title":"Responsive layout for narrow viewports"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T18:50:12.318634102Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-f6c313","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"sort_order":"a98"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T19:01:56.228096266Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-73e685","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\nEvery API call currently reads the full event log and replays all events to project the current issue state. This is O(n) in the total event count for every read. As projects grow to thousands of events, this becomes a bottleneck.\n\n## Current architecture\n\n1. `storage.ReadEvents()` — reads entire `issues.db` from disk, parses every JSON line\n2. `ProjectIssues(events)` — replays all events to build the issue map\n3. Server caches the result and invalidates on mtime change — but any write (including sort-order drags) triggers a full re-read + re-project\n\n## Problem scenarios\n\n- Board drag-and-drop: each reorder writes an event, invalidates cache, triggers full replay on next poll\n- Active project with 5000+ events: every 30s SSE fallback poll replays the full log\n- `beats list` on CLI: full replay every invocation\n\n## Proposed approach\n\n### Snapshot + incremental tail\n\n1. **Snapshot file** — periodically write a materialized snapshot of the projected state to `.beats/snapshot.json` (or binary format). Contains the full issue map + the event count it was built from.\n2. **Incremental apply** — on read, load the snapshot, then only replay events after the snapshot's event count. If snapshot covers events 1-4000 and the log has 4050 events, only replay 50.\n3. **Snapshot triggers** — rebuild snapshot on `beats save` (explicit), on archive, or when the tail exceeds a threshold (e.g., 200 uncommitted events).\n\n### Server-side: smarter cache invalidation\n\nThe server already caches `cachedEvents` and `cachedIssues`. Improve this:\n- **Append-only detection** — if file size grew but didn't shrink, only read the new bytes (seek to last known position)\n- **Pending event projection** — when `AddPendingEvent` is called, apply the single event to the cached issue map instead of marking the whole cache dirty\n\n### What NOT to do\n- Don't use a database (SQLite etc.) — the append-only JSONL format is a feature (git-friendly, mergeable)\n- Don't eagerly project on write — that adds latency to the write path\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Snapshot file written on save/archive\n- [ ] Read path loads snapshot + replays only tail events\n- [ ] Server append-only detection avoids full re-read\n- [ ] Benchmark: 5000-event project reads in \u003c10ms (vs current ~50-100ms)","estimate":8,"labels":["improvement"],"status":"PLANNED","title":"Incremental state projection — avoid full replay on every request"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T19:19:44.763740994Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-6324e2","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"The project has no LICENSE file. Can't release publicly without one — users and organizations won't adopt a tool with ambiguous licensing. Pick a license and add it to the repo root.","estimate":1,"labels":["improvement"],"status":"PLANNED","title":"Add LICENSE file"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T19:40:19.896144856Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-d346a7","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add a CHANGELOG.md following Keep a Changelog format. Retroactively document the current state as v0.3.0 and establish the format for v1.0.0. Should cover: features, bugfixes, breaking changes per release.","estimate":2,"labels":["improvement"],"status":"PLANNED","title":"CHANGELOG for release tracking"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T19:40:22.220820455Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-603536","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\nNo pipeline exists to cut a release with downloadable binaries. Users currently need `go install` which requires a Go toolchain.\n\n## Needed\n\n- goreleaser config (`.goreleaser.yaml`) for cross-compilation: linux/mac/windows x amd64/arm64\n- GitHub Actions workflow for tagged releases (`v*` tag triggers build + publish)\n- Embed frontend assets before build (the `make frontend` step)\n- Homebrew tap formula (optional, nice-to-have)\n- Checksums + signing for binary verification\n\n## Output\n\n`gh release create v1.0.0` produces downloadable binaries for all platforms with embedded web UI assets.","estimate":3,"labels":["improvement"],"status":"PLANNED","title":"Release automation — goreleaser + cross-compiled binaries"},"created_at":"2026-06-15T19:40:26.551226943Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.177 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
