{"id":"xpo-918bd8","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-0efc193e-0354-4785-bc23-ab344a32e9ad","text":"## Summary\n\n**Root cause**: `onKeyDown={handleKeyDown}` was attached to both the `\u003cinput\u003e` element and its parent `\u003cdiv\u003e` in `CommandPalette.tsx`. Arrow key events fired on the input, then bubbled to the parent, calling `setSelectedIndex` twice per keypress — each using a functional updater (`i =\u003e i + 1`), so both increments applied.\n\n**Fix**: Removed the duplicate `onKeyDown` from the `\u003cinput\u003e`. The event naturally bubbles to the parent `\u003cdiv\u003e` where it's handled once."},"created_at":"2026-06-16T07:20:13.091035587Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-918bd8","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-16T07:21:24.970360019Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-adb33e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"The unread count badge currently counts the number of updates, which inflates what we actually do see in the inbox. For example one issue with 5 updates creates one card in the inbox but the badge in the sidebar says \"5\".","labels":["improvement"],"sort_order":"b22","title":"Unread count badge should count issues modified instead of global change events"},"created_at":"2026-06-16T07:23:21.141406975Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-adb33e","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a2l"},"created_at":"2026-06-16T07:23:36.94788679Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-adb33e","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"},"created_at":"2026-06-16T07:26:00.379707903Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-adb33e","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-89a1bc15-7b95-4b31-9039-e5b0596ecf01","text":"## Summary\n\n**Root cause**: `handleInboxStatus` in `internal/server/handlers.go` returned `len(beats.BuildInbox(...))` as the unread count. `BuildInbox` returns one item per event, but the web UI groups events by issue ID — so 5 updates to 1 issue showed a badge of \"5\" instead of \"1\".\n\n**Fix**: Count distinct issue IDs from the inbox items instead of raw item count. Now the sidebar badge matches what the user actually sees in the inbox view."},"created_at":"2026-06-16T07:26:52.33792405Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-adb33e","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-16T07:30:15.976062886Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-10af26","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Inbox redesign — nested event cards, natural sentences, unread count fix","description":"Redesigned the inbox view:\\n\\n- Card header: StatusIcon + bold accent-colored issue ID + title + event count\\n- Nested event cards with expand/collapse — latest event always visible, older behind \\\"K more\\\" toggle\\n- Natural sentence format: \\\"**Alice** started working on this\\\", \\\"**Bob** left a comment\\\"\\n- Event icons colored only for status changes; everything else neutral\\n- Unread badge counts distinct issues instead of raw events\\n- Width aligned to `max-w-4xl` standard\\n- Inverted default avatar colors for dark theme\\n- Removed redundant blue unread dot (tabs handle read/unread separation)","status":"DONE","labels":["improvement"]},"created_at":"2026-06-16T07:44:49.13157969Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
