{"id":"xpo-a24553","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-9e704403-7918-4843-a8e9-696346463a73","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded focus trap, auto-focus, and focus restoration to `Modal.tsx`:\n\n- **Focus trap**: Tab/Shift+Tab cycles through focusable elements within the modal. If no focusable elements exist, Tab is suppressed.\n- **Auto-focus**: On open, focus moves to the first focusable element inside the dialog (falls back to the dialog container itself).\n- **Focus restoration**: On close, focus returns to the element that was active when the modal opened.\n- Dialog container has `tabIndex={-1}` and `outline-none` as a focusable fallback.\n\nAll consumers of `\u003cModal\u003e` (e.g. `NewIssueModal`) get these behaviors automatically."},"created_at":"2026-06-16T08:45:40.80158941Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.178 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
