{"id":"xpo-e9d927","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Rebrand beats as `Exponential` with `xpo` binary","description":"## Summary\n\nRebrand from `beats` to **Exponential** (`xpo` binary). Enabling exponentially faster development with AI agents.\n\nProduct name, package names, and directories use `exponential`. The compiled binary, CLI commands, MCP server/tools, env vars, data directories, and commit prefixes use `xpo`. Default issue prefix for new repos becomes generic `issue-`.\n\n## Key Decisions\n\n| Item | Old | New |\n|------|-----|-----|\n| Go module | `github.com/palarix/beats` | `github.com/palarix/exponential` |\n| Binary output | `beats` | `xpo` |\n| Binary source dir | `cmd/beats/` | `cmd/exponential/` |\n| Core package dir | `internal/beats/` | `internal/exponential/` |\n| Core package name | `package beats` | `package exponential` |\n| Data dir | `.beats/` | `.xpo/` |\n| User config | `~/.config/beats/` | `~/.config/xpo/` |\n| Env prefix | `BEATS_*` | `XPO_*` |\n| MCP tools | `beats_list`, etc. | `xpo_list`, etc. |\n| MCP server name | `\"beats\"` | `\"xpo\"` |\n| Frontend brand | \"Beats\" | \"Exponential\" |\n| Commit prefix | `beats:` | `xpo:` |\n| Default ID prefix | `beats-` | folder-derived (fallback `\"issue-\"`) |\n| Skill dirs | `claude/skills/beats*` | `claude/skills/xpo*` |\n| CSS class | `prose-beats` | `prose-exponential` |\n| localStorage keys | `beats-*` | `exponential-*` |\n\nClean break — no backward compatibility, no migration, no deprecated env var fallbacks.\n\n## Scope\n\nFull implementation plan in `rename.md`. Covers 9 phases: directory renames, Go module + imports, package rename, string literals, frontend, build/CI, config/settings, documentation, tests.\n\n## Estimated touch points\n\n- ~60 Go source files\n- ~10 frontend files\n- ~170+ doc references\n- CI workflow, Makefile, Dockerfile, .mcp.json, CLAUDE.md","status":"PLANNED","estimate":8,"assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","labels":["feature","epic"]},"created_at":"2026-06-17T07:36:08.826438783Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.179 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-e9d927","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-17T08:27:19.073098881Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.179 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-fb6376","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Drop `xpo_` prefix from MCP tool names","description":"The MCP server is named `\"xpo\"`, so Claude's permission system produces `mcp__xpo__xpo_list` — a stutter. Drop the `xpo_` prefix from tool names so they become `list`, `show`, `add`, `update`, `comment`, `link`, `start`, `merge`, `history`. Permissions then read `mcp__xpo__list`, etc.\n\n## Touch points\n\n- `internal/mcpserver/tools.go` — 9 tool name strings\n- `internal/mcpserver/integration_test.go` — tool name references in tests\n- `.claude/settings.json` — permission allowlist entries\n- `CLAUDE.md`, `README.md`, docs — tool name references (part of Phase 8 docs update)","status":"PLANNED","estimate":1,"assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","labels":["improvement"]},"created_at":"2026-06-17T08:57:24.9724719Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.179 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-e9d927","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-7b239e96-52b3-4491-89a9-944f02d2d481","text":"## Summary\n\nFull rebrand from Beats to Exponential (`xpo` binary) completed across the entire codebase.\n\n### What changed\n\n- **Go module**: `github.com/palarix/beats` → `github.com/palarix/exponential`\n- **Directories**: `cmd/beats/` → `cmd/exponential/`, `internal/beats/` → `internal/exponential/`, skill dirs → `xpo*`\n- **Package**: `package beats` → `package exponential`, all exported symbols renamed (`InitProject`, `GenerateAgentDocs`, etc.)\n- **Runtime**: data dir `.xpo/`, config `~/.config/xpo/`, env `XPO_*`, MCP tools `xpo_*`, commit prefix `xpo:`\n- **Frontend**: brand \"Exponential\", localStorage `exponential-*`, CSS `prose-exponential`, default prefix `issue-`, reactive browser title `Project ❯ View`\n- **Build**: `Makefile` → `xpo`, `Dockerfile` → `xpo`, GitHub Actions → `xpo-*`\n- **Tests**: all hardcoded IDs, branch names, env vars, tool names, helper functions updated\n- **Documentation**: README, CHANGELOG, CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, GEMINI.md, design docs, skill docs — zero `beats` references remaining\n- **issues.db**: all issue ID prefixes rewritten from `beats-` to `xpo-`\n\n### Verification\n\n- `make test` — all 9 packages pass\n- `make build` — produces `xpo` binary\n- `rg 'beats'` / `rg 'Beats'` — zero hits outside `rename.md` and `.xpo/issues.db` historical text"},"created_at":"2026-06-17T09:59:27.932466332Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.179 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-e9d927","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-17T09:59:33.007066791Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.179 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-9ba68b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"`xpo pulse` — CLI analytical health check","description":"## Summary\n\n`xpo pulse` is the analytical health check for your project pipeline. Instead of reading a static Kanban board, it calculates the immediate tempo, cadence, and system health from the local Git history and event log.\n\n## Output Sections\n\n### Velocity Stream\nCurrent running story points completed per week (e.g., `218 pts/wk`), with trend direction and spark graph over recent weeks.\n\n### Cycle vs. Lead Time\nThe exact gap between how fast an active task is completed (cycle time — time from DOING to DONE) versus how long issues sit stale in the backlog before being picked up (lead time — time from CREATE to DONE). Surfaces bottlenecks: fast execution but slow triage means the backlog is the constraint, not the work itself.\n\n### Agent Efficiency\nBreakdown of which tasks were fully automated by the agent versus which required human override due to failed test suite loops, rejected PRs, or manual intervention. Derived from the event log's `created_by` field and status transition patterns (e.g., DOING → BLOCKED → DOING cycles indicate retries).\n\n## Design Notes\n\n- Reads from `.xpo/issues.db` event log and local git history — no network calls\n- Output is a compact terminal dashboard (not a TUI — just formatted text, like `git shortlog`)\n- Should reuse existing metrics logic from `internal/server/metrics.go` where possible\n- Consider color-coded indicators: green/yellow/red for health thresholds\n- The web UI already has a Dashboard with some of these metrics — `xpo pulse` is the CLI equivalent, optimized for quick glances in the terminal","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","CLI"]},"created_at":"2026-06-17T10:02:07.001531166Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.179 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-e282c2","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"`xpo drive` — autonomous agent execution loop","description":"## Summary\n\n`xpo drive` turns the local issue tracker into a conductor that hands off bounded workloads to AI coding agents. It runs a continuous loop: pick the next task, feed it to the agent, verify the result, commit, and move on.\n\n## Execution Loop\n\n### 1. Context Assembly\nReads the highest-priority, unassigned micro-story (1–3 story points) from the local xpo graph. Skips issues with unresolved `blocked_by` dependencies. Transitions the selected issue to DOING.\n\n### 2. Scope Containment\nPackages the issue's technical specifications, acceptance criteria (from description and checklist items), and relevant repository context files. Feeds this as a structured prompt directly into the agent.\n\n### 3. Autonomous Execution\nThe agent spins up a local git branch (`xpo start`), writes code, and runs the local testing framework (`make test` or configured test command).\n\n### 4. Auto-Commit\nIf tests pass: creates a git commit, merges the branch (`xpo merge`), flips the issue to DONE, and immediately grabs the next ticket. If tests fail: marks the issue BLOCKED with a comment explaining the failure, moves to the next eligible issue.\n\n## Design Considerations\n\n- Must integrate with Claude Code (and potentially other agents) — likely spawns a subprocess or uses the agent SDK\n- Needs a configurable test command (defaults to `make test`)\n- Should respect a max-iterations or time-budget flag to prevent runaway loops\n- `--dry-run` flag to show what it would pick up without executing\n- `--once` flag to process a single issue and stop\n- Agent identity should be set via `XPO_AGENT_IDENTITY` so commits are attributed correctly\n- Failure handling: after N consecutive failures, pause and surface a summary rather than burning through the backlog\n- Consider a `--filter` flag to scope to specific labels or epics","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":8,"labels":["feature","CLI"]},"created_at":"2026-06-17T10:03:05.614551685Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.179 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-9ba68b","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\n`xpo pulse` is the analytical health check for your project pipeline. Instead of reading a static Kanban board, it prints a compact summary of tempo, cadence, and system health from the local event log.\n\n## Output\n\n```\nxpo pulse\n┌──────────────────────────────┐\n│  Agent Velocity: 218 pts/wk  │\n│  Median Cycle Time: 12m      │\n│  Lead Time: 4h               │\n│  WIP: 3 active, 1 stale      │\n│  Blockers: 2                  │\n│  Agent / Human: 85% / 15%    │\n└──────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\nA single glance at your pipeline's vital signs. Each line maps to a metric already computed in `internal/server/metrics.go` — this command just reads the event log directly and prints the subset that matters for a terminal health check.\n\n## Metrics\n\n- **Agent Velocity** — story points completed in the last 7 days, extrapolated to per-week\n- **Median Cycle Time** — median time from DOING → DONE across recent completions\n- **Lead Time** — median time from CREATE → DONE (surfaces triage bottlenecks)\n- **WIP** — count of issues in DOING, plus how many are stale (no activity in N days)\n- **Blockers** — count of issues in BLOCKED status\n- **Agent / Human** — percentage of completions by agent vs. human (derived from `created_by` on the DONE transition event)\n\n## Design Notes\n\n- Reads from `.xpo/issues.db` — no server needed\n- Reuse metrics logic from `internal/server/metrics.go` where possible\n- Box-drawing output via `lipgloss` or raw unicode — keep it simple, no TUI\n- Color-coded values: green for healthy, yellow for warning, red for attention"},"created_at":"2026-06-17T10:03:44.403324392Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.179 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-e282c2","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\n`xpo drive` turns the local issue tracker into a conductor that hands off bounded workloads to AI coding agents. It runs a continuous loop: pick the next task, feed it to the agent, verify the result, commit, and move on.\n\n## Output\n\n```\nxpo drive --agent=claude\n● Running ticket: [EPIC-4] Status LWW state-machine guard\n✔ Testing passed (14 property-based assertions)\n✔ Git commit pushed [ae3f1c]\n✔ Ticket closed. (1.8 pts, 8m cycle)\n\n● Running ticket: [EPIC-5] Description LWW with loser preserved\n✔ Testing passed (7 assertions)\n✔ Git commit pushed [c41b09]\n✔ Ticket closed. (2 pts, 12m cycle)\n\n● Running ticket: [BUG-3] Race condition in login flow\n✘ Testing failed (auth_test.go:142)\n⚠ Ticket blocked. Moving on.\n\n■ Drive complete. 3 picked, 2 closed (3.8 pts), 1 blocked. 20m elapsed.\n```\n\n## Execution Loop\n\n### 1. Context Assembly\nReads the highest-priority, unassigned micro-story (1–3 story points) from the local xpo graph. Skips issues with unresolved `blocked_by` dependencies. Transitions the selected issue to DOING.\n\n### 2. Scope Containment\nPackages the issue's technical specifications, acceptance criteria (from description and checklist items), and relevant repository context files. Feeds this as a structured prompt directly into the agent.\n\n### 3. Autonomous Execution\nThe agent spins up a local git branch (`xpo start`), writes code, and runs the local testing framework (`make test` or configured test command).\n\n### 4. Auto-Commit\nIf tests pass: creates a git commit, merges the branch (`xpo merge`), flips the issue to DONE with cycle time noted, and immediately grabs the next ticket. If tests fail: marks the issue BLOCKED with a comment explaining the failure, moves to the next eligible issue.\n\n## Flags\n\n- `--agent=claude` — agent to use (required)\n- `--once` — process a single issue and stop\n- `--dry-run` — show what it would pick up without executing\n- `--filter=label` — scope to specific labels or epics\n- `--max=N` — stop after N tickets\n- `--test-cmd=\"make test\"` — override test command\n\n## Design Considerations\n\n- Spawns agent as subprocess or uses the agent SDK\n- Agent identity set via `XPO_AGENT_IDENTITY` so commits are attributed correctly\n- After N consecutive failures, pause and surface a summary rather than burning through the backlog\n- Final summary line shows totals: picked, closed, blocked, points, elapsed time"},"created_at":"2026-06-17T10:04:29.69430682Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.179 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-e282c2","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\n`xpo drive` picks up the next eligible ticket, hands it to an AI coding agent, verifies the result, and commits. One ticket per run — the loop is the caller's decision (shell loop, cron, CI trigger).\n\n## Output\n\n```\nxpo drive --agent=claude\n● Picked: [xpo-4fa8dd] Description LWW with loser preserved (2 pts)\n✔ Branch created: xpo-4fa8dd/description-lww\n✔ Testing passed (7 assertions)\n✔ Git commit pushed [c41b09]\n✔ Ticket closed. (2 pts, 12m cycle)\n```\n\nOn failure:\n\n```\nxpo drive --agent=claude\n● Picked: [xpo-267e29] Status LWW state-machine guard (3 pts)\n✘ Testing failed (auth_test.go:142)\n⚠ Ticket blocked. See xpo-267e29 for details.\n```\n\n## Execution Flow\n\n### 1. Pick\nSelects the highest-priority, unassigned PLANNED issue with 1–3 story points. Skips issues with unresolved `blocked_by` dependencies. Transitions to DOING.\n\n### 2. Package\nAssembles the issue's description, acceptance criteria, and relevant repo context. Feeds this as a structured prompt to the agent.\n\n### 3. Execute\nAgent creates a branch (`xpo start`), writes code, runs the test command.\n\n### 4. Close or Block\n- **Tests pass**: commit, merge (`xpo merge`), transition to DONE, print cycle time.\n- **Tests fail**: transition to BLOCKED, add a comment with the failure output, exit non-zero.\n\n## Flags\n\n- `--agent=claude` — agent to use (required)\n- `--dry-run` — show which ticket would be picked without executing\n- `--filter=label` — scope to specific labels or epics\n- `--test-cmd=\"make test\"` — override test command\n- `--id=xpo-xxx` — skip selection, drive a specific ticket\n\n## Design Considerations\n\n- One ticket, one run, clean exit code (0 = closed, 1 = blocked/failed, 2 = nothing to pick)\n- Spawns agent as subprocess or uses agent SDK\n- Agent identity set via `XPO_AGENT_IDENTITY`\n- Continuous mode is the caller's concern: `while xpo drive --agent=claude; do :; done`"},"created_at":"2026-06-17T10:07:04.221929017Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.179 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
