{"id":"xpo-4889dc","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-f14f449d-b37b-45fe-abff-40845fbd03e2","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented `xpo demo \u003coutput-directory\u003e` — a demo project generator that creates a fully populated Upurr Eats project.\n\n### Files added\n\n- `internal/demo/demo.go` — generator logic: types, personas, timestamp resolution, JSONL writer, config.yaml writer\n- `internal/demo/seed.go` — all narrative seed data: 132 issues across 7 epics, 593 total events spanning 7 narrative phases\n- `internal/demo/demo_test.go` — tests for generation, data integrity, chronological ordering, and ref validity\n- `cmd/exponential/demo.go` — CLI command with `--force` flag and safety check\n\n### Files modified\n\n- `cmd/exponential/main.go` — added \"demo\" to both allowed-without-config and version-check-exception lists\n\n### What the demo generates\n\n- **132 issues** across 7 epics: Core Platform, Menu \u0026 Ordering, Delivery \u0026 Logistics, Payments \u0026 Billing, Cat Profiles, Cat Mood Detection (descoped), Tech Debt \u0026 Reliability\n- **593 events** total: creates, status transitions, comments, and dependency links\n- **12 personas** (devs, designers, PMs, QA, AI agents — including an intern named Whiskers McFluff)\n- **7 narrative arcs**: kickoff → first sprint → payment incident (P0 double-charge) → feature descope → tech debt sprint → launch crunch → post-launch bugs\n- **Hybrid timestamps**: offsets anchored to `now - 60 days`, so the dashboard's \"last 14 days\" window always shows the launch crunch and post-launch activity\n- **Safety**: refuses to overwrite existing `issues.db` without `--force`\n\n### Design decisions\n\n- Generator writes JSONL directly rather than going through the transport layer — simpler, faster, no side effects (no git commits, no config dependency)\n- Seed data uses stable refs (like `\"CP-1\"`, `\"INC-2\"`) that get mapped to real nanoid-style IDs (`upe-000001`) at generation time\n- Config.yaml uses `upe-` prefix, fibonacci estimation, 2-week cycles, and all 12 personas as contributors\n- The 60-day window was chosen so that the most exciting phases (launch crunch, post-launch) land in the dashboard's default time windows"},"created_at":"2026-06-17T15:36:20.070831585Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.179 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-4889dc","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-2deaef6e-2c84-4172-8f1b-0cc4ee0e8d3a","text":"## Velocity and density improvements\n\nAfter review, the initial seed data had unrealistic velocity (~40 pts/week for a 12-person team) and multi-day gaps with zero story points burned.\n\n### Changes\n\n1. **Bumped estimates** across ~50 existing issues — more 5s and 8s, fewer 1s and 2s, matching what a real fibonacci-estimation team would produce\n2. **Added 48 gap-filler issues** — continuous development work (tests, tooling, infra, polish) that fills dead zones between the main narrative phases\n3. **Added 15 launch polish issues** — pre-launch prep and final hardening that fills the June 7-12 gap\n4. **Added 3 pre-launch bridge issues** — fills the June 1-3 gap between refactor and launch\n\n### Updated stats\n\n| Metric | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Total issues | 132 | 180 |\n| Total events | 593 | 779 |\n| Total story points | 344 | 686 |\n| Avg weekly velocity | ~40 pts/week | ~71 pts/week |\n| Min weekly velocity | ~0 | 32 pts |\n| Zero-burn weekdays | many + multi-day streaks | 6 scattered, max 2 consecutive |\n| Last 14 days (W24) | 11 pts | 64 pts |"},"created_at":"2026-06-17T16:11:33.885429685Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.179 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-4889dc","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-81e12861-9f81-4232-a25c-e2396c9b0c53","text":"## Rewrite: small team + AI agents, velocity trending up\n\nComplete rewrite of the seed data based on feedback: the target audience is small dev teams using xpo with AI agents, not enterprise teams.\n\n### Cast (6 personas, was 12)\n- **Sarah Chen** — Founder / CTO (architecture, reviews, incident leadership)\n- **Jake Morrison** — Full-stack engineer (Stripe, complex integrations)\n- **Luna Garcia** — Designer / Product (design specs, product decisions)\n- **Claude** — AI agent (backend, tests, refactoring)\n- **Devin** — AI agent (frontend, infra, DevOps)\n- **Whiskers** — Custom internal AI agent (routine tasks, docs, data work)\n\n### Pacing\n- AI agents: 2-8 hour cycle times (pick up and ship same day)\n- Humans: 8-48 hour cycle times (reviews, architecture, design)\n- 63% of issues created by AI agents\n\n### Velocity shape (marketing-approved)\n```\nW17:  55 ↑  ███████████████████████████\nW18:  62 ↑  ███████████████████████████████\nW19:  52 ↓  ██████████████████████████       ← pre-incident\nW20:  50 ↓  █████████████████████████        ← incident\nW21:  35 ↓  █████████████████                ← trough\nW22:  42 ↑  █████████████████████\nW23:  44 ↑  ██████████████████████\nW24:  88 ↑  ████████████████████████████████████████████  ← launch peak\n```\n\n- Post-incident: 35 → 42 → 44 → 88 (monotonically increasing)\n- Dashboard: 102 pts last 7d vs 41 prev 7d = **+61, trending UP**\n- 200 issues, 461 DONE pts"},"created_at":"2026-06-18T07:57:07.373641786Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.179 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-4889dc","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-3c53db18-0c2b-4f9d-abca-2e749a40370c","text":"## Final implementation\n\n### What shipped\n\n**`xpo demo \u003coutput-directory\u003e`** generates a realistic Upurr Eats project database.\n\n**Files added:**\n- `internal/demo/demo.go` — generator: personas, workweek snap, JSONL writer, config writer\n- `internal/demo/seed.go` — narrative seed data: 200 issues across 7 phases\n- `internal/demo/demo_test.go` — 4 tests: generation, data integrity, ref validity, chronological order\n- `cmd/exponential/demo.go` — CLI command with `--force` flag and safety check\n\n**Files modified:**\n- `cmd/exponential/main.go` — added \"demo\" to allowed/exception lists\n- `web/index.html` — favicon → `xpo.svg`\n- `web/src/components/Layout/Layout.tsx` — sidebar logo → `xpo.svg`, removed text label, layout fix\n\n### Demo stats\n- **200 issues**, 872 events, 6 personas (3 humans + 3 AI agents)\n- **63% agent-created** — AI agents do the heavy lifting\n- **Dashboard**: +61 pts trending UP\n- **Velocity**: post-incident recovery 31→52→62→69, peaking at launch\n- **Workweek cadence**: Mon=planning (creates+planned), Tue-Thu=shipping, Fri=testing, Sat-Sun=zero\n- **Safety**: refuses overwrite without `--force`"},"created_at":"2026-06-18T08:31:12.674775294Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.179 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
