{"id":"xpo-b8f7e8","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-51c99518-d884-4398-a21c-33efd8b0f354","text":"## Summary\n\nExternal changes to `issues.db` (from CLI/MCP) now appear in the GUI instantly via SSE, no more 30-second polling delay.\n\n### Server-side\n\n- **New `internal/server/watch.go`** — uses fsnotify to watch `issues.db` directly (file-level watch for WRITE events on macOS kqueue) plus the parent directory for CREATE events. CHMOD events are filtered out to avoid noisy broadcasts from the server's own reads. Writes are debounced at 150ms.\n- **`internal/server/sse.go`** — added `REFRESH` event type mapping (though currently broadcasting as `UPDATE` for compatibility)\n- **`internal/server/server.go`** — calls `WatchDB()` on server startup; removed `WriteTimeout` from the HTTP server config as it was killing the long-lived SSE connection after 15 seconds of silence\n\n### Client-side\n\n- **`web/src/hooks/useSSE.ts`** — removed 30-second fallback polling entirely; added `refresh` event listener; stabilized EventSource connection by storing `onEvent` in a ref (prevents connection churn when the callback identity changes)\n- **`web/src/App.tsx`** — dropped `fallbackInterval` parameter from `useSSE` call\n\n### Root causes addressed\n\n1. CLI/MCP writes bypassed HTTP handlers so no SSE event was broadcast\n2. `WriteTimeout: 15s` on the HTTP server killed SSE connections before the 30s keepalive could fire — masked by the old polling fallback\n3. `onEvent` in the useEffect dependency array caused EventSource reconnection churn"},"created_at":"2026-06-18T10:21:43.666723Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.179 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
