{"id":"xpo-8d8169","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-18T10:25:09.698797Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.179 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-9ce88e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"The UI uses arbitrary `var(--color-*)` values throughout instead of proper Tailwind theme tokens, causing color clashes — e.g. hover states that are invisible because a component and its parent both resolve to the same `bg-hover` value.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe design system defines a layering hierarchy in CSS variables but components bypass it with inline `[var(...)]` Tailwind classes. There's no enforcement that a component uses the correct surface level, and hover/active states collapse when layers overlap.\n\n## Proposed token structure\n\n- **`bg-surface`** — deep black, the app background\n- **`bg-surface-1`** — containers that sit on the background (sections, sidebar)\n- **`bg-surface-2`** — surfaces on surfaces (cards, inputs, group headers)\n- **`bg-surface-3`** — elevated surfaces (popovers, dropdowns, modals)\n- **`text-on-surface`** / **`text-muted`** — text colors that work on any surface level\n- **`border-default`** / **`border-subtle`** — semantic border tokens\n- **`hover-surface-N`** — hover states that are always one step above their resting surface\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define the tokens in `@theme` so Tailwind generates proper utility classes\n- Replace all `[var(--color-*)]` usages with the semantic tokens\n- Ensure hover states are always visually distinct from their resting surface","labels":["improvement","WebApp"],"title":"Migrate UI to semantic Tailwind surface/layer tokens"},"created_at":"2026-06-18T11:35:13.409883Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.179 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-8d8169","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-afba5d6a-ed35-4828-ba6b-261292e52816","text":"## Summary\n\nUnestimated issues now show a dashed triangle icon with a default \"1\" value, visually distinct from the solid triangle used for deliberately estimated issues.\n\n### Changes\n\n- **New `web/src/components/ui/EstimateBadge.tsx`** — reusable component using Lucide `Triangle` / `TriangleDashed` icons, with rounded-full pill shape and hover state\n- **`web/src/components/Board/BoardCard.tsx`** — replaced inline SVG estimate rendering with `EstimateBadge`, now always visible (was hidden when unestimated)\n- **`web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx`** — replaced inline SVG + conditional logic with `EstimateBadge`\n- **`web/src/components/ui/index.ts`** — exported `EstimateBadge`"},"created_at":"2026-06-18T11:36:07.501876Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.179 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
