{"id":"xpo-9ce88e","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-1f8ba26f-a3cb-4af9-8540-9e8eb243f954","text":"## Summary\n\nMigrated the entire UI from ad-hoc `bg-*` / `border-*` CSS variables to a semantic surface layering system with per-layer hover states.\n\n### New token hierarchy\n\n```\nLayer       Bg        Hover       Border\nbase        #070707               \nsurface     #0f0f0f   #161616     border-subtle   #1e1e1e\nsurface-1   #161616   #1c1c1c     border-default  #282828\nsurface-2   #1c1c1c   #222222     border-elevated #2a2a2a\nsurface-3   #222222   #2a2a2a     border-overlay  #323232\nsurface-4   #2a2a2a\n```\n\n### Migration scope (~33 files)\n\n- `bg-sidebar` → `base`\n- `bg-primary` → `surface`\n- `bg-secondary` / `bg-tertiary` → `surface-1`\n- `bg-elevated` → `surface-2` (cards) or `surface-3` (popovers/modals)\n- `bg-hover` → per-layer: `hover-surface`, `hover-surface-1`, `hover-surface-2`, `hover-surface-3`\n- `border-card` → consolidated into `border-subtle`\n- Fixed broken refs: `--color-accent-hover`, `--color-surface-elevated` in Card.tsx\n\n### Additional polish\n\n- All surface/border values normalized to pure neutral grays (removed blue tint)\n- Main content area gets a subtle diagonal gradient for dimensionality\n- `EstimateBadge` hover fixed to use `hover-surface-1` (visible above row hover)"},"created_at":"2026-06-18T13:12:53.977353Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.179 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-9ce88e","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-18T13:12:54.23228Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.179 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-643465","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-18T14:33:53.030553Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.126 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-643465","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-96a63640-1b83-4a2d-bcb0-e62d046b9dab","text":"## Summary\n\nMoved the project selector from mid-sidebar to the bottom as a dropdown, and extracted a shared icon system as a follow-on cleanup.\n\n### Project selector dropdown\n\n- Removed the static \"Projects\" section from the middle of the sidebar nav\n- Added `ProjectSelector` component at the bottom of the sidebar (between spacer and user avatar)\n- Trigger button shows current project name + chevron (or just folder icon when collapsed)\n- Popover opens upward with all projects listed; current project highlighted with bold text and background\n- Clicking another project navigates to its port (same `\u003ca\u003e` behavior as before)\n- Closes on outside click or Escape\n- Collapsed sidebar: popover gets `minWidth: 200px` to extend beyond the narrow sidebar\n\n### Shared icon system\n\nCreated `web/src/components/ui/icons.tsx` with 28 reusable icon components (24x24 heroicons-style + 16x16 custom), each accepting optional `className` prop. Updated 20 component files to use shared icons, eliminating ~63 duplicate inline SVGs across the codebase. Icons with strokeWidth mismatches or unique paths were intentionally left inline.\n\n### Files changed\n\n- `web/src/components/ui/icons.tsx` — new shared icon library\n- `web/src/components/ui/index.ts` — barrel export for icons\n- `web/src/components/Layout/Layout.tsx` — project selector + all icons replaced (~510 → ~305 lines)\n- 18 other component files updated to import shared icons"},"created_at":"2026-06-18T19:17:38.712769Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.126 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-643465","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-18T19:17:41.492094Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.126 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-de5157","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Fix stale branch stats when git state changes independently","description":"The web server caches projected issues (including git branch stats from `applyBranchInference()`). The cache is only invalidated when `issues.db` changes on disk. But git state — new commits, new branches — changes independently of the database.\n\nWhen an agent is implementing code on a feature branch, the GUI shows stale (or zero) branch stats until the agent also writes an xpo comment or status update that touches `issues.db`.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd a `WatchGitRefs()` method that watches `.git/refs/heads/` (recursively) and `.git/packed-refs` via fsnotify. On any ref change: debounce 150ms, nil `cachedIssues`, broadcast SSE.\n\nUnlike `WatchDB()`, the git watcher must directly nil `cachedIssues` under write lock because `dbStale()` won't detect git changes. `cachedEvents` stays valid — only the derived issue projection needs recomputation.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":2,"assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","labels":["bug","backend"]},"created_at":"2026-06-20T09:08:04.059465438Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.181 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-de5157","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-20T09:08:10.882352021Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.181 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-de5157","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-eeddd10d-3ce0-48ad-b69b-e1fc0becf5c1","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded `WatchGitRefs()` — an fsnotify-based watcher for `.git/refs/heads/` (recursive) and `.git/packed-refs`. When any git ref changes (new commit, new/deleted branch, `git gc`), the cached issues are invalidated and an SSE update is broadcast so the GUI refreshes branch stats immediately.\n\n### Files changed\n\n- **`internal/server/watch_git.go`** (new) — `WatchGitRefs()` method on `*Server`. Watches refs/heads recursively (handles hierarchical branch names like `upe-0000c2/foo`), debounces 150ms, then nils `cachedIssues` under write lock and broadcasts SSE. Degrades gracefully if no `.git/` dir or fsnotify fails.\n- **`internal/server/server.go`** — wired `WatchGitRefs()` into `ServeOn()` after `WatchDB()`.\n- **`cmd/exponential/serve.go`** — wired both `WatchDB()` and `WatchGitRefs()` into headless serve mode (WatchDB was previously missing there too).\n- **`internal/server/watch_git_test.go`** (new) — 8 tests covering: nil SSEHub, no git dir, ref modify, new branch, branch delete, nested branch dirs, packed-refs, and SSE broadcast.\n\n### Rationale\n\nThe key difference from `WatchDB()`: the git watcher directly nils `cachedIssues` because `dbStale()` doesn't detect git changes. `cachedEvents` stays valid — only the derived projection (which calls `applyBranchInference()`) needs recomputation. This avoids re-reading `issues.db` on every git change."},"created_at":"2026-06-20T09:10:23.22513513Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.181 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-de5157","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-20T09:11:07.946822056Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.181 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-e282c2","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\n`xpo drive` is a supervisor loop that orchestrates AI coding agents to implement tickets autonomously. xpo is the state machine, not the brain — it decides which prompt to send next and parses structured JSON responses. No API key, no SDK, no model dependency. The agent is a black box that accepts text and returns text (or modifies files).\n\n## Core Design\n\nEach step is a subprocess call with a different prompt. xpo's only job is orchestrating the sequence and parsing the response to decide the next step. The key design surface is **structured output contracts**: each prompt ends with an output format directive, and xpo extracts JSON from stdout.\n\nJSON extraction must be **lenient** — agents routinely wrap JSON in markdown fences, emit preamble text, or append commentary. xpo finds the first `{...}` blob in stdout and parses that, rather than requiring strict JSON-only output.\n\n## Execution Loop\n\n### Step 1 — EVALUATE SPEC\n\n```\nprompt: \"Here's the issue spec: {spec}. Is it implementation-ready?\n         Respond ONLY in JSON: {ready: bool, revised_spec?: string}\"\nxpo:    parse → if !ready, update spec, re-evaluate\n        parse → if ready, proceed\n```\n\n### Step 2 — ASSEMBLE CONTEXT\n\n```\nprompt: \"Here's the spec: {spec}. Identify the files, modules,\n         and patterns relevant to implementation.\n         Respond ONLY in JSON: {context: string, files: string[]}\"\nxpo:    capture context blob for step 3\n```\n\n### Step 3 — IMPLEMENT\n\n```\nprompt: \"Implement this: {context_from_step_2}.\n         Test with: {test_cmd}. Work on branch {branch}.\"\nxpo:    agent modifies worktree, xpo computes git diff\n```\n\n### Step 4 — EVALUATE RESULT\n\n```\nprompt: \"Spec: {spec}. Diff: {diff}. Test output: {test_output}.\n         Did this meet the goal?\n         Respond ONLY in JSON: {done: bool, feedback?: string}\"\nxpo:    parse → if done, proceed to step 5\n        parse → if !done, goto step 3 with {feedback} appended\n```\n\nSteps 3–4 loop up to `max_retries` (default 3). If the coder can't satisfy the supervisor in 3 tries, the ticket is genuinely blocked and a human should look at it.\n\n### Step 5 — SUMMARIZE\n\n```\nprompt: \"Summarize what was done: {spec}, {final_diff}, {cycle_time}\"\nxpo:    print to terminal, attach as xpo comment, transition to DONE\n```\n\n## Supervisor / Coder Separation\n\nThe one thing worth codifying in config is whether the supervisor and coder are the same agent or different:\n\n```toml\n[drive]\nsupervisor = \"claude\"    # evaluation steps (1, 2, 4, 5)\ncoder = \"claude\"         # implementation step (3)\nmax_retries = 3\ntest_cmd = \"make test\"\n```\n\nSomeone could run Opus as supervisor and Sonnet as coder, or Claude as supervisor and Codex as coder. xpo doesn't care — it's just passing prompts and parsing responses. This is the differentiating feature.\n\n## Status Transitions\n\n`xpo drive` maps naturally to xpo's existing status model:\n\n- **Pick**: select a PLANNED ticket (or `--id` to target one), transition to DOING\n- **Success**: commit, transition to DONE, attach summary comment\n- **Retry exhausted**: transition to BLOCKED, attach failure details\n- Exit codes: 0 = done, 1 = blocked/failed, 2 = nothing to pick\n\n## Output\n\n```\nxpo drive\n● Picked: [xpo-4fa8dd] Description LWW with loser preserved (2 pts)\n✔ Spec ready\n✔ Context assembled (7 files)\n✔ Implementation attempt 1/3\n✔ Evaluation: passed\n✔ Summary attached\n✔ Ticket closed. (2 pts, 8m cycle)\n```\n\nOn retry:\n\n```\nxpo drive\n● Picked: [xpo-267e29] Status LWW state-machine guard (3 pts)\n✔ Spec ready\n✔ Context assembled (4 files)\n✘ Implementation attempt 1/3 — tests failed\n✔ Implementation attempt 2/3\n✔ Evaluation: passed\n✔ Ticket closed. (3 pts, 14m cycle)\n```\n\nOn failure:\n\n```\nxpo drive --id=xpo-abc123\n● Driving: [xpo-abc123] Complex migration (5 pts)\n✔ Spec ready\n✘ Implementation attempt 1/3 — tests failed\n✘ Implementation attempt 2/3 — tests failed\n✘ Implementation attempt 3/3 — tests failed\n⚠ Ticket blocked after 3 attempts. See xpo-abc123 for details.\n```\n\n## Flags\n\n- `--dry-run` — show which ticket would be picked without executing\n- `--filter=label` — scope to specific labels or epics\n- `--test-cmd=\"make test\"` — override test command\n- `--id=xpo-xxx` — skip selection, drive a specific ticket\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- ~300 lines of orchestration: a loop, prompt templates, a JSON extractor, and subprocess management\n- Agent invoked as subprocess (e.g. `claude -p`, `aider`, `codex`, or any command that accepts stdin/args and writes to stdout)\n- Agent identity set via `XPO_AGENT_IDENTITY`\n- Branch created via `xpo start`, merged via `xpo merge` on success\n- Continuous mode is the caller's concern: `while xpo drive; do :; done`"},"created_at":"2026-06-21T10:01:04.319075Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-e282c2","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\n`xpo drive` is a supervisor loop that orchestrates AI coding agents to implement tickets autonomously. xpo is the state machine, not the brain — it decides which prompt to send next and parses structured JSON responses. No API key, no SDK, no model dependency. The agent is a black box that accepts text and returns text (or modifies files).\n\n## Core Design\n\nEach step is a subprocess call with a different prompt. xpo's only job is orchestrating the sequence and parsing the response to decide the next step. The key design surface is **structured output contracts**: each prompt ends with an output format directive, and xpo extracts JSON from stdout.\n\nJSON extraction must be **lenient** — agents routinely wrap JSON in markdown fences, emit preamble text, or append commentary. xpo finds the first `{...}` blob in stdout and parses that, rather than requiring strict JSON-only output.\n\n## Execution Loop\n\n### Step 1 — EVALUATE SPEC\n\n```\nprompt: \"Here's the issue spec: {spec}. Is it implementation-ready?\n         Respond ONLY in JSON: {ready: bool, revised_spec?: string}\"\nxpo:    parse → if !ready, update spec, re-evaluate\n        parse → if ready, proceed\n```\n\n### Step 2 — ASSEMBLE CONTEXT\n\n```\nprompt: \"Here's the spec: {spec}. Examine the repository and identify\n         the files, modules, and patterns relevant to implementation.\n         Also determine the appropriate test command for this project.\n         Respond ONLY in JSON: {context: string, files: string[], test_cmd: string}\"\nxpo:    capture context blob and test_cmd for step 3\n```\n\nThe supervisor agent detects the best-suited test command by examining the repo (Makefile, package.json, go.mod, etc.) and returns it as part of the structured response. This keeps xpo dumb — no built-in heuristics for project type detection.\n\n**Test command precedence** (highest wins):\n1. `--test-cmd` flag (one-shot CLI override)\n2. `[drive] test_cmd` in project config (persistent override)\n3. Supervisor-suggested `test_cmd` from step 2 (agent-detected default)\n\nIf none of the three produce a value, xpo errors before starting the implementation step.\n\n### Step 3 — IMPLEMENT\n\n```\nprompt: \"Implement this: {context_from_step_2}.\n         Test with: {test_cmd}. Work on branch {branch}.\"\nxpo:    agent modifies worktree, xpo computes git diff\n```\n\n### Step 4 — EVALUATE RESULT\n\n```\nprompt: \"Spec: {spec}. Diff: {diff}. Test output: {test_output}.\n         Did this meet the goal?\n         Respond ONLY in JSON: {done: bool, feedback?: string}\"\nxpo:    parse → if done, proceed to step 5\n        parse → if !done, goto step 3 with {feedback} appended\n```\n\nSteps 3–4 loop up to `max_retries` (default 3). If the coder can't satisfy the supervisor in 3 tries, the ticket is genuinely blocked and a human should look at it.\n\n### Step 5 — SUMMARIZE\n\n```\nprompt: \"Summarize what was done: {spec}, {final_diff}, {cycle_time}\"\nxpo:    print to terminal, attach as xpo comment, transition to DONE\n```\n\n## Supervisor / Coder Separation\n\nThe one thing worth codifying in config is whether the supervisor and coder are the same agent or different:\n\n```toml\n[drive]\nsupervisor = \"claude\"    # evaluation steps (1, 2, 4, 5)\ncoder = \"claude\"         # implementation step (3)\nmax_retries = 3\n# test_cmd = \"make test\" # optional — if omitted, supervisor detects in step 2\n```\n\nSomeone could run Opus as supervisor and Sonnet as coder, or Claude as supervisor and Codex as coder. xpo doesn't care — it's just passing prompts and parsing responses. This is the differentiating feature.\n\n## Status Transitions\n\n`xpo drive` maps naturally to xpo's existing status model:\n\n- **Pick**: select a PLANNED ticket (or `--id` to target one), transition to DOING\n- **Success**: commit, transition to DONE, attach summary comment\n- **Retry exhausted**: transition to BLOCKED, attach failure details\n- Exit codes: 0 = done, 1 = blocked/failed, 2 = nothing to pick\n\n## Output\n\n```\nxpo drive\n● Picked: [xpo-4fa8dd] Description LWW with loser preserved (2 pts)\n✔ Spec ready\n✔ Context assembled (7 files, test: make test)\n✔ Implementation attempt 1/3\n✔ Evaluation: passed\n✔ Summary attached\n✔ Ticket closed. (2 pts, 8m cycle)\n```\n\nOn retry:\n\n```\nxpo drive\n● Picked: [xpo-267e29] Status LWW state-machine guard (3 pts)\n✔ Spec ready\n✔ Context assembled (4 files, test: go test ./...)\n✘ Implementation attempt 1/3 — tests failed\n✔ Implementation attempt 2/3\n✔ Evaluation: passed\n✔ Ticket closed. (3 pts, 14m cycle)\n```\n\nOn failure:\n\n```\nxpo drive --id=xpo-abc123\n● Driving: [xpo-abc123] Complex migration (5 pts)\n✔ Spec ready\n✘ Implementation attempt 1/3 — tests failed\n✘ Implementation attempt 2/3 — tests failed\n✘ Implementation attempt 3/3 — tests failed\n⚠ Ticket blocked after 3 attempts. See xpo-abc123 for details.\n```\n\n## Flags\n\n- `--dry-run` — show which ticket would be picked without executing\n- `--filter=label` — scope to specific labels or epics\n- `--test-cmd=\"make test\"` — override test command (takes precedence over config and agent detection)\n- `--id=xpo-xxx` — skip selection, drive a specific ticket\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- ~300 lines of orchestration: a loop, prompt templates, a JSON extractor, and subprocess management\n- Agent invoked as subprocess (e.g. `claude -p`, `aider`, `codex`, or any command that accepts stdin/args and writes to stdout)\n- Agent identity set via `XPO_AGENT_IDENTITY`\n- Branch created via `xpo start`, merged via `xpo merge` on success\n- Continuous mode is the caller's concern: `while xpo drive; do :; done`"},"created_at":"2026-06-21T10:07:12.700699Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
