{"id":"xpo-e282c2","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-dc047c11-68e8-4be0-a71b-1175b4f9eea9","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented `xpo drive` — the autonomous agent execution loop.\n\n### Files changed\n\n- `internal/config/config.go` — added `DriveConfig` struct with `supervisor`, `coder`, `max_retries`, `test_cmd` fields; defaults set in `LoadConfig()`\n- `internal/exponential/drive.go` — core orchestration: 5-step supervisor loop (evaluate spec, assemble context, implement, evaluate result, summarize), lenient JSON extraction, subprocess management for supervisor/coder agents, issue picking with priority sort and blocker filtering\n- `cmd/exponential/drive.go` — cobra command with `--id`, `--filter`, `--test-cmd`, `--dry-run`, `--max-retries`, `--supervisor`, `--coder` flags\n- `internal/exponential/branches_test.go` — fixed 3 failing git tests by passing `-c safe.bareRepository=all` in the `runGit` test helper\n\n### Design decisions\n\n- **Agent interface**: agents are invoked as subprocesses. For `claude`, uses `claude -p --dangerously-skip-permissions {prompt}`. Other agents receive `{agent} {prompt}` — simple and extensible.\n- **JSON extraction**: lenient — finds the first `{...}` blob in stdout rather than requiring strict JSON-only output, handling markdown fences and preamble text.\n- **Test command precedence**: CLI flag \u003e config \u003e supervisor-detected (step 2 JSON response).\n- **Issue picking**: selects PLANNED issues, filters out those with unresolved blockers, sorts by priority (desc) then estimate (asc for tractability).\n- **Status transitions**: PLANNED -\u003e DOING on pick, DONE on success, BLOCKED if retries exhausted.\n- **Merge strategy**: squash merge with branch deletion on success."},"created_at":"2026-06-21T10:23:57.972541Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-b6ccab","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"`xpo drive` auto-recovery: dispatch fix-it agent on failure instead of crashing","description":"## Summary\n\nWhen `xpo drive` hits an unexpected failure (merge conflict, dirty worktree, agent crash, test setup issue), it should dispatch a recovery agent to try to fix the problem before giving up. Currently it crashes out with a recovery hint and waits for human intervention.\n\n## Design\n\nWrap each phase in a recovery loop:\n\n1. Try phase\n2. If fails with a fixable error, dispatch fix-it agent: \"This happened: {error}. The state is: {context}. Fix it.\"\n3. Retry phase\n4. If fix-it also fails, block ticket with full context and move on\n\n### Fixable vs. terminal errors\n\n**Fixable** (dispatch agent): merge conflicts, dirty worktree, test setup issues, agent output parse failures, spec revision loops\n\n**Terminal** (bail immediately): API key expired, disk full, agent binary missing, timeout exceeded\n\n### Flag\n\n`--no-recovery` suspends auto-recovery and falls back to current behavior (stop on first failure with recovery hint). Useful for debugging or when the user wants to inspect failures manually.\n\n### User expectation\n\n\"I go to bed, you work.\" The system should be resilient enough that a transient failure at 2am doesn't mean 6 hours of idle time. The current `recoverHint` call sites become candidates for fix-it dispatch.","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":5,"dependencies":[{"source_id":"xpo-b6ccab","target_id":"xpo-e282c2","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-06-21T12:48:13.758327Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-e282c2","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-10d3f9ba-26b3-44c8-8dcc-0423e07195a5","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented `xpo drive` — the autonomous agent execution loop.\n\n### Architecture\n\n- **`AgentExecutor` interface** (`agent.go`) with `ClaudeExecutor` (uses `--output-format json` for structured output + token/cost tracking) and `GenericExecutor` (plain subprocess fallback). Enables pluggable agents via config or CLI flags.\n- **Core orchestration** (`drive.go`) — 5-step supervisor loop: evaluate spec → plan implementation → implement → test + review → summarize. Structured JSON output contracts with lenient extraction.\n- **CLI command** (`cmd/exponential/drive.go`) with flags: `--id`, `--filter`, `--dry-run`, `--no-merge`, `--resume`, `--max-retries`, `--supervisor`, `--coder`, `--test-cmd`.\n- **Config** (`DriveConfig`) — `supervisor`, `coder`, `max_retries`, `test_cmd`, `timeout` in `[drive]` section.\n\n### Key behaviors\n\n- **Issue picking**: priority-aware (1=Urgent first), excludes epics with children, filters unresolved blockers, respects board sort order with `CreatedAt` tiebreaker\n- **Auto-assign sort order**: `AddIssue` now generates fractional-index sort keys when none provided (fixes wonky board ordering for MCP/CLI-created issues)\n- **Resume support**: `--resume` finds DOING issues; bare `xpo drive` auto-picks a single DOING issue before falling back to PLANNED\n- **Recovery hints**: errors after work starts include issue ID, branch name, and `xpo drive --resume` / discard commands\n- **Phase-based output**: Pre-flight → Preparation → Implementation → Testing → Summary → Cleanup, each with spinner, result lines, and phase timing\n- **Token tracking**: Claude executor parses `total_cost_usd`, input tokens (including cache), output tokens\n- **Agent identity**: attributed to the agent (e.g. `claude \u003cagent@hostname\u003e`) not the user\n- **Clean merge**: comment + DONE transition committed on feature branch before squash merge\n\n### Also fixed\n\n- `runGit` test helper passes `-c safe.bareRepository=all` (fixes 3 pre-existing test failures)\n- `WithGitLock` — `git.lock` added to `.gitignore` via `xpo init`\n- Follow-up filed: xpo-b6ccab (auto-recovery on failure)"},"created_at":"2026-06-21T12:48:35.09405Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
