{"id":"xpo-3e5244","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-faa0b677-91a8-4e6b-9612-88f95a67ef7d","text":"## Summary\n\nReplaced the drive summary step with a structured walkthrough.\n\n### Changes\n\n- `buildSummaryPrompt` → `buildWalkthroughPrompt` in `drive.go` — prompts for 5 sections: Rationale, Changes (file-by-file), Decisions, How to verify, Risks\n- \"Summary\" phase renamed to \"Walkthrough\" in terminal output\n- `lastTestOutput` tracked through the implementation loop so the walkthrough prompt has test context\n- Issue comment header changed from \"xpo drive — completed\" to \"xpo drive — walkthrough\"\n- Walkthrough prompt receives spec, diff, test command, and last test output"},"created_at":"2026-06-21T15:35:31.086157Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-3e5244","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-21T15:35:35.324206Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-d35639","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Cannot move epic from PLANNED to BACKLOG while children are PLANNED","description":"## Problem\n\nMoving a PLANNED epic back to BACKLOG requires manually moving each sub-issue to BACKLOG first. The forward direction works (auto-progress moves children BACKLOG→PLANNED when parent moves to PLANNED), but there's no reverse automation.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nMoving an epic backward (e.g. PLANNED→BACKLOG) should either:\n1. Auto-regress children to match (symmetric with auto-progress), or\n2. Allow the parent to move independently without requiring children to be in a lower status first\n\n## Context\n\nThe auto-progress automation in `update.go` only handles forward transitions. Need to investigate whether the web UI is also blocking this or if it's purely a backend constraint.","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":2,"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-06-21T15:58:29.996876Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-d35639","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## Problem\n\nTwo related issues with epic status and child auto-progression:\n\n### 1. UI/state mismatch\nThe web UI displays an epic as PLANNED (inferred from its children being PLANNED), but the stored status is BACKLOG. This causes `xpo show` and `xpo drive` to see a different status than what the user sees in the browser. Drive skips the issue because it's BACKLOG, even though the board shows it in the PLANNED column.\n\n### 2. No reverse auto-progression\nMoving a PLANNED epic back to BACKLOG requires manually moving each sub-issue to BACKLOG first. The forward direction works (auto-progress moves children BACKLOG→PLANNED when parent moves to PLANNED), but there's no reverse automation.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nEither:\n1. The web UI should not display an inferred status that differs from the stored status — or the stored status should be updated to match, OR\n2. Status inference should be consistent across web UI, CLI (`show`, `list`), and drive pick logic\n\nFor reverse progression: moving an epic backward should either auto-regress children or allow the parent to move independently."},"created_at":"2026-06-21T16:10:34.916801Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-492476","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Problem\n\nWhen an epic's children have a different status than the epic itself (e.g. epic is BACKLOG but children are PLANNED), the current inferred status display is confusing. The epic shows as PLANNED in the board but `xpo show` says BACKLOG. Users can't distinguish inferred from explicit status.\n\n## Prior art\n\nThe UI renders the parent epic in each status column where its children exist — the epic appears multiple times with reduced opacity on the \"borrowed\" instances. This avoids inferred status entirely.\n\n## Options to explore\n\n1. **multi-rendering** — show the epic in each column where its children live, faded in non-native columns\n2. **No inference** — show epics at their actual status only; children in different columns stand on their own\n3. **Visual distinction** — some icon/badge treatment that clearly communicates \"inferred\" without being confused with another status\n\n## Context\n\nThe inferred DOING status (dashed half-circle) works because it's visually distinct from all other states. Inferred PLANNED is harder because it collides with BACKLOG (dashed) or looks like regular PLANNED (solid). This needs a design decision, not a quick fix.","estimate":3,"labels":["improvement"],"status":"BACKLOG","title":"Design: how to display epics with children in different status groups"},"created_at":"2026-06-21T16:16:31.246087Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-d35639","type":"DELETE","payload":{},"created_at":"2026-06-21T16:17:15.677401Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-9253d8","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Context\n\nThe current automation system (4 config flags + read-time inference) creates confusing UI/state mismatches. Epics show inferred statuses that don't match stored state, causing problems for CLI, drive, and user expectations.\n\n## New model\n\nAllow mixed statuses by default. Software dev is messy — a BACKLOG epic with DOING children is normal, not a bug.\n\n### 1. Ghost parent rendering (web UI)\n\nShow the epic at its actual stored status. In any status column where its children live but the epic doesn't, render a faded \"ghost\" card linking to the real epic. No inference, no phantom status.\n\n### 2. First-start trigger (opt-in config)\n\nOne-way event hook:\n- IF any child transitions out of BACKLOG/PLANNED\n- AND the parent is still in BACKLOG/PLANNED\n- THEN move the parent to DOING\n\nWrite-time, real event, auditable.\n\n### 3. Last-completed trigger (opt-in config)\n\nOne-way event hook:\n- IF the last child transitions to DONE\n- AND the parent is In Progress\n- THEN move the parent to DONE\n\nWrite-time, real event, auditable. Replaces the current read-time `auto_complete_parent` inference.\n\n### 4. \"Move children?\" prompt (web UI)\n\nWhen the user changes a parent's status via drag-drop or status picker, show a confirmation: \"Also move children to {status}?\" User decides per-action. Not automated, not configurable — just a UX affordance.\n\n### 5. Keep branch inference for DOING\n\nThe only read-time inference that stays. A local git branch matching an issue ID is a real signal that can't be captured as a write-time event. The dashed half-circle icon already communicates this.\n\n### What gets removed\n\n- `auto_progress_parent` (read-time inference in projection.go)\n- `auto_progress_sub_issues` (write-time cascade in update.go)\n- `auto_complete_parent` (read-time inference in projection.go — replaced by last-completed trigger)\n- `auto_close_sub_issues` (write-time cascade — replaced by \"move children?\" prompt)\n- `InferredStatus` flag on issues (except for branch inference)\n\n### Config\n\n```yaml\nautomations:\n  first_start: true    # any child starts → parent starts\n  last_completed: true # last child done → parent done\n```\n\nReplaces the current 4-flag config. Migration should map old flags to new ones where possible.","labels":["epic"],"status":"BACKLOG","title":"Rework status automation: ghost parents, first-start/last-completed triggers"},"created_at":"2026-06-21T16:44:59.04938Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-def976","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Render faded \"ghost\" copies of parent issues in status columns where their children live but the parent doesn't. Ghost cards are non-draggable, show the epic title + child count, and link to the real issue. No status inference — the parent's stored status is authoritative.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"xpo-9253d8","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Ghost parent rendering in board UI"},"created_at":"2026-06-21T16:45:06.309638Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-a113aa","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Opt-in write-time automation: when any child transitions out of BACKLOG/PLANNED and the parent is still in BACKLOG/PLANNED, emit a real UPDATE event moving the parent to DOING. Configurable via `automations.first_start`.","estimate":2,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"xpo-9253d8","status":"BACKLOG","title":"First-start trigger: parent auto-starts when any child starts"},"created_at":"2026-06-21T16:45:08.805344Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-33234e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Opt-in write-time automation: when the last child transitions to DONE and the parent is in DOING, emit a real UPDATE event moving the parent to DONE. Replaces the current read-time `auto_complete_parent` inference. Configurable via `automations.last_completed`.","estimate":2,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"xpo-9253d8","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Last-completed trigger: parent auto-closes when last child is done"},"created_at":"2026-06-21T16:45:10.695432Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-f2fcb8","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"When a user changes a parent's status via drag-drop or status picker in the web UI, show a confirmation dialog: \"Also move N children to {status}?\" User decides per-action. Not automated, not configurable — just a UX affordance. Only offered when children exist and would be affected.","estimate":3,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"xpo-9253d8","status":"BACKLOG","title":"\"Move children?\" prompt on parent status change"},"created_at":"2026-06-21T16:45:12.701607Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-33e051","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Remove `auto_progress_parent`, `auto_progress_sub_issues`, `auto_complete_parent`, `auto_close_sub_issues` config flags and their implementations. Remove `InferredStatus` from projection (except branch inference for DOING). Add config migration mapping old flags to new `first_start`/`last_completed`.","estimate":3,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"xpo-9253d8","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Remove old automation flags and read-time inference"},"created_at":"2026-06-21T16:45:14.850043Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
