{"id":"xpo-3cc045","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"MCP list tool: rename `statuses` to `status`, accept string or array","description":"The `statuses` parameter name on the MCP `list` tool is unnatural — AI agents consistently pass `status` (singular) instead, causing validation errors. Renamed to `status` with a `flexStrings` type that accepts either a single string or an array via custom JSON unmarshaling.","status":"DONE","estimate":1,"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-06-21T16:53:46.052743Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-3cc045","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-7bc390d4-2d46-42fc-98a2-fb93cecf79ac","text":"## Summary\n\nRenamed `statuses` to `status` in `listIn` struct in `tools.go`. Added `flexStrings` type with custom `UnmarshalJSON` that accepts either `\"PLANNED\"` or `[\"PLANNED\", \"DOING\"]`. Updated the call site to cast `flexStrings` to `[]string`."},"created_at":"2026-06-21T16:53:51.509163Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-bbd43a","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-21T16:55:52.772963Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-bbd43a","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-4f2cdb6d-030c-40db-96cb-74801b71b680","text":"## Summary\n\nTwo guards against self-referencing parent_id:\n\n- **Backend**: `update.go` rejects `parent_id == id` with a clear error before processing the update event\n- **Frontend**: `Backlog.tsx` skips the nest action when `nestTarget === droppedId` (aborted drag-drop on same issue)"},"created_at":"2026-06-21T16:56:59.103291Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
