{"id":"xpo-def976","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-0874fe9b-1d55-4531-929b-b68ff0254d64","text":"## Summary\n\nGhost parent rendering was already implemented in `useBacklogRows.ts` and `Backlog.tsx` — it just wasn't exercised because the old automation system inferred parent statuses, making ghosts unnecessary.\n\nWith the automation rework (xpo-33e051), ghost parents now appear naturally on filtered tabs (Active, Backlog) when a parent's children are in a status group the parent isn't in.\n\n### Behavior\n- **\"All\" tab**: breadcrumb style (parent title shown inline) — no ghosts since all groups are visible\n- **Filtered tabs**: ghost parent at 50% opacity, not draggable, all interactions work (context menu, status/label/estimate pickers update the real issue), children auto-expanded under the ghost\n- Ghost shows the parent's actual status icon (e.g. PLANNED icon in In Progress group)\n\nNo code changes needed — the feature was unblocked by removing read-time inference."},"created_at":"2026-06-21T17:44:41.532845Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
