{"id":"xpo-f2fcb8","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-21T17:45:20.101641Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-f2fcb8","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-d2c897e4-1121-4211-a982-7607f91e8eb6","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented \"Update sub-issues?\" prompt when changing a parent's status via the status picker in the Backlog view.\n\n### Behavior\n- Clicking a parent's status icon and selecting a new status triggers a confirmation dialog if the issue has sub-issues in a different status\n- Dialog shows: title (\"Update sub-issues?\"), description with issue name and target status icon, and a rich table of affected sub-issues (status, title, labels, estimate)\n- Three options: **Abort** (revert, far left), **Just this issue** (parent only), **Update all** (parent + sub-issues)\n- Drag-drop unchanged — it already moves parent + same-status children together via `getDragGroup`\n\n### Also\n- Modal title font-size increased to 1rem globally for better heading hierarchy\n- Updated `.xpo/config.yaml` to new automation fields"},"created_at":"2026-06-21T18:22:03.27725Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-f2fcb8","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-21T18:22:03.55744Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-9253d8","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-21T18:24:07.374083Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-f48f47","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Velocity double-counts points from parent issues","description":"## Problem\n\n`computePulseMetrics()` in `internal/server/metrics.go` iterates over **all** issues and sums story points for any issue with a DONE status event in the time window. When the `last_completed` automation auto-closes a parent issue, that parent gets a real `UPDATE` event with `status: DONE`, so `latestStatusTimestamps()` returns a non-nil `doneAt` for it.\n\nThe velocity loop then counts the parent's points **on top of** all its children's points — classic double-counting. This inflates `last_7d_points`, `prior_7d_points`, weekly buckets, and daily buckets.\n\n## Fix\n\nBuild a set of parent IDs before the main loop. Skip parent issues when accumulating velocity, throughput, and bucket counts — only leaf issues should contribute points.","status":"DOING","sort_order":"a0","assignee":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-06-21T18:36:07.389921Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-f48f47","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-a175b297-d9ac-4380-9b18-27f3f1ea8a72","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed velocity double-counting caused by parent issues (epics) being included in point totals alongside their children.\n\n**Root cause:** `computePulseMetrics()` in `internal/server/metrics.go` iterated over all issues and summed story points for any issue with a DONE event in the time window. When the `last_completed` automation auto-closed a parent, that parent got a real status event, so its points were counted on top of all its children's points.\n\n**Fix:** Added a `parentIDs` set built before the main loop (any issue referenced as a `ParentID` by another issue). The velocity, throughput, and bucket accumulation now skips parent issues — only leaf issues contribute points. The trend `Completed` counter still counts parents since it tracks issue count, not points.\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `internal/server/metrics.go` — added parent-ID set, guarded velocity/throughput/bucket accumulation with `!isParent`\n- `internal/server/metrics_test.go` — added `TestMetrics_VelocityExcludesParents` covering an epic with two children (5 + 8 = 13 pts), verifying the parent's points are excluded from both velocity and throughput"},"created_at":"2026-06-21T18:37:16.012794Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-f48f47","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-21T18:38:06.082581Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-f48f47","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-8e924cb3-958d-409d-9638-81c13936317c","text":"## Follow-up: calendar-week velocity windows\n\nSwitched velocity/throughput comparison from a rolling 7-day window to completed calendar weeks (Mon–Sun).\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `internal/server/metrics.go` — replaced `last7dStart`/`prior7dStart` rolling offsets with `thisWeekStart`/`lastWeekStart`/`priorWeekStart` calendar-week boundaries via `startOfWeek()`\n- `internal/server/metrics_test.go` — updated `TestMetrics_Throughput`, `TestMetrics_Velocity`, and `TestMetrics_VelocityExcludesParents` to use fixed dates aligned to calendar weeks; added `TestMetrics_VelocityExcludesCurrentWeek`\n- `web/src/components/Dashboard/Dashboard.tsx` — label changed from \"pts last 7d\" to \"pts last week\"\n\n**Rationale:** Rolling windows straddle work weeks mid-week, making the delta noisy. Calendar weeks give apples-to-apples comparisons. Current (partial) week still appears in the daily chart and weekly buckets but doesn't affect the headline number or delta."},"created_at":"2026-06-21T19:26:38.178454Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-f48f47","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-21T19:27:25.799729Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.185 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
