{"id":"xpo-599117","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-29T07:04:15.555516917Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.193 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-599117","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-5c19f2f3-f267-406e-88a2-d2235c14ba92","text":"## Summary\n\nRenamed `--color-base` to `--color-chrome` in the `@theme` block (`web/src/index.css`) and updated the single usage in `web/src/components/Layout/Layout.tsx`.\n\n## Root cause\n\nTailwind v4 resolves the `text-base` utility ambiguously when both `--text-base` (font-size) and `--color-base` (color) exist in `@theme`. It picked the color interpretation, generating `color: var(--color-base)` (`#070707`, near-black) instead of the expected `font-size: var(--text-base)`. This overrode the intended `text-[var(--color-text-primary)]` color on the comment textarea (and any other element using both `text-base` and a `text-[...]` color utility) due to CSS source order.\n\n## Fix\n\nRenaming `--color-base` → `--color-chrome` eliminates the collision. `text-base` now correctly resolves to `font-size` + `line-height`, and the explicit color utility works as intended.\n\n## Files changed\n\n- `web/src/index.css` — renamed `--color-base` → `--color-chrome`\n- `web/src/components/Layout/Layout.tsx` — updated `bg-[var(--color-base)]` → `bg-[var(--color-chrome)]`"},"created_at":"2026-06-29T07:08:39.975898873Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.193 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-599117","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-bb14d3fc-d176-4f76-8eb5-2938d9a45f71","text":"## Update\n\nAdded global focus-visible styles for text inputs and textareas, and a `focus-within` border highlight on the comment textarea container.\n\n### Additional changes\n\n- `web/src/index.css` — added `@layer base` rule giving textareas and text inputs a subtle `box-shadow` ring (`--color-border-focus`) on `focus-visible`\n- `web/src/components/IssueDetail/ActivityTimeline.tsx` — comment container gets `focus-within:border-[var(--color-border-focus)]`; textarea gets `focus-visible:shadow-none` to suppress the global ring (container handles it)"},"created_at":"2026-06-29T07:15:44.59198663Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.193 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-599117","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-29T07:15:47.890637828Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.193 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-01fc4c","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-29T07:17:31.997498731Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.193 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-01fc4c","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-d655ff20-8756-44e1-81eb-4221d470e27b","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed the new issue dialog to focus the title input instead of the close button on open, and fixed ESC key leaking through to the background view.\n\n### Changes\n\n- `web/src/components/ui/Modal.tsx` — initial focus logic now checks if React's `autoFocus` already placed focus inside the dialog before overriding; added `e.stopPropagation()` on ESC to prevent the event from reaching background keydown listeners\n- `web/src/index.css` — removed overly broad global focus-visible rule that was causing regressions on inline inputs; kept targeted `focus-within` on the comment textarea container\n- `web/src/components/IssueDetail/ActivityTimeline.tsx` — removed `focus-visible:shadow-none` that was only needed to counteract the now-removed global rule\n\n### Root cause\n\nThe Modal's `useEffect` used `requestAnimationFrame` to focus the first focusable element (the close button), overriding React's `autoFocus` on the title input. The ESC handler called `onClose()` without `stopPropagation()`, so the event also triggered the IssueDetail's keydown listener."},"created_at":"2026-06-29T07:22:26.529650339Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.193 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-01fc4c","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-29T07:22:30.681140988Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.193 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
