{"id":"xpo-c5b991","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-4b53f454-250b-4d3e-9eb9-30fca6993c99","text":"## Summary\n\nParent issue collapse/expand state is now persisted to localStorage and shared across all backlog tabs.\n\n### Approach\n\nReplaced the ephemeral `expandedNodes` state with a localStorage-backed mechanism:\n\n- `toggleNode` writes collapsed IDs directly to localStorage under key `exponential-backlog-nodes-collapsed`, then bumps a counter to trigger recomputation\n- `expandedNodes` is derived via `useMemo` that reads localStorage on every recomputation — starts with all parents expanded, then removes the collapsed set\n- New parents automatically appear expanded since only explicitly collapsed IDs are stored\n\n### Files changed\n\n- `web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx` — replaced `expandedNodes` state with `nodeToggleCount` counter; `expandedNodes` derived via `useMemo` reading directly from localStorage; `toggleNode` writes to localStorage and bumps counter"},"created_at":"2026-06-29T14:02:00.920072083Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.193 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
