{"id":"xpo-ac11d8","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"MCP tool operations don't appear in Inbox notifications","description":"## Problem\n\nEvents created by MCP tool operations (comment, status update, etc.) never appear in the Inbox notification feed. Two root causes:\n\n### 1. Identity collision — self-exclusion filter\n\n`BuildInbox` in `internal/exponential/inbox.go:73` skips events where `createdBy` matches the current user:\n\n```go\nif identityMatches(evt.CreatedBy, me) {\n    continue // don't notify about your own actions\n}\n```\n\nThe MCP server's `resolveAgentIdentity` (`internal/mcpserver/identity.go:24`) falls back to the user's git config identity when `XPO_AGENT_IDENTITY` is not set and no MCP `clientInfo` is available. This means agent-generated events look like self-actions and are silently filtered out.\n\n### 2. No SSE broadcast from MCP handlers\n\nMCP tool handlers (`internal/mcpserver/tools.go`) write events to `issues.db` via `exponential.Client` → `LocalTransport` → `storage.AppendEvent`, but never call `broadcastEvent()`. The only real-time signal comes from the `WatchDB` filesystem watcher (`internal/server/watch.go`), which fires a generic `UPDATE` SSE event with no issue ID or event type — a blunt \"refresh everything\" signal rather than a typed notification.\n\nIn contrast, the web UI REST handlers (`handleDraft` in `handlers.go`) call `broadcastEvent()` explicitly after each write, producing typed SSE events.\n\n## Fix\n\n### Identity\n- Ensure MCP tools always write with a distinct agent identity, per the CLAUDE.md convention: `Claude Code \u003cagent@host.local\u003e`\n- `resolveAgentIdentity` should prefer MCP `clientInfo` or `XPO_AGENT_IDENTITY` and only fall back to git identity as a last resort, with a distinguishing suffix (e.g. appending `(agent)`)\n\n### SSE\n- Have MCP tool handlers call `broadcastEvent()` after writing, or refactor the event-write path so that `storage.AppendEvent` triggers SSE broadcast automatically regardless of caller\n\n## Key files\n\n- `internal/exponential/inbox.go` — `BuildInbox`, self-exclusion logic\n- `internal/mcpserver/identity.go` — `resolveAgentIdentity`\n- `internal/mcpserver/tools.go` — MCP tool handlers (no SSE calls)\n- `internal/server/handlers.go` — `handleDraft` (calls `broadcastEvent`)\n- `internal/server/watch.go` — `WatchDB` filesystem watcher","status":"PLANNED","priority":2,"sort_order":"b4U","dependencies":[{"source_id":"xpo-ac11d8","target_id":"xpo-11dfd1","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug","WebApp"]},"created_at":"2026-06-30T09:36:02.037745013Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.195 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-ac11d8","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"title":"Inbox self-exclusion filter hides agent-on-behalf-of-user events","description":"## Problem\n\n`BuildInbox` in `internal/exponential/inbox.go:73` unconditionally skips events where `createdBy` matches the current user:\n\n```go\nif identityMatches(evt.CreatedBy, me) {\n    continue // don't notify about your own actions\n}\n```\n\nThis makes sense for direct user actions (you don't need a notification for something you just did in the UI). But it breaks when an agent acts on your behalf — the agent writes events under your identity (correctly, since it's your work), but then the inbox hides them as \"self-actions.\"\n\nThe secondary issue is that MCP tool handlers don't call `broadcastEvent()` for SSE, so even if the filter were fixed, there's no real-time push — only the filesystem watcher's generic refresh signal.\n\n## Fix\n\nThe self-exclusion rule needs a way to distinguish \"user did this interactively\" from \"something did this on the user's behalf.\" Options:\n\n1. **Source channel marker** — events could carry a `source` field (e.g. `web`, `cli`, `mcp`, `api`) so the inbox filter can exclude only `web`-originated self-events\n2. **Time-based heuristic** — don't exclude self-events older than N seconds (if you did it yourself, you'd see it within seconds; agent work happens over minutes)\n3. **Opt-in self-notifications** — user setting to disable the self-exclusion filter entirely\n\nOption 1 is the cleanest since it preserves the useful \"don't notify me about what I just clicked\" behavior while surfacing agent work.\n\nThe SSE gap (`internal/mcpserver/tools.go` never calls `broadcastEvent()`) should also be addressed — either by having MCP handlers broadcast, or by refactoring so `storage.AppendEvent` triggers SSE automatically.\n\n## Key files\n\n- `internal/exponential/inbox.go` — `BuildInbox`, self-exclusion logic\n- `internal/mcpserver/tools.go` — MCP tool handlers (no SSE calls)\n- `internal/server/handlers.go` — `handleDraft` (calls `broadcastEvent`)\n- `internal/server/watch.go` — `WatchDB` filesystem watcher\n- `internal/model/types.go` — `Event` struct (would need `Source` field for option 1)"},"created_at":"2026-06-30T09:41:36.204232119Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.195 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-ac11d8","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-30T09:49:43.052244783Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.195 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-ac11d8","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-3847122c-de22-447f-a6c9-2b5eede816ae","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed MCP tool operations not appearing in Inbox notifications. Two root causes addressed:\n\n### Source channel marker on events\n- Added `Source` field to `model.Event` (`json:\"source,omitempty\"`) — backward-compatible with existing event log\n- `LocalTransport.appendEvent()` stamps `Source` on every event before writing\n- Web UI REST handler (`handleDraft`) sets `Source: \"web\"`\n- MCP tool handlers set `Source: \"mcp\"` via `Client.Source`\n- CLI/legacy events default to `\"\"` (empty)\n\n### Inbox self-exclusion fix\n- `BuildInbox` now only self-excludes when `evt.Source != \"mcp\"` — interactive web actions are still hidden (you don't need a notification for what you just clicked), but agent-on-behalf-of-user events always surface\n\n### SSE broadcast from MCP handlers\n- Added `onEvent` callback to MCP `toolset`, wired to `Server.BroadcastEvent`\n- All mutating MCP tool handlers (`add`, `update`, `comment`, `link`, `start`, `merge`) call `t.broadcast()` after successful writes\n- `RegisterTools` accepts the callback; `serve.go` wires it to the server's SSE hub\n\n### Files changed\n- `internal/model/types.go` — `Event.Source` field\n- `internal/exponential/client.go` — `Client.Source`, synced to transport\n- `internal/exponential/local_transport.go` — `LocalTransport.Source`, stamped in `appendEvent`\n- `internal/exponential/inbox.go` — `BuildInbox` self-exclusion now respects source\n- `internal/mcpserver/server.go` — `toolset.onEvent`, `broadcast()`, updated `RegisterTools` signature\n- `internal/mcpserver/tools.go` — broadcast calls in all mutating handlers\n- `internal/server/server.go` — exported `BroadcastEvent`\n- `internal/server/handlers.go` — `client.Source = \"web\"`\n- `cmd/exponential/serve.go` — wired `srv.BroadcastEvent` into MCP registration\n- `internal/mcpserver/tools_test.go` — updated `RegisterTools` call sites"},"created_at":"2026-06-30T10:02:53.115834629Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.196 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","source":"mcp"}
