{"id":"xpo-ac11d8","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-7aa0eabd-69ef-4c4e-89d5-8d99dfd581eb","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented dual-identity attribution for MCP events and fixed Inbox visibility.\n\n### Event model\n- `model.Event` — new `OnBehalfOf` field recording the principal (user) the actor (agent) works for\n- `LocalTransport.appendEvent()` stamps both `Source` and `OnBehalfOf` on every event\n\n### MCP identity\n- `clientFor` — `UserOverride` is always the agent identity (from `resolveAgentIdentity`); `OnBehalfOf` is the authenticated HTTP user or git config user\n- Events now carry both: `created_by: \"claude-code/2.1.196 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e\"`, `on_behalf_of: \"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e\"`\n\n### Inbox\n- `BuildInbox` self-exclusion uses the principal (`OnBehalfOf` fallback to `CreatedBy`), skips only non-mcp self-actions\n- Participation check considers `OnBehalfOf` — if your agent touched an issue, you participate\n- `InboxItem` includes `on_behalf_of` in API response\n\n### Frontend\n- Change summary banner shows agent identity with \"(You)\" when `on_behalf_of` matches current user, e.g. \"claude-code/2.1.196 (You) · Status completed · 1 new comment\""},"created_at":"2026-06-30T10:23:12.570179734Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.196 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","source":"mcp"}
