{"id":"xpo-797c59","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"The `.xpo/git.lock` file is a runtime lockfile that should never be tracked by git. When it exists as an untracked file, it causes `xpo merge` to fail with \"working tree has uncommitted changes.\"\n\n`xpo doctor` (or `xpo init`) should ensure `.xpo/.gitignore` exists and contains `git.lock`. Currently this has to be done manually.","labels":["improvement","CLI"],"sort_order":"aK","status":"BACKLOG","title":"xpo doctor should create .xpo/.gitignore with git.lock"},"created_at":"2026-06-30T11:00:04.121739274Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.196 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-0d4ca2","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"relates_to","source_id":"xpo-0d4ca2","target_id":"xpo-ac11d8"}],"description":"When merging an issue via `xpo merge`, the DONE status transition event isn't written before the merge commit. This means the activity timeline, inbox notifications, and change summary banner never show the \"completed\" event — they only see the MERGE event.\n\nThe merge flow should record the DONE status transition as a separate event before the merge, so the full lifecycle (DOING → DONE → MERGE) is captured in the event log and surfaces correctly in notifications.","labels":["bug","Backend"],"sort_order":"aL","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Merge flow doesn't record DONE transition before merging"},"created_at":"2026-06-30T11:00:11.666843734Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.196 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-797c59","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-06-30T11:01:56.317926107Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
