{"id":"xpo-e01041","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-06-30T11:11:22.129215023Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-e01041","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"Change `xpo drive` so the issue ID is accepted as an optional positional argument instead of requiring the `--id` flag.\n\n## Current behavior\n\n`xpo drive --id \u003cID\u003e` drives a specific issue; `xpo drive` (no flag) auto-picks a PLANNED issue.\n\n## Desired behavior\n\n- `xpo drive \u003cID\u003e` — drives the specified issue (ID as first positional arg).\n- `xpo drive` — auto-picks a PLANNED issue (unchanged).\n- Remove the `--id` flag entirely.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. `cmd/exponential/drive.go`: change the cobra command to accept an optional positional arg (`Args: cobra.MaximumNArgs(1)`), read `args[0]` when present, and remove the `--id` flag registration.\n2. `driveCmd.Use` updated to `drive [issue-id]` to reflect the new usage.\n3. The `--dry-run` hint output in `internal/exponential/drive.go` (`log.info(\"xpo drive --id \" + issue.ID)`) updated to `xpo drive \u003cID\u003e` (no flag).\n4. All other flags (`--filter`, `--test-cmd`, `--dry-run`, `--no-merge`, `--resume`, `--max-retries`, `--supervisor`, `--coder`) remain unchanged.\n5. `make test` passes."},"created_at":"2026-06-30T11:12:25.121008547Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude \u003cagent@NICSPC\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-e01041","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-a6dbe0a8-8bcc-48d7-9768-98c51cb8413f","text":"## Summary\n\nRefactored `xpo drive` to accept the issue ID as an optional positional argument instead of the `--id` flag, matching the pattern used by `xpo merge`.\n\n### Changes\n\n**`cmd/exponential/drive.go`**\n- Removed the `driveID` package-level variable\n- Updated `driveCmd.Use` from `\"drive\"` to `\"drive [issue-id]\"`\n- Added `Args: cobra.MaximumNArgs(1)` and `ValidArgsFunction: completeIssueIDs` for shell completion\n- Changed `Run` to pass `args` through to `runDrive(args)`\n- Updated `runDrive` to extract the ID from `args[0]` when present\n- Removed the `--id` flag registration; all other flags unchanged\n\n**`internal/exponential/drive.go`**\n- Updated dry-run hint from `xpo drive --id \u003cID\u003e` to `xpo drive \u003cID\u003e`\n- Updated the multiple-in-progress error message from `\"use --id to specify\"` to `\"specify the issue ID as an argument\"`\n\n### Rationale\n\nFollowed the exact pattern from `cmd/exponential/merge.go` (positional arg with `MaximumNArgs(1)` + `completeIssueIDs`). This is simpler and more ergonomic — `xpo drive abc123` vs `xpo drive --id abc123`.\n\n`make test` and `make build` both pass."},"created_at":"2026-06-30T11:14:31.161500556Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.196 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-e01041","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-06-30T11:14:35.249385346Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.196 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-e01041","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-775b8e65-54fc-4b13-af27-ace76b58e4d0","text":"## xpo drive — walkthrough\n\n## PR Walkthrough: `xpo drive` accepts issue ID as positional arg\n\n### Rationale\n\nThe `--id` flag was unnecessary ceremony — every other subcommand that takes an issue ID (`xpo merge`, `xpo show`) uses a positional arg. This aligns `drive` with that convention. A flag-to-positional migration is the simplest path; there's no backward-compat concern since this is a CLI, not an API.\n\n### Changes\n\n**`cmd/exponential/drive.go`** — The cobra command definition. Removed the `driveID` package-level var and its `--id` flag registration. Set `Args: cobra.MaximumNArgs(1)` so the command accepts zero or one positional arg. Updated `Use` to `\"drive [issue-id]\"` for help text. Added `ValidArgsFunction: completeIssueIDs` for shell tab-completion (reuses the existing completer from `merge`). The `Run` closure now passes `args` into `runDrive(args)`, which extracts `args[0]` when present.\n\n**`internal/exponential/drive.go`** — Two string updates. The dry-run hint changed from `xpo drive --id \u003cID\u003e` to `xpo drive \u003cID\u003e`. The multiple-in-progress error message changed from `\"use --id to specify\"` to `\"specify the issue ID as an argument\"`. No logic changes.\n\n### How to verify\n\n```bash\nmake test                          # all tests pass\nmake build                         # binary compiles\n\n# Positional arg works\n./xpo drive xpo-e01041             # drives that specific issue\n\n# Auto-pick still works\n./xpo drive                        # picks a PLANNED issue\n\n# Too many args rejected\n./xpo drive abc def                # should error: \"accepts at most 1 arg\"\n\n# Dry-run output shows new syntax\n./xpo drive --dry-run              # hint should read \"xpo drive \u003cID\u003e\", not \"xpo drive --id \u003cID\u003e\"\n\n# Old flag is gone\n./xpo drive --id xpo-e01041        # should error: unknown flag\n```\n\n### What to look out for\n\nThere are no tests for the cobra command wiring itself (`cmd/exponential` has `[no test files]`). The change is small enough that manual verification covers it, but it means a future regression in arg parsing would only surface at runtime. Not a blocker for this PR, but worth noting."},"created_at":"2026-06-30T11:15:34.37749308Z","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg <nicbet@gmail.com>","created_by":"claude \u003cagent@NICSPC\u003e"}
