{"id":"xpo-668fbc","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-daf156e9-e0bf-4f38-9a3b-666c0208651d","text":"## Summary\n\nReworked the Merge view diff experience with unified/split toggle, file tree, and numerous polish fixes.\n\n### Diff toggle\n- Segmented `Unified | Split` button, persisted in localStorage\n- **Unified**: sticky gutter columns with opaque tinted backgrounds (`--color-diff-gutter-add/del` tokens), box-shadow borders that don't detach during scroll, horizontal scrolling for long lines\n- **Split**: single-table layout for guaranteed row alignment, paired del/add lines with empty-row padding, truncated long lines, hunk headers on both sides\n\n### File tree\n- Collapsible directory tree built from diff-parsed paths (single source of truth — no more path mismatches with `FileInfo`)\n- Single-child directory flattening (e.g. `internal/server/` instead of nested `internal/` → `server/`)\n- File status color derived from diff content (green for add-only, red for delete-only)\n- Clicking a file smooth-scrolls to its card in the diff column instead of filtering\n\n### Diff cards\n- Each file renders as a bordered rounded card with spacing between them\n- Card headers show filename + `+N -N` stats (computed from diff lines)\n- Meta lines (diff headers, rename info, etc.) are hidden\n- Hunk headers render as full-width blue-tinted rows with sticky gutter cells\n\n### Follow-up\n- Syntax highlighting on diff lines (filed separately — requires reconstructing full file from diff context for accurate tokenization, similar to GitHub's Tree-sitter approach)"},"created_at":"2026-06-30T19:57:50.091844858Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.196 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
