{"id":"xpo-0d4ca2","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-7e64e98b-0d1e-4c6b-aeb1-411bfa17d171","text":"## Summary\n\nExtracted `applyUpdate()` from `UpdateIssue()` in `update.go` to separate the core business logic (event building, cascading automations, appending to `issues.db`) from the git commit step.\n\nUpdated `MergeIssue()` in `merge.go` to call `appendEvent(MERGE)` then `applyUpdate(DONE)` before the git commit, so the event log records MERGE → DONE in the correct causal order. All cascading side effects (e.g. `LastCompleted` parent auto-close) now fire during merge and land in the same commit.\n\nStrengthened `merge_test.go` to assert both MERGE and DONE events exist in the raw event log, and that MERGE precedes DONE.\n\n### Files changed\n\n- `internal/exponential/update.go` — split `UpdateIssue` into `applyUpdate` (events + side effects) and `UpdateIssue` (+ git commit)\n- `internal/exponential/merge.go` — call `applyUpdate(DONE)` after appending MERGE event, before git commit\n- `internal/exponential/merge_test.go` — assert MERGE → DONE event ordering in the log"},"created_at":"2026-07-01T19:22:20.32069481Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.197 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
