{"id":"xpo-22a371","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Implement the foundational artifact system:\n\n- Add `ARTIFACT` event type to the JSONL event stream\n- Define `ArtifactPayload` struct with `artifact_type`, `filename`, and `action` fields\n- Implement disk I/O for `.xpo/artifacts/\u003cissue-id\u003e/` layout (lazy directory creation, file read/write/delete)\n- Add `ArtifactSummary` to the `Issue` struct and update projection to replay `ARTIFACT` events\n- Implement business logic methods on `Client`: `AddArtifact`, `ReadArtifact`, `DeleteArtifact`, `ListArtifacts`\n- Implement first-class convenience methods: `WriteSpec`, `ReadSpec`, `DeleteSpec`, `WriteWalkthrough`, `ReadWalkthrough`, `DeleteWalkthrough`\n- Validation: issue must exist, no path traversal in filenames, reserved names (`spec.md`, `walkthrough.md`) blocked in generic methods\n- Upsert semantics: check projected `Artifacts` list to determine `created` vs `updated` action\n\nSee spec: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-03-issue-artifacts-design.md`","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"xpo-0a7c15","sort_order":"b4w","status":"PLANNED","title":"Artifact storage layer and event model"},"created_at":"2026-07-03T10:53:35.797377292Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.199 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-6f1db9","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Register three new MCP tools with operation enums and output schema envelopes:\n\n- **`xpo__spec`** — operations: `write`, `read`, `delete`. Filename always `spec.md`.\n- **`xpo__walkthrough`** — operations: `write`, `read`, `delete`. Filename always `walkthrough.md`.\n- **`xpo__artifact`** — operations: `add`, `read`, `delete`, `list`. Requires `filename`. Rejects reserved names with error directing caller to dedicated tool.\n\nExtend **`xpo__show`** output with an `artifacts` array: `{ type, filename, updated_at, updated_by }`. Empty array if none exist. Content not inlined.\n\nAll tools return `{ ok, issue_id, path, ... }` on success, `{ ok: false, error }` on failure. All delegate to the shared business logic layer.\n\nSee spec: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-03-issue-artifacts-design.md`","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"xpo-0a7c15","sort_order":"aK","status":"BACKLOG","title":"MCP tools for artifacts"},"created_at":"2026-07-03T10:53:43.080296737Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.199 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-4589a9","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add `xpo artifact` command group with subcommands:\n\n- `xpo artifact add \u003cissue-id\u003e` — add/update an artifact\n  - `--spec` flag: write as spec (implicit `spec.md`)\n  - `--walkthrough` flag: write as walkthrough (implicit `walkthrough.md`)\n  - `--name \u003cfilename\u003e`: required for generic artifacts\n  - `--file \u003cpath\u003e`: read content from file (otherwise stdin)\n- `xpo artifact show \u003cissue-id\u003e \u003cfilename\u003e` — print content to stdout\n  - `--spec` / `--walkthrough` shorthands accepted\n- `xpo artifact delete \u003cissue-id\u003e \u003cfilename\u003e` — remove an artifact\n- `xpo artifact list \u003cissue-id\u003e` — list artifacts for an issue\n\nAll subcommands delegate to the shared business logic layer.\n\nSee spec: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-03-issue-artifacts-design.md`","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"xpo-0a7c15","sort_order":"aL","status":"BACKLOG","title":"CLI commands for artifacts"},"created_at":"2026-07-03T10:53:47.752110319Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.199 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-ac2167","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Two surgical swaps in `drive.go`:\n\n1. **Spec phase** — replace `c.UpdateIssue(issue.ID, UpdatePayload{Description: \u0026revisedSpec})` with `c.WriteSpec(issue.ID, revisedSpec)`. The original issue description is preserved.\n\n2. **Walkthrough phase** — replace `c.AddComment(issue.ID, \"## xpo drive -- walkthrough\\n\\n\" + text)` with `c.WriteWalkthrough(issue.ID, walkthrough)`. No more walkthrough comment.\n\nEverything else in the drive loop stays the same.\n\nSee spec: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-03-issue-artifacts-design.md`","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"xpo-0a7c15","sort_order":"aM","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Update xpo drive to use artifact system"},"created_at":"2026-07-03T10:53:52.353983549Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.199 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-75e913","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Display artifacts on the issue detail page in the web UI:\n\n- Show an artifacts section listing all artifacts for the issue (from `xpo__show` response)\n- Render spec and walkthrough content as markdown\n- Render generic artifacts based on file extension inference (markdown, code, plain text)\n- Handle empty state (no artifacts)\n\nSee spec: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-03-issue-artifacts-design.md`","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"xpo-0a7c15","sort_order":"aN","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Web UI: render artifacts on issue detail view"},"created_at":"2026-07-03T10:53:55.371415259Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.199 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-4f1ba7","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Update project documentation to cover the artifact system:\n\n- README: document `.xpo/artifacts/` layout, spec/walkthrough concepts, and how artifacts travel with the code\n- CLI help text: `xpo artifact --help` and subcommand help\n- MCP tool descriptions: ensure `xpo__spec`, `xpo__walkthrough`, `xpo__artifact` have clear, agent-friendly descriptions\n- CLAUDE.md: update agent instructions to reference artifact tools for specs and walkthroughs\n\nSee spec: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-03-issue-artifacts-design.md`","labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"xpo-0a7c15","sort_order":"aO","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Documentation: artifact system in README and help text"},"created_at":"2026-07-03T10:53:59.061323473Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.199 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
