{"id":"xpo-22a371","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-936fe243-c622-4824-80ab-937037e3be30","text":"## Task 2: Artifact disk I/O and business logic — done\n\nImplemented the disk I/O and business-logic layer on `LocalTransport`, on top of the Task 1 event model (`model.EventTypeArtifact`, `model.ArtifactPayload`, `model.ArtifactSummary`, `Issue.Artifacts`, projection).\n\n**Summary**\n\nNew file `internal/exponential/artifact.go`:\n- `AddArtifact(issueID, artifactType, filename, content string) error` — public entry point; rejects the reserved filenames `spec.md`/`walkthrough.md` (reserved for Task 3's `WriteSpec`/`WriteWalkthrough`), then delegates to `writeArtifact`.\n- `writeArtifact(...)` (unexported) — shared implementation: validates filename, resolves the issue via `GetIssue()`, lazily creates `.xpo/artifacts/\u003cissue-id\u003e/`, writes the file, determines `created` vs `updated` by checking the issue's projected `Artifacts`, appends an `ARTIFACT` event via `appendEvent()`. Deliberately skips the reserved-name check so Task 3 can call it directly with `spec.md`/`walkthrough.md`.\n- `ReadArtifact(issueID, filename string) (string, error)` — reads the file, clear \"not found\" error when missing.\n- `DeleteArtifact(issueID, filename string) error` — removes the file, looks up the artifact type from the projection (defaults to `\"generic\"`), appends an `ARTIFACT` event with `action: \"deleted\"`.\n- `ListArtifacts(issueID string) ([]model.ArtifactSummary, error)` — returns the issue's projected artifacts (always non-nil).\n- `validateArtifactFilename` — blocks empty names, path separators, absolute paths, and `..` traversal (covers `../evil.md`, `sub/../../evil.md`, `/etc/passwd`).\n\nNew file `internal/exponential/artifact_test.go` — 11 tests covering happy path, upsert (created→updated), issue-not-found, reserved-filename rejection, path-traversal rejection, read/delete not-found, and list (empty + populated).\n\n**Rationale / deviations**\n\nThe brief's sample code imported `internal/storage` in `artifact.go` but never used it — dropped that import to compile cleanly; issue resolution and persistence already go through `GetIssue()`/`appendEvent()`. `AutoCommit` git-commit wiring (used elsewhere for `.xpo/issues.db`) was intentionally left out for artifact files — not mentioned in the design spec or task briefs. Flagging as a possible follow-up if artifact files should also be auto-committed when `Config.AutoCommit` is set.\n\n**Verification**\n\n- `go test ./internal/exponential/ -run \"TestAddArtifact|TestReadArtifact|TestDeleteArtifact|TestListArtifacts\" -v` — all 11 PASS\n- `make build` — succeeds (full CLI + web assets)\n- `make test` — full suite passes, no regressions\n- `go vet ./internal/exponential/...` and `gofmt -l` — clean\n\nFull report: `.superpowers/sdd/task-2-report.md`. Issue remains in `DOING` — Tasks 3 (spec/walkthrough convenience methods) and 4 (Transport/Client wiring) are still outstanding within this issue."},"created_at":"2026-07-03T12:13:02.865160111Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.199 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-ac2167","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-0733050d-e838-44fb-b3a0-ab23f35aa2d8","text":"## Note from storage layer review\n\nWhen integrating `xpo drive` with the artifact system, the `AutoCommit` mechanism needs to be extended to stage artifact files under `.xpo/artifacts/` alongside `.xpo/issues.db`. Currently `AutoCommit` only stages `issues.db`, so in unattended `xpo drive` runs, the ARTIFACT event would be committed but the artifact file itself would remain unstaged."},"created_at":"2026-07-03T12:47:48.379946819Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.199 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-75e913","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-d188cf7c-025a-470b-8a85-4ce7cd42dac2","text":"## Note from storage layer review\n\nARTIFACT events are currently invisible in the inbox and activity timeline (`IsMeaningfulActivityEvent` and `isMeaningfulInboxEvent` both return false for unknown event types). When building the Web UI for artifacts, consider adding ARTIFACT to these filters so spec/walkthrough creation/updates show up in activity feeds."},"created_at":"2026-07-03T12:47:51.166990287Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.199 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-22a371","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-05e506e7-4b23-447b-86a4-5fd1ee4a6abb","text":"## Implementation Summary\n\nImplemented the foundational artifact storage layer across 5 commits on branch `xpo-22a371-artifact-storage-layer`.\n\n### What changed\n\n**`internal/model/types.go`** — Added `EventTypeArtifact` constant, `ArtifactPayload` struct (with `artifact_type`, `filename`, `action` fields), `ArtifactSummary` struct (with JSON tags), and `Artifacts []ArtifactSummary` field on the `Issue` struct.\n\n**`internal/exponential/projection.go`** — Added `EventTypeArtifact` case to `ProjectIssues`. Handles `created`/`updated` (upsert by filename) and `deleted` (filter out) actions. Advances `UpdatedAt` and appends to `Events`.\n\n**`internal/exponential/artifact.go`** — New file with all artifact business logic on `LocalTransport`:\n- `validateArtifactFilename` — rejects empty, path traversal, absolute paths, and `\".\"`\n- `writeArtifact` (unexported) — shared implementation: validates, resolves issue ID, creates directory lazily, writes file, determines `created`/`updated` from projection, appends ARTIFACT event\n- `AddArtifact` — public API that rejects reserved filenames (`spec.md`, `walkthrough.md`) then delegates to `writeArtifact`\n- `ReadArtifact`, `DeleteArtifact`, `ListArtifacts`\n- `WriteSpec`/`ReadSpec`/`DeleteSpec`, `WriteWalkthrough`/`ReadWalkthrough`/`DeleteWalkthrough` — convenience wrappers\n\n**`internal/exponential/transport.go`** — Added 10 artifact methods to the `Transport` interface.\n\n**`internal/exponential/client.go`** — Added 10 delegation methods on `Client` (all follow `syncLocal` + delegate pattern).\n\n**`internal/exponential/remote_transport.go`** — Added 10 `ErrLocalOnly` stubs.\n\n**`internal/ui/history.go`** — Added `EventTypeArtifact` case to `RenderHistory`, displaying `\"\u003cfilename\u003e \u003caction\u003e\"`.\n\n### Test coverage\n\n20 new tests across `projection_test.go`, `artifact_test.go`, `client_artifact_test.go`, and `history_test.go`. Covers: create/update/delete projection, happy paths, upsert semantics, issue-not-found, reserved filename rejection, path traversal rejection, short ID resolution, empty list, and history rendering. Full suite passes with no regressions.\n\n### Downstream notes\n\n- AutoCommit integration for artifact files noted on xpo-ac2167 (drive task)\n- Inbox/timeline visibility for ARTIFACT events noted on xpo-75e913 (web UI task)"},"created_at":"2026-07-03T12:48:16.799805568Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.199 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
