{"id":"xpo-4589a9","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-3f1ac2c8-f1d6-44ae-bdd4-8e40eb64fdb2","text":"## Implementation Summary\n\nNew file `cmd/exponential/artifact.go` — the `xpo artifact` command group with four subcommands.\n\n### What changed\n\n**`xpo artifact add \u003cissue-id\u003e`** — writes an artifact via `--spec`, `--walkthrough`, or `--name \u003cfilename\u003e`. Content from `--file \u003cpath\u003e` or piped stdin. Mutually exclusive flag validation. Dispatches to `client.WriteSpec`, `client.WriteWalkthrough`, or `client.AddArtifact`.\n\n**`xpo artifact show \u003cissue-id\u003e [filename]`** — prints raw content to stdout. Accepts positional filename or `--spec`/`--walkthrough` shorthands. Dispatches to `client.ReadArtifact`.\n\n**`xpo artifact delete \u003cissue-id\u003e [filename]`** — removes an artifact. Same filename resolution as `show`. Dispatches to `client.DeleteArtifact`.\n\n**`xpo artifact list \u003cissue-id\u003e`** — table output with TYPE, FILENAME, UPDATED, UPDATED BY columns. Uses `humanize.Time()` for relative timestamps, `ui.RenderCell`/`ui.MutedStyle`/`ui.AccentStyle` for consistent formatting.\n\n**Helpers:** `resolveAddFilename` (mutual exclusion for add flags), `resolveReadFilename` (positional-vs-shorthand for show/delete), `readArtifactContent` (`--file` \u003e piped stdin \u003e error).\n\nAll subcommands use `completeIssueIDs` for shell autocomplete and `cobra.ExactArgs`/`cobra.RangeArgs` for arg validation.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `make build` — succeeds\n- `make test` — full suite passes, no regressions\n- Manual testing of all subcommands and error paths:\n  - `add --spec` via stdin pipe, `show --spec`, `list`, `delete` by positional filename\n  - `add --name` for generic artifacts, `show` by positional, `list` with multiple artifacts\n  - Error: no flags → clear message about `--name`\n  - Error: `--spec --walkthrough` → mutual exclusion\n  - Error: no content source → clear message about `--file` or stdin\n  - Error: `--name spec.md` → reserved filename rejection from business logic\n  - Error: `show` without filename → clear message"},"created_at":"2026-07-03T13:59:41.892408061Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.199 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
