{"id":"xpo-ac2167","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-08e4564d-38d4-4ecd-bde7-e4b1279d4f04","text":"## Implementation Summary\n\nThree surgical changes to wire `xpo drive` into the artifact system.\n\n### What changed\n\n**`internal/exponential/drive.go`** — Two swaps:\n1. **Spec phase** (line 386-390): Replaced `c.UpdateIssue(issue.ID, UpdatePayload{Description: \u0026desc}, \"drive\")` with `c.WriteSpec(issue.ID, spec)`. The original issue description is now preserved; the refined spec goes to `spec.md` as a first-class artifact.\n2. **Walkthrough phase** (line 503-504): Replaced `c.AddComment(issue.ID, \"## xpo drive — walkthrough\\n\\n\" + walkthrough)` with `c.WriteWalkthrough(issue.ID, walkthrough)`. No more walkthrough comments cluttering the activity feed; the walkthrough is a proper artifact viewable in the tabbed UI.\n\n**`internal/exponential/client.go`** — Extended `GitCommit` to also `git add .xpo/artifacts/` alongside `.xpo/issues.db`, so artifact files written during drive runs are committed on the feature branch before merge.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `make build` — succeeds\n- `make test` — full suite passes, no regressions"},"created_at":"2026-07-03T15:24:33.068985129Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.199 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
