{"id":"xpo-4f1ba7","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-8d8ffb44-ecc0-4954-9f58-01136d029f23","text":"## Summary\n\nDocumentation-only changes across four files to cover the artifact system.\n\n### `cmd/exponential/artifact.go`\n\nAdded `Long` descriptions to four cobra commands:\n\n- `artifactCmd` — explains what artifacts are, the three types (spec, walkthrough, generic), and the storage layout under `.xpo/artifacts/\u003cissue-id\u003e/`.\n- `artifactShowCmd` — documents `--spec`/`--walkthrough` shorthands vs positional filename arg.\n- `artifactDeleteCmd` — same filename resolution docs as show.\n- `artifactListCmd` — documents the four output columns: TYPE, FILENAME, UPDATED, UPDATED BY.\n\n`artifactAddCmd` already had a complete `Long` and was left unchanged.\n\n### `internal/mcpserver/tools.go`\n\nUpdated MCP tool `Description` strings:\n\n- `spec` — now mentions purpose (design spec before implementation), supported operations, and when to use it.\n- `walkthrough` — now mentions purpose (post-implementation summary), supported operations.\n- `artifact` — now mentions all four operations and the spec.md/walkthrough.md restriction.\n\n### `README.md`\n\n- New **Artifacts** section between CLI reference and Web UI: concept explanation, first-class vs generic artifacts, CLI usage examples for all subcommands, and storage layout diagram.\n- Added `spec`, `walkthrough`, `artifact` rows to the MCP tools table.\n\n### `CLAUDE.md`\n\n- Added `mcp__xpo__spec`, `mcp__xpo__walkthrough`, `mcp__xpo__artifact` rows to the MCP tool table.\n- New **Specs and Walkthroughs** subsection under Usage Notes: read spec before implementation, write walkthrough after, use artifact for supplemental files.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `make cli` — compiles successfully\n- `make test` — full suite passes, no regressions\n- `xpo artifact --help` — prints multi-line description covering all three artifact types"},"created_at":"2026-07-03T15:31:42.879282029Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.199 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
