{"id":"xpo-9c01f2","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"xpo drive: link to walkthrough artifact instead of printing markdown","description":"When `xpo drive` completes, the `log.walkthrough(walkthrough)` call on line 505 of `drive.go` renders the full walkthrough markdown to the terminal via glamour. Now that walkthroughs are stored as first-class artifacts (written on line 502 via `WriteWalkthrough`), dumping the raw content to stdout is redundant and noisy.\n\n## Desired behavior\n\nReplace the full-text walkthrough dump with a short one-liner that tells the user where to read it, e.g.:\n\n```\n  ✔ Walkthrough saved → xpo show \u003cissue-id\u003e --walkthrough\n```\n\nThis keeps the terminal output focused on progress/status while pointing the user to the canonical artifact.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Remove the `log.walkthrough(walkthrough)` call (line 505).\n- Replace it with a brief log line linking to the walkthrough artifact (e.g. `log.ok` or `log.info` with a `xpo show` hint).\n- The `driveLogger.walkthrough` method and its glamour rendering can be removed if no other caller exists.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":1,"sort_order":"b5O","dependencies":[{"source_id":"xpo-9c01f2","target_id":"xpo-ac2167","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-07-03T15:57:24.943117804Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.199 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-9c01f2","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-07-03T16:01:22.52462772Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
{"id":"xpo-9c01f2","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-7df9be03-d23b-45d0-b903-a1c9e89acc9e","text":"## Summary\n\nReplaced the full walkthrough markdown dump with a concise status line in `internal/exponential/drive.go`:\n\n- **Replaced** `log.walkthrough(walkthrough)` with `log.ok(fmt.Sprintf(\"Walkthrough saved → xpo artifact show %s --walkthrough\", issue.ID))` — prints `  ✔ Walkthrough saved → xpo artifact show \u003cid\u003e --walkthrough` on completion.\n- **Removed** the `driveLogger.walkthrough` method (glamour-based terminal rendering) — no remaining callers.\n- **Removed** the `wordWrap` helper function — only used by the deleted `walkthrough` method.\n- **Removed** the `github.com/charmbracelet/glamour` import — only used by the deleted method.\n\nAll other imports (`strings`, `ui`, `unicode`, etc.) remain in use and were kept.\n\n## Rationale\n\nNow that walkthroughs are persisted as first-class artifacts via `WriteWalkthrough`, dumping the full markdown to the terminal is redundant. A one-liner pointing to `xpo artifact show` keeps terminal output focused on progress while directing the user to the canonical artifact.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `make build` — compiles cleanly.\n- `make test` — all tests pass, no regressions."},"created_at":"2026-07-03T16:04:19.417616671Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.199 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
