{"id":"xpo-d16187","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-5388c52c-9d79-4384-8c62-6c1d1ed7ae61","text":"## Summary\n\nReplaced the static braille spinner in `xpo drive` with a full streaming progress display.\n\n### Changes\n\n- **`internal/exponential/agent.go`**: Added `RunStreaming` method to `claudeExecutor` that uses `--output-format stream-json --verbose --include-partial-messages`. Parses `content_block_start` (tool use, thinking), `content_block_delta` (text, partial JSON for tool args), and `content_block_stop` events into `StreamEvent` callbacks. Extracts tool details (file paths, commands) from partial JSON using substring matching since deltas arrive incrementally.\n\n- **`internal/exponential/drive.go`**: \n  - Added `streamDisplay` with background render ticker (25fps) for smooth spinner animation independent of stream event frequency\n  - Two-line display: step header (`○ label`) + detail sub-line (`└ ⠹ Reading …/file.go`) that collapses when done\n  - Compact mode for single-step phases (Implementation) — detail line directly under phase header\n  - Cycling thinking verbs (Thinking, Pondering, Tinkering, Hacking, Brewing, etc.) for idle/thinking states, rotating every 3s\n  - Tool-specific labels: Reading, Editing, Writing for file ops; raw command for Bash; \"Loading tools\" for ToolSearch\n  - Detail line truncated to terminal width to prevent wrap corruption\n  - Collapsible phases: active phase shows `●` with expanded steps, completed phases collapse to `✔ Phase (Xs)`\n  - Overall header line: `Driving [id] [title] (agent)`\n  - Concise final line: `✔ Done (time · tokens · cost)`\n\n### Rationale\n\nThe original UX showed a static spinner label (\"Evaluating spec\") for potentially minutes with no indication of what the agent was doing. Streaming events give real-time feedback: which files are being read, when the agent is thinking, what commands it's running."},"created_at":"2026-07-11T11:22:46.609735Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.206 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-e8b3cd","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-651f9f03-99a5-459c-9d9e-8a3f7b65f3cd","text":"## Summary\n\nAddressed slow spec evaluation and high token usage in `xpo drive` through three changes:\n\n### Changes\n\n- **Supervisor model override** (`agent.go`, `config.go`): Added `model` field to `DriveAgentConfig`. Supervisor defaults to `sonnet` via config (`drive.supervisor.model: sonnet`). Supervisor calls (spec eval, planning, review, walkthrough) are text analysis tasks that don't need Opus. The `--model` flag is passed to the `claude` CLI.\n\n- **Session reuse** (`agent.go`): `claudeExecutor` captures `session_id` from the first call's response and passes `--resume \u003cid\u003e` on subsequent calls. The ~140k system context (tools, MCP servers, CLAUDE.md) gets prompt-cached after the first load. Both supervisor and coder executors reuse their respective sessions. Supervisor prompts reframed as conversational follow-ups (\"Next task: ...\", \"Final task: ...\") to work naturally in a resumed session.\n\n- **Test command validation** (`drive.go`, `setup.go`): `xpo init` no longer writes a default `test_cmd`. When no test command is configured, the Testing phase skips with a hint. When a configured command fails with a non-1 exit code (127=not found, 2=make error), it's treated as a config problem and skipped rather than sending the coder into a retry loop. The eval prompt explicitly tells the supervisor when tests were skipped.\n\n### Result\n\nFibonacci script benchmark: 3m38s / 709k in / $0.74 → 1m41s / 435k in / $0.36. Roughly half the cost and time."},"created_at":"2026-07-11T11:22:58.706571Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.206 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
