{"id":"xpo-d9092f","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-f5719dce-7403-4823-9dba-6bb047598eb7","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed markdown paste handling in `web/src/components/MarkdownEditor.tsx`.\n\n**Root cause:** The `tiptap-markdown` v0.9.0 clipboard extension uses ProseMirror's `clipboardTextParser` hook, which is only invoked when the clipboard contains no HTML. Most paste sources (VS Code, browsers, notes apps, terminals on macOS) include both `text/plain` and `text/html` in the clipboard data. When ProseMirror detects HTML, it uses its DOM parser — which treats markdown syntax (`**bold**`, `# heading`, etc.) as literal text — and `clipboardTextParser` is never called.\n\n**Fix:** Replaced the no-op `handlePaste` with logic that:\n1. Extracts `text/plain` and `text/html` from the clipboard\n2. If HTML exists, strips all tags and compares to the plain text — if they differ, the HTML has real formatting (e.g. pasted from a web page), so we defer to ProseMirror's default HTML handling\n3. If the HTML is just a thin wrapper (tag-stripped content matches plain text), we parse the plain text as markdown using `tiptap-markdown`'s parser and insert as rich content\n4. If there's no HTML at all, we also parse as markdown\n\nThis preserves correct behavior for pasting rich content from web pages while fixing the core bug of markdown text being shown verbatim."},"created_at":"2026-07-12T05:57:04.648806Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-762a91","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"When adding a new issue, and title or description contain content, we should prompt the user on whether to discard the issue draft or cancel to keep editing. This prevents accidentally discarding issues when hitting Escape.","labels":["improvement"],"sort_order":"b70","title":"Prompt before discarding new issue"},"created_at":"2026-07-12T06:21:37.533999Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"xpo-762a91","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"sort_order":"Zz","status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-07-12T06:34:27.446193Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"xpo-758398","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"When creating a new issue, we should give the user the option to save what they have written so far as an issue draft. Drafts could go into an `.xpo/drafts` folder and serialize the \"new issue\" dialog data as a JSON object. No issue ID is assigned yet. A new \"Drafts\" menu item appears in the navigation bar when drafts are present (with a counter badge). \n\nThe \"Drafts\" overview shows a list of drafts users have been working on. Users can open any draft to continue editing the issue draft. From there a draft can either be discarded (draft JSON deleted without rendering an issue) or an issue be created (draft JSON used to add a new issue).","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"b7a","title":"Issue Drafts"},"created_at":"2026-07-12T06:26:59.473398Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"xpo-758398","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"sort_order":"Zx"},"created_at":"2026-07-12T06:27:06.967764Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
