{"id":"xpo-2ba758","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"relates_to","source_id":"xpo-2ba758","target_id":"xpo-e5865f"}],"description":"`GenerateAgentDocs(prefix string)` in `internal/exponential/agents.go:59` accepts a `prefix` parameter but immediately discards it:\n\n```go\nfunc GenerateAgentDocs(prefix string) string {\n    _ = prefix\n    return `...`\n}\n```\n\nThe caller (`AppendAgentInstructions`) passes the project's issue ID prefix, but it never appears in the generated output. The prefix should likely be interpolated somewhere in the agent instructions (e.g. in examples showing issue IDs) so agents know the project's ID format.","labels":["bug"],"sort_order":"b6s","title":"GenerateAgentDocs() ignores its prefix parameter"},"created_at":"2026-07-12T08:27:14.602311Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
