{"id":"xpo-e5865f","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-e9b19f93-8746-4578-b010-b60572d5f5b8","text":"## Redesign: stub + skill split\n\nBased on review feedback, the single-file approach was replaced with a portable two-layer architecture:\n\n**Agent instruction file** (CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md / etc.) — thin always-on stub (~17 lines) containing only hard invariants: no ghost work, MCP-only, BACKLOG approval, bug filing freedom, \"load `xpo-workflow` skill before implementation\", MCP failure handling, agent identity.\n\n**`.claude/skills/xpo-workflow/`** — on-demand skill following the Agent Skills spec:\n- `SKILL.md` — full 8-step lifecycle procedure with portable frontmatter\n- `references/spec-guide.md` — spec template and scaling rules\n- `references/mcp-tools.md` — tool table with harness-naming caveat\n\nKey improvements over the single-file version:\n- ~90% of content loads on-demand instead of every turn\n- Harness-neutral MCP tool naming (\"call `list` on the xpo server\" not `mcp__xpo__list`)\n- Fixed status graph (`DOING ⇄ BLOCKED`, not linear)\n- Resolved ambiguities flagged in review (stop and ask for blockers, assignee on DOING, concurrent assignment, MCP failure behavior)\n- Removed redundant \"Usage Notes\" section\n- Comment vs walkthrough distinction tightened\n- Agents with `SkillDir` get stub + skill; agents without get full inline docs\n\n`xpo init` auto-detects installed agents and writes to the correct harness skill directory. Tests pass, idempotent on re-init."},"created_at":"2026-07-12T12:31:49.979853Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-cd0f62","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Drag-and-drop reorder drops parent relationship on child issues","description":"When a parent epic is in progress (DOING) but its child issues are still in BACKLOG, reordering the child issues via drag-and-drop in the web UI removes the `parent` relationship from the child issue.\n\n**Steps to reproduce:**\n1. Create an epic and add child issues\n2. Transition the epic to DOING\n3. Leave child issues in BACKLOG\n4. Drag-and-drop to reorder the child issues\n\n**Expected:** Reordering preserves the parent-child relationship.\n\n**Actual:** The child issue loses its parent link after reordering.","sort_order":"b7K","labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-07-12T13:06:06.018062Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-2792c3","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"MCP show tool does not reflect backlog sort order","description":"After reordering issues in the backlog via the web UI, the sort order is not reflected in the JSON returned by the MCP `show` tool (or `list`). The issues come back in their original order rather than the user-defined order.\n\n**Steps to reproduce:**\n1. Create several backlog issues\n2. Reorder them via drag-and-drop in the web UI\n3. Call the MCP `list` or `show` tool\n\n**Expected:** Issues are returned in the user-defined sort order.\n\n**Actual:** Issues are returned in their original (creation) order, ignoring the drag-and-drop reordering.","sort_order":"b7m","labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-07-12T13:06:09.098384Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-748873","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Drive trails: record and render agent execution narratives","description":"## Problem\n\n`xpo drive` runs have rich narrative structure — spec evaluation, coder attempts, reviewer verdicts, retries, budget spend — but none of it is persisted. The event log only records bookend state changes (DOING → DONE or BLOCKED). All execution detail is printed to stdout and lost.\n\nThis makes drive runs unwatchable, unreplayable, and unshareable.\n\n## Vision\n\nMake the `.xpo/issues.db` event log visual and watchable by recording **drive trails** — per-run JSONL files stored as artifacts — and building renderers on top of them.\n\nThe watchable unit is not code or tokens. It's state transitions and judgment moments: the reviewer rejecting the coder's work, retries burning budget, the spec being revised. The drive loop already has narrative structure (pick ticket → spec → coder attempt → review verdict → retry or pass → commit) — it just needs to be captured and rendered.\n\n## Design Decision: Artifacts, Not Inline Events\n\nDrive events stored inline in `issues.db` would bloat the event log and slow down `ProjectIssues()` (which replays every event on every read). A single drive run with 2 retries would add 15-20 events at 1-3 KB each — ten runs would double the log.\n\nInstead, drive trails are stored as **artifact files**:\n\n```\n.xpo/artifacts/\u003cissue-id\u003e/drive-\u003crun-id\u003e.jsonl\n```\n\nThe issue event log gets a single lightweight `ARTIFACT` pointer event per run. The trail file carries the full execution narrative. This keeps the issue log lean while making every run independently replayable from any repo clone.\n\n## Build Phases\n\n### Phase 0: Instrument — Drive Trail Recording\nAdd trail recording to `DriveIssue()`. Each run produces a JSONL file with typed events: `drive_start`, `spec_eval`, `attempt_start`, `test_result`, `verdict`, `drive_end`. Includes run ID, timestamps, token/cost tracking, reviewer feedback.\n\n### Phase 1: Recap Cards\nAuto-generated summary at the end of each run: ticket title, rounds fought, verdict trail, diffstat, budget spent, link to merged commit. The daily shareable unit — an agent contributor posting its own work summary.\n\n### Phase 2: Replay\n`xpo drive replay \u003crun-id\u003e` renders the trail as a time-compressed timeline. Skip silent thinking stretches, dwell on judgment moments. Every historical run becomes replayable from the repo.\n\n### Phase 3: Spectator Mode\nLive read-only view of an in-progress drive: tickets moving across columns, \"now playing\" strip (current ticket, active role, retry count, tokens spent). The crown jewel — build last.\n\n## Design Rules\n\n1. **Don't sanitize failure.** Retries, rejected reviews, exhausted budgets — leave them in. Visible failure reads as a real system.\n2. **Stakes must be real.** Every recap links a real merged commit anyone can inspect.\n3. **Show the spend.** Running token/cost counter. People will watch a number climb and argue about whether ticket X was worth $1.40.","status":"BACKLOG","sort_order":"b8E","labels":["epic","feature"]},"created_at":"2026-07-13T08:30:49.013989Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-ca0f2f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Drive trail recording — instrument DriveIssue() to emit JSONL trails","description":"Instrument `DriveIssue()` in `internal/exponential/drive.go` to emit a per-run JSONL trail file at `.xpo/artifacts/\u003cissue-id\u003e/drive-\u003crun-id\u003e.jsonl`. Each event is a self-contained JSON object with a monotonic sequence number, typed event field, and run-scoped metadata.\n\nThis is the prerequisite for all renderers (recap, replay, spectator). No trail, no show.","status":"BACKLOG","parent_id":"xpo-748873","estimate":5,"sort_order":"b8g","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-07-13T08:30:55.889235Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-e3d44b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Recap cards — auto-generated run summaries","description":"Generate a recap card at the end of each drive run from the trail file: ticket title, attempt count, verdict trail (\"reviewer rejected ×2: AC-3 not met → passed\"), diffstat, token/cost spend, link to merged commit.\n\nOutput as markdown and optionally as a shareable image. This is the daily posting unit — an agent contributor summarizing its own work.","status":"BACKLOG","parent_id":"xpo-748873","estimate":3,"sort_order":"b98","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-07-13T08:30:58.787899Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-2f3900","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Drive replay — render trail files as time-compressed timelines","description":"`xpo drive replay \u003crun-id\u003e` renders a trail JSONL as a time-compressed timeline. Skip silent stretches, dwell on judgment moments (verdicts, retries). Every historical run in the repo becomes replayable from any checkout — no screen recording needed.\n\nDepends on trail recording being in place.","status":"BACKLOG","parent_id":"xpo-748873","estimate":5,"sort_order":"b9a","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-07-13T08:31:01.590887Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-a168ae","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Spectator mode — live read-only drive dashboard","description":"Live public read-only view of an in-progress drive run: tickets moving across columns, \"now playing\" strip (current ticket, active role, retry N/M, tokens spent), scorecard ticking. The crown jewel — mission control for xpo building xpo.\n\nDepends on trail recording and probably the web frontend's SSE/WebSocket infrastructure.","status":"BACKLOG","parent_id":"xpo-748873","estimate":8,"sort_order":"bA2","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-07-13T08:31:04.015606Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
