{"id":"xpo-7a4b19","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"xpo-7a4b19","target_id":"xpo-ca0f2f"}],"description":"Watch `.xpo/artifacts/*/drive-*.jsonl` for appended lines using fsnotify. Each new line is broadcast as a granular `drive_event` SSE message to connected clients.\n\nFollows the existing `WatchDB()` / `WatchGitRefs()` pattern. SSE message includes the full trail event JSON plus the issue ID, so the frontend can route it to the correct view.\n\nThis makes CLI-initiated drives visible in the web UI for free — any `xpo drive` from any terminal shows up in real time.","estimate":3,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"xpo-748873","sort_order":"bAU","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Trail watcher — broadcast trail events via SSE"},"created_at":"2026-07-13T10:26:24.820566Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-575923","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"React component in the issue detail view that renders drive trail events as a visual timeline. Two modes:\n\n- **Static**: for completed runs, fetches the trail JSONL via the existing `GET /api/issues/{id}/artifacts/{filename}` endpoint and renders the full timeline.\n- **Live**: for in-progress runs, subscribes to `drive_event` SSE messages and renders events as they arrive. Shows a \"now playing\" strip: current phase, active role, attempt N/M, running token/cost counter.\n\nIncludes verdict rendering (pass/fail with feedback), test result indicators, cost accumulation, and wall time.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","frontend"],"parent_id":"xpo-748873","sort_order":"bAw","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Trail viewer component — timeline rendering in issue detail"},"created_at":"2026-07-13T10:26:29.832905Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-234823","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"`POST /api/issues/{id}/drive` starts `xpo drive \u003cissue-id\u003e` as a child subprocess. Returns immediately with `{ run_id, pid }`. Progress is delivered through the trail watcher + SSE, not the HTTP response.\n\n**Subprocess model**: the server shells out to the xpo binary (same binary, `os.Args[0]`). Natural crash isolation — a failing drive doesn't take down the server. Server tracks the PID and exposes `GET /api/drive/status` and `POST /api/issues/{id}/drive/stop` for lifecycle management.\n\n**Frontend**: the \"Start Work\" button gains a \"Drive\" option (or replaces Start Work for PLANNED issues). Clicking it fires the POST, then the trail viewer component activates and shows the live timeline.\n\n**Constraints**: at most one drive subprocess at a time (or per-issue). Server rejects concurrent drive requests with 409.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","backend","frontend"],"parent_id":"xpo-748873","sort_order":"bBO","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Drive from UI — subprocess launch via API endpoint"},"created_at":"2026-07-13T10:26:37.516754Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
