{"id":"xpo-762a91","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-93d5920c-494e-42b8-8f97-6fdb65d67a96","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded a discard confirmation dialog to the new-issue modal in `NewIssueModal.tsx`.\n\nWhen the user tries to close the modal (Escape, backdrop click, X button, or Cancel) while `title` or `description` has content, a small alert dialog appears on top asking \"Discard this issue?\" with Cancel and Discard buttons. The new-issue form stays visible behind the dialog so the user can review their draft.\n\nIf the form is empty, all close paths work immediately with no prompt.\n\nA capture-phase keydown listener traps Escape while the confirmation is showing, preventing it from leaking to parent views. Form reset logic was consolidated into a shared `resetForm` helper used by both the create-success and discard paths.\n\nDraft saving is out of scope (xpo-758398)."},"created_at":"2026-07-14T07:06:10.136422Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-762a91","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-07-14T07:06:13.880469Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-df91c4","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"action":"created","artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md"},"created_at":"2026-07-14T07:34:36.082767Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-df91c4","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"In all input fields that support [Markdown](https://commonmark.org/), we should show a formatting bar (popover) when a user has an active text selection.\n\nOptions in the formatting bar should be:\n\n- \"Text type\" (Body Text, heading 1, heading 2, heading 3, heading 4),\n- Bold, Italic, Strikethrough, Underline\n- Link\n- Quote\n- Inline Code\n- Code block\n- List (Numbered, Ordered, Checklist)\n\nEach option should be rendered as an icon button with a representative icon. Some options may in turn open a popover with options (text type, list).","status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-07-14T09:13:48.23218Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-7d3c63","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"xpo-7d3c63","target_id":"df91c4"}],"description":"The comment input in `ActivityTimeline.tsx` uses a plain `\u003ctextarea\u003e`. Replace it with the TipTap-based `MarkdownEditor` component so that comments get the formatting bar (BubbleMenu) and all other markdown editing features (keyboard shortcuts, paste handling, etc.).","labels":["improvement","UI","WebApp"],"sort_order":"bBq","title":"Migrate comment input to MarkdownEditor"},"created_at":"2026-07-14T08:22:23.799421Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-df91c4","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-b71cebe0-0a55-45a1-aa03-7319bb027aa3","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded a floating formatting bar (BubbleMenu) to all MarkdownEditor instances. Selecting text shows a toolbar with formatting options; deselecting hides it.\n\n### Changes\n\n- **`FormattingBar.tsx`** (new) — TipTap `BubbleMenu`-based toolbar with: text type dropdown (Body/H1–H4), inline marks (Bold, Italic, Strikethrough, Underline), inline link editor (URL input swaps the toolbar content), blockquote, inline code, code block, and list dropdown (bullet, numbered, checklist). Dropdowns render as portals to `document.body` to avoid overflow clipping. Active formatting state is reflected on buttons.\n\n- **`MarkdownEditor.tsx`** — Added `Underline` extension, renders `FormattingBar` alongside `EditorContent`. Added `onTransaction` handler so programmatic formatting changes (e.g. `setLink`) set the `dirty` flag and propagate via `onChange`. The blur handler now checks `bubbleMenuRef` so focus moving to the link URL input doesn't trigger save/exit.\n\n### Design decisions\n\n- **Inline link editor** rather than a dropdown portal — avoids focus/blur issues where the IssueDetail description editor would exit edit mode when the link input stole focus.\n- **`appendTo={document.body}`** on BubbleMenu to escape overflow clipping from modal containers. Required a manual blur handler (capture-phase) because the default blur handler's `parentNode.contains(relatedTarget)` check always returns true when parent is `body`.\n- **Stable prop refs** (`appendToBody`, `bubbleMenuOptions`) outside the component to prevent the BubbleMenu plugin from re-dispatching on every render.\n\n### Follow-up\n\nFiled xpo-7d3c63 to migrate the comment `textarea` to MarkdownEditor so comments also get the formatting bar."},"created_at":"2026-07-14T09:19:58.432821Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
