{"id":"xpo-d662a2","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"action":"updated","artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md"},"created_at":"2026-07-14T11:01:51.673261Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-6c8ca4","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"xpo-6c8ca4","target_id":"d662a2"}],"description":"Add a `--lfs` flag to `xpo init` that configures Git LFS for the `.xpo/attachments/` directory. When enabled, adds a `.gitattributes` rule (`xpo/attachments/** filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text`) and records the choice in `.xpo/config.yaml` (`attachments.lfs: true`). Without the flag, attachments are committed directly to git.\\n\\nThis must be a decision at init time because migrating from direct-to-git to LFS later requires `git lfs migrate import`, which rewrites all history — a poison pill on shared repos.\\n\\n`xpo doctor` should warn if attachments exist and LFS is not configured but the attachment directory is growing large.","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"bCI","title":"LFS support for attachments at init time"},"created_at":"2026-07-14T11:12:05.053046Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-d662a2","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"action":"updated","artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md"},"created_at":"2026-07-14T11:12:44.893165Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-6c8ca4","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"Add a `--lfs` flag to `xpo init` that configures Git LFS for the `.xpo/attachments/` directory. When enabled, adds a `.gitattributes` rule (`xpo/attachments/** filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text`) and records the choice in `.xpo/config.yaml` (`attachments.lfs: true`). Without the flag, attachments are committed directly to git.\n\nThis must be a decision at init time because migrating from direct-to-git to LFS later requires `git lfs migrate import`, which rewrites all history — a poison pill on shared repos.\n\n`xpo doctor` should warn if attachments exist and LFS is not configured but the attachment directory is growing large."},"created_at":"2026-07-14T11:14:22.050551Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"xpo-147414","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Relationship links in issue details view shows the issue id hash but is missing the prefix, so the hyperlink does not point to a page. For the case that we call the WebUI with an invalid issue ID we should show a nice \"not found\" screen with a helpful message and guiding the user back to the backlog or search.","labels":["bug"],"sort_order":"bCs","title":"Relationship links in issue details view broken"},"created_at":"2026-07-14T13:31:48.79247Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
