{"id":"xpo-147414","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-3bfaf5e7-f86c-49e2-8992-34383732aa5b","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed two bugs:\n\n**Broken dependency links** — `LinksToDependencies()` in `internal/inputs/inputs.go` stored user-provided target IDs without resolving them to full `xpo-` prefixed IDs. The MCP `add` and `update` tools now resolve each dependency target via `c.GetIssue()` before storing, matching what the `link` tool already did. The PropertySidebar also falls back to suffix matching (`t.id.endsWith(dep.target_id)`) to handle old events with prefixless IDs. The link `href` now uses the resolved `target.id` when available.\n\n**No 404 page** — navigating to `#/issues/\u003cinvalid-id\u003e` silently showed the Backlog. Now renders an EmptyState-styled \"Issue not found\" page with the searched ID and a \"Back to Backlog\" button. The issue lookup in `App.tsx` also falls back to suffix matching for robustness.\n\n### Files changed\n\n- `internal/mcpserver/tools.go` — resolve dependency target IDs in `add` and `update` tools\n- `web/src/components/IssueDetail/PropertySidebar.tsx` — suffix fallback for dependency lookup, use resolved ID in link href\n- `web/src/App.tsx` — suffix fallback for issue lookup, 404 page for invalid issue IDs"},"created_at":"2026-07-14T13:58:43.471873Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
