{"id":"xpo-d41e32","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-07-14T14:38:24.844982Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-fbfc30","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"Comprehensive audit of all input paths (MCP tools, HTTP API handlers, shared input layer) revealed multiple validation gaps. This story covers hardening all write paths with consistent validation.\n\n## Critical\n\n1. **`handleDraft` (HTTP)** — the web UI's write endpoint bypasses ALL validation. `CreatePayload` and `UpdatePayload` are deserialized from JSON and passed directly to the service layer without validating status, title, estimate, parent ID, dependency target IDs, link types, or cycle ID. Also ignores `json.Unmarshal` errors. Registered under `issue.create` capability but handles UPDATE, COMMENT, and DELETE operations.\n\n2. **Capability mismatch** — `handleDraft` route uses `issue.create` but processes update/comment/delete. A user with only create capability can modify and delete issues.\n\n## High\n\n3. **MCP `update` tool** — does not validate estimate against the configured estimation system, unlike the `add` tool.\n\n4. **CycleID** — never validated as a valid `YYYY-MM-DD` date or checked against existing cycles during create/update in any code path (MCP, HTTP, CLI). `CycleForID()` exists but is only called in `handleCycleProgress`.\n\n5. **MCP `link` tool** — no self-link check (source == target) and no duplicate link detection. An issue can be linked to itself, and the same link can be added multiple times.\n\n## Medium\n\n6. **No length limits** — title, description, comment body, assignee, label names, artifact content, spec/walkthrough content have no length bounds in any handler.\n\n7. **Negative estimates** — bypass the `payload.Estimate \u003e 0` guard in MCP `add` and are never validated.\n\n8. **Assignee format** — no validation despite the `\"Name \u003cemail\u003e\"` jsonschema hint. Any arbitrary string is accepted.\n\n9. **Label color format** — HTTP label handlers (`handleAddLabel`, `handleUpdateLabel`) accept any string as a color value. No hex color validation.\n\n10. **Priority bounds** — no bounds checking on the priority integer field in any path.\n\n## Low\n\n11. **Response IDs** — MCP `update`, `spec`, `walkthrough`, and `artifact` tools return the raw user-provided issue ID in responses rather than the resolved canonical ID.\n\n12. **MCP `list` status filter** — not validated against known statuses (silently matches nothing for invalid values).\n\n13. **MCP `merge` strategy** — silently defaults invalid strategy strings to squash instead of returning an error.\n\n14. **HTTP `handleMergeIssue`** — silently swallows JSON decode errors and proceeds with defaults.\n\n## Implementation approach\n\n- Centralize validation in the shared `inputs` layer where possible.\n- Have `handleDraft` route through the same `ToCreatePayload`/`ToUpdatePayload` validation as MCP tools.\n- Add issue ID resolution for all ID-referencing fields at the handler level (already done for parent and dependency targets in the MCP tools).\n- Add `ValidateEstimate` to the update path.\n- Add `CycleForID` validation to create/update paths.\n- Add self-link and duplicate link checks to the `link` tool.\n- Add reasonable length limits to string fields.\n- Fix capability mapping for `handleDraft`."},"created_at":"2026-07-14T14:40:02.460146Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-fbfc30","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"labels":["epic"]},"created_at":"2026-07-15T05:37:10.187408Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-49cbfe","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"The web UI's write endpoint `handleDraft` in `internal/server/handlers.go` deserializes `CreatePayload` and `UpdatePayload` from JSON and passes them directly to the service layer without any validation. Unlike the MCP tools, this path does not validate status, title, estimate, parent ID, dependency target IDs, link types, or cycle ID. It also ignores `json.Unmarshal` errors.\n\nRoute through the same `ToCreatePayload`/`ToUpdatePayload` validation as MCP tools, or add equivalent validation inline. Handle unmarshal errors with proper 400 responses.","labels":["bug"],"parent_id":"xpo-fbfc30","sort_order":"bEM","title":"handleDraft bypasses all input validation"},"created_at":"2026-07-15T05:29:34.764082Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-ddb470","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"The `handleDraft` route is registered under `issue.create` capability but the handler also processes UPDATE, COMMENT, and DELETE operations. A user with only `issue.create` capability can modify and delete issues.\n\nEither split into separate routes with appropriate capabilities, or register under a broader capability like `issue.write`.","labels":["bug"],"parent_id":"xpo-fbfc30","sort_order":"bEo","title":"handleDraft capability mismatch"},"created_at":"2026-07-15T05:29:37.529515Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-7868ea","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"The MCP `update` tool does not validate the estimate/story_points field against the configured estimation system, unlike the `add` tool which calls `config.ValidateEstimate()`. An agent can set story_points to any integer (including negative values) through the update path.\n\nAdd the same `ValidateEstimate` call as the `add` tool.","labels":["bug"],"parent_id":"xpo-fbfc30","sort_order":"bFG","title":"MCP update tool missing estimate validation"},"created_at":"2026-07-15T05:29:39.880341Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-a90985","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"The MCP `link` tool does not check whether source and target are the same issue, and does not detect duplicate links. An issue can be linked to itself, and the same source-target-kind triple can be added multiple times.\n\nAdd a self-link check (`src.ID == tgt.ID`) and duplicate detection against the existing dependency list before appending.","labels":["bug"],"parent_id":"xpo-fbfc30","sort_order":"bFi","title":"MCP link tool allows self-links and duplicates"},"created_at":"2026-07-15T05:29:42.655504Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-e75d09","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"The `cycle_id` field is stored raw without any validation in all code paths (MCP, HTTP, CLI). A value like \"not-a-date\" or \"2026-13-45\" would be stored without error. The `CycleForID()` function exists in `internal/config/cycle.go` and correctly validates date format, but is only called in `handleCycleProgress`.\n\nCall `CycleForID()` validation in the create and update paths when a non-empty cycle_id is provided.","labels":["bug"],"parent_id":"xpo-fbfc30","sort_order":"bGA","title":"CycleID never validated during create or update"},"created_at":"2026-07-15T05:29:46.897406Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-75f1cf","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"No length limits exist on title, description, comment body, assignee, label names, artifact content, or spec/walkthrough content in any handler. An agent or malformed request could store arbitrarily large strings.\n\nAdd reasonable length limits: title (500 chars), description (100KB), comment body (100KB), assignee (200 chars), label names (100 chars), artifact/spec/walkthrough content (1MB).","labels":["improvement"],"parent_id":"xpo-fbfc30","sort_order":"bGc","title":"Add length limits to string input fields"},"created_at":"2026-07-15T05:29:49.717736Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-0f562c","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"The MCP `update`, `spec`, `walkthrough`, and `artifact` tools return the raw user-provided issue ID in responses rather than the resolved canonical ID. For example, if the user passes a short ID like `d662a2`, the response contains that short ID instead of `xpo-d662a2`.\n\nUse the resolved ID from `GetIssue()` in all response objects.","labels":["improvement"],"parent_id":"xpo-fbfc30","sort_order":"bH4","title":"Resolve issue IDs in MCP tool responses"},"created_at":"2026-07-15T05:29:52.321991Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-e7f899","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Remaining low-priority validation gaps from the input audit:\n\n- **Negative estimates** — bypass the `payload.Estimate \u003e 0` guard in MCP `add` and are never validated. Negative values are silently accepted.\n- **Assignee format** — no validation despite the `\"Name \u003cemail\u003e\"` jsonschema hint. Any arbitrary string is accepted.\n- **Label color format** — HTTP label handlers (`handleAddLabel`, `handleUpdateLabel`) accept any string as a color value. No hex color validation.\n- **Priority bounds** — no bounds checking on the priority integer field in any path.\n- **MCP `list` status filter** — not validated against known statuses. Invalid values silently match nothing.\n- **MCP `merge` strategy** — silently defaults invalid strategy strings to squash instead of returning an error.\n- **HTTP `handleMergeIssue`** — silently swallows JSON decode errors and proceeds with defaults.","labels":["improvement"],"parent_id":"xpo-fbfc30","sort_order":"bHW","title":"Minor validation gaps across MCP and HTTP handlers"},"created_at":"2026-07-15T05:31:14.483778Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
