{"id":"xpo-ddb470","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-587de173-0ad6-4b80-bde2-4bf2bda3b36a","text":"## Summary\n\nThe `handleDraft` endpoint was registered with `issue.create` capability but handled CREATE, UPDATE, COMMENT, and DELETE operations — a user with only `issue.create` could update, comment on, and delete issues.\n\nAdded a `requireCapability` helper method on `Server` (`server.go`) that checks the request's user against a specific capability, returning 403 if denied. Each branch in `handleDraft` now checks the appropriate capability: `issue.create`, `issue.update`, `issue.comment`, `issue.delete`.\n\nThe route registration was changed from `issue.create` to `issue.read` (baseline authentication) since the per-branch checks now enforce the correct capability.\n\n### Files changed\n\n- `internal/server/server.go` — added `requireCapability` method\n- `internal/server/handlers.go` — per-branch capability checks in `handleDraft`\n- `internal/server/router.go` — changed route capability from `issue.create` to `issue.read`"},"created_at":"2026-07-15T05:56:24.493696Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
