{"id":"xpo-a90985","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-02121d4f-edf4-4113-b31e-2ec59c7b63dc","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded two checks to the MCP `link` tool handler in `internal/mcpserver/tools.go`, after resolving source and target IDs:\n\n1. **Self-link check** — rejects if `src.ID == tgt.ID` with \"cannot link an issue to itself\".\n2. **Duplicate check** — scans `src.Dependencies` for an existing entry with the same `TargetID` and `Kind`. Rejects if found.\n\nDifferent link kinds to the same target are still allowed (e.g. `blocks` and `relates_to` to the same issue)."},"created_at":"2026-07-15T08:53:39.686936Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-a90985","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-8026050e-da3b-400a-b9d0-37fc37094f23","text":"Also added: when a dependency target can't be resolved (deleted issue or stale data), the PropertySidebar now shows the ID in muted italic with \"(deleted)\" instead of rendering a broken link. The remove button still works so users can clean up stale links."},"created_at":"2026-07-15T09:28:08.704791Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.207 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
