{"id":"xpo-0f562c","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-f524d5ff-8f5e-4c29-950a-38c6362c2563","text":"## Summary\n\nResolved raw user-provided issue IDs in all MCP tool response objects by calling `c.GetIssue()` early in each handler and using the canonical `issue.ID` throughout.\n\n### Changed handlers in `internal/mcpserver/tools.go`:\n\n- **`update`** — added `GetIssue()` call; use resolved ID in `UpdateIssue()`, `broadcast()`, and response struct.\n- **`comment`** — previously called `GetIssue()` but discarded the result; now uses `issue.ID` in `AddComment()`, `broadcast()`, and response.\n- **`start`** — added `GetIssue()` call; use resolved ID in `StartWork()`, `broadcast()`, and response.\n- **`merge`** — added `GetIssue()` call; use resolved ID in `MergeIssue()`, `broadcast()`, and response.\n- **`spec`** — added `GetIssue()` call; use resolved ID in path construction, `WriteSpec()`/`ReadSpec()`/`DeleteSpec()`, `broadcast()`, and response.\n- **`walkthrough`** — same pattern as `spec`.\n- **`artifact`** — same pattern as `spec`, covering all four operations (add/read/delete/list).\n\n### Rationale\n\nThe `show` and `link` handlers already followed this pattern correctly. The fix brings all other handlers into alignment so that short/partial IDs passed by users are always resolved to the canonical form (e.g. `d662a2` → `xpo-d662a2`) in every response and broadcast."},"created_at":"2026-07-19T06:14:01.307434Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.214 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
