{"id":"xpo-e7f899","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-99d566b8-3d64-4530-abcf-12ebc5c87840","text":"## Summary\n\nClosed all seven validation gaps across MCP and HTTP handlers:\n\n### Changes in `internal/exponential/client.go`:\n- **Priority bounds** — added `[0, 4]` range check in both `ValidateCreatePayload` and `ValidateUpdatePayload`.\n- **Assignee format** — added `validateAssigneeFormat()` helper that checks angle-bracket syntax and requires `@` in the email portion. Called from both validation functions.\n- **Negative estimates** — already handled by existing code (no change needed).\n\n### Changes in `internal/mcpserver/tools.go`:\n- **`list` status filter** — validate each status string against known values before querying; return a clear error for invalid ones.\n- **`merge` strategy** — added `default` case that rejects unknown strategy strings with an error (empty string still defaults to squash).\n\n### Changes in `internal/server/handlers.go`:\n- **Label color format** — added `hexColorRe` regex (`^#?[0-9a-fA-F]{6}$`) and validate in both `handleAddLabel` and `handleUpdateLabel`.\n- **HTTP `handleMergeIssue`** — return 400 on JSON decode errors instead of swallowing them; added strategy validation with the same pattern as MCP.\n\n### Rationale\n\nAll fixes follow the existing validation style: check early, return a descriptive error message naming the invalid value. No breaking changes for valid inputs."},"created_at":"2026-07-19T06:21:26.666423Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.214 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
