{"id":"xpo-154098","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Execute `drive` and `loop` commands in a sandbox like `Seatbelt` on MacOS or `Bubblewrap` on Linux and WSL2. The model is **opt-in** and can be enabled with the `--sandbox` flag.","labels":["feature","Backend","CLI"],"sort_order":"bIg","title":"Sandbox mode for `xpo drive` and `xpo loop`"},"created_at":"2026-07-20T07:15:08.635356Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"xpo-154098","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"estimate":2},"created_at":"2026-07-20T07:15:08.712546Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"xpo-564cdb","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"title":"Change --no-merge flag to --review and make configurable","description":"Currently, `xpo drive` will execute work on a separate code branch and at the end of the implementation merge the changes back to trunk. A `--no-merge` flag is available to disable the automated merging. To make the behaviour indicator more explicit, change the `--no-merge` flag to `--review` for `xpo drive` to leave changes on the branch, adding a walkthrough and letting users review the changes on the branch through the UI. A link to the review page should be printed to the terminal.\n\nThe default behaviour should be configurable in `.xpo/config.yaml` ","sort_order":"Zz"},"created_at":"2026-07-20T07:20:50.111449Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
