{"id":"xpo-2ba758","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-07-20T07:24:23.089734Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"xpo-337854","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Board view sorts issues differently from Backlog within status columns","description":"## Bug\n\nThe Board view shows issues in a different order within each status column compared to the Backlog view.\n\n### Root cause\n\n`buildContainers` in `Board.tsx` calls `sortGroup(issues, 'manual')` on **all issues as a single flat list** before splitting into status columns. The comparator is inconsistent:\n\n- DONE vs DONE → compared by `updated_at`\n- DONE vs non-DONE → compared by `sort_order`\n- non-DONE vs non-DONE → compared by `sort_order`\n\nThis violates transitivity: if DONE_A \u003e NON_DONE_X \u003e DONE_B by `sort_order`, but DONE_A \u003c DONE_B by `updated_at`, the sort result is non-deterministic.\n\nThe Backlog avoids this by **grouping issues by status first**, then sorting within each group independently — DONE by `updated_at` (recency), all others by the user's selected sort key.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nWithin each status column, the Board should show issues in the same order as the Backlog: sort_order for non-DONE statuses, updated_at (recency) for DONE.\n\n### Fix\n\nRewrite `buildContainers` to group by status first, then sort within each column using `sortGroup` — DONE with `'updated'`, others with `'manual'`.","status":"PLANNED","priority":2,"sort_order":"bCK","labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-07-20T07:31:51.837158Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.215 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-337854","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"created"},"created_at":"2026-07-20T07:32:05.136096Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.215 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-337854","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-07-20T07:32:08.777235Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.215 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-337854","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-bf30ded7-134c-4ae4-b0a3-6039d8996076","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed `buildContainers` in `web/src/components/Board/Board.tsx` to sort issues within each status column independently, matching the Backlog's behavior.\n\n**Before:** All issues were sorted as a single flat list via `sortGroup(issues, 'manual')`, then split by status. The comparator was inconsistent when mixing DONE and non-DONE issues (DONE-vs-DONE used `updated_at`, everything else used `sort_order`), violating transitivity and producing non-deterministic within-column ordering.\n\n**After:** Issues are grouped by status first, then each column is sorted independently:\n- DONE column: `sortGroup(columnIssues, 'updated')` — recency\n- All other columns: `sortGroup(columnIssues, 'manual')` — `sort_order` (fractional indexing)\n\nThis eliminates the cross-status comparator inconsistency and produces the same within-column ordering as the Backlog view.\n\nAll tests pass, build succeeds."},"created_at":"2026-07-20T07:33:45.81286Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.215 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
