{"id":"xpo-dbd580","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Improve prose-exponential markdown rendering","description":"The rendered markdown in the web UI (specs, walkthroughs, comments, descriptions) has visual issues that make it look unpolished:\n\n1. **Tables** have no styling at all — no borders, padding, or header distinction\n2. **Headings** are too close in size to body text (h2 at 1.1em is barely distinguishable) and all share the same top margin regardless of level\n3. **Lists** have excessive left indentation that pushes text away from the left edge\n4. **Vertical rhythm** between block elements (paragraphs, lists, code blocks, blockquotes) is slightly cramped\n5. **Inline code** font size is slightly too large relative to surrounding text\n6. **Heading line-height** inherits the body's 1.75 which is too loose for heading text\n\nAll styles live in `.prose-exponential` in `web/src/index.css`. The Tiptap editor styles must stay in sync with the read-only rendering styles to avoid layout shifts between editing and preview.","status":"DONE","estimate":1,"sort_order":"bJG","labels":["improvement","UI","WebApp"]},"created_at":"2026-07-27T15:51:27.136086Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-dbd580","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"created"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T15:51:42.10393Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-dbd580","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-c1fa2b58-bd9d-45f0-b881-8a710098bf58","text":"**Summary** — Overhauled `.prose-exponential` styles in `web/src/index.css` to fix markdown rendering quality.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n- **Tables**: Added full grid borders (`border: 1px solid` on table/th/td), cell padding `0.5em 0.75em`, header row with `background: var(--color-surface-1)` and muted text. Matching styles added for Tiptap editor tables.\n- **Headings**: Graduated top margins — h1 `2.5em`, h2 `2em`, h3 `1.5em`, h4 `1.25em`. Shared bottom margin `0.75em`. Added `line-height: 1.3`. Bumped sizes: h1 `1.375em`, h2 `1.2em`, h3 `1.05em`.\n- **Lists**: Reduced `padding-left` from `1.5em` to `1.125em` so markers sit within the text column. Added `padding-left: 0.375em` on `li` for marker-to-text gap. Nested lists keep `1.5em` indent.\n- **Vertical rhythm**: Paragraphs `0.875em` (from `0.75em`), code blocks/blockquotes `1em`, HRs `1.5em`.\n- **Inline code**: `0.875em` (from `0.9em`), tighter vertical padding.\n- **List paragraphs**: Added `li \u003e p` rules to prevent double-margin stacking.\n\n**Rationale** — The biggest gap was tables having zero styling. The heading hierarchy was flat (h2 at 1.1em barely distinguishable from body). List indentation pushed text too far right. All changes apply to both read-only rendering and the Tiptap editor to maintain parity."},"created_at":"2026-07-27T15:51:55.962897Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-dbd580","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"walkthrough","filename":"walkthrough.md","action":"created"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T15:52:24.08934Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-a8be39","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Move issue detail scrollbar to right edge with sticky sidebar","description":"The issue detail view currently has two independent scroll containers side by side — the main content on the left and the property sidebar on the right, with the scrollbar sitting between them.\n\n**Desired behavior:**\n- Single scroll container for the entire body area, with the scrollbar at the browser's right edge\n- Property sidebar is sticky-positioned so it stays visible while the main content scrolls\n- Sidebar gets its own overflow scroll for shorter viewports where it can't fit entirely","status":"DONE","estimate":1,"sort_order":"bJq","labels":["improvement","UI","WebApp"]},"created_at":"2026-07-27T15:59:50.397413Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-a8be39","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"created"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T16:00:03.267515Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-a8be39","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-4462c335-373d-4412-835c-f231cf8b6407","text":"**Summary** — Changed the issue detail layout from two independent scroll containers to one shared scroll container with a sticky sidebar.\n\n**Changes in `IssueDetail.tsx`:**\n- The body row (`flex-1 flex overflow-hidden`) became the scroll container: `flex-1 overflow-y-auto`\n- Added an inner `flex min-h-full` wrapper around content + sidebar\n- The main content div dropped `overflow-y-auto` (no longer its own scroll container), kept `flex-1 min-w-0`\n- Removed `scrollbarGutter: \"stable both-edges\"` style (no longer needed — scrollbar is at the viewport edge)\n\n**Changes in `PropertySidebar.tsx`:**\n- Root div changed from `w-80 overflow-y-auto shrink-0` to `w-80 shrink-0 sticky top-0 self-start max-h-screen overflow-y-auto`\n- `sticky top-0 self-start` keeps it pinned at the top of the scroll container\n- `max-h-screen overflow-y-auto` gives it its own scroll when content exceeds viewport height\n\n**Rationale** — The previous layout placed the scrollbar between content and sidebar, which felt unnatural. Moving to a single scroll container puts the scrollbar at the right edge where users expect it. The sticky sidebar ensures metadata remains visible while scrolling long issue content."},"created_at":"2026-07-27T16:00:16.525651Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-a8be39","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"walkthrough","filename":"walkthrough.md","action":"created"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T16:00:31.652117Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-a8be39","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-bff2bbf1-007a-44a8-8f1b-8e3b4b1470b9","text":"**Follow-up fixes:**\n\n1. Sidebar was at window edge instead of hugging content — moved `max-w-4xl mx-auto` from the inner content wrapper to the outer flex row as `max-w-[76rem] mx-auto` (content 56rem + sidebar 20rem), so content and sidebar are centered as a unit.\n2. Content jumped when switching tabs — restored `scrollbarGutter: \"stable\"` on the scroll container.\n3. Sidebar top didn't align with title — added `pt-12` to the sidebar root (matching the content's `py-12`), changed inner padding from `p-5` to `px-5 pb-5`."},"created_at":"2026-07-27T16:06:46.921267Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-13153f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Tighten activity timeline spacing for system entries","description":"System entries in the activity timeline (status changes, merges, artifact updates, estimate changes) had the same `space-y-4` gap as comment entries, making the timeline feel stretched. System entries are compact single-line items and should be visually grouped tighter, with comments retaining more generous spacing.","status":"DONE","estimate":1,"sort_order":"bKQ","labels":["improvement","UI","WebApp"]},"created_at":"2026-07-27T16:10:26.962779Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-13153f","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-ce20a904-d3cb-4746-9ba6-39f54fedc371","text":"**Summary** — Tightened vertical spacing between activity timeline entries in `ActivityTimeline.tsx`.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Container gap: `space-y-4` (16px) → `space-y-2` (8px)\n- System entry padding: `py-2` → `py-1.5` (slightly tighter)\n- Comment entries: added `!mt-4` override to keep generous spacing around comment cards\n\n**Rationale** — System entries are compact single-line items (status changes, merges, artifact updates). The original 16px gap treated them the same as multi-line comment cards, making the timeline feel stretched. Now system entries group tightly while comments remain visually distinct."},"created_at":"2026-07-27T16:10:36.239236Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-a6a17e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Reset scroll position when navigating between issues","description":"When navigating between issues using the arrow keys or the \u003c \u003e buttons in the issue detail view, the scroll position from the previous issue is retained. This means if you scrolled down on a long issue and then navigate to the next one, you land partway through the content instead of at the top.\n\n**Fix:** Add a `useEffect` keyed on `issue.id` that resets the scroll container's `scrollTop` to 0 when the issue changes.","status":"DONE","estimate":1,"sort_order":"bL0","labels":["bug","UI","WebApp"]},"created_at":"2026-07-27T16:29:40.105924Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-a6a17e","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-2969bdc9-6804-4dc5-b7d4-b04a8adcfbca","text":"**Summary** — Added a `scrollRef` on the body scroll container in `IssueDetail.tsx` and a `useEffect` keyed on `issue.id` that calls `scrollTo(0, 0)` when the issue changes.\n\n**Changes in `IssueDetail.tsx`:**\n- Added `const scrollRef = useRef\u003cHTMLDivElement\u003e(null)` (line 63)\n- Added `useEffect(() =\u003e { scrollRef.current?.scrollTo(0, 0); }, [issue.id])` (lines 65-67)\n- Added `ref={scrollRef}` to the body scroll container div\n\n**Rationale** — The scroll container persists across issue navigations (prev/next arrows, keyboard shortcuts). Without resetting, React re-renders the content inside the same scroll container, preserving the old scroll offset."},"created_at":"2026-07-27T16:29:48.36095Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
