{"id":"xpo-dbdfd3","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"When a parent issue is \"In Progress\" that has a number of sub-issue, it counts the entire sum of story points of all sub-issues regardless of whether they have been completed or not towards the parent issue's story points used to calculate the sum of story points in that status. On the parent issue itself the \"story points\" column shows the correct amount of not yet completed story points across all sub-issues.\n\nExample:\\\nparent foo is the only issues currently In Progress and shown with 4 story points, the status header for in progress shows 12 story points: 4 not yet completed from sub-issues and 8 from already completed sub-issues.","labels":["bug"],"sort_order":"bLa","title":"Effort count wrong in backlog status section header"},"created_at":"2026-07-29T18:52:32.468833Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"xpo-dbdfd3","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-07-29T18:52:32.53479Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"xpo-e928c1","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Currently all labels are in the same column (in Backlog) or metadata row (in detail view and story cards on board), and they are ordered by their creation order.\n\nIt would be nice if we had a primary label to the between status icon and title text (on backlog) and next to the title (on board, details view) and metadata labels separately, ordered alphabetically.","labels":["improvement"],"sort_order":"bMA","title":"Show \"primary\" label separate from \"metadata\" labels"},"created_at":"2026-07-31T09:38:49.13154Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"xpo-e928c1","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-07-31T09:38:49.201419Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"xpo-f7ea12","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Overview\n\nFlip `xpo start` and `xpo merge` to use git worktrees by default, making concurrent multi-session work safe by design instead of by luck.\n\n**Motivating incident:** Two Claude sessions ran in parallel on the same repo. The issues.db event stream handled concurrency perfectly, but `xpo start` does its git work (`checkout -b`) in the primary checkout. A second session's `start` would have switched the checkout out from under the first session's uncommitted work. It only went cleanly because the checkout happened to be idle on main at that moment.\n\n## Design: Hub-and-Spoke\n\n- **Hub**: Primary checkout stays parked on `main` permanently. It owns `issues.db` and is the merge integration point.\n- **Spokes**: Each `xpo start` creates a worktree at `.xpo/worktrees/\u003cbranch\u003e/` (gitignored, following Claude Code's convention). Code changes happen exclusively in worktrees.\n- **Opt-out**: `--no-wt` flag on both commands, or `worktrees: false` in config.\n\n## Stories\n\n1. **Hub-rooted storage** -- discover hub root from any worktree, route all issues.db reads/writes there\n2. **`xpo start` with worktrees** -- create worktree, return path, setup hook, `--no-wt`\n3. **`xpo merge` with worktree cleanup** -- merge from hub, remove worktree, prune\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- **xpo-c762f7** (gitattributes `merge=union`) -- still needed for `--no-wt` fallback and repos not using worktrees","labels":["epic"],"sort_order":"bMB","status":"PLANNED","title":"Worktree-based git operations"},"created_at":"2026-08-04T10:48:51.317505Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.221 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-580061","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\nThe storage layer gains a \"hub root\" concept so that all `issues.db` reads/writes route through the primary checkout (on `main`), even when the MCP server or CLI runs from a worktree.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Add `HubRoot()` to `internal/exponential/git.go` -- discovers the primary checkout via `git rev-parse --path-format=absolute --git-common-dir` (parent of the shared `.git` dir)\n- Modify `storage.ReadEvents()` and `appendEvent()` to resolve `issues.db` path through `HubRoot()` instead of relative cwd\n- `GitCommit()` stages hub-rooted `.xpo/issues.db`\n\n## Effect\n\n- MCP servers in worktrees read/write the hub's event log\n- The board (watching the hub on main) reflects real-time state from all agents\n- Feature branches carry only code; events serialize through the hub\n- Event commit cadence: per-merge (unchanged from today)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `HubRoot()` returns the primary checkout path from any worktree\n- [ ] `HubRoot()` returns cwd when not in a worktree (backward compatible)\n- [ ] `storage.ReadEvents()` reads from `\u003chub\u003e/.xpo/issues.db`\n- [ ] `appendEvent()` writes to `\u003chub\u003e/.xpo/issues.db`\n- [ ] Board reflects status changes made from worktree MCP servers in real time","estimate":3,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"xpo-f7ea12","sort_order":"bMC","status":"PLANNED","title":"Hub-rooted storage layer"},"created_at":"2026-08-04T10:49:05.339146Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.221 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-1765ca","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\n`xpo start` creates a git worktree instead of checking out in the primary checkout. Returns the worktree path so agents/users can `cd` into it.\n\n## Changes\n\n### New git helpers (`internal/exponential/git.go`)\n\n- `WorktreeAdd(path, branch, base string) error` -- wraps `git worktree add`\n- `WorktreeRemove(path string) error` -- wraps `git worktree remove`\n- `WorktreeList() ([]WorktreeEntry, error)` -- parses `git worktree list --porcelain`\n- `FindWorktreeForBranch(branch string) (string, bool)` -- returns path if branch has an existing worktree\n\n### `StartWork()` changes (`internal/exponential/start.go`)\n\n- Default path: `git worktree add .xpo/worktrees/\u003cbranch\u003e -b \u003cbranch\u003e \u003cbase\u003e`\n- If branch exists locally: `git worktree add .xpo/worktrees/\u003cbranch\u003e \u003cbranch\u003e`\n- Ensure `.xpo/worktrees/` is in `.gitignore`\n- Run `worktree_setup` hook (from config) in the new worktree directory\n- Return `worktreePath` alongside `branchName`\n\n### `--force` + worktree constraint\n\nGit prohibits a branch being checked out in two worktrees. `start --force`:\n1. Find existing worktree via `FindWorktreeForBranch()`\n2. `git worktree remove --force` the existing one\n3. Create a fresh worktree\n\n### `--no-wt` flag\n\nFalls back to current `git checkout -b` behavior. Wired in `cmd/exponential/update.go`.\n\n### MCP tool (`internal/mcpserver/tools.go`)\n\nAdd `worktree_path` to `startOut`:\n\n```go\ntype startOut struct {\n    ID           string   `json:\"id\"`\n    Branch       string   `json:\"branch\"`\n    WorktreePath string   `json:\"worktree_path,omitempty\"`\n    Messages     []string `json:\"messages\"`\n}\n```\n\n### Config (`internal/config/config.go`)\n\n- `Worktrees bool` (default `true`)\n- `WorktreeSetup string` (optional shell command)\n\n### Init (`internal/exponential/setup.go`)\n\nAdd `.xpo/worktrees/` to the `.gitignore` entries written by `InitProject()`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `xpo start \u003cid\u003e` creates worktree at `.xpo/worktrees/\u003cbranch\u003e/`\n- [ ] CLI prints the worktree path\n- [ ] MCP `start` returns `worktree_path` in response\n- [ ] `worktree_setup` hook runs in the new worktree when configured\n- [ ] `--no-wt` preserves current checkout behavior\n- [ ] `worktrees: false` in config disables worktrees globally\n- [ ] `--force` removes existing worktree and creates fresh\n- [ ] `.xpo/worktrees/` added to `.gitignore` by init and on first WT creation\n- [ ] Two concurrent `start` calls for different issues succeed without interfering","estimate":5,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"xpo-f7ea12","sort_order":"bMD","status":"PLANNED","title":"xpo start with worktrees"},"created_at":"2026-08-04T10:49:21.309544Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.221 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-f96832","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\n`xpo merge` runs from the hub (primary checkout on main) and cleans up the worktree after a successful merge.\n\n## Changes\n\n### `MergeIssue()` (`internal/exponential/merge.go`)\n\n- Assert the hub is on `main` before merging (no checkout switch needed)\n- After successful merge: `git worktree remove \u003cpath\u003e` + `git worktree prune`\n- Worktree cleanup happens alongside branch deletion (existing `deleteBranch()`)\n- On merge failure: worktree preserved for manual conflict resolution\n\n### `--no-wt` flag\n\nFalls back to current behavior (checkout main, merge, checkout back). Wired in `cmd/exponential/merge.go`.\n\n### Merge from worktree cwd\n\nIf `merge` is called from inside a worktree (not the hub), it should either:\n- Detect this and refuse with a helpful error (\"run merge from the hub checkout\")\n- Or delegate to the hub automatically\n\nDecision: refuse with a helpful error pointing to the hub path. Simpler, and merge is a deliberate action.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `xpo merge` succeeds from the hub without switching branches\n- [ ] Worktree is removed after successful merge\n- [ ] `git worktree prune` runs after removal\n- [ ] Branch deletion still works (local + remote)\n- [ ] Merge failure preserves the worktree for manual resolution\n- [ ] `--no-wt` preserves current checkout-switch behavior\n- [ ] Merge from a worktree cwd gives a clear error message\n- [ ] Worktree cleanup works even when `--keep-branch` is set (WT removed, branch kept)","estimate":3,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"xpo-f7ea12","sort_order":"bME","status":"PLANNED","title":"xpo merge with worktree cleanup"},"created_at":"2026-08-04T10:49:31.3282Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.221 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
