{"id":"xpo-c762f7","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## Problem\n\nWhen two branches append events to `.xpo/issues.db` concurrently, git produces conflict markers on merge. The file is append-only JSONL -- both sides' lines are valid and should both survive -- but git's default merge strategy doesn't know that.\n\n## Solution\n\n### 1. `xpo init` writes `.gitattributes`\n\nSet `merge=union` in `.gitattributes`:\n\n```\n.xpo/issues.db merge=union\n```\n\nThis tells git to keep lines from both sides on a merge, which is exactly the right semantic for an append-only event log. No conflict markers, no manual resolution.\n\n### 2. Existing repos: retroactive fix\n\n- `xpo init --force` (re-init) adds the `.gitattributes` entry if missing\n- `xpo doctor` detects and reports the missing entry with a fix command\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `xpo init` creates/updates `.gitattributes` with the `merge=union` rule for `.xpo/issues.db`\n- [ ] `xpo init --force` on existing projects adds the rule without breaking other `.gitattributes` entries\n- [ ] `xpo doctor` warns when the rule is missing\n- [ ] Two branches that each append events merge cleanly without conflict markers\n\n## Related\n\n- **xpo-f7ea12** (worktree epic) -- under the hub model events serialize through main, but `merge=union` is still needed for `--no-wt` fallback and repos not using worktrees\n- **xpo-3a219e** (order-independent replay) -- union merge can interleave lines in any order, so replay must not depend on file position","status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-08-04T10:50:27.771245Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.221 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-886099","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"When we change the status of a parent issue from the backlog, a popup window asks us if we also want to transition children. for partially completed epics, this also resets already done children to the new status, those should a) remain untouched and b) be excluded from the preview windows (maybe a line below the preview windows \"x completed issues will not be updated\")","labels":["bug"],"sort_order":"bMo","title":"Epic status update `move all` window should not update completed"},"created_at":"2026-08-04T10:52:29.904662Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
