{"id":"xpo-580061","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-56bf2e78-e2ca-4ca6-9c9b-95078c40589c","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented hub-rooted storage so all `.xpo/issues.db` and `.xpo/artifacts/` operations route through the primary checkout (\"hub\"), even when running from a git worktree.\n\n### New file\n- `internal/storage/root.go` — `HubRoot()` discovers the primary checkout via `git rev-parse --path-format=absolute --git-common-dir`, caches per-process. `XpoDir()` returns `\u003chub\u003e/.xpo`. `ResetHubRoot()` for tests.\n\n### Updated callsites (14 production files)\n- **Storage layer** (`storage/storage.go`, `read.go`, `archive.go`, `collapse.go`) — all `filepath.Join(\".xpo\", ...)` replaced with `filepath.Join(XpoDir(), ...)`. `readCommittedBytes` uses `git -C \u003chub\u003e` to target the hub's committed state.\n- **Git staging** (`exponential/client.go`, `add.go`, `comment.go`, `update.go`, `delete.go`, `merge.go`) — all `git add .xpo/issues.db` commands now use `git -C \u003chub\u003e add .xpo/issues.db` so they target the hub's index.\n- **Artifact paths** (`exponential/artifact.go`) — `artifactDir()` uses `storage.XpoDir()`.\n- **Git lock** (`exponential/gitlock.go`) — lock path routed through `storage.XpoDir()`.\n- **Server** (`server/server.go`, `server/watch.go`) — `statDB()` and `WatchDB()` resolve through `storage.XpoDir()`.\n- **MCP tools** (`mcpserver/tools.go`) — spec, walkthrough, and artifact response paths use `storage.XpoDir()`.\n\n### Rationale\nUsed `storage.HubRoot()` in the `storage` package (rather than a separate utility package) because `storage` already shells out to git (in `collapse.go`) and is imported by all consumers. Avoided dependency injection or init-time `SetRoot()` — the `sync.Once` lazy discovery is simpler and backward compatible (falls back to `\".\"` in non-git contexts).\n\n### Test results\nAll 10 packages pass, zero failures. Tests are backward compatible because `HubRoot()` returns `\".\"` when run outside a git repo (which test tmpdir contexts are)."},"created_at":"2026-08-04T11:06:11.782965Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.221 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
