{"id":"xpo-f96832","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-58f19d52-0224-434e-9af2-ea57871bf721","text":"## Summary\n\nImplemented worktree-aware merge. When `worktrees: true`, `MergeIssue` skips `CheckoutBranch(base)` (hub is already on main), verifies the hub branch, and removes the worktree after a successful merge.\n\n### Changes\n\n- **`internal/exponential/merge.go`** — Added `IsWorkingTreeCleanIgnoringXpo()` (ignores `.xpo/` changes in clean check), `HubBranch()` (queries hub's current branch via `git -C \u003chub\u003e`). `MergeIssue` now has a worktree path: verifies hub is on default branch, skips checkout, cleans up worktree after merge. Worktree removal always happens regardless of `--keep-branch` (worktrees are ephemeral).\n- **`cmd/exponential/merge.go`** — Added `--no-wt` flag. Clean check uses `IsWorkingTreeCleanIgnoringXpo()` when worktrees enabled (events accumulate uncommitted on hub until merge).\n- **`internal/mcpserver/tools.go`** — Same clean check logic; moved `clientFor()` call earlier to access `Config.Worktrees` before the check.\n\n### Design decisions\n\n- Worktree cleanup is non-fatal: if `WorktreeRemove` fails, it's a warning, not a merge failure. The merge already succeeded.\n- Worktrees are always removed on merge, even with `--keep-branch`. Keeping a branch doesn't mean keeping a directory — you can always `xpo start --force` to recreate the worktree.\n- Hub branch verification: if the hub isn't on main, the merge refuses with a clear message. This catches the case where someone manually checked out a branch on the hub.\n\n### Test results\nAll 10 packages pass, zero failures."},"created_at":"2026-08-04T12:23:19.595423Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.221 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
