{"id":"xpo-f7ea12","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-08-04T12:23:37.761231Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.221 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-f16a94","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"The Board and Backlog views render every issue as a real DOM node. At ~5k issues (100k events), this causes a noticeable ~1s lag when switching views.\n\n## Problem\n\n- Board: each status column mounts all its issues as DOM nodes\n- Backlog: similarly renders every filtered row\n- The DONE column already caps at 5 visible items with a \"+N more\" button, but no other column or the backlog has any render bound\n\n## Approach\n\nApply a render cap to all views — filter/sort the full in-memory dataset first, then only mount the first N DOM nodes. A \"+N more\" button reveals additional batches.\n\n- **Board columns**: cap at ~50 visible items per column\n- **Backlog list**: cap at ~100 visible rows\n\nKey constraint: filtering, sorting, and searching must operate on the **full** issue set in React state. The cap is purely a rendering optimization — the \"+N more\" count reflects remaining *filtered* items, not total.\n\n## Context\n\nStress-tested with a 100k-event project (4,912 issues, 33k comments, 21 MB NDJSON). Event projection into memory takes ~450ms which is fine. The bottleneck is DOM rendering, not data loading.","labels":["improvement","WebApp"],"sort_order":"bMB","status":"PLANNED","title":"Cap rendered issue count in Board and Backlog views"},"created_at":"2026-08-06T07:56:38.617142Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.223 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-ee99a5","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"When transitioning a parent issue to another status, we get a preview window of all sub-issues that would also transition. The table lists ALL story labels, and long titles, causing table cells to wrap. The preview dialog also does not scroll.","labels":["bug"],"sort_order":"bMo","title":"Transition sub-issues preview shows all labels"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:38:56.608956Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
