{"id":"xpo-e928c1","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-43620e23-b857-495d-881d-f42544f6066f","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded `splitLabels()` utility to partition issue labels into **primary** (matching `default_labels` config) and **metadata** (everything else) groups. All three views — backlog, board, and detail sidebar — now render metadata labels first (alphabetically), then primary labels (in config order).\n\nSeveral visual treatments for primary labels were explored during user testing (solid colored background badges, tinted backgrounds, colored indicator strips) but all added visual noise without enough benefit. The final implementation keeps all labels visually identical using the existing `LabelBadge` — only the sort order changes.\n\nA `LabelIndicator` component (small colored strip bars) was built and retained in `Badge.tsx` for potential future use but is not rendered in any view currently.\n\n### Files changed\n\n- `web/src/utils/labels.ts` — `splitLabels()`, `contrastTextColor()`\n- `web/src/components/ui/Badge.tsx` — `LabelIndicator` component\n- `web/src/components/ui/index.ts` — barrel export\n- `web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx` — sorted label rendering\n- `web/src/components/Board/BoardCard.tsx` — sorted label rendering\n- `web/src/components/IssueDetail/PropertySidebar.tsx` — sorted label rendering\n"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T09:14:39.936249Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.224 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
