{"id":"xpo-886099","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-9e053e10-0b7d-409a-990d-051945e191a2","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed the \"Update sub-issues?\" modal to exclude children with status `DONE` from both the preview list and the bulk status update.\n\n### Changes in `Backlog.tsx`\n\n- **`handleQuickStatus`**: Added `\u0026\u0026 i.status !== \"DONE\"` to the child filter. Also counts DONE children separately and passes `doneCount` to the modal state.\n- **`applyStatusChange`**: Added the same `DONE` exclusion to the child filter used during the actual bulk update.\n- **Modal UI**: When DONE children exist, a note is shown below the preview list: \"N completed issue(s) will not be updated.\" If all non-DONE children already match the target status, no modal appears — the parent updates directly.\n\n### Rationale\n\nCompleted work should never be reverted by a parent status cascade. The fix is minimal — three filter additions and a UI note — with no changes to the API or data model.\n"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T09:28:27.677042Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.224 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
