{"id":"xpo-377101","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"relates_to","source_id":"xpo-377101","target_id":"xpo-cd0f62"}],"description":"In Active/Backlog views, when an issue appears both as a real row (in its own status group) and as a ghost parent (in a child's status group), clicking a popover (status, labels, etc.) on either row opens it on both. The popover state is keyed by `issueId`, and the same ID appears twice in the DOM.\n\n**Steps to reproduce:**\n1. Create an epic in DOING with some children in DOING and some in PLANNED\n2. Switch to the Active view\n3. The epic appears as a real row in DOING and as a ghost parent in PLANNED\n4. Click the status dropdown on either row — both open simultaneously\n\n**Expected:** Only the clicked row's popover opens.\n\n**Actual:** Both the real and ghost row react to the popover toggle.","labels":["bug"],"sort_order":"bMg","title":"Ghost parent row duplicates popover when real parent is also visible"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T10:41:45.285858Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.224 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-cd0f62","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T10:41:52.343745Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.224 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-cd0f62","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-a66385ef-1663-4be2-bc78-552fd5cc0445","text":"## Summary\n\nGuarded all parent relationship changes behind the Alt modifier during drag-and-drop. Normal DnD only reorders (`sort_order` and optionally `status`), never touches `parent_id`.\n\n### Changes\n\n**`Backlog.tsx` — `performDrop`**: Only sets/clears `parent_id` when `altHeld` is true. Without Alt, the update payload contains only `sort_order` and optionally `status`.\n\n**`Backlog.tsx` — `handleDndMove`**: Refactored indicator constraint logic into two helpers:\n- `findAfterTree(parentIdx)` — finds the indicator position after a parent's entire child tree\n- `isSiblingPosition(draggedParentId, targetRow, position)` — returns whether a drop position is valid without changing parent\n\nThe main handler now reads top-to-bottom: group headers → self/cross-group skip → raw position → no-op suppression → expanded parent redirect → Alt (any position) → sibling constraint with tree redirect.\n\n**Landing site docs** (`expo-landing`):\n- `keyboard-shortcuts.md` — added Alt+drag unparent row and explanation\n- `parent-sub-issues.md` — added \"Remove from parent\" section with CLI and web board instructions\n\n### Filed separately\n\nxpo-377101 — ghost parent row duplicates popover when real parent is also visible (relates_to)\n"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T11:15:54.925705Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.224 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
