{"id":"xpo-dbdfd3","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T11:24:37.459148Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.224 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-991c8d","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Centralize issue metric calculations (estimates, child counts, label splits)","description":"Computed issue metrics — effective estimates, incomplete points, child counts, label ordering — are calculated independently in multiple places:\n\n- **Backend** (`projection.go`): aggregates parent estimates from all children (ignores DONE status)\n- **Frontend group header** (`useBacklogRows.ts`): recomputes effective estimates with DONE exclusion\n- **Frontend row badge** (`Backlog.tsx`): computes `childPointsTotal - childPointsDone`\n- **Label splitting** (`Backlog.tsx`, `BoardCard.tsx`, `PropertySidebar.tsx`): each view calls `splitLabels()` independently\n\nThis duplication is fragile and has already caused bugs (xpo-dbdfd3). Two options:\n\n1. **Backend API enrichment**: Expose computed fields (`effective_estimate`, `incomplete_points`, `child_done_count`) on the issue API response so the frontend doesn't need to recompute.\n2. **Frontend computation layer**: A shared hook that derives all metrics from the raw issue list once, consumed by all views.\n\nOption 1 is preferred — the backend projection already walks the issue graph, it should expose the correct numbers rather than raw aggregations that the frontend has to fix.","sort_order":"bN8","dependencies":[{"source_id":"xpo-991c8d","target_id":"xpo-dbdfd3","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["improvement"]},"created_at":"2026-08-07T11:30:06.45124Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.224 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-dbdfd3","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-bb1a363d-d2da-46fd-81b4-31db4a40ff3d","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed the status group header story point calculation in `useBacklogRows.ts`. Replaced the fragile `epicIds`-based exclusion with proper effective-estimate logic:\n\n- **Leaf issues**: own `estimate || 1` (unchanged)\n- **Parents with children visible in the group**: skipped entirely (children counted individually, avoids double-counting)\n- **Parents with all children in other groups**: sum of incomplete children's estimates only (excludes DONE)\n\nThe `groupIssueIds` set was hoisted out of the `expandedGroups` block so it's available for both the header calculation and the tree building.\n\nFiled xpo-991c8d to centralize all metric calculations long-term.\n"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T11:30:20.090585Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.224 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
