{"id":"xpo-377101","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-0d902c3e-2234-42a5-8e86-8de9e648cfb7","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed ghost parent popover duplication by changing the popover state key from `issueId` to `rowIndex` in `Backlog.tsx`.\n\nThe root cause was that `openPopover` state was keyed by `issueId`. When the same issue appeared as both a real row and a ghost parent, both rows matched `openPopover?.issueId === issue.id`, so clicking a popover on either row opened it on both.\n\nEach row has a unique index in the `rows` array, so keying by `rowIndex` ensures only the clicked row's popover opens — even when the same issue appears multiple times.\n\nChanges:\n- `openPopover` type: `{ issueId: string, type }` → `{ rowIndex: number, type }`\n- All popover toggle clicks: `issue.id` → row index `i`\n- All popover visibility checks: `openPopover?.issueId === issue.id` → `openPopover?.rowIndex === i`\n- Keyboard handler: `row.issue.id` → `focusedIndexRef.current`"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T12:22:36.016661Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.224 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
