{"id":"xpo-b44c4c","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-d4424b69-551f-4e66-8d5a-6e66116bb1b0","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded two icon-only buttons (Expand All / Collapse All) to the backlog toolbar in `Backlog.tsx`.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Imported `ChevronsUpDown` and `ChevronsDownUp` from `lucide-react`\n- Added `expandAllNodes` callback — clears the `exponential-backlog-nodes-collapsed` localStorage key so all parent nodes expand\n- Added `collapseAllNodes` callback — sets the localStorage key to all `childrenByParent` keys so all parent nodes collapse\n- Rendered the two buttons between the Filter and Sort controls, conditionally visible only when parent issues exist (`childrenByParent.size \u003e 0`)\n- Icons match the MergeView's expand/collapse pattern for consistency\n\n**Rationale:** The existing per-node chevron toggle works well for individual issues, but users with many nested issues needed a quick way to expand or collapse the entire tree. Using localStorage persistence keeps the behavior consistent with the existing node toggle mechanism."},"created_at":"2026-08-07T12:32:51.835729Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.224 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
