{"id":"xpo-2792c3","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-662a83f3-57eb-4748-8b38-41e8412c88e2","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed `SortIssues` in `internal/exponential/projection.go` to sort by `SortOrder` (fractional-index key) instead of `CreatedAt`.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Root sorting now compares `SortOrder` lexicographically, falling back to `CreatedAt` only when sort orders are equal\n- Child sorting within a group uses the same `SortOrder`-first comparison, preserving the existing parent-first guard\n\n**Rationale:** The web UI was already re-sorting client-side via its `sort.ts` manual mode, masking the fact that the server returned creation order. MCP tools and CLI consumed the server order directly, so drag-and-drop reordering in the web UI had no effect on their output. The projection's `backfillSortOrder` already ensures every issue has a non-empty `SortOrder`, so the lexicographic comparison is always well-defined."},"created_at":"2026-08-07T15:34:40.684311Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.224 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
