{"id":"xpo-f16a94","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-d3b8bdb0-9f58-4e96-bcd9-845e96ea2012","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded render caps to both Board and Backlog views to limit DOM nodes.\n\n**Board (`BoardColumn.tsx`):**\n- Added `COLUMN_VISIBLE_COUNT = 50` constant\n- Generalized the existing DONE-column cap pattern to all columns — each column now uses the appropriate cap (5 for DONE, 50 for all others)\n- The existing `showAll` state, `visibleIds` slicing, and \"+N more\" button work unchanged\n\n**Backlog (`Backlog.tsx`):**\n- Added `GROUP_VISIBLE_COUNT = 100` constant\n- Added `showAllGroups` state (`Set\u003cstring\u003e`) to track which status groups have been expanded past the cap\n- Wrapped the `issueRows.map()` in an IIFE that slices to the first 100 rows unless the group is in the \"show all\" set\n- Added a \"+N more\" button after the capped rows, styled with the existing muted-text pattern\n- Original row indices are preserved — the cap only affects which rows are mounted, not their index values, so keyboard navigation, DnD drop indicators, and popover anchoring continue to work correctly\n\n**Rationale:** Pure rendering optimization — filtering, sorting, and searching still operate on the full in-memory dataset. The \"+N more\" button reveals all remaining items in a single click. The DONE column keeps its tighter 5-item cap since completed issues are rarely browsed."},"created_at":"2026-08-07T16:11:15.850238Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.224 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
