{"id":"xpo-ff3cb7","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"In the Issue Detail view, the sub-issues table rows wrap to multiple lines when a child issue has many labels. The labels overflow the row instead of being clipped.\n\n**Steps to reproduce:**\n1. Open a parent issue with sub-issues that have 5+ labels each\n2. Observe the sub-issues table\n\n**Expected:** Rows stay single-line; excess labels are clipped.\n\n**Actual:** Labels cause the row to wrap, producing multi-line rows with broken layout.","labels":["bug"],"sort_order":"a0","status":"DOING","title":"Sub-issues table rows wrap when issue has many labels"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T17:36:22.361072Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.224 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-ff3cb7","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-76612728-ef0f-4d12-a9d5-360285dfc90b","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed row wrapping in `SubIssuesTable.tsx` by:\n\n- Added `overflow-hidden` to the row's `\u003ca\u003e` element to prevent content from expanding the row\n- Changed the spacer `\u003cdiv className=\"flex-1\" /\u003e` to `\u003cdiv className=\"flex-1 shrink-[9999] min-w-0\" /\u003e` so it collapses first when space is tight\n- Wrapped the labels in a container `\u003cdiv className=\"flex items-center gap-1.5 shrink-0 overflow-hidden max-w-[50%]\"\u003e` that clips excess labels and caps at 50% of the row width\n\n**Rationale:** The row was `flex items-center` with no overflow constraint. Labels rendered as direct flex children couldn't be clipped individually. Wrapping them in a constrained container lets the row stay single-line while showing as many labels as fit."},"created_at":"2026-08-07T17:36:32.969294Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.224 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
