{"id":"xpo-7eff79","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"In the Notifications (Inbox) view, issue cards render all labels, causing overflow and clipping when an issue has 5+ labels. Should cap at 2 labels with \"+N\" like the sub-issues table and cascade dialog.","labels":["bug"],"sort_order":"a0","status":"DOING","title":"Notification inbox labels overflow when issue has many labels"},"created_at":"2026-08-07T21:59:52.584151Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.224 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-7eff79","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-22a962ed-55c7-4f76-a0e7-278329484565","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed label overflow in `Inbox.tsx` by applying the same cap pattern used elsewhere: show the first 2 labels, then \"+N\" for any extras.\n\n**Change:** `issue.labels.map(...)` → `issue.labels.slice(0, 2).map(...)` plus a conditional `+{count}` span when `labels.length \u003e 2`."},"created_at":"2026-08-07T21:59:58.479785Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.224 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
