{"id":"xpo-cf75df","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Add worktree isolation guidance to xpo-workflow skill","description":"## Problem\n\nThe generated `xpo-workflow` skill (produced by `GenerateSkillMD()` → `generateWorkflowBody()` in `internal/exponential/agents.go`) doesn't mention worktree isolation for parallel issue work, even though the `start` MCP tool creates worktrees by default and returns the path.\n\nThree gaps:\n\n1. **Step 4 (Start)** tells agents to manually `update` status to DOING — should instead instruct them to call the `start` tool, which handles both the status transition and worktree creation, and returns the `worktree_path`.\n2. **Step 5 (Implement \u0026 Test)** doesn't tell agents that all file operations must happen inside the worktree path returned by `start`.\n3. **MCP tools reference table** (`generateMCPToolsBody()`) is missing `start` and `merge` entries — those tools were added after the table was written.\n\n## Impact\n\nWithout this guidance, agents using the generated workflow skill will:\n- Use `update` instead of `start`, missing worktree creation entirely\n- Edit files in the hub checkout instead of the worktree\n- Have no awareness that parallel issues can be safely isolated via worktrees\n- Not know about the `merge` tool for clean worktree-aware completion\n\n## Fix\n\nUpdate `generateWorkflowBody()` and `generateMCPToolsBody()` in `internal/exponential/agents.go`.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":2,"sort_order":"a5","labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-08-08T12:53:15.959961Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
