{"id":"xpo-cf75df","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-d91709e6-cfc1-46eb-b309-14c4d47f7da2","text":"## Summary\n\nUpdated `generateWorkflowBody()` and `generateMCPToolsBody()` in `internal/exponential/agents.go`:\n\n- **Step 4 (Start)**: replaced the manual `update` instruction with guidance to call the `start` tool, explaining `worktree_path` return, parallel isolation, and `force: true` for resuming.\n- **Step 5 (Implement \u0026 Test)**: added a leading bullet reminding agents to work inside the worktree path.\n- **Step 9 (Complete)**: added `merge` tool guidance for worktree-aware completion (branch merge + cleanup + MERGE event).\n- **MCP tools table**: added `start` and `merge` rows.\n\n**Rationale**: The `start` and `merge` tools were added after the workflow skill text was written. Without this update, agents following the generated skill would use `update` instead of `start`, bypassing worktree creation entirely and editing files in the hub checkout.\n\n**Status**: `make test` passes, `make build` passes."},"created_at":"2026-08-08T12:55:50.277038Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-cf75df","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-661b3381-485e-4de9-bf3e-1a50fafbe088","text":"## Additional change: explicit review gate\n\nAdded three reinforcing stops to prevent agents from blasting through completion comment → walkthrough → commit → merge without user approval:\n\n1. **Step 6 (Completion Comment)**: bold \"Stop here and wait\" callout — the completion comment is a handoff, not a green light.\n2. **Step 8 (Walkthrough)**: prerequisite check — if the user hasn't responded since the completion comment, you're not on this step.\n3. **Step 9 (Complete)**: explicit gate checklist — commit and merge only when user has approved, tests pass, and walkthrough is attached. Silence after a completion comment does not count as approval."},"created_at":"2026-08-08T12:58:02.612738Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-cf75df","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T13:11:44.756833Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-cf75df","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-364a3c16-5ea6-4242-bb75-5e455b7a2626","text":"## Summary (final)\n\nThree changes across two files:\n\n**`internal/exponential/agents.go`** — workflow skill text:\n- Step 4: `start` tool instead of manual `update`, worktree path guidance, parallel isolation\n- Step 5: work inside the worktree path\n- Step 6: explicit \"Stop here and wait\" gate after completion comment\n- Step 8: prerequisite check — user must have responded before writing walkthrough\n- Step 9: `merge` tool for worktree-aware completion, explicit gate checklist\n- MCP tools table: added `start` and `merge` rows\n\n**`internal/exponential/setup.go`** — idempotent init:\n- `InitProject` no longer errors when `.xpo/` exists without `--force`\n- `config.yaml` write guarded by `result.Created || force` — re-running init won't overwrite customizations\n- Everything else (issues.db, gitignore, gitattributes) was already idempotent\n\n**`cmd/exponential/init.go`** — UX:\n- Prints \"`.xpo` directory already exists, refreshing agent configuration\" on re-run\n\n**Rationale**: Existing projects need `xpo init` to be safe to re-run so they can pick up updated skill text. The config.yaml guard is the only change needed — the rest of Phase 1 was already idempotent.\n\n**Status**: `make test` passes, `make build` passes."},"created_at":"2026-08-08T13:12:58.201321Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
