{"id":"xpo-8f7b7a","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-5fa1844e-2588-4982-ba50-19668186875f","text":"## Summary\n\n- Changed `GenerateAgentStub` heading from `# Exponential Agent Instructions` to `# Agent Instructions`\n- Added `HasAgentInstructions()` and `findAgentInstructionsOffset()` helpers that detect both the current and legacy headings\n- Modified `AppendAgentInstructions()` to replace an existing agent instructions section (from heading to EOF) instead of only appending — makes re-running `xpo init` update stale instructions\n- Updated `DetectAgentFiles()` to use the new dual-heading detection\n- Simplified `init.go` to always call `AppendAgentInstructions` (removed the skip-if-exists check)\n- Added 8 new tests covering heading detection, replacement of legacy/current headings, preservation of user content above the section, appending to files without a section, and stub heading verification\n\n## Rationale\n\nThe old approach was purely idempotent — it detected `# Exponential Agent Instructions` and skipped the file entirely. This meant projects that ran `xpo init` before the xpo-workflow skill rule was added (or any other template change) would be stuck with stale instructions forever. The new approach replaces from the heading to EOF, which is safe because agent instructions are always the last section in the file.\n\n## Status\n\nAll tests pass (13 agent tests + full suite).\n"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T13:42:25.597165Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
