{"id":"xpo-408db9","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"`xpo merge` via MCP should default to deleting the branch after merge","description":"## Problem\n\nWhen `merge` is called via the MCP server without explicitly passing `delete_branch: true`, the branch is left behind after a squash merge. The worktree is cleaned up, but the branch persists as dead weight.\n\nThe headless `drive.go` path already passes `DeleteBranch: true`, but the MCP tool defaults to `false` — so agent-driven merges via MCP always leave stale branches.\n\n## Fix\n\nDefault `DeleteBranch` to `true` in the MCP merge handler (`internal/mcpserver/tools.go`) when the caller doesn't explicitly set it.\n","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a5","labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-08-08T13:44:56.91997Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
