{"id":"xpo-408db9","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T13:45:12.33083Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-408db9","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@macbook.local\u003e"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T13:45:18.860323Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-408db9","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-00499671-a252-4b48-b885-f48e2e814c97","text":"## Summary\n\n- Replaced `delete_branch` (opt-in) with `keep_branch` (opt-out) in the MCP merge tool (`internal/mcpserver/tools.go`) and REST API handler (`internal/server/handlers.go`)\n- Both now pass `DeleteBranch: !KeepBranch` to `MergeOptions`, so branches are deleted by default after merge\n- `drive.go` and CLI `merge` command unchanged — they call `MergeOptions` directly with explicit flags\n\n## Rationale\n\nAfter a squash merge, the issue branch is dead weight. The MCP and REST interfaces are used by agents that don't explicitly pass `delete_branch: true`, leaving stale branches. Flipping to opt-out (`keep_branch`) aligns with the default-delete behavior that `drive.go` already used.\n\n## Status\n\nBuild clean, all tests pass.\n"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T13:46:54.419189Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
