{"id":"xpo-5f9ee7","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Problem\n\nWhen issues have many labels, the backlog rows get squished — titles are truncated to just a few characters and other metadata (priority, story points, dates) gets pushed to the edge. The label pills consume all available horizontal space.\n\nThe sub-issues table and notification inbox already cap labels at 2 with a `+N` overflow indicator. The backlog rows and board cards do not.\n\n## Fix\n\nApply the same `.slice(0, 2)` + `+N` overflow pattern used in `SubIssuesTable.tsx` and `Inbox.tsx` to:\n- Backlog row labels (`Backlog.tsx` ~line 1636-1648)\n- Board card labels (`BoardCard.tsx` ~line 140-145)\n","labels":["bug"],"sort_order":"a5","status":"PLANNED","title":"Cap labels at 2 with +N overflow in backlog and board views"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T13:49:55.31523Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
