{"id":"xpo-5f9ee7","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@macbook.local\u003e"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T13:50:14.364571Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-5f9ee7","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-0a66315e-cc01-4b30-8287-0aec8d0817f0","text":"## Summary\n\n- **`Backlog.tsx`** (~line 1636): Combined `metadata` + `primary` label arrays, sliced to 2, added `+N` overflow span\n- **`BoardCard.tsx`** (~line 140): Same pattern applied to board card labels\n\nBoth now match the existing capped rendering in `SubIssuesTable.tsx` and `Inbox.tsx`.\n\n## Rationale\n\nConsistent with the existing `+N` overflow pattern already used in sub-issues table and inbox. Metadata labels render first (they tend to be more specific), then primary labels fill the remaining slots.\n\n## Status\n\nFrontend builds, all tests pass. Ready for visual review.\n"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T13:51:37.767408Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-5f9ee7","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T14:03:35.504641Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-5f9ee7","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-dca50f34-167d-437b-8ce3-4ffd39ab4738","text":"## Summary\n\n- Created `OverflowLabels` component (`web/src/components/ui/OverflowLabels.tsx`) that dynamically measures available row space and fits as many labels as possible\n- Uses a hidden measurer for label widths + `ResizeObserver` on the row for available width\n- Replaced inline label rendering in `Backlog.tsx` with `\u003cOverflowLabels\u003e`\n- Added `data-backlog-row` attribute to the row div for measurement targeting\n- Board cards kept at static cap of 2 (narrow fixed-width context)\n\n## Rationale\n\nA hard cap at 2 wasted space on wide rows and was too aggressive on all row widths. The dynamic approach measures the row width, subtracts fixed elements (id, status, priority, estimate, date, etc.), and fits labels into the remaining space. This adapts to window resizes and varying row content.\n\n## Status\n\nFrontend builds, all tests pass. Ready for visual review — I can't verify the UI myself.\n"},"created_at":"2026-08-08T14:03:44.609317Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
