{"id":"xpo-9091b7","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Fix broken drag-and-drop sorting in backlog views","description":"Drag-and-drop sorting in the backlog is broken across multiple views:\n\n1. **\"All Issues\" — breadcrumbed children are not draggable.** The `isSiblingPosition` guard short-circuits on `depth === 0` before checking shared `parent_id`, so breadcrumbed children (depth 0 with a parent in a different status group) can never show a drop indicator among their siblings.\n\n2. **\"All Issues\" — `performDrop` uses wrong peer set for breadcrumbed children.** Even if draggable, the `depth \u003e 0` branch gate in `performDrop` sends breadcrumbed children (depth 0) into the top-level sorting path, computing `sort_order` against unrelated depth-0 issues instead of actual siblings.\n\n3. **\"Active\"/\"Backlog\" — ghost parents are unsortable and arbitrarily positioned.** Ghost parents have `canDrag = false` and are appended after all top-level issues in `Set` insertion order with no `sort_order`-based positioning.\n\n4. **\"Active\"/\"Backlog\" — child-of-ghost sorting uses invisible cross-status siblings.** `performDrop` computes sibling order from all children of a parent regardless of status, but the visual list only shows same-status children. Invisible siblings shift the computed position.\n\n### Files involved\n- `web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx` — `performDrop`, `isSiblingPosition`, `handleDndMove`, `canDrag`\n- `web/src/components/Backlog/useBacklogRows.ts` — ghost parent ordering","status":"PLANNED","priority":2,"sort_order":"a5","labels":["bug","frontend"]},"created_at":"2026-08-09T12:50:48.294273Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-9091b7","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"created"},"created_at":"2026-08-09T12:51:17.667436Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.226 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-c58af8","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Squash/FF merge overwrites main's issues.db when worktrees disabled","description":"## Bug\n\nWhen `worktrees: false` in `.xpo/config.yaml`, `xpo merge` with squash or ff-only strategy overwrites `issues.db` events on `main` with the feature branch's version.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`.gitattributes` declares `merge=union` for `.xpo/issues.db`, which correctly unions event lines during a 3-way merge (`--no-ff`). However, **squash merges** (`--squash`) and **fast-forward merges** (`--ff-only`) do not invoke the merge driver — they apply the branch's diff directly, replacing main's `issues.db` with the branch's version.\n\nIn the worktree model this isn't a problem because the hub stays on `main` and all `issues.db` writes go to the hub. In non-worktree mode, the feature branch carries its own diverged copy of `issues.db`, and the squash merge stages it over main's.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. Set `worktrees: false` in `.xpo/config.yaml`\n2. Create and start an issue — this creates a feature branch from `main`\n3. On the feature branch, make code changes and commit\n4. Switch back to `main` and make another xpo operation (e.g. merge a different branch, add an issue) — main's `issues.db` now has events the feature branch doesn't\n5. Run `xpo merge` for the first issue (squash strategy)\n6. **Result:** main's `issues.db` loses the events from step 4\n\n## Fix\n\nBefore the squash/ff merge, save main's `issues.db`. After the merge, union the lines from both versions (simulating `merge=union`), then proceed with appending MERGE/DONE events.","status":"PLANNED","priority":1,"sort_order":"a6","labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-08-30T09:33:46.879441Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.251 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
