{"id":"xpo-c58af8","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-60b7960c-d6ed-45cd-b056-b7456ca0ea31","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed `MergeIssue` in `internal/exponential/merge.go` to preserve main's `issues.db` during squash and ff-only merges when worktrees are disabled.\n\n**What changed:**\n- Before the git merge, main's `issues.db` is read into memory when `!useWorktrees` and strategy is squash or ff\n- After the merge, a `unionLines` helper merges both versions — all lines from main, plus any branch-only lines not already present — simulating the `merge=union` driver that git skips for squash/ff\n- The unioned result is written back before MERGE/DONE events are appended\n\n**Files:**\n- `internal/exponential/merge.go` — added pre-merge snapshot, post-merge union, and `unionLines` helper\n- `internal/exponential/merge_test.go` — added `TestMergeIssue_SquashPreservesMainIssuesDB` (end-to-end: diverged issues.db survives squash merge) and `TestUnionLines` (unit tests for the helper)\n\n## Rationale\n\nThe `merge=union` gitattribute only fires during 3-way merges (`--no-ff`). Squash and ff-only merges apply the branch diff directly, which replaces main's `issues.db` with the branch's version. The fix reads main's version before the merge and unions it with whatever the merge produces, matching `merge=union` semantics.\n\n## Status\n\nAll tests passing (including new tests), no regressions. Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-08-30T09:37:36.758624Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.251 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
