{"id":"xpo-9091b7","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"title":"Hierarchy toggle for backlog views with consistent DnD","description":"Backlog drag-and-drop is broken because the current rendering mixes two models — nested children under visible parents and breadcrumbed children at depth 0 — forcing every DnD function to handle both representations of the same relationship.\n\nReplace the hybrid with a per-view toggle (\"Show hierarchy\") that switches between two internally consistent modes:\n\n- **Nested mode:** full parent-child tree with ghost rows for cross-status context. DnD reorders within the tree; Alt-drag reparents.\n- **Flat mode:** everything at depth 0, breadcrumbs for children. DnD is pure flat reordering; no nesting interactions.\n\nEach mode has one data model and one DnD code path. The four existing DnD bugs (breadcrumbed children not draggable, wrong peer set, ghost parents unsortable, cross-status sibling interference) are resolved by eliminating the hybrid that caused them.\n\n### Files involved\n- `web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx` — toggle UI, DnD logic branching on mode\n- `web/src/components/Backlog/useBacklogRows.ts` — row building for nested vs flat mode, ghost row generation"},"created_at":"2026-08-30T10:54:28.440366Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.251 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
