{"id":"xpo-9091b7","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-5bf7090d-8c6d-4037-8363-04585ed72ea0","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded a per-view hierarchy toggle to the backlog that switches between nested (tree) and flat (breadcrumbed) rendering. Each mode has a single consistent data model, eliminating the hybrid that broke DnD.\n\n**`web/src/components/Backlog/useBacklogRows.ts`** — rewritten with `hierarchyMode` parameter:\n- **Flat mode:** all issues at depth 0, breadcrumb for children, no ghosts, no tree recursion\n- **Nested mode, \"All Issues\":** full tree — children nest under their root ancestor in the parent's status group regardless of child status\n- **Nested mode, status tabs:** ghost parents interleaved by `sort_order` (not appended at end), ghost children shown as dimmed context under visible parents\n\n**`web/src/components/Backlog/Backlog.tsx`:**\n- Toggle state per view in `localStorage` (`exponential-backlog-hierarchy-\u003ctab\u003e`), default nested\n- Toggle icon button in toolbar — indented-lines (hierarchy active) vs equal-lines (flat active); expand/collapse buttons hidden in flat mode\n- `canDrag`: ghost children blocked, ghost parents allowed\n- `isSiblingPosition`: flat mode returns true for all same-group rows; nested mode also accepts breadcrumbed siblings sharing `parent_id`\n- `performDrop`: ghost parents never change status; sibling set filtered by status (fixes cross-status interference); uses `parent_id` presence (not just depth) for child detection\n- Alt-drag nesting disabled in flat mode\n- Ghost child rows dimmed (`opacity-50`) like ghost parents\n\n## Rationale\n\nOne toggle, two clean modes. Each mode has one data model and one DnD code path. The four original DnD bugs are resolved by eliminating the hybrid that caused them.\n\n## Status\n\nFrontend builds cleanly, all Go tests pass. Ready for tophat — test the toggle in All Issues, Active, and Backlog tabs with epics that span multiple status groups."},"created_at":"2026-08-30T14:14:38.039299Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.251 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
