{"id":"xpo-7e5f34","type":"CREATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"relates_to","source_id":"xpo-7e5f34","target_id":"xpo-2792c3"}],"description":"Issues created via the MCP `add` tool without an explicit `sort_order` get no sort key, so they sort by creation order instead of appending at the end of their status group.\n\nThe web UI's three creation paths all call `computeAppendKey` to generate a key after the global max. The MCP tool should do the equivalent server-side — compute a sort key that places the new issue at the end of its status group when `sort_order` is not provided in the input.\n\nRelated: xpo-2792c3 (MCP list/show not reflecting backlog sort order — fixed the read side; this fixes the write side).","labels":["bug"],"sort_order":"bNa","status":"BACKLOG","title":"MCP `add` tool should set default sort_order"},"created_at":"2026-08-31T11:00:24.032231Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.251 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-65e8e3","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add a fourth tab \"Done\" alongside \"All Issues\", \"Active\", and \"Backlog\" that shows only completed issues (status = DONE).\n\nCurrently, DONE issues are visible in the \"All Issues\" tab under a collapsed group, but there's no dedicated view for browsing completed work. A dedicated tab makes it easier to review what's been shipped, search through completed issues, and audit history.\n\n### Scope\n- New tab in `TAB_CONFIGS` with `statuses: [\"DONE\"]`\n- Same flat/nested toggle support as other tabs\n- Default sort by `updated` (most recently completed first), matching the existing DONE group behaviour in \"All Issues\"\n- Hierarchy mode persisted independently (`exponential-backlog-hierarchy-done`)","labels":["feature","frontend"],"sort_order":"a5","status":"PLANNED","title":"Add \"Done\" view tab to the backlog"},"created_at":"2026-08-31T11:01:10.559204Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.251 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-a18d46","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add an optional `resolution` field to issues, set during the DONE transition. This separates workflow state (status) from outcome (resolution).\n\n### Resolution values\n\n`completed` (default), `duplicate`, `wont_fix`, `cannot_reproduce`\n\n### UI: \"Complete Issue\" dialog\n\nTriggered whenever an issue transitions to DONE — via status popover, drag-and-drop to DONE group, or cascade prompt. The dialog contains:\n\n- **Resolution** dropdown (default: `completed`)\n- **Completion comment** text field (optional, markdown)\n- **Complete** / **Cancel** buttons\n\nIf the issue has children, the existing cascade prompt (\"Update sub-issues?\") should integrate with or precede the completion dialog.\n\nThe happy path (just hit Complete with defaults) should be zero-friction — the dialog appears but completing with \"completed\" resolution and no comment requires a single click.\n\n### Status icon variants\n\nDONE issues with non-default resolution should show a subtle visual distinction:\n\n- `completed` — standard green checkmark (existing)\n- `duplicate` — duplicate/copy icon or overlaid indicator\n- `wont_fix` — strikethrough or crossed-out variant\n- `cannot_reproduce` — question mark variant or similar\n\n### Data model\n\n- `resolution` field on the Issue model (string, optional, only meaningful when status = DONE)\n- UPDATE event payload gains optional `resolution` field\n- Clearing resolution (reopening) should clear it automatically when status moves away from DONE\n\n### MCP / CLI\n\n- `update` tool accepts `resolution` field (validated: must be one of the enum values)\n- `merge` tool: resolution defaults to `completed` (a successful merge is always a completion)\n- `show` / `list` tools return `resolution` when set\n- `list` tool gains `--resolution` filter\n\n### Board view\n\nBoard cards in the DONE column should show the resolution icon variant. Dragging to DONE column should trigger the same completion dialog.","labels":["feature","frontend","Backend"],"sort_order":"a6","status":"PLANNED","title":"Issue resolution field and completion dialog"},"created_at":"2026-08-31T11:06:30.114878Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.251 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-7e5f34","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"PLANNED"},"created_at":"2026-08-31T11:06:55.790079Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"xpo-7e5f34","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"title":"MCP and CLI `add` should set default sort_order","description":"Issues created via the MCP `add` tool or the CLI `xpo add` without an explicit `sort_order` get no sort key, so they sort by creation order instead of appending at the end of their status group.\n\nThe web UI's three creation paths all call `computeAppendKey` to generate a key after the global max. The backend should do the equivalent server-side — compute a sort key that places the new issue at the end of its status group when `sort_order` is not provided in the input.\n\nThis affects both:\n- MCP `add` tool (`internal/mcpserver/tools.go`)\n- CLI `xpo add` command (`cmd/exponential/add.go`)\n\nRelated: xpo-2792c3 (MCP list/show not reflecting backlog sort order — fixed the read side; this fixes the write side).","sort_order":"Zu"},"created_at":"2026-08-31T13:06:23.494261Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.251 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
