{"id":"xpo-748873","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"sort_order":"bO2V"},"created_at":"2026-08-31T11:21:12.198245Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"xpo-a49ec2","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"title":"Dependencies view: interactive dependency graph","description":"Replace the flat dependency table in the web UI with an interactive directed graph visualization.\n\n### Requirements\n\n- Render `blocks` / `blocked_by` / `depends_on` relationships as a DAG\n- Nodes show: status icon (color-coded), title (truncated), issue ID\n- Resolved blockers (DONE) shown with muted/strikethrough styling\n- Critical path highlighted: which issues need to unblock first\n- Circular dependencies shown as warnings\n- Clicking a node navigates to the issue detail\n- Summary line: \"N of M blockers resolved\"\n\n### Design direction\n\nGraph/chart visualization (not a table or tree). Consider using inline SVG with a simple layered layout — dependencies flow left-to-right or top-to-bottom. Nodes are compact cards, edges are directed arrows. Status coloring makes blocker state visible at a glance.\n\n### Scope\n\n- Replaces the current dependency list/table on the issue detail view\n- Also consider a standalone \"Dependencies\" page showing the full project dependency graph (filtered by epic or status)\n\nConsolidates xpo-8d6b52 (status-aware relationship display) into this issue.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":3,"sort_order":"Zwl","labels":["feature","frontend"]},"created_at":"2026-08-31T11:25:24.75499Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.251 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-8d6b52","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-08-31T11:24:58.365055Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.251 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-8d6b52","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-451929da-c9b2-43a7-ae3a-3bc8613108ad","text":"Consolidated into xpo-a49ec2 — the graph visualization subsumes status-aware display as a core feature (status-colored nodes, resolved blocker styling)."},"created_at":"2026-08-31T11:25:04.727118Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.251 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
