{"id":"xpo-ceb434","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Summary\n\nSplit the current `xpo init` command into focused subcommands with clear responsibilities, and update `xpo doctor` to match.\n\n## Current Behavior\n\n`xpo init` does too many things: writes the `.xpo.toml` config, modifies `CLAUDE.md`, and installs project skills — all in one shot.\n\n## Proposed Changes\n\n### 1. `xpo init` — config only\n- Write `.xpo.toml` (or equivalent config) into the project root\n- **Do not** touch `CLAUDE.md`\n- **Do not** install project skills\n\n### 2. `xpo init skill` — skill installation\n- New subcommand dedicated to installing the xpo skill into an agent harness\n- Prompt the user: install **globally** (user-level) or **locally** (project-level)?\n- Support different agent harnesses (e.g. Claude Code, Cursor, Windsurf, etc.) and take the appropriate installation path for each\n- Should be idempotent — safe to re-run\n\n### 3. `xpo doctor` — updated checks\n- Reflect the new split: check config separately from skill installation\n- Report which harness is detected and whether the skill is installed (globally, locally, or not at all)\n- Guide the user to the correct fix command (`xpo init` vs `xpo init skill`)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `xpo init` writes config only — no side effects on `CLAUDE.md` or skill files\n- [ ] `xpo init skill` installs the skill, respecting the user's scope choice (global vs local)\n- [ ] `xpo init skill` handles at least Claude Code; architecture supports adding more harnesses\n- [ ] `xpo doctor` distinguishes between missing config and missing skill installation\n- [ ] Existing projects that already ran the old `xpo init` continue to work","labels":["feature","CLI"],"sort_order":"a5","status":"PLANNED","title":"Separate `xpo init` from skill installation"},"created_at":"2026-09-06T08:08:40.59792088Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.259 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-cb6b49","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Problem\n\nA recurring workflow failure:\n\n1. User has scratch files on `main` (e.g. `idea.md`, `thoughts.md`) from AI discussions\n2. A feature issue is created and `xpo start` creates a worktree off `main`\n3. Work is completed in the worktree, tests pass\n4. `xpo merge` fails because the hub checkout (`main`) is not clean — untracked or modified files block the merge\n5. **The agent panics** — it starts stashing on `main`, stashing on the worktree, and generally thrashing. This corrupts history and is especially destructive because `.xpo/issue.db` updates from the worktree are designed to land on `main` — stashing those changes breaks the database sync\n\nThis has happened multiple times. The root cause is that `xpo merge` is too strict about hub cleanliness, and agents have no recovery path that doesn't make things worse.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n`xpo merge` should succeed when untracked files on the hub checkout don't conflict with the incoming branch. Specifically:\n\n- **Untracked files** that don't exist in the merge branch: ignore them entirely — they're not in conflict\n- **Modified tracked files** that don't conflict with the merge: auto-stash before merge, pop after (or warn and proceed)\n- **Actual conflicts**: fail with a clear, actionable error message that tells the agent exactly what to do (and what NOT to do)\n\n## Design Considerations\n\n- The error message on failure is critical — agents read it and act on it. A vague \"working tree not clean\" produces the stash-thrashing loop. A specific \"file X conflicts with incoming branch; commit or remove it before merging\" gives agents a narrow, safe action\n- `.xpo/issue.db` must never be stashed or reset — it flows from worktree to hub by design\n- Consider using `git merge --no-commit` + check + `git merge --continue` pattern to inspect before finalizing\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `xpo merge` succeeds when hub has untracked files that don't conflict with the merge branch\n- [ ] `xpo merge` succeeds when hub has modified tracked files that don't conflict\n- [ ] On actual conflicts, the error message is specific and agent-safe (no ambiguous \"not clean\" messages)\n- [ ] `.xpo/issue.db` is never stashed or discarded during merge\n- [ ] Existing clean-hub merges continue to work unchanged","labels":["bug","CLI","dx"],"sort_order":"a6","status":"PLANNED","title":"`xpo merge` should tolerate untracked files on the hub checkout"},"created_at":"2026-09-06T09:02:49.828816032Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.259 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
