{"id":"xpo-cb6b49","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@nicbet.local\u003e"},"created_at":"2026-09-06T15:49:45.897728978Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.259 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-cb6b49","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-40a04a22-b7c8-4978-bc0b-5c6677c1de1a","text":"## Summary\n\nReplaced the overly strict `IsWorkingTreeCleanIgnoringXpo()` pre-merge check with `HubCleanForMerge(branch)`, which categorizes dirty files instead of rejecting them all:\n\n- **`.xpo/` files** — ignored (unchanged behavior)\n- **Untracked files (`??`)** — now ignored. Git merge itself will catch real collisions with a specific error.\n- **Modified tracked files** — only blocked if they overlap with files changed on the merge branch (checked via `git diff --name-only base...branch`)\n\n### Files changed\n\n- `internal/exponential/merge.go` — deleted `IsWorkingTreeCleanIgnoringXpo()`, added `HubCleanForMerge(branch)`, updated merge failure message to be agent-safe (\"Do NOT stash or reset\")\n- `cmd/exponential/merge.go` — replaced branching worktree/non-worktree check with single `HubCleanForMerge()` call\n- `internal/mcpserver/tools.go` — same replacement; restructured to resolve issue before the check so branch name is available\n- `internal/server/handlers.go` — updated `handleMergeability` and `handleMergeIssue` to use `HubCleanForMerge()`\n- `internal/exponential/merge_test.go` — added 5 new tests covering: clean tree, untracked files allowed, .xpo changes allowed, non-conflicting modifications allowed, conflicting modifications blocked with specific error\n\n### Rationale\n\nThe old check treated any non-`.xpo/` dirty file as a blocker. Untracked scratch files (e.g. `idea.md`) on `main` would fail the merge, and the generic error message (\"commit or stash them first\") caused agents to stash indiscriminately — corrupting `.xpo/issues.db` and polluting git history.\n\n### Decisions made\n\n- Kept `IsWorkingTreeClean()` for `drive.go` (different concern — general preflight, not merge-specific)\n- Error messages explicitly include \"Do NOT stash\" to short-circuit agent stash-thrashing\n- The conflict check uses `git diff --name-only base...branch` (three-dot) to compare only the branch's divergent changes\n\n### Status\n\nAll tests passing (including 5 new ones), full suite green, ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-09-06T15:54:44.286154371Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.259 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-67a1c4","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"`computeBranchStats` misses uncommitted changes in worktrees","description":"## Problem\n\n`computeBranchStats` in `internal/exponential/branches.go` only detects uncommitted changes when `branch == CurrentBranch()` (line 142). In worktree mode, the server runs from the hub checkout which is on `main`, not the issue's branch — so `fillUncommittedStats` never fires for worktree branches.\n\nThis means:\n- A worktree with uncommitted changes shows `commits: 0, has_uncommitted: false`\n- The merge view button in the web UI requires `commits \u003e 0 || has_uncommitted` — so it never appears until you commit\n- You can't use the merge view to review changes before committing\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n`computeBranchStats` should detect uncommitted changes inside a worktree directory when the branch has 0 commits ahead of base. The merge view button should appear as soon as there are changes (committed or not) in the worktree.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`fillUncommittedStats` runs `git diff --shortstat HEAD` and `git diff --shortstat --cached` in the current working directory. In worktree mode, these commands need to target the worktree directory (via `git -C \u003cworktree_path\u003e`) instead of the hub.\n\n## Fix\n\nWhen `commits == 0` and the branch has a worktree (detectable via `FindWorktreeForBranch`), run the uncommitted stats commands with `git -C \u003cworktree_path\u003e` instead of relying on `CurrentBranch()`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Worktree branches with uncommitted changes show `has_uncommitted: true` in branch stats\n- [ ] The merge view button appears for worktree issues with uncommitted changes\n- [ ] Non-worktree (checkout) mode behavior is unchanged","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a5","labels":["bug","frontend","Backend"]},"created_at":"2026-09-06T18:54:23.220764351Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.259 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-3bfbc8","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Walkthrough tab in the merge view","description":"## Summary\n\nAdd a \"Walkthrough\" tab to the merge view that renders the issue's `spec.md` walkthrough content. When a walkthrough exists, it should be the default active tab — the reviewer sees the narrative explanation of what was built before diving into diffs.\n\n## Rationale\n\nThe walkthrough is the durable implementation record: what was built, why, how the pieces fit together, and key decisions. Surfacing it in the merge view makes it the natural pre-merge reading, right alongside the commits and diffs. Currently walkthroughs are only accessible via the CLI (`xpo walkthrough read`), which means reviewers have to go out of their way to find them.\n\n## Behavior\n\n- Add a \"Walkthrough\" tab alongside the existing tabs (Commits, Files, Diff, etc.)\n- Render the walkthrough markdown content in the tab\n- If a walkthrough exists, make it the default active tab when opening the merge view\n- If no walkthrough exists, fall back to the current default tab\n- The tab should not appear if no walkthrough is attached to the issue\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Walkthrough tab appears in the merge view when the issue has a walkthrough\n- [ ] Tab renders the walkthrough markdown\n- [ ] Walkthrough tab is the default when present\n- [ ] Tab is hidden when no walkthrough exists\n- [ ] Existing merge view behavior unchanged for issues without walkthroughs","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a6","labels":["feature","frontend"]},"created_at":"2026-09-06T19:01:08.338770135Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.259 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
