{"id":"xpo-67a1c4","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-945c40b0-c404-4c48-860a-daa8fa178be2","text":"## Summary\n\nModified `fillUncommittedStats` in `internal/exponential/branches.go` to accept a `dir` parameter. When non-empty, all git commands use `git -C \u003cdir\u003e` to target that directory instead of the current working directory.\n\nUpdated `computeBranchStats` to check for a worktree via `FindWorktreeForBranch` when `commits == 0` and the branch is not the current branch. If a worktree exists, `fillUncommittedStats` is called with the worktree path.\n\n## Rationale\n\nMinimal change — a single new parameter and one new `else if` branch. The `gitCmd` helper inside `fillUncommittedStats` keeps the diff logic clean while supporting both modes (hub CWD and remote worktree directory).\n\n## Decisions made\n\nNone beyond the spec. The approach matches the issue's suggested fix exactly.\n\n## Status\n\n- `make test` — all tests pass\n- `make cli` — compiles cleanly\n- Ready for review"},"created_at":"2026-09-06T19:07:08.724028948Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.259 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
