{"id":"xpo-3bfbc8","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-687d58d8-cd20-4ec3-aee0-8e1cd1a95c14","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded a \"Walkthrough\" tab to `MergeView.tsx` that renders the issue's `walkthrough.md` as Markdown. When a walkthrough artifact exists on the issue, it becomes the default active tab — the reviewer sees the narrative explanation before diving into diffs.\n\nChanges in `web/src/components/IssueDetail/MergeView.tsx`:\n- Extended the `Tab` type with `\"walkthrough\"`\n- Added `hasWalkthrough` check against `issue.artifacts`\n- Fetch walkthrough content via existing `fetchArtifactContent` in the data-load `useEffect`\n- Added walkthrough tab header with `BookOpen` icon, rendered first (before Commits/Files/Conversation), only when a walkthrough exists\n- Added walkthrough content pane using `react-markdown` with `remarkGfm` and `remarkBreaks`, styled with `prose-exponential`\n- Default tab is `\"walkthrough\"` when present, falls back to `\"files\"` otherwise\n\n## Rationale\n\nReused the exact same patterns from `IssueDetail.tsx` — same API call (`fetchArtifactContent`), same markdown rendering stack, same CSS class. No new dependencies or backend changes needed.\n\n## Decisions made\n\nNone beyond the spec.\n\n## Status\n\n- `make frontend` — builds cleanly\n- `make test` — all tests pass\n- Ready for review"},"created_at":"2026-09-06T19:49:20.656869639Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.259 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-90b533","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Worktree diff/files API endpoints ignore worktree directory","description":"## Problem\n\n`GetWorkingTreeDiffText()` and `ListWorkingTreeFilesChanged()` in `internal/exponential/review.go` run `git diff HEAD` without `-C \u003cworktree\u003e`, so they execute against the server's working directory (the main repo root) instead of the issue's worktree.\n\nThis means the merge view shows \"Files changed (1)\" in the tab badge (computed correctly by `computeBranchStats` which *is* worktree-aware) but the actual file tree and diff content are empty.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nSame class of bug as xpo-67a1c4. The worktree-aware fix was applied to `computeBranchStats` in `branches.go` but the review endpoints were not updated.\n\nAffected functions:\n- `GetWorkingTreeDiffText()` (review.go ~line 173) — runs `git diff HEAD` without `-C`\n- `ListWorkingTreeFilesChanged()` (review.go ~line 205) — runs `git diff --numstat HEAD` / `git diff --name-status HEAD` without `-C`\n- `handleGetIssueFiles` (handlers.go ~line 949) — calls the above without passing worktree path\n- `handleGetIssueDiff` (handlers.go ~line 974) — calls the above without passing worktree path\n\n## Fix\n\n1. Add a `dir` parameter to `GetWorkingTreeDiffText` and `ListWorkingTreeFilesChanged` (and the underlying `listFilesChangedFromDiff`)\n2. When `dir` is non-empty, prepend `-C \u003cdir\u003e` to git commands (same pattern as `fillUncommittedStats`)\n3. In the handlers, resolve the worktree path via `FindWorktreeForBranch` and pass it through\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Merge view file list shows changed files for worktree branches with uncommitted changes\n- [ ] Merge view diff shows actual diff content for worktree branches\n- [ ] Non-worktree behavior unchanged","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a5","dependencies":[{"source_id":"xpo-90b533","target_id":"xpo-3bfbc8","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug","Backend"]},"created_at":"2026-09-06T20:19:11.789635412Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.259 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-90b533","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING"},"created_at":"2026-09-06T20:19:15.989080113Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.259 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-90b533","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@arch.local\u003e"},"created_at":"2026-09-06T20:19:22.335832018Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.259 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-90b533","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-0803cea0-e02f-453a-a136-087b250c835d","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded a `dir` parameter to `GetWorkingTreeDiffText` and `ListWorkingTreeFilesChanged` in `internal/exponential/review.go`. When non-empty, all git commands use `git -C \u003cdir\u003e` to target the worktree directory instead of the server's cwd.\n\nUpdated `handleGetIssueFiles` and `handleGetIssueDiff` in `internal/server/handlers.go` to resolve the worktree path via `FindWorktreeForBranch` before calling the diff/files functions.\n\n## Rationale\n\nSame pattern as the xpo-67a1c4 fix for `fillUncommittedStats` — propagate the worktree directory to git commands that need it.\n\n## Decisions made\n\n- `FindWorktreeForBranch` returns `(\"\", false)` for non-worktree branches. Passing `\"\"` to the updated functions preserves the original behavior (no `-C` flag), so the non-worktree path is unchanged with no extra branching needed.\n\n## Status\n\n- `make test` — all tests pass\n- Ready for review"},"created_at":"2026-09-06T20:20:29.742361953Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.259 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-ebb248","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Hide branch SHA when issue has no commits","description":"## Problem\n\nWhen an issue branch has 0 commits (only uncommitted worktree changes), the UI shows the base branch's HEAD SHA as the \"branch head.\" This is technically correct but confusing — it looks like the branch has its own commit when it doesn't.\n\n## Desired Behavior\n\n- **Board / backlog cards**: Show only the branch icon, no SHA badge, when `commits == 0`\n- **Detail view / merge view**: Show \"No commits — uncommitted changes only\" instead of the SHA when `commits == 0 \u0026\u0026 has_uncommitted`\n\n## Rationale\n\nThe SHA is only meaningful when the branch has diverged from base. Showing it at 0 commits adds visual noise and suggests work has been committed when it hasn't.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Board cards with 0 commits show branch icon without SHA\n- [ ] Detail/merge view shows descriptive text instead of SHA when `commits == 0`\n- [ ] Cards/views with commits \u003e 0 still show the SHA as before","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a5","labels":["enhancement","frontend"]},"created_at":"2026-09-06T20:25:10.447031371Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.259 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-2d6b57","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Diff output breaks with `diff.mnemonicPrefix` git config","description":"## Problem\n\nWhen the user has `diff.mnemonicPrefix = true` in their git config, `git diff` uses context-dependent prefixes (`c/`/`w/` for commit/worktree, `i/` for index, etc.) instead of the standard `a/`/`b/`. The frontend's `parseDiffByFile` regex matches ` b/(.+)$` to extract filenames, which fails with non-standard prefixes — resulting in an empty file tree and diff viewer despite the \"Files changed\" badge showing the correct count.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`GetWorkingTreeDiffText` and `GetDiffText` in `internal/exponential/review.go` run bare `git diff` without forcing standard prefixes. The frontend parser assumes `a/`/`b/`.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd `--src-prefix=a/` and `--dst-prefix=b/` flags to all `git diff` commands that produce raw diff text (not `--numstat`/`--name-status` which are unaffected). This normalizes output regardless of user git config.\n\nAffected functions:\n- `GetWorkingTreeDiffText` (review.go)\n- `GetDiffText` (review.go)\n- `GetCommitDiffText` (review.go)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Merge view shows file tree and diffs when `diff.mnemonicPrefix = true`\n- [ ] Merge view still works when `diff.mnemonicPrefix` is not set\n- [ ] Commit-level diffs also work with mnemonic prefixes","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a6","dependencies":[{"source_id":"xpo-2d6b57","target_id":"xpo-90b533","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug","Backend"]},"created_at":"2026-09-06T21:11:54.379067775Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.259 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
