{"id":"xpo-ebb248","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-f7751401-866e-41c0-9cc9-cc09feb766ec","text":"## Implementation complete\n\n**Summary**\n\nTwo files changed:\n\n- **`web/src/components/ui/BranchBadge.tsx`** — the SHA text (`head_sha.slice(0, 6)`) now only renders when `commits \u003e 0`. At 0 commits the badge shows just the branch icon (plus the existing amber dot for uncommitted changes).\n\n- **`web/src/components/IssueDetail/PropertySidebar.tsx`** — the SHA pill in the branch stats card now has three states:\n  - `commits \u003e 0`: shows the SHA pill (truncated to 7 chars, matching git convention)\n  - `commits == 0 \u0026\u0026 has_uncommitted`: shows italic \"uncommitted changes only\" label\n  - `commits == 0 \u0026\u0026 !has_uncommitted`: hidden entirely\n\n**Rationale**\n\nMinimal, targeted changes — the conditional logic already existed in `BranchBadge` (`hasCommits` / `hasUncommitted` flags), so the SHA display just needed to be gated behind the same check. The detail sidebar needed a ternary to distinguish the three states.\n\n**Status** — frontend builds, all tests pass, ready for review.\n"},"created_at":"2026-09-07T06:20:56.433886Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
