{"id":"xpo-ebb248","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-09-07T06:44:15.459562Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-d6b4de","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Problem\n\nWhen modifying code that was shaped by a prior design decision, an agent needs to understand *why* it was built that way before changing it. Today the path is: notice something in the code → `git blame` to find the issue ID → `show` + `walkthrough read`. That's three hops and requires already knowing which file to blame.\n\nThere's no way to ask \"what design rationale exists around branch badges?\" and get relevant fragments back.\n\n## Proposed Solution\n\nAdd a new MCP tool (e.g. `rationale` or `search`) that does full-text search across all specs and walkthroughs in `.xpo/artifacts/*/spec.md` and `walkthrough.md`.\n\n### Interface\n\n```\nxpo rationale --query \"branch badge display\"\n```\n\nReturns matching fragments with:\n- Issue ID and title\n- Which document matched (spec or walkthrough)\n- The relevant section/paragraph\n- Match context (surrounding lines)\n\n### Search signals\n\n- Full-text match against spec and walkthrough markdown content\n- Issue title and labels as boosting signals\n- Recency as a tiebreaker (more recent issues ranked higher)\n\n### MCP tool shape\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"rationale\",\n  \"parameters\": {\n    \"query\": \"free-text search query\",\n    \"limit\": \"max results (default 5)\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Rationale\n\nThis enables agents to efficiently check prior design rationale before writing a spec or modifying existing behavior. Without it, the xpo-workflow skill can't practically ask agents to \"check related rationale\" because there's no efficient way to find it.\n\nA lightweight implementation (full-text search with ranking) would already be a big step up — embeddings/vector search can come later if needed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] New MCP tool `rationale` that searches spec and walkthrough content\n- [ ] Returns issue ID, title, document type, and matching fragment\n- [ ] Results ranked by relevance (text match + title/label boost + recency)\n- [ ] CLI equivalent (`xpo rationale --query \"...\"`)\n","labels":["feature","mcp"],"sort_order":"a5","status":"PLANNED","title":"MCP tool: search across specs and walkthroughs"},"created_at":"2026-09-07T06:50:24.796278Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
