{"id":"xpo-5a17a7","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-dc12dedc-721c-4387-a402-7c91c6f66e05","text":"**Summary:** Added filtered empty state to `Backlog.tsx`. When `filteredIssues` is empty but the project has issues, the view now shows a contextual `EmptyState` instead of a blank area.\n\nTwo cases are handled:\n- **Tab has no matching statuses** — tab-specific message (e.g. \"No active issues\" / \"Issues that are Planned, In Progress, or Blocked will appear here.\")\n- **User filters/search exclude everything** — generic \"No matching issues\" / \"Try adjusting your filters or search.\"\n\n**Rationale:** Mirrors the pattern already used in `MyIssues.tsx`. Reuses the existing `EmptyState` component and the dashed-rectangle SVG icon for visual consistency.\n\n**Decisions made:** None beyond the spec.\n\n**Status:** Frontend builds clean, all tests pass. Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-09-07T06:57:37.031953Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
