{"id":"xpo-b109e5","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-0199acba-30f1-4603-bb43-9b04fd217a19","text":"**Summary:** Added a `.filter()` to the ghost child construction in `useBacklogRows.ts` nested mode. Ghost children are now excluded when their status is outside the current tab's `visibleStatuses`.\n\n**Rationale:** The existing code showed all children of a real parent as ghost rows regardless of status. This is correct for the \"All Issues\" tab (all statuses visible), but in filtered tabs like Active it caused DONE children to appear as ghost rows — contradicting the filter.\n\n**Decisions made:** None beyond the spec.\n\n**Status:** Frontend builds clean, all tests pass. Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-09-07T07:01:05.195943Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-b109e5","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"action":"updated","artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md"},"created_at":"2026-09-07T07:04:04.334074Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-b109e5","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-749a5681-97a2-4cd8-b1c0-d5c873c61ffc","text":"**Summary:** Two changes in `useBacklogRows.ts` and `Backlog.tsx`:\n\n1. **Correctness fix:** Ghost children are now filtered by `visibleStatuses` — a DONE child no longer appears under a DOING parent in the Active tab.\n2. **Toggle:** \"Show ghost items\" option in the view menu (nested mode only). Defaults to on. When off, all ghost parents and ghost children are hidden. Persisted to `localStorage`.\n\n**Rationale:** The `visibleStatuses` filter is the baseline correctness fix. The toggle gives users control over whether they want tree context at all — some find ghosts helpful, others find them noisy.\n\n**Decisions made:** Toggle is global (not per-tab) since ghost visibility is a layout preference, not a per-view filter. Placed after \"Show empty groups\" in the menu since they're related layout options.\n\n**Status:** Frontend builds clean, all tests pass. Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-09-07T07:05:26.986999Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-b109e5","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"action":"updated","artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md"},"created_at":"2026-09-07T07:10:41.911801Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-b109e5","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-3f26b927-320f-4f60-a84f-7d1cdc8467fa","text":"**Updated approach after review.**\n\n**Summary:** Ghost children are now filterable by the tab's `visibleStatuses` via a \"Cross-status ghosts\" toggle in the view options menu (nested mode only).\n\nChanges in `useBacklogRows.ts`:\n- Ghost child filter: `groupIssueIds.has(c.id) || showGhosts || visibleStatuses.includes(c.status)`\n- Toggle on (default): all ghost children shown (original behavior)\n- Toggle off: only ghost children within the tab's statuses shown\n- Ghost parents always show — they provide structural context for orphaned children and don't affect DnD\n\nChanges in `Backlog.tsx`:\n- `showGhosts` state with `localStorage` persistence\n- \"Cross-status ghosts\" toggle in view menu, nested mode only\n\n**Decisions made:**\n- Ghost parents are never filtered — removing them would orphan real children or require promoting them to top-level (which breaks DnD sort ordering)\n- Toggle defaults to on to preserve existing behavior\n- Label is \"Cross-status ghosts\" rather than \"Show ghost items\" since ghosts always show — the toggle controls scope\n\n**Status:** Frontend builds clean, all tests pass. Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-09-07T07:10:49.393465Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
