{"id":"xpo-9ba68b","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-18a291b6-90d2-458d-8410-693f0a0a82cb","text":"## Summary\n\n- Exported `ComputePulseMetrics` and all related types from `internal/server/metrics.go` (capitalized type names: `PulseMetrics`, `AttentionItem`, `WorkloadEntry`, etc.)\n- Added `cmd/exponential/pulse.go` — new `xpo pulse` CLI command with `--json` flag\n- Added `internal/ui/pulse.go` — lipgloss box-drawing renderer with color-coded values (green/yellow/red thresholds)\n- Added `internal/ui/pulse_test.go` — tests for rendering and `formatDuration`\n- Updated `internal/server/metrics_test.go` to use exported constant names\n\n## Rationale\n\nReuses the existing `ComputePulseMetrics` function from the server package rather than reimplementing metrics. The CLI reads events directly via `storage.ReadEvents()` — no web server needed. Avoided an import cycle (`ui` → `server` → `exponential` → `ui`) by defining a flat `PulseData` struct in the `ui` package and mapping from `PulseMetrics` in the CLI command.\n\n## Decisions made\n\n- Added `Throughput` as a 6th metric row (issues/wk) since the data was already computed and complements velocity (points vs count)\n- Used rounded box border (`lipgloss.RoundedBorder()`) for a clean look matching the mockup style\n- Dropped the \"Agent / Human\" line from the mockup — `ComputePulseMetrics` doesn't compute that split, and adding it would expand scope\n\n## Status\n\nAll tests passing (`make test`), `xpo pulse` and `xpo pulse --json` both work. Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-09-07T07:26:21.050596Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
