{"id":"xpo-d82dc7","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-87f372c9-6d72-41ae-bf7c-aede6df5ed09","text":"## Summary\n\nRestructured `xpo history` into a unified timeline command with two modes:\n\n- **`xpo history \u003cid\u003e`** — rich, human-readable activity timeline for a single issue\n- **`xpo history`** (no args) — project-wide timeline across all issues (last 50 events by default)\n\nNew flags: `--json` (JSONL output), `--reverse` (newest first), `--since \u003cduration\u003e` (e.g. `24h`, `7d`, `2w`), `--limit N` (global mode only).\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `cmd/exponential/history.go` — rewired to support both modes with new flags\n- `cmd/exponential/duration.go` — `parseDuration()` helper for `--since` (supports `m`, `h`, `d`, `w`)\n- `internal/ui/timeline.go` — new `RenderTimeline()` with rich per-event descriptions, `FormatActor()` with on_behalf_of support, `DescribeEvent()`, `RenderTimelineJSON()`\n- Removed `internal/ui/history.go` (old table renderer) — no remaining callers\n- `internal/ui/helpers_test.go` — moved `captureStdout` here (was only in deleted `history_test.go`)\n- `internal/ui/timeline_test.go` — 18 tests covering all event types, actor formatting, JSON output, text wrapping\n- `cmd/exponential/duration_test.go` — 7 tests for duration parsing\n\n## Rationale\n\nSingle command with `--json` is simpler than separate `xpo history` / `xpo log` commands. The `--json` flag pattern already exists on `pulse`, `comment`, `add`, and `update`. The timeline rendering mirrors the web UI's `ActivityTimeline.tsx` — expanding UPDATE events to show specific field changes, rendering full comment text in bordered blocks, and handling MERGE events (which the old renderer missed entirely).\n\n## Decisions made\n\n- Put `parseDuration` in `cmd/exponential` (not a new `internal/cli` package) since it's only used by the command\n- `captureStdout` test helper moved to `helpers_test.go` rather than duplicating it\n\n## Status\n\nAll tests passing (`make test`), CLI builds and works against live data.\n"},"created_at":"2026-09-07T08:01:05.761469Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
