{"id":"xpo-d6b4de","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-a73bf74e-04ad-4018-a465-c2eaeb9e7633","text":"## Implementation complete\n\n### Summary\n\nAdded `rationale` MCP tool and CLI command for BM25-ranked full-text search across specs and walkthroughs.\n\n**New files:**\n- `internal/exponential/rationale.go` — search engine: tokenizer, BM25 scorer, IDF computation, proximity bonus, best-fragment extraction with paragraph-boundary expansion\n- `internal/exponential/rationale_test.go` — unit tests for tokenizer, proximity, fragment extraction, BM25 score properties\n- `cmd/exponential/rationale.go` — CLI command `xpo rationale \"query\" [--limit N]`\n\n**Modified files:**\n- `internal/exponential/transport.go` — added `SearchRationale` to `Transport` interface\n- `internal/exponential/client.go` — added `Client.SearchRationale` delegation\n- `internal/exponential/remote_transport.go` — added `ErrLocalOnly` stub\n- `internal/mcpserver/tools.go` — `rationaleIn`/`rationaleOut` types, handler, registration\n- `internal/mcpserver/tools_test.go` — 6 handler tests (basic search, no matches, empty query, limit, title boost, spec+walkthrough)\n- `internal/mcpserver/integration_test.go` — added `rationale` to tool list check\n\n### Rationale\n\nFollowed the existing `LocalTransport` → `Transport` → `Client` → MCP handler pattern. BM25 scoring chosen over substring matching for: multi-term matching, IDF weighting of rare terms, term frequency saturation, document length normalization. Proximity bonus and title/label boost layered on top for quality.\n\n### Decisions made\n\n- Named the tokenizer `wordTokens` to avoid conflict with existing `tokenize` in `duplicates.go` (different signature — returns `[]string` vs `map[string]bool`)\n- Fragment extraction uses a sliding 100-token window scored by IDF-weighted term density, then expands to paragraph boundaries — produces much better context than first-match extraction\n\n### Status\n\nAll tests passing (full `make test`), CLI binary compiles, smoke-tested against real repo artifacts with good results."},"created_at":"2026-09-07T08:52:35.150293Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
