{"id":"xpo-758398","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"When creating a new issue, we should give the user the option to save what they have written so far as an issue draft. Drafts could go into an `.xpo/drafts` folder and serialize the \"new issue\" dialog data as a JSON object with no issue ID is assigned yet. Also, a new \"Drafts\" menu item appears in the navigation bar when drafts are present (with a counter badge).\n\nThe \"Drafts\" overview shows a list of drafts users have been working on. Users can open any draft to continue editing the issue draft. From there a draft can either be discarded (draft JSON deleted without rendering an issue) or an issue be created (draft JSON used to add a new issue)."},"created_at":"2026-09-07T15:21:43.395368Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
{"id":"xpo-2c6297","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"In the Merge view, the walkthrough and conversation tab content stretches full width. Long prose is hard to read at wide viewports.\n\n### Expected\nContent should have a max-width and be centered, similar to how GitHub PR descriptions render.\n\n### Found during\nTophatting xpo-c08d52 lint fixes.","labels":["bug","frontend"],"sort_order":"bPt","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Merge view: walkthrough and conversation tabs should be narrower and centered"},"created_at":"2026-09-07T15:35:13.908172Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-af0b09","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"The Merge view fetches commits, files, and diff on mount but does not re-fetch when the underlying branch changes (e.g. a new commit is pushed while the view is open).\n\n### Expected\nSSE events or polling should trigger a refresh of the merge view data when disk content changes.\n\n### Found during\nTophatting xpo-c08d52 lint fixes.","labels":["bug","frontend"],"sort_order":"bQL","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Merge view does not update when new commits are pushed"},"created_at":"2026-09-07T15:35:18.742549Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-0b2c6c","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"In almost every view, when content overflows vertically and a scrollbar appears, the entire layout shifts left to accommodate the scrollbar width. This causes a visual jump.\n\n### Expected\nUse `overflow-y: overlay` or `scrollbar-gutter: stable` to prevent layout shift when scrollbars appear.\n\n### Found during\nTophatting xpo-c08d52 lint fixes.","labels":["bug","frontend"],"sort_order":"bQn","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Long content causes horizontal scrollbar that shifts layout left"},"created_at":"2026-09-07T15:35:24.85022Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-0b193b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"When an artifact file (spec.md or walkthrough.md) is modified on disk (e.g. by an agent writing a spec), the issue detail panel does not re-render to show the updated content. The user must navigate away and back.\n\n### Expected\nSSE events for artifact changes should trigger a re-fetch of the artifact content in the detail panel.\n\n### Found during\nTophatting xpo-c08d52 lint fixes.","labels":["bug","frontend"],"sort_order":"bRF","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Disk changes to spec.md / walkthrough.md don't live-update the UI"},"created_at":"2026-09-07T15:35:30.031082Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-5d3fb0","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"The inline create issue row inside a backlog status group has a strange layout. The title input doesn't align with existing issue rows because it's missing the issue ID column placeholder.\n\n### Expected\nThe inline create row should visually match the issue row layout — either with a placeholder/dimmed ID column or proper alignment that accounts for the missing column.\n\n### Found during\nTophatting xpo-c08d52 lint fixes.","labels":["bug","frontend"],"sort_order":"bRh","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Inline create row in status group has broken layout — needs placeholder ID"},"created_at":"2026-09-07T15:35:35.545551Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-374512","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"The FilterMenu and ViewOptionsMenu popovers align their right edge to the button's right edge. This makes them hard to reach with the mouse — the popover extends far to the left of the button.\n\n### Expected\nPopovers should try to center on the trigger button, falling back to edge-aligned only when viewport constraints require it.\n\n### Found during\nTophatting xpo-c08d52 lint fixes.","labels":["bug","frontend"],"sort_order":"bS9","status":"BACKLOG","title":"FilterMenu and ViewOptionsMenu popovers should center on trigger button"},"created_at":"2026-09-07T15:35:40.51266Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-87503f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Two issues with Board view keyboard support:\n\n1. The `?` keyboard help overlay doesn't document the `1`–`6` shortcuts for jumping to columns\n2. There are no `s`/`l`/`e` shortcuts for quickly setting status/labels/estimate on the focused card (unlike the backlog view)\n\n### Expected\n- `?` help should list all available Board shortcuts including column numbers\n- Add `s`/`l`/`e` quick-set shortcuts matching the backlog's keyboard UX\n\n### Found during\nTophatting xpo-c08d52 lint fixes.","labels":["bug","frontend"],"sort_order":"bSb","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Board view: keyboard help missing column shortcuts, no s/l/e quick-set"},"created_at":"2026-09-07T15:35:47.015782Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-911a91","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"When the context menu is opened near the right or bottom edge of the browser window, the flyout sub-menus (status, priority, labels, etc.) extend outside the visible viewport and get clipped.\n\n### Expected\nSub-menu positioning should detect available space and flip direction (open left instead of right, or above instead of below) when near edges, similar to how the main menu already clamps itself.\n\n### Found during\nTophatting xpo-c08d52 lint fixes.","labels":["bug","frontend"],"sort_order":"bT3","status":"BACKLOG","title":"ContextMenu sub-menus clip outside viewport near window edges"},"created_at":"2026-09-07T15:35:52.77018Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-f539b6","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Collection of frontend UX issues found during tophatting — layout shifts, popover positioning, live-update gaps, keyboard shortcut coverage, and content width/alignment.","labels":["epic","frontend"],"sort_order":"bTV","status":"BACKLOG","title":"UI Polish"},"created_at":"2026-09-07T15:36:17.583591Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
