{"id":"xpo-ab47db","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Bug\n\nOn the **Dependencies** view (`/dependencies`), pressing `/` correctly focuses the search input. However, pressing `ESC` does not dismiss or exit the search — the input remains focused and the filter stays active.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nPressing `ESC` while the search input is focused should:\n- Clear the search query\n- Remove focus from the search input\n- Return keyboard control to the graph/page\n\n## Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Open the Dependencies view\n2. Press `/` — search input gains focus\n3. Type a query\n4. Press `ESC`\n5. **Actual:** search remains focused/active\n6. **Expected:** search is dismissed and focus returns to the page","labels":["bug","frontend"],"parent_id":"xpo-f539b6","sort_order":"bTV","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Dependencies view: ESC doesn't exit search after `/` focuses it"},"created_at":"2026-09-07T15:54:28.987465Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-e5d2e4","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Feature\n\nOn the **Backlog** view, pressing `[` and `]` should cycle through the view tabs (e.g. Board, List, Dependencies).\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\n- `[` switches to the previous tab\n- `]` switches to the next tab\n- Wrapping behavior at the edges (first/last tab) is acceptable either way\n\n## Current Behavior\n\nNo keyboard shortcut exists for switching between view tabs — users must click.","labels":["feature","frontend"],"parent_id":"xpo-f539b6","sort_order":"bTx","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Backlog view: `[` and `]` should switch view tabs"},"created_at":"2026-09-07T15:55:20.5731Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
