{"id":"xpo-5d3fb0","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-eafb66ec-e9d7-43b5-a0bb-c351cfaea2a2","text":"**Summary:** Updated the inline create row in `Backlog.tsx` to match normal issue row layout:\n- Wrapped `PriorityIcon` and `StatusIcon` in `w-6 h-6 -m-1` containers matching the issue row's button sizing\n- Replaced the fixed `w-28` spacer with a dimmed `xpo-······` placeholder using the same mono/tabular-nums styling as `CopyableId`\n\n**Rationale:** The columns now align because they use the same structural wrappers as the real issue rows, rather than approximating widths with fixed spacers.\n\n**Decisions:** Used `opacity-40` on the placeholder ID to make it clearly non-interactive while still giving visual alignment context.\n\n**Status:** Lint and tests pass, ready for tophat."},"created_at":"2026-09-07T16:01:30.892244Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-00198b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Add `mode` parameter to `xpo start` CLI and MCP tool","description":"## Problem\n\nThe `xpo start` command decides whether to create a git worktree or a plain branch based solely on the global `worktrees` setting in `.xpo/config.yml`. There is no way to override this per-invocation.\n\n- **CLI:** Has a `--no-wt` flag that negates the config, but no positive `--wt` flag to force worktrees when the config default is `false`.\n- **MCP tool:** Accepts only `id` and `force` — no override at all.\n\n## Proposed Change\n\nAdd a `mode` parameter (values: `worktree`, `branch`) to both the CLI flag set and the MCP tool input struct, allowing callers to override the global config on a per-issue basis.\n\n### CLI\n\nReplace the `--no-wt` boolean flag with a `--mode` string flag accepting `worktree` or `branch`. When set, it overrides `cfg.Worktrees` before calling `StartWork`. When omitted, the global config applies as today.\n\n### MCP\n\nAdd an optional `mode` field (`\"worktree\"` | `\"branch\"`) to the `startIn` struct in `internal/mcpserver/tools.go`. When provided, override `cfg.Worktrees` in the handler before calling `StartWork`.\n\n### Core\n\nNo changes needed to `StartWork` itself — it already branches on `c.Config.Worktrees`.\n\n## Files to touch\n\n- `cmd/exponential/update.go` — replace `--no-wt` with `--mode`\n- `internal/mcpserver/tools.go` — add `mode` to `startIn`, apply override in handler\n- Tests covering both paths","status":"PLANNED","estimate":2,"sort_order":"bUQ","labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-09-07T16:03:34.896683Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-5d3fb0","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"walkthrough","filename":"walkthrough.md","action":"created"},"created_at":"2026-09-07T16:04:01.051596Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
