{"id":"xpo-00198b","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-bd929292-ba69-47c4-91de-08b6e38edaf6","text":"## Implementation complete\n\n### Summary\n\n- **`cmd/exponential/update.go`** — Replaced `startNoWorktree` bool / `--no-wt` flag with `startMode` string / `--mode` flag accepting `\"worktree\"` or `\"branch\"`. Invalid values exit with an error. Empty string (omitted) preserves existing global config behavior.\n- **`internal/mcpserver/tools.go`** — Added `Mode` field to `startIn` struct. The `start` handler validates the value and, when set, creates a shallow copy of the config with the override applied to avoid mutating the shared `t.cfg` (thread-safe for concurrent MCP calls).\n\n### Rationale\n\nShallow-copying the config in the MCP handler avoids a race condition — `t.cfg` is shared across all concurrent tool calls, so mutating it directly would leak the override to other requests. The CLI doesn't need this since each invocation is a single process.\n\n### Decisions made\n\nNone beyond the spec — the approach matched the issue description exactly.\n\n### Status\n\n`make test` passes (lint + Go tests). Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-09-07T16:08:35.574841Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
