{"id":"xpo-0b2c6c","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-02cfdb62-1cdb-4309-925d-985ba079bece","text":"**Summary:** Added global `scrollbar-gutter: stable` rule in `index.css` after the existing scrollbar styling block. Removed the one-off inline `scrollbarGutter: \"stable\"` from `IssueDetail.tsx`.\n\n**Rationale:** A single global rule catches all scroll containers (Backlog, Board, Dashboard, Cycles, Dependencies, etc.) without touching each component individually. The `stable` value reserves gutter space even when no scrollbar is visible, preventing the layout shift.\n\n**Decisions:** Applied the rule globally via `* { scrollbar-gutter: stable }` rather than scoping to specific containers — this is safe because it only reserves space on elements that actually have `overflow: auto/scroll`, and the thin 6px scrollbar means the reserved gutter is minimal.\n\n**Status:** Lint and tests pass, ready for tophat."},"created_at":"2026-09-07T16:16:26.204088Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
