{"id":"xpo-374512","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-0f1d1f47-5569-4eb4-a4d0-0a79197fe20f","text":"**Summary:** Centered both popover menus on their trigger buttons:\n- `FilterMenu.tsx`: Changed `left = aRect.right - mRect.width` to `left = aRect.left + aRect.width / 2 - mRect.width / 2`, with viewport clamping on both edges\n- `Backlog.tsx` ViewOptionsMenu: Replaced `right-0` with `left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2`\n\n**Rationale:** Centering makes the menu feel anchored to its trigger rather than floating off to the left.\n\n**Status:** Lint and tests pass, ready for tophat."},"created_at":"2026-09-07T16:21:51.110023Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-93e234","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Nested mode: skip ghost children when parent is already visible","description":"## Bug\n\nIn nested hierarchy mode, ghost children are shown under a parent in every status group the parent appears in — even when the parent's own status group is visible on the same tab. This causes the entire child list to appear twice (e.g. UI Polish's 9 children show under both Planned and In Progress on the Active tab).\n\n### Expected\n\nGhost children should only be injected when the parent's own status group is **not visible** in the current view. If the parent appears in its real status group on the same tab, children should only appear there — not duplicated under every ghost parent row.\n\n### Current Behavior\n\nSee screenshot: `xpo-f539b6` (UI Polish, status DOING) appears in the In Progress group with all children as ghosts. The same children also appear under Planned because some of them are PLANNED. The parent shows as a ghost in Planned with all children listed again — redundant duplication.\n\n### Found during\n\nTophatting UI Polish epic work.","status":"BACKLOG","parent_id":"xpo-f539b6","sort_order":"bUs","labels":["bug","frontend"]},"created_at":"2026-09-07T16:25:05.992548Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
