{"id":"xpo-af0b09","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-bc243c06-481b-4de6-ae62-de5833f8c67d","text":"**Summary:** Added `bs.head_sha` to the MergeView data-loading `useEffect` dependency array in `MergeView.tsx`.\n\n**Rationale:** The server already watches git refs and broadcasts SSE events on ref changes. App.tsx re-fetches issues (including `branch_stats`) on every SSE event. By depending on `head_sha`, MergeView re-fetches its detailed data (commits, files, diff, mergeability) whenever the branch tip moves — no polling or new SSE subscriptions needed.\n\n**Status:** Lint and tests pass, ready for tophat."},"created_at":"2026-09-07T21:59:00.425255Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-af0b09","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-00e98544-27cd-4472-9710-b525c71321a3","text":"**Update:** Added three changes beyond the original `head_sha` dependency:\n\n1. **Refresh button** — `RefreshCw` icon in the merge view top bar, next to the close button. Calls `refreshData()` to manually re-fetch commits, files, diff, and mergeability. Solves the core UX problem: user reviews code, tells agent to fix something, clicks refresh to see the updated diff without leaving the view.\n\n2. **`.xpo/` filtering** — files with paths starting with `.xpo/` are filtered from both the files list and the parsed diff map, hiding `issues.db` and other xpo internals from the merge view.\n\n3. **Extracted `refreshData` callback** — the fetch logic is now a `useCallback` shared between the mount effect and the refresh button.\n\n**Status:** Lint passes, ready for tophat."},"created_at":"2026-09-08T05:40:10.880545Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-fad57f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Mergeability check falsely blocks on uncommitted working directory changes","description":"## Bug\n\nThe mergeability check reports \"these tracked files have local changes that conflict with the incoming branch\" when there are uncommitted changes in the working directory on the feature branch. This is incorrect — the check should compare the committed states of `main` and the branch tip, not the working directory state.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Start work on a branch (`xpo start`)\n2. Make changes and don't commit yet\n3. Open the merge view for that issue\n4. Mergeability shows an error about local changes conflicting\n\n### Expected\n\nMergeability should compare committed branch tip vs. committed main. Uncommitted working directory changes are not relevant to whether the branch *can* merge — the user just needs to commit first. If anything, the message should say \"uncommitted changes — commit before merging\" rather than \"local changes conflict with the incoming branch.\"\n\n### Root Cause\n\nThe mergeability API endpoint likely runs a test merge that fails because the working tree is dirty. It should either stash/ignore working directory state or compare only the committed refs.\n\n### Found during\n\nTophatting xpo-af0b09 merge view refresh.","status":"BACKLOG","sort_order":"bVK","labels":["bug","Backend"]},"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:01:21.082642Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-af0b09","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:02:43.923742Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-af0b09","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-4e1406a0-c9e4-4c4a-9a2a-223e54ae3499","text":"**Final update:** All changes committed and ready:\n\n1. **Auto-refresh** via `bs.head_sha` dependency\n2. **Manual refresh button** in the tab bar (right end, away from X)\n3. **`.xpo/` filtering** from files list and diff\n4. **Scrollbar approach changed**: `scrollbar-gutter: stable` → `overflow-y: scroll` (6px thin scrollbar, not 15px gutter). Top bar padding adjusted to `pl-5 pr-3`.\n5. **Code reformatted** by user (MergeView.tsx, IssueDetail.tsx)\n\nFiled xpo-fad57f for the mergeability check bug (backend, separate issue).\n\n**Status:** Lint and tests pass, ready for tophat."},"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:02:50.25476Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-09ebcc","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Extract TopBar into a shared first-class component","description":"## Improvement\n\nEach view (MergeView, IssueDetail, Backlog, etc.) creates its own top bar with slightly different padding, height, background, and border styles. This leads to inconsistencies (e.g. `px-5` vs `pl-5 pr-3`, varying heights) and makes global changes like the scrollbar gutter padding adjustment tedious.\n\n### Expected\n\nA shared `TopBar` component (e.g. `components/ui/TopBar.tsx`) that standardizes:\n- Height (`h-12`)\n- Padding (accounting for scrollbar gutter)\n- Background and border styles\n- Layout (left content, center content, right actions)\n\nViews compose `TopBar` with their specific content via slots/children rather than duplicating the bar markup.\n\n### Found during\n\nAdjusting MergeView top bar padding for scrollbar gutter — had to do it per-view instead of in one place.","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"xpo-f539b6","sort_order":"bUQ","labels":["improvement","frontend"]},"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:04:08.027634Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
