{"id":"xpo-af0b09","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DONE"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:05:03.995059Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-db1b0a","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Bug\n\nWhen the merge view is open and `xpo merge` runs in the background (or the branch is otherwise deleted), the app crashes with:\n\n```\nCannot read properties of undefined (reading 'head_sha')\n```\n\n### Root Cause\n\n`MergeView.tsx` uses `const bs = issue.branch_stats!` (non-null assertion) and the data-loading `useEffect` depends on `bs.head_sha`. When the merge completes and SSE updates the issue, `branch_stats` becomes `undefined` — the non-null assertion fails and the component crashes on re-render.\n\n### Fix\n\nGuard `bs.head_sha` access: use optional chaining (`issue.branch_stats?.head_sha`) in the dependency array, and handle the case where `branch_stats` disappears (e.g. close the merge view automatically or show a \"branch merged\" state).\n\n### Found during\n\nTophatting xpo-af0b09 merge view refresh — the `head_sha` dependency was added in that issue.","labels":["bug","frontend"],"parent_id":"xpo-f539b6","sort_order":"bUR","status":"PLANNED","title":"MergeView crashes when branch is deleted while view is open"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:05:39.374035Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
