{"id":"xpo-d049dc","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Bug\n\nDragging issues on the backlog view feels slow and sluggish. The drag overlay lags behind the cursor, likely caused by excessive re-renders or effects firing during the drag operation.\n\n### Expected\n\nDrag and drop should feel instant — the overlay should track the cursor at 60fps with no perceptible lag.\n\n### Probable Cause\n\nThe Backlog component is large with many `useEffect` hooks, memoized computations, and state updates. During a drag, DnD context updates may trigger cascading re-renders of the entire issue list and its effects.\n\n### Found during\n\nTophatting UI Polish epic work.","labels":["bug","frontend"],"parent_id":"xpo-f539b6","sort_order":"bUQ","status":"PLANNED","title":"Backlog view: drag and drop is slow and sluggish"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:07:19.352278Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
