{"id":"xpo-09ebcc","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-10d9bdb9-fea9-45e1-8e85-27f92a18df4d","text":"## Implementation complete\n\n### Summary\n\nCreated a shared `TopBar` component at `web/src/components/ui/TopBar.tsx` with three layout slots (`left`, `center`, `right`) and migrated all 13 views to use it.\n\n**New files:**\n- `web/src/components/ui/TopBar.tsx` — the shared component\n- `web/src/utils/cn.ts` — `cn()` utility using `clsx` + `tailwind-merge` for safe class merging\n\n**Migrated views:** Backlog, Board, Dashboard, Timeline, Dependencies, DepGraph, IssueDetail, MergeView, MyIssues, Inbox, Labels, PendingChanges, PendingEventsPanel, Cycles\n\n### Rationale\n\n- **Slots instead of children:** `left`, `center`, `right` props let TopBar own the three-column flex layout. Views declare *what* goes where without managing `ml-auto` / `flex-1` spacers.\n- **`cn()` utility added:** `clsx` + `tailwind-merge` enables safe class overrides (e.g. `px-4` overriding default `pl-5 pr-3` for PendingEventsPanel). The existing Button.tsx pattern of template literal concatenation can't handle conflicting Tailwind utilities.\n- **Center slot uses flex centering** (`flex-1 flex justify-center`), not absolute positioning — avoids overlap risk with left/right content and matches the existing Dependencies search pattern.\n\n### Decisions made\n\n- **No slot wrapper divs on left/right** — callers provide their own flex container with their preferred gap. Avoids imposing a default gap that doesn't fit all views.\n- **Cycles restructured** — changed from `overflow-y-auto` on the root div to `flex flex-col` with TopBar above a `flex-1 overflow-y-auto` scroll area. The inline `h1` heading was removed.\n- **Labels normalized** from `h-13 px-6` to the standard `h-12 pl-5 pr-3`.\n- **Backlog search moved** from the right section to the `center` slot.\n\n### Status\n\n- ESLint: clean\n- TypeScript: clean\n- `go vet`: clean\n- Go tests: all passing\n- Ready for visual review\n"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:38:34.412853Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-eb76cd","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Improvement\n\nThe Timeline view currently uses tabs (All / Issues / Commits) to filter event types. This is limiting — it only supports single-selection and doesn't scale as more event types are added.\n\n### Expected\n\nReplace the tab-style filter with a filter button (matching the Backlog/MyIssues filter pattern) that opens a checklist popover:\n\n- Each event type has a checkbox (issues, commits, comments, etc.)\n- **All** / **None** shortcut buttons at the top\n- Multiple types can be active simultaneously\n- Filter button shows an active-filter indicator dot when not all types are selected\n\n### Why\n\n- Tabs imply exclusive selection; event filtering is naturally multi-select\n- Scales to more event types without crowding the top bar\n- Consistent with the filter pattern used in Backlog and MyIssues","labels":["improvement","frontend"],"parent_id":"xpo-f539b6","sort_order":"bUQ","status":"PLANNED","title":"Replace Timeline tabs with event-type filter menu"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:53:08.942572Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-e1acfd","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Bug\n\nIn the FilterMenu (priority, labels, status dropdowns), the hover/selection background highlights have inconsistent widths — some items' backgrounds don't extend to the full width of the menu, creating a visually uneven appearance.\n\n### Expected\n\nAll menu item hover and selection backgrounds should span the full width of the menu consistently, with uniform padding on both sides.\n\n### Found during\n\nTopBar extraction top-hat — visible in the priority filter dropdown on Backlog view.","labels":["bug","frontend"],"parent_id":"xpo-f539b6","sort_order":"bUR","status":"PLANNED","title":"Fix uneven hover/selection backgrounds in filter menu items"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:59:06.902415Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
