{"id":"xpo-e5d2e4","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-8d3b1a73-b62d-439c-b17e-75c521929473","text":"## Implementation complete\n\n**Summary**\n\n- Added `[` and `]` key handlers to the existing keyboard listener in `Backlog.tsx` (~line 1173). They cycle through the four sub-tabs (`all → backlog → active → done`) using the `TAB_CONFIGS` key order, with wrapping at both edges.\n- Added stable refs (`activeTabRef`, `onTabChangeRef`) following the same pattern used by other refs in the handler.\n- Added \"Previous tab\" / \"Next tab\" entries to the Backlog section of `KeyboardHelp.tsx`.\n\n**Rationale**\n\nPlaced the handler early in the `keydown` listener (before the `f` / `/` / arrow keys) so it fires regardless of focused row state. Uses `isEditableTarget` guard already in place, plus the meta/ctrl guard, so it's suppressed in inputs.\n\n**Status** — `make test` and `make lint` pass. Ready for review.\n"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T07:20:59.079067Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
