{"id":"xpo-570a07","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Goal\n\nReplace the current pattern of per-view custom HTML+CSS with a unified component tree that enforces consistent styling and behavior across all views.\n\n### Current state\n\nEvery view (Backlog, Board, Cycles, Timeline, Dependencies, Labels, My Issues, Inbox, Dashboard) builds its own top bar, scroll container, keyboard handler, and empty state from raw divs and duplicated CSS classes. Identical patterns are copy-pasted:\n\n- **Underlined tab bar** — 3 views with identical `border-b-2` button markup\n- **Filter icon + FilterMenu** — 3 views with identical state/ref/toggle/popup wiring\n- **Search input with kbd hint** — 2 views with identical input+icon+hint markup\n- **Toolbar icon button** — 5 instances of the same `w-7 h-7` bordered button\n- **Issue count badge** — 3 views with identical `text-xs tabular-nums` span\n- **View shell** — all 9 views wrap content in `h-full flex flex-col` + `overflow-y-auto`\n- **Keyboard handler** — 5 views with the same `useEffect`+`addEventListener`+`isEditableTarget` boilerplate\n- **Title-only left slot** — 5 views rendering an identical `text-sm font-medium` span\n\n### Target component tree\n\n```\nApp\n├── Layout\n│   ├── Sidebar (NavItem[])\n│   └── ViewContainer          ← wraps every view\n│       ├── TopBar\n│       │   ├── left:  Tabs | ViewTitle\n│       │   ├── center: SearchInput (optional)\n│       │   └── right: IconButton[] + CountBadge\n│       └── ViewContent        ← scrollable area\n│           ├── {view-specific content}\n│           └── EmptyState (when empty)\n```\n\n### Approach\n\nExtract one shared component at a time, migrate consumers, delete duplicated code. Each story is independently shippable — no big-bang rewrite.","labels":["epic","frontend"],"sort_order":"bUS","status":"PLANNED","title":"Refactor WebUI to component tree"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T07:32:23.771224Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-d47781","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## What\n\nExtract a generic `Tabs` component from the identical underlined tab-bar pattern used in three views.\n\n## Current duplication\n\nBacklog, My Issues, and Timeline all render the same markup:\n- `Object.entries(CONFIG).map(...)` producing `\u003cbutton\u003e` elements\n- Identical CSS: `text-sm font-medium h-full border-b-2 -mb-px transition-colors duration-[var(--duration-fast)]`\n- Active state: `text-[var(--color-text-primary)] border-[var(--color-text-primary)]`\n- Inactive state: `text-[var(--color-text-muted)] border-transparent hover:text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]`\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```tsx\ninterface TabsProps\u003cT extends string\u003e {\n  items: { id: T; label: string }[];\n  activeId: T;\n  onChange: (id: T) =\u003e void;\n}\n```\n\n## Behavior\n\n- Renders the underlined tab buttons\n- Handles `[` / `]` keyboard cycling with wrapping (guarded by `isEditableTarget`)\n- Suppressed when a popover is open or focus is in an input\n\n## Consumers\n\n- **Backlog** — 4 tabs (All Issues, Backlog, Active, Done) — remove inline tab buttons and `[`/`]` handler\n- **My Issues** — 2 tabs (Assigned, Created) — remove inline tab buttons, gain `[`/`]` for free\n- **Timeline** — 3 tabs (All, Events, Commits) — remove inline tab buttons, gain `[`/`]` for free\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `Tabs` component renders identically to current tab bars\n- [ ] `[`/`]` cycling works in all three views\n- [ ] Keyboard help modal updated\n- [ ] No visual regression in any tab bar","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","frontend"],"parent_id":"xpo-570a07","sort_order":"bUT","status":"PLANNED","title":"Extract `Tabs` component with `[`/`]` keyboard cycling"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T07:32:35.984262Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-ef6602","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## What\n\nExtract a shared `SearchInput` component from the identical search-input pattern in Backlog and Dependencies.\n\n## Current duplication\n\nBoth views render:\n- `h-8 pl-8 pr-10` input with magnifying glass SVG on the left\n- `\u003ckbd\u003e` hint showing `/` when empty, `Esc` when populated\n- `/` keyboard shortcut to focus, `Escape` to clear and blur\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```tsx\ninterface SearchInputProps {\n  value: string;\n  onChange: (value: string) =\u003e void;\n  placeholder?: string;\n  className?: string;\n}\n```\n\n## Behavior\n\n- Renders the search input with magnifying glass icon and keyboard hint badge\n- Registers `/` to focus (via parent keyboard handler or internal listener)\n- `Escape` clears the value and blurs the input\n\n## Consumers\n\n- **Backlog** center slot — replace inline markup\n- **Dependencies** center slot — replace inline markup\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `SearchInput` renders identically to current search inputs\n- [ ] `/` focuses, `Esc` clears+blurs in both views\n- [ ] Keyboard hint toggles between `/` and `Esc` based on content","estimate":2,"labels":["feature","frontend"],"parent_id":"xpo-570a07","sort_order":"bUU","status":"PLANNED","title":"Extract `SearchInput` component with `/` focus and `Esc` clear"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T07:32:41.146084Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-4235c6","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## What\n\nExtract a shared `IconButton` component from the repeated `w-7 h-7` bordered toolbar button pattern.\n\n## Current duplication\n\nFive instances across four views use the same markup:\n- `w-7 h-7 rounded-[var(--radius-md)] bg-[var(--color-surface-1)] border border-[var(--color-border-default)]`\n- Hover: `hover:bg-[var(--color-hover-surface-1)]`\n- Contains an SVG icon, optional active-indicator dot, optional tooltip\n\nInstances: Backlog (filter + view options), My Issues (filter), Inbox (filter), Board (view options).\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```tsx\ninterface IconButtonProps {\n  icon: ReactNode;\n  onClick: () =\u003e void;\n  active?: boolean;\n  tooltip?: string;\n  className?: string;\n}\n```\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] All 5 instances migrated to `IconButton`\n- [ ] Active indicator dot renders when `active` is true\n- [ ] Tooltip shows on hover when provided\n- [ ] No visual regression","estimate":1,"labels":["feature","frontend"],"parent_id":"xpo-570a07","sort_order":"bUV","status":"PLANNED","title":"Extract `IconButton` component for toolbar actions"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T07:32:46.14341Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-e16962","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## What\n\nExtract a `FilterButton` that bundles the filter icon button, active dot, popover state, anchor ref, and `f` keyboard toggle into a single component.\n\n## Current duplication\n\nBacklog, My Issues, and Inbox all wire up:\n- `useState(showFilterMenu)` + `useRef(filterBtnRef)`\n- `f` key toggles the filter menu, `Escape` closes it\n- Active dot when filters are non-default\n- `\u003cFilterMenu anchorRef={...} onClose={...} /\u003e`\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```tsx\ninterface FilterButtonProps {\n  issues: Issue[];\n  filters: FilterState;\n  onFilterChange: (filters: FilterState) =\u003e void;\n}\n```\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- Depends on `IconButton` being extracted first\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Backlog, My Issues, and Inbox migrated to `FilterButton`\n- [ ] `f` keyboard shortcut works in all three views\n- [ ] Active indicator shows when filters are non-default\n- [ ] No visual regression","estimate":2,"labels":["feature","frontend"],"parent_id":"xpo-570a07","sort_order":"bUW","status":"PLANNED","title":"Extract `FilterButton` component (IconButton + FilterMenu wiring)"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T07:32:51.259139Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-f27a3e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## What\n\nExtract a `CountBadge` component from the repeated issue-count display in TopBar right slots.\n\n## Current duplication\n\nBoard, My Issues, and Dashboard all render:\n```tsx\n\u003cspan className=\"text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] tabular-nums\"\u003e\n  {count} {count === 1 ? \"issue\" : \"issues\"}\n\u003c/span\u003e\n```\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```tsx\ninterface CountBadgeProps {\n  count: number;\n  label?: string; // default \"issue\"/\"issues\"\n}\n```\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] All 3 instances migrated\n- [ ] Singular/plural handled correctly\n- [ ] No visual regression","estimate":1,"labels":["feature","frontend"],"parent_id":"xpo-570a07","sort_order":"bUX","status":"PLANNED","title":"Extract `CountBadge` component for issue counts"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T07:32:54.105264Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-250ddf","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## What\n\nExtract a `ViewTitle` component from the plain-text title pattern used in TopBar left slots.\n\n## Current duplication\n\nBoard, Cycles, Labels, Dashboard, and Inbox all render:\n```tsx\n\u003cspan className=\"text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-text-primary)]\"\u003eView Name\u003c/span\u003e\n```\n\nSome also include a subtitle or secondary info alongside the title.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```tsx\ninterface ViewTitleProps {\n  title: string;\n  subtitle?: ReactNode;\n}\n```\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] All 5 title-only views migrated\n- [ ] Subtitle renders when provided (e.g., Dependencies stat counters)\n- [ ] No visual regression","estimate":1,"labels":["feature","frontend"],"parent_id":"xpo-570a07","sort_order":"bUY","status":"PLANNED","title":"Extract `ViewTitle` component for TopBar left slot"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T07:32:57.589855Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-c26f7b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## What\n\nExtract a `ViewContainer` component that provides the standard view shell used by all 9 views.\n\n## Current duplication\n\nEvery view wraps its content in:\n```tsx\n\u003cdiv className=\"h-full flex flex-col relative\"\u003e\n  \u003cTopBar ... /\u003e\n  \u003cdiv className=\"flex-1 overflow-y-auto ...\"\u003e\n    {content}\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n```\n\nScroll behavior varies slightly (some use `overflow-y-scroll`, some `overflow-y-auto`, Board uses `overflow-hidden`) but the shell is the same.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```tsx\ninterface ViewContainerProps {\n  topBar: ReactNode;\n  scroll?: 'auto' | 'scroll' | 'hidden';\n  contentRef?: RefObject\u003cHTMLDivElement\u003e;\n  children: ReactNode;\n}\n```\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] All 9 views migrated to `ViewContainer`\n- [ ] Scroll behavior preserved per-view\n- [ ] `contentRef` wiring works for views that need it (Backlog scroll tracking)\n- [ ] No visual regression","estimate":2,"labels":["feature","frontend"],"parent_id":"xpo-570a07","sort_order":"bUZ","status":"PLANNED","title":"Extract `ViewContainer` shell wrapping TopBar + scrollable content"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T07:33:02.617158Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-caf557","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## What\n\nExtract a `useViewKeyboard` hook to replace the repeated `useEffect` + `addEventListener('keydown')` + guard boilerplate used in 5 views.\n\n## Current duplication\n\nBacklog, Board, My Issues, Inbox, and Dependencies all follow:\n```typescript\nuseEffect(() =\u003e {\n  const handler = (e: KeyboardEvent) =\u003e {\n    if (isEditableTarget(e)) return;\n    if (e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey) return;\n    // view-specific keys...\n  };\n  document.addEventListener(\"keydown\", handler);\n  return () =\u003e document.removeEventListener(\"keydown\", handler);\n}, [deps]);\n```\n\nEach view defines its own key→action map inline.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```tsx\nuseViewKeyboard(\n  handlers: Record\u003cstring, (e: KeyboardEvent) =\u003e void\u003e,\n  options?: {\n    enabled?: boolean;        // e.g., disable when popover open\n    deps?: DependencyList;\n  }\n);\n```\n\nThe hook handles:\n- `isEditableTarget` guard\n- `metaKey`/`ctrlKey` suppression\n- Registering/cleaning up the listener\n- Stable refs for handlers to avoid stale closures\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] All 5 views migrated to `useViewKeyboard`\n- [ ] Guard behavior identical to current (no shortcuts in inputs, no meta/ctrl)\n- [ ] Popover-open suppression works\n- [ ] All existing keyboard shortcuts continue to work\n- [ ] No duplicate listeners","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","frontend"],"parent_id":"xpo-570a07","sort_order":"bUa","status":"PLANNED","title":"Extract `useViewKeyboard` hook for view-level keyboard handling"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T07:33:09.51189Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-e16962","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"dependencies":[{"kind":"depends_on","source_id":"xpo-e16962","target_id":"xpo-4235c6"}]},"created_at":"2026-09-08T07:33:12.846338Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-de3808","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## What\n\nRestructure `App.tsx` from a monolithic component that owns all view state and renders views inline, into a formal component hierarchy:\n\n```\nApp\n└── Layout\n    ├── Sidebar\n    │   └── NavItem[]\n    └── ViewRouter\n        └── View (one of: Dashboard, Backlog, Board, ...)\n            └── ViewContainer\n                ├── TopBar\n                │   ├── left:  Tabs | ViewTitle\n                │   ├── center: SearchInput?\n                │   └── right: IconButton[] | CountBadge\n                └── ViewContent (scrollable)\n                    └── {view-specific content} | EmptyState\n```\n\n## Current state\n\n`App.tsx` is the god component — it:\n- Owns state for every view (`view`, `backlogTab`, `myIssuesTab`, `selectedIssue`, filters, sort, etc.)\n- Renders the Layout shell and sidebar inline\n- Switches between views with a chain of conditionals\n- Passes 10+ props into each view component\n\nThere is no `View` abstraction. Each view is a standalone component that receives a bag of props and handles its own shell, TopBar, scroll, and keyboard wiring.\n\n## Proposed changes\n\n1. **`ViewRouter`** — replaces the conditional chain in App.tsx. Maps the current `view` string to a view component. Each view owns its own local state (tab, filters, sort) instead of hoisting it all to App.\n2. **`View` contract** — each view renders a `ViewContainer` with a `TopBar` and content area. Views compose from the shared components (Tabs, SearchInput, FilterButton, etc.) rather than building ad-hoc.\n3. **State colocation** — move view-specific state (e.g. `backlogTab`, `myIssuesTab`, filter state) down from App into the owning view component. App only owns truly global state (the current view, issue data, SSE connection).\n4. **`Sidebar`** — already extracted as part of Layout, but should receive the view list and active view as props from ViewRouter rather than being wired directly in App.\n\n## Why this is the capstone\n\nThe leaf component stories (Tabs, SearchInput, IconButton, etc.) extract reusable pieces. This story wires them into a coherent tree. Without it, the shared components exist but the god-component structure remains.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nShould be done **after** the leaf component extractions so it can compose from them. Not a hard block — this story can proceed with the existing inline patterns and adopt the shared components as they land — but the cleanest path is leaves first, then this.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `App.tsx` no longer renders view-specific content directly\n- [ ] Each view owns its local state (tabs, filters, sort)\n- [ ] App only owns global state (current view, issues, SSE, selected issue)\n- [ ] `ViewRouter` maps view string → component\n- [ ] All views render through `ViewContainer` → `TopBar` + `ViewContent`\n- [ ] No behavioral or visual regression\n- [ ] Keyboard shortcuts continue to work across all views","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","frontend"],"parent_id":"xpo-570a07","sort_order":"bUb","status":"PLANNED","title":"Refactor App into Layout → Sidebar + ViewRouter → View hierarchy"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T07:35:27.918288Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
