{"id":"xpo-5d1c38","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## What\n\nRefactor the existing `ui/Popover.tsx` into a proper anchor-ref-based positioning primitive that all floating elements can use.\n\n## Current state\n\nThere are **7+ independent positioning implementations** across the codebase, each rolling its own `getBoundingClientRect` + clamp-to-viewport logic:\n- `Popover.tsx` — marker-parent auto-position (hidden `\u003cspan\u003e`)\n- `ContextMenu.tsx` — x,y coords + viewport clamp + sub-menu flip\n- `FilterMenu.tsx` — anchor-center + sub-menu right-align + flip\n- `InlineDropdown.tsx` — below-button\n- `FormattingBar.tsx` DropdownPortal — below-anchor\n- `Backlog.tsx` ViewMenu — center-below-button (inline, not a component)\n- `Timeline.tsx` CommitPopover — below-button (inline)\n\nClick-outside dismissal is also duplicated **8+ times** with the same `mousedown` + `contains` pattern.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```tsx\ninterface PopoverProps {\n  anchorRef: RefObject\u003cHTMLElement\u003e;\n  open: boolean;\n  onClose: () =\u003e void;\n  placement?: 'bottom' | 'bottom-center' | 'bottom-start' | 'bottom-end' | 'right';\n  offset?: number;\n  className?: string;\n  children: ReactNode;\n}\n```\n\n## Behavior\n\n- Renders via `createPortal` to body\n- Positions relative to `anchorRef` using `getBoundingClientRect`\n- Clamps to viewport bounds (flip/shift as needed)\n- Click-outside dismissal (excluding anchor element)\n- Escape dismissal\n- Handles resize/scroll repositioning\n\n## Consumers (migrate incrementally)\n\n- Existing `Popover` usages (13 instances across Backlog, Board, PropertySidebar)\n- `InlineDropdown` — rewrite on top of Popover\n- `FormattingBar` DropdownPortal — replace with Popover\n- Inline ViewMenus in Backlog/Board — extract and use Popover\n- Timeline CommitPopover and PersonFilter — use Popover\n- Eventually: FilterMenu and ContextMenu positioning layers\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Anchor-ref positioning with placement options\n- [ ] Viewport clamping (no overflow off-screen)\n- [ ] Click-outside + Escape dismissal built in\n- [ ] Existing Popover consumers migrated with no visual regression\n- [ ] `InlineDropdown` rewritten on Popover primitive","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","frontend"],"parent_id":"xpo-570a07","sort_order":"bUc","status":"PLANNED","title":"Extract `Popover` primitive with anchor-ref positioning and dismissal"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T07:41:33.192691Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-de8d06","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## What\n\nBuild a composable `Menu` → `MenuItem` / `SubMenu` system on top of the Popover primitive, with built-in keyboard navigation.\n\n## Current state\n\nMenu-like UI is built bespoke in multiple places:\n- **ContextMenu** (~465 lines) — monolithic, mixes menu structure, sub-menu rendering, positioning, keyboard handling, and business logic (API calls, delete confirmation)\n- **FilterMenu** — two-panel menu with sub-menus, its own keyboard handler (↑↓←→ Enter Space Escape)\n- **Backlog/Board ViewMenu** — inline in view components, not extracted\n- **InlineDropdown** — no keyboard navigation at all\n- **CommandPalette** — its own ↑↓ Enter Escape system\n\nSub-menu positioning is duplicated between ContextMenu and FilterMenu (right-preference + left-flip + vertical clamp).\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```tsx\n// Menu — a list of items, handles keyboard nav\n\u003cMenu\u003e\n  \u003cMenuItem icon={...} label=\"Edit\" shortcut=\"E\" onClick={...} /\u003e\n  \u003cMenuItem icon={...} label=\"Delete\" shortcut=\"⌘⌫\" variant=\"danger\" onClick={...} /\u003e\n  \u003cMenuDivider /\u003e\n  \u003cSubMenu icon={...} label=\"Set Status\"\u003e\n    \u003cMenuItem ... /\u003e\n  \u003c/SubMenu\u003e\n\u003c/Menu\u003e\n```\n\n## Behavior\n\n- `Menu`: renders a list of items, manages `focusIndex`, handles ↑↓ arrow keys, Enter to select, Escape to close, letter shortcuts\n- `MenuItem`: renders icon + label + optional shortcut hint + optional check/active state. Hover and keyboard focus styling.\n- `SubMenu`: renders a `MenuItem` trigger that opens a nested `Menu` to the right (with flip-left logic). ← closes sub-menu, → opens it.\n- `MenuDivider`: horizontal separator\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- Depends on the Popover primitive for sub-menu positioning\n\n## Consumers (migrate incrementally)\n\n- **ContextMenu** — decompose into Menu/MenuItem/SubMenu, extract business logic out\n- **FilterMenu** — rebuild with Menu/SubMenu for the dimension list and sub-panels\n- **ViewMenus** (Backlog, Board) — extract from inline JSX into Menu compositions\n- **InlineDropdown** — gain keyboard nav for free\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `Menu`/`MenuItem`/`SubMenu`/`MenuDivider` components\n- [ ] ↑↓ arrow navigation, Enter to select, Escape to close\n- [ ] SubMenu flyout with right-preference + flip-left + vertical clamp\n- [ ] Letter shortcut support (e.g., `S` for status)\n- [ ] ContextMenu refactored to compose from these primitives\n- [ ] FilterMenu refactored to compose from these primitives\n- [ ] No behavioral or visual regression","estimate":5,"labels":["feature","frontend"],"parent_id":"xpo-570a07","sort_order":"bUd","status":"PLANNED","title":"Extract `Menu`, `MenuItem`, `SubMenu` composable menu system"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T07:41:46.884138Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-9a7907","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## What\n\nReplace the three near-identical picker components with a single configurable `Picker` component.\n\n## Current duplication\n\n`StatusPicker`, `PriorityPicker`, and `EstimatePicker` are **structurally identical** — they differ only in:\n- The options array\n- The icon rendered per item\n- Label formatting\n\nEach duplicates:\n- Filter input state + ref + `requestAnimationFrame` auto-focus\n- `focusIndex` state with ↑↓ arrow key handling\n- Number key quick-select (1–5)\n- Enter to select, Escape to close\n- Identical CSS classes for item rows\n- Identical hover/keyboard focus highlighting\n- An identical `CheckIcon` SVG (literally defined 3 times in 3 files)\n\n`LabelPicker` is slightly different (multi-select with checkboxes, Space to toggle) but shares 80% of the logic.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```tsx\ninterface PickerOption\u003cT\u003e {\n  value: T;\n  label: string;\n  icon?: ReactNode;\n}\n\ninterface PickerProps\u003cT\u003e {\n  options: PickerOption\u003cT\u003e[];\n  value: T;                      // current value (for check indicator)\n  onSelect: (value: T) =\u003e void;\n  onClose: () =\u003e void;\n  multiSelect?: boolean;         // for LabelPicker\n  filterPlaceholder?: string;\n  numberKeys?: boolean;           // enable 1-5 quick select\n}\n```\n\n## Behavior\n\n- Filter input with auto-focus\n- ↑↓ arrow key navigation with wrap\n- Enter to select (Space to toggle in multi-select mode)\n- Number keys 1–5 for quick select (when enabled)\n- Escape to close\n- Check icon / checkbox for current selection\n- Shared `CheckIcon` component (extracted once)\n\n## Consumers\n\n- `StatusPicker` → `\u003cPicker options={STATUS_OPTIONS} numberKeys ... /\u003e`\n- `PriorityPicker` → `\u003cPicker options={PRIORITY_OPTIONS} numberKeys ... /\u003e`\n- `EstimatePicker` → `\u003cPicker options={ESTIMATE_OPTIONS} numberKeys ... /\u003e`\n- `LabelPicker` → `\u003cPicker options={labels} multiSelect ... /\u003e`\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Single `Picker` component replaces all 4 pickers\n- [ ] Filter, arrow nav, number keys, Enter/Space/Escape all work\n- [ ] Single `CheckIcon` definition\n- [ ] Used in Popover, ContextMenu sub-menus, and NewIssueModal\n- [ ] No visual or behavioral regression","estimate":3,"labels":["feature","frontend"],"parent_id":"xpo-570a07","sort_order":"bUe","status":"PLANNED","title":"Unify `StatusPicker`, `PriorityPicker`, `EstimatePicker` into generic `Picker`"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T07:41:58.595224Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
