{"id":"xpo-08fb57","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-98dd017e-f560-4972-96ed-162db8f2b75b","text":"## Implementation complete\n\n**Summary:** Added `}` (Shift+]) and `{` (Shift+[) keyboard shortcuts to expand/collapse all status group sections in the Backlog view.\n\n**Changes:**\n- `Backlog.tsx` — added `expandAllGroups()` and `collapseAllGroups()` functions with localStorage persistence and scroll position preservation via `requestAnimationFrame`. Wired `{`/`}` keys into the existing keyboard handler, placed right after the `[`/`]` tab-cycling block.\n- `KeyboardHelp.tsx` — added `}` Expand all groups and `{` Collapse all groups entries to the Backlog shortcut section.\n\n**Rationale:** Used `{`/`}` instead of `e`/`c` to avoid conflicting with the existing `e` estimate picker shortcut. The shifted bracket keys are a natural extension of the `[`/`]` tab-cycling pattern.\n\n**Decisions:** Scope is status groups only (not tree nodes) per the issue description. `expandAllGroups` only expands groups that have issues in them (empty groups stay collapsed).\n\n**Status:** `make test` passes, ready for review.\n"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T07:53:16.434972Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
