{"id":"xpo-d049dc","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-bbb0c440-776f-4a2d-9ecc-c942b63d2d89","text":"## Summary\n\nTwo-part fix for sluggish drag-and-drop in the backlog view:\n\n**Part 1 — Ref-based DnD visuals.** Replaced the three `useState` hooks for drag visual state (`dropIndicator`, `dropGroupStatus`, `dropNestTargetId`) with `useRef` + direct DOM manipulation. During a drag, `handleDndMove` fires on every pointer move — previously each call triggered up to 3 `setState` calls → full re-render of the entire ~2500-line component. Now it writes to refs and touches 1–2 DOM nodes via `applyIndicatorDOM`, `applyGroupDOM`, `applyNestDOM`. Zero React re-renders during the drag.\n\n- Drop indicator line: CSS pseudo-elements driven by `data-drop=\"above|below\"` attribute + `--indicator-left` custom property on the row wrapper (`backlog-dnd.css`)\n- Group highlight: inline `boxShadow`/`background` styles on the `[data-group-status]` wrapper + transparent header override\n- Nest target highlight: inline `boxShadow`/`background` styles on `[data-backlog-row]` element\n\n**Part 2 — Memoized row components.** Extracted `BacklogGroupHeader` and `BacklogIssueRow` as `React.memo` components. Each row only re-renders when its own props change — not when unrelated state changes elsewhere in Backlog. This also prevents unnecessary re-renders from focus changes, popover opens, and other non-DnD interactions.\n\n### Files changed\n\n- `BacklogIssueRow.tsx` — new memoized issue row component (~300 lines extracted from inline JSX)\n- `BacklogGroupHeader.tsx` — new memoized group header component (~100 lines extracted)\n- `backlog-dnd.css` — CSS for drop indicator pseudo-elements\n- `Backlog.tsx` — converted DnD visual state to refs, added DOM manipulation helpers, wired up new components, cleaned up 13 unused imports\n\n### Rationale\n\nOption A (refs only) would fix the hot path but leave the component structurally fragile — any future state addition would hit the same problem. Option C (refs + memo) fixes the root cause: the render tree now has proper component boundaries, and the high-frequency DnD visuals bypass React entirely.\n\n### Decisions made\n\n- Used inline styles (not Tailwind classes) for group/nest highlights to avoid Tailwind JIT purging issues and `classList` conflicts with React's `className` reconciliation\n- Used `data-drop` attribute + CSS pseudo-elements for the indicator line — avoids a persistent floating element and works naturally with the row wrapper's existing `position: relative`\n- `activeId` stays in React state (only changes on drag start/end, not during move) — the one-time re-render on start/end is acceptable and necessary for `canDrag`/`isDropTarget` props\n\n## Status\n\n`make test` passes (lint + Go tests). `make frontend` builds clean. Ready for review.\n"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T08:58:17.105578Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
