{"id":"xpo-93e234","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-153035f0-c792-4373-b9a8-20fdcbb7dd21","text":"## Implementation complete\n\n**Summary:** Modified `useBacklogRows.ts` to skip ghost parent injection when the real parent is already visible on the current tab.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Added `filteredIssueIds` set at the top of the memo for efficient lookup\n- Added a filter on `orphanedChildren` when building `ghostParentIds`: if the real parent's status is in `visibleStatuses` and the parent is in `filteredIssues`, the ghost parent is suppressed — those children already appear as ghost children under the real parent\n- Edge case handled: terminal status groups (DONE, CANCELED, DUPLICATE) with `showGhosts=false` still get ghost parents, because the real parent's ghost-child filter would hide terminal children\n\n**Rationale:** The ghost parent mechanism exists to give orphaned children hierarchy context when their parent isn't visible. When the parent IS visible (same tab), the children already appear under it as ghost children — the ghost parent just creates duplication.\n\n**Decisions made:** Group header counts and story points are unchanged. They reflect \"issues with this status\" regardless of where they render visually. The suppressed children still contribute to their status group's metrics.\n\n**Status:** `make test` passes, ready for review.\n"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T11:04:57.807571Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-93e234","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"action":"updated","artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T11:15:51.469663Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-93e234","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-621b1686-59ab-4473-bb7e-b743b92dcb38","text":"## Updated implementation\n\n**Correction:** The initial fix suppressed ghost parents — wrong direction. The correct fix suppresses **ghost children** under the real parent when the child's status group is already visible on the same tab.\n\n**Change in `useBacklogRows.ts`:** In the ghost child filter for real parents, added `visibleStatuses.includes(c.status)` check. If the child's status group is visible on this tab, the child is skipped as a ghost child — it already appears in its own status group (under a ghost parent).\n\n**Status:** `make test` passes, user confirmed correct semantics. Ready for review.\n"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T11:17:38.692584Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
