{"id":"xpo-d5c047","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"`xpo merge` should auto-checkout main in branch mode","description":"## Bug\n\n`xpo merge` rejects the merge when the hub checkout is on the feature branch:\n\n```\nError: hub checkout is on xpo-93e234-nested-mode-skip-ghost-children-when-parent-is,\nnot main — park the hub on the default branch before merging\n```\n\nIn worktree mode this check is correct — the hub stays on main and worktrees branch off it. But in branch mode there is no separate hub; the single checkout IS on the feature branch. The user (or agent) has to manually `git checkout main` before calling merge, which defeats the ergonomics of branch mode.\n\n### Expected\n\nWhen `xpo merge` detects branch mode (no worktree path for this issue), it should automatically checkout the default branch before performing the merge, then proceed normally.\n\n### Found during\n\nMerging xpo-93e234 in branch mode.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":1,"sort_order":"bUf","dependencies":[{"source_id":"xpo-d5c047","target_id":"xpo-93e234","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-09-08T11:21:46.689137Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
