{"id":"xpo-d5c047","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-6e092a5e-a77b-4ed0-9f51-a5a711e25869","text":"## Implementation complete\n\n**Summary:** Added a runtime worktree check in `internal/exponential/merge.go` after the config-based `useWorktrees` decision. If `Config.Worktrees` is true but `FindWorktreeForBranch(branch)` finds no worktree, `useWorktrees` falls back to false — the branch mode path then calls `CheckoutBranch(base)` automatically.\n\n**Rationale:** The config is a default, not a contract. `xpo start --mode branch` overrides it per-issue, and merge should respect that. Checking for an actual worktree at runtime is the simplest, most reliable detection.\n\n**Status:** `make test` passes, ready for review.\n"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T11:24:57.488018Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
