{"id":"xpo-2dd9a8","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-85a6d566-0ab3-4813-b9e4-2e340b8efafe","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded a `hasVisibleChildren` field to `RowItem` in `useBacklogRows.ts` that reflects whether a parent has children that would actually render in the current status group/tab, after ghost filtering. The existing `hasChildren` field is unchanged (still based on all children) so progress counters and estimate badges continue working.\n\n**`useBacklogRows.ts`** — moved `allVisual` computation before the parent row push; set `hasVisibleChildren: allVisual.length \u003e 0` on the parent row. Ghost child rows get `hasVisibleChildren: false`. Flat mode rows mirror `hasChildren` (chevron not shown in flat mode).\n\n**`BacklogIssueRow.tsx`** — chevron condition changed from `hasChildren` to `hasVisibleChildren`. The existing spacer in the else branch preserves layout alignment.\n\n**`Backlog.tsx`** — keyboard shortcuts (`ArrowRight`/`ArrowLeft`) and DnD drop-target logic updated to use `hasVisibleChildren` for consistency.\n\n## Rationale\n\nSeparate field avoids breaking the progress/estimate logic that still needs the full children count. Moving `allVisual` computation earlier is a minimal restructure of `addTree`.\n\n## Status\n\n`make test` passes. Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-09-08T11:35:50.020079Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
