{"id":"xpo-7a5bba","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-e7fe9d0e-e4d5-4e7e-b3eb-4700e4447f95","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded 11 new test cases to `internal/exponential/merge_test.go`, plus a shared `setupMergeRepo` helper to reduce boilerplate.\n\n**New tests:**\n- `TestMergeIssue_MergeStrategy` — --no-ff merge, verifies two-parent commit + DONE status\n- `TestMergeIssue_FFStrategy` — fast-forward merge, verifies single-parent commit\n- `TestMergeIssue_FFStrategy_Diverged` — FF on diverged branches, verifies error + clean state\n- `TestMergeIssue_CustomCommitMessage` — squash with custom message, verifies commit subject\n- `TestMergeIssue_NoBranch` — issue with no branch, verifies \"no branch found\" error\n- `TestMergeIssue_ZeroCommits` — branch with zero commits ahead, verifies \"no commits ahead\" error\n- `TestMergeIssue_Conflict` — squash merge conflict, verifies error + \"Do NOT stash\" warning\n- `TestMergeIssue_DeleteBranch` — `DeleteBranch: true`, verifies branch removal\n- `TestMergeIssue_WorktreeCleanup` — real linked worktree, verifies removal after merge\n- `TestMergeIssue_WorktreeHubWrongBranch` — hub on wrong branch in worktree mode, verifies error\n- `TestMergeIssue_FFPreservesMainIssuesDB` — FF strategy with diverged issues.db, verifies union preservation\n\n**Rationale:** Only squash happy path was tested. The auto-checkout regression (xpo-1fccf2) would have been caught by `TestMergeIssue_BranchModeWithWorktreesEnabled` (added earlier this session).\n\n**Status:** `make test` passes (all 15 merge tests green). Test-only changes, no production code modified. Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-09-08T12:03:01.333047Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-b83765","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Add test coverage for git.go operations","description":"## Problem\n\n`internal/exponential/git.go` has **zero tests**. It contains all core git operations: `DefaultBranch`, `BranchExists`, `CreateAndCheckoutBranch`, `CheckoutBranch`, `WorktreeAdd/Remove/List`, `FindWorktreeForBranch` — 10 `exec.Command` calls total.\n\nThe merge auto-checkout regression (xpo-1fccf2) originated from `FindWorktreeForBranch` matching the hub checkout as a worktree. This is the highest-risk untested file in the project.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `DefaultBranch` — correct detection, fallback when no remote\n- `BranchExists` — exists / doesn't exist\n- `CreateAndCheckoutBranch` — creates and switches, error on collision\n- `CheckoutBranch` — switches, error on nonexistent branch\n- `WorktreeAdd` / `WorktreeRemove` / `WorktreeList` — full lifecycle\n- `FindWorktreeForBranch` — linked worktree match, hub checkout match (should not match), no match","status":"PLANNED","estimate":3,"sort_order":"bUf","labels":["improvement","CLI"]},"created_at":"2026-09-08T12:17:35.092887Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-f20122","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Add test coverage for local_transport.go","description":"## Problem\n\n`internal/exponential/local_transport.go` has **zero tests**. It is the core state layer — every MCP tool and CLI command funnels through it. Functions: `appendEvent`, `GetIssue`, `resolveIssue` (prefix-match resolution with ambiguous-match and not-found branches), `FindIssue`, `GetInbox`.\n\n`resolveIssue` is especially risky — it does prefix matching and has distinct error paths for ambiguous vs not-found that are only tested indirectly via higher-level tests.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":3,"sort_order":"bUg","labels":["improvement","CLI"]},"created_at":"2026-09-08T12:17:37.691952Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-5bf8b9","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Add test coverage for server write-path handlers","description":"## Problem\n\n`internal/server/handlers.go` has ~40% test coverage. ~30 handlers, 20 tested. The untested write path includes: `handleSave` (applies pending drafts), `handleMergeIssue` (HTTP merge endpoint), `handleStartWork`, `handleMergeability`, `handleGetCycles`, `handleCycleProgress`, all label CRUD handlers, and inbox status/read handlers.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":5,"sort_order":"bUh","labels":["improvement","WebApp"]},"created_at":"2026-09-08T12:17:39.695722Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-29495d","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Add test coverage for start.go worktree edge cases","description":"## Problem\n\n`internal/exponential/start.go` has 11 tests but is missing coverage for: worktree setup command (`WorktreeSetup` config), worktree already exists for a different issue, and branch name collision when worktree dir exists but branch doesn't.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":2,"sort_order":"bUi","labels":["improvement","CLI"]},"created_at":"2026-09-08T12:17:41.255649Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-f31793","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Add MCP-layer tests for start and merge tools","description":"## Problem\n\n`internal/mcpserver/tools.go` has 30+ tests but the `start` and `merge` tool handlers are untested at the MCP layer. The `start` handler has mode-override logic (config-copy pattern on lines 513-521) that isn't covered — the same pattern that caused the merge auto-checkout regression.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":3,"sort_order":"bUj","labels":["improvement","CLI"]},"created_at":"2026-09-08T12:17:43.304686Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-ada827","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Add test coverage for checks.go and storage/root.go","description":"## Problem\n\nTwo foundational files have **zero tests**:\n\n- `internal/exponential/checks.go` — `CheckGitRepo`, `CheckGithubWorkflows`, `CheckGitHooks`. Used as guards before git operations. If `CheckGitRepo` misbehaves, worktree/branch logic takes the wrong path silently.\n- `internal/storage/root.go` — `HubRoot()` and `XpoDir()`. Foundational path resolution used by every read/write operation. `HubRoot` caches on first call and `ResetHubRoot` clears it. A stale cache silently corrupts paths across the entire system.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":2,"sort_order":"bUk","labels":["improvement","CLI"]},"created_at":"2026-09-08T12:17:45.707978Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
