{"id":"xpo-5f02c1","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Fix DefaultBranch to detect local default when no remote exists","description":"## Bug\n\n`DefaultBranch()` in `git.go` only checks `refs/remotes/origin/HEAD` and falls back to hardcoded `\"main\"`. In a local-only repo initialized with a non-standard branch (e.g. `trunk`), it returns `\"main\"` — which may not exist. `StartWork` then tries to branch from a nonexistent `main`.\n\nFound by external test coverage audit: the spec for xpo-b83765 required `trunk` → `trunk`, but the test was written to expect the fallback `\"main\"`, locking in the bug.\n\n## Fix\n\nWhen `origin/HEAD` fails, fall back to detecting the current branch via `git symbolic-ref HEAD` (the init branch) before hardcoding `\"main\"`.\n\n## Related\n\n- xpo-b83765 spec line 15 defined the requirement\n- `TestDefaultBranch_FallbackWithoutRemote` needs to expect `\"trunk\"`","status":"PLANNED","estimate":1,"sort_order":"bUf","dependencies":[{"source_id":"xpo-5f02c1","target_id":"xpo-b83765","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug","CLI"]},"created_at":"2026-09-08T12:41:20.624909Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-67f916","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Fix merge abort after squash conflict and restore test contract","description":"## Bug\n\nTwo issues:\n\n1. `git merge --abort` after a failed `--squash` merge does not clean up the index because squash conflicts don't set `MERGE_HEAD`. The working tree remains dirty after the abort.\n2. `TestMergeIssue_Conflict` was written to skip the cleanliness assertion, contradicting the spec (xpo-7a5bba spec line 22) which requires verifying filename in error, abort success, and clean state.\n\n## Fix\n\n1. Replace `git merge --abort` with `git reset --merge` (or `git reset HEAD`) for squash strategy failures — this properly resets the index.\n2. Restore the full test contract: verify conflicting filename in error, clean working tree after abort.\n\n## Related\n\n- xpo-7a5bba spec line 22 defined the full contract\n- `merge.go:163-165` is the abort path","status":"PLANNED","estimate":2,"sort_order":"bUg","dependencies":[{"source_id":"xpo-67f916","target_id":"xpo-7a5bba","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug","CLI"]},"created_at":"2026-09-08T12:41:26.334396Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-c41bea","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Fix sort_order not persisted on status transition","description":"## Bug\n\n`buildUpdate` in `update.go` appends the primary event at line 54, then mutates the payload's `SortOrder` at lines 57-75. Since the event was already appended (copied into the slice), the generated sort order is never persisted.\n\nFound by external audit: `TestUpdateIssue_StatusChange` only checks the resulting status, so the bug stays hidden.\n\n## Fix\n\nMove the sort_order computation before the event append, or mutate the event in the slice after computing the key.\n\n## Related\n\n- `internal/exponential/update.go:54-75`\n- `internal/exponential/update_test.go:10`","status":"PLANNED","estimate":1,"sort_order":"bUh","labels":["bug","CLI"]},"created_at":"2026-09-08T12:41:29.34706Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
