{"id":"xpo-5f02c1","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-7e329b70-517b-424d-bed5-b3f5bde7bbd2","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed `DefaultBranch()` in `git.go` to detect the local default branch when no remote is configured.\n\n**Production change:** New fallback chain in `DefaultBranch()`:\n1. `git symbolic-ref refs/remotes/origin/HEAD` (remote default)\n2. `git config init.defaultBranch` (local git config)\n3. Probe for `main` then `master` branch existence\n4. Hardcoded `\"main\"`\n\nAll three methods use `-C hub` to target the hub root, not the current directory.\n\n**Test changes:**\n- `TestDefaultBranch_FallbackWithoutRemote` → renamed to `TestDefaultBranch_LocalBranchWithoutRemote`, now expects `\"trunk\"` with `init.defaultBranch` set\n- Added `TestDefaultBranch_NoGitRepo` for the final `\"main\"` fallback\n- `initTestRepo` now calls `storage.ResetHubRoot()` for test isolation\n- Added `storage.ResetHubRoot()` to `TestMergeIssue_Squash` (pre-existing test missing it)\n\n## Status\n\n`make test` passes. Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-09-08T12:45:18.642377Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
