{"id":"xpo-3da9ff","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Enforce PLANNED-only start in StartWork","description":"## Bug\n\n`StartWork` accepts BACKLOG issues and transitions them directly to DOING. The xpo workflow requires issues to be in PLANNED status before starting — BACKLOG issues should be rejected with an error telling the user to plan the issue first.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd a guard in `StartWork` that rejects BACKLOG status with a descriptive error. Update or add a test for the BACKLOG → DOING rejection.\n\n## Design decision\n\nPer user: StartWork should only accept PLANNED → DOING. This matches the workflow spec at `.claude/skills/xpo-workflow/SKILL.md:53`.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":1,"sort_order":"bUf","labels":["bug","CLI"]},"created_at":"2026-09-08T12:53:43.637107Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-caf3a6","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Fix MCP merge test to cover default strategy","description":"## Problem\n\n`TestMCPMerge_Squash` explicitly passes `Strategy: \"squash\"` instead of testing the default (empty string). It also only checks for a non-empty SHA — it doesn't verify squash semantics (single-parent commit).\n\n## Fix\n\n- Add `TestMCPMerge_DefaultStrategy` that passes `Strategy: \"\"` and verifies the result is a squash (single-parent commit on main).\n- Existing `TestMCPMerge_Squash` can stay as-is for the explicit case.\n\nFound by external test coverage audit (medium finding).","status":"PLANNED","estimate":1,"sort_order":"bUg","labels":["improvement","CLI"]},"created_at":"2026-09-08T12:53:52.029022Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-2c6717","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Fix remote mutation tests to validate request payloads","description":"## Problem\n\nThe mock server in `remote_transport_test.go` accepts every update, comment, and delete without validating the request. Tests assert only \"no error\" or \"some message\". They would pass if the wrong event type, issue ID, payload, reason, or cascade flag were sent.\n\n## Fix\n\nMake the mock handler validate:\n- Correct HTTP method and path (issue ID in URL)\n- Request body contains expected fields (status, text, reason, cascade)\n- Return errors for malformed or unexpected requests\n\nUpdate the tests to verify the returned messages reference the correct issue.\n\nFound by external test coverage audit (medium finding).","status":"PLANNED","estimate":2,"sort_order":"bUh","labels":["improvement","CLI"]},"created_at":"2026-09-08T12:53:59.88447Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
