{"id":"xpo-328657","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Fix low-priority test assertion quality issues from audit","description":"## Problem\n\nExternal audit identified several tests with weak assertions that would pass on incorrect behavior:\n\n1. `TestFilterIssues_NoFilters_DoneCountLimited` asserts `doneCount \u003c= 3` — returning zero completed issues passes (`list_test.go:76-94`)\n2. Force-worktree takeover (`TestStartWork_Worktree_ForceRemovesExisting`) checks message and non-empty path but doesn't verify the recreated worktree exists on disk (`start_test.go:407-439`)\n3. `FindIssue` archive fallback at `local_transport.go:87-122` is untested — only active-store path has coverage\n4. Three `GetIssue` tests duplicate `resolve_test.go` while harder archive/ambiguity interactions are omitted\n\n## Fix\n\n1. Tighten `DoneCountLimited` assertion to verify `doneCount \u003e 0 \u0026\u0026 doneCount \u003c= 3`\n2. Add `os.Stat` check on the worktree path after force takeover\n3. Add `TestFindIssue_ArchivedFallback` that seeds an issue in the archive and verifies `FindIssue` returns it with `archived=true`\n4. Remove duplicate `GetIssue` tests from `local_transport_test.go` that overlap with `resolve_test.go`; add `TestGetIssue_AmbiguousShortID` instead","status":"PLANNED","estimate":2,"sort_order":"bUf","labels":["improvement","CLI"]},"created_at":"2026-09-08T13:00:57.244998Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
