{"id":"xpo-961910","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"## Feature\n\nAdd an optional `default_branch` field to `.xpo/config.yaml` that explicitly sets the base branch for branching, merging, and diff operations. This is the most reliable signal — it's explicit, doesn't depend on git state, and survives clone/worktree/CI scenarios where `init.defaultBranch` or remote `HEAD` might not be set.\n\n## Design\n\n**Config field:** `default_branch: \"main\"` (or `trunk`, `develop`, etc.)\n\n**`DefaultBranch()` fallback chain becomes:**\n1. `Config.DefaultBranch` (explicit, authoritative)\n2. `origin/HEAD` (remote default)\n3. `init.defaultBranch` (local git config)\n4. Probe `main`/`master`\n5. Hardcoded `\"main\"`\n\n**Signature change:** `DefaultBranch()` is currently a package-level function with no config access. It needs to either become a method on `Client` or accept the config value as a parameter. Callers (`StartWork`, `MergeIssue`, `resolveIssueBranch`, etc.) already have `c.Config`.\n\n**`xpo init`:** could auto-detect and write the field.\n\n## Callers to update\n\n- `StartWork` (start.go)\n- `MergeIssue` (merge.go)\n- `resolveIssueBranch` (server/handlers.go)\n- `HubCleanForMerge` (merge.go)\n- Any CLI commands that call `DefaultBranch()` directly","estimate":2,"labels":["feature","CLI"],"sort_order":"bUf","status":"PLANNED","title":"Add optional default_branch config to .xpo/config.yaml"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T13:06:06.765254Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
