{"id":"xpo-961910","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-8539f3f3-9f30-4783-95a0-8a55164706ba","text":"## Implementation Complete\n\n### Summary\n\nAdded `default_branch` config field and a global config accessor (`config.Get()` / `config.Set()`) so `DefaultBranch()` can read config without parameter threading.\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n- `internal/config/config.go` — added `DefaultBranch` field to `Config` struct; added `Get()`, `Set()`, `Reset()` global accessor functions using `sync.RWMutex`\n- `internal/exponential/git.go` — `DefaultBranch()` now checks `config.Get().DefaultBranch` as the first step in its fallback chain, before any git commands\n- `cmd/exponential/main.go` — wired `config.Set(cfg)` after `LoadConfig()` in `PersistentPreRunE`\n- `internal/exponential/setup.go` — `xpo init` auto-detects and writes `default_branch` to the config template\n- `internal/config/config_test.go` — tests for global accessor, config loading with/without `default_branch`\n- `internal/exponential/git_test.go` — tests for config override, empty config fallthrough, nil config fallthrough\n\n### Rationale\n\nKept `DefaultBranch()` as a zero-arg package-level function. The global config accessor follows the same singleton pattern as `storage.HubRoot()`. No caller changes needed — the 14 existing call sites work as-is.\n\n### Decisions made\n\n- Used `sync.RWMutex` over `atomic.Pointer` for clarity (set-once, read-many pattern)\n- `Get()` returns `*Config` (may be nil) — intentional for `xpo init` where no config exists yet\n- Placed `default_branch` early in the config template (after `prefix`) for visibility\n\n### Status\n\n`make test` passes (go vet + eslint + all Go tests). Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-09-08T13:22:23.064106Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
