{"id":"xpo-4ded6b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Redesign keyboard help overlay: view-aware, live search, new layout","description":"## What\n\nRedesign the `KeyboardHelp` overlay to be view-aware, searchable, and better organized.\n\n### Current problems\n\n- The overlay dumps all shortcut groups in a flat 2-column grid with no awareness of which view is active\n- Shortcut data is hardcoded in the component, completely disconnected from actual handlers — docs drift from reality\n- No way to search/filter shortcuts\n- Missing sections entirely (Board, My Issues)\n\n### Requirements\n\n**View-aware display**\n- The overlay knows which view is active and shows that view's shortcuts prominently (expanded by default)\n- Global shortcuts always visible\n- Other views' shortcuts collapsed or secondary\n\n**Live search**\n- Search input auto-focused on open\n- Filters across all shortcuts by key name, description, or group\n- Instant filtering as you type\n\n**New layout**\n- Organized by collapsible sections instead of a flat grid\n- Current view's section expanded, others collapsed\n- Compact kbd badges on the right, descriptions on the left\n\n### Prerequisite\n\nDepends on xpo-caf557 (`useViewKeyboard` hook) — the centralized shortcut registry provides the data source so the overlay reads from the same definitions the views actually use, eliminating doc drift.","status":"PLANNED","parent_id":"xpo-570a07","estimate":3,"sort_order":"bUf","dependencies":[{"source_id":"xpo-4ded6b","target_id":"xpo-caf557","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["feature","frontend"]},"created_at":"2026-09-08T13:53:03.478049Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
