{"id":"xpo-87503f","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-76d4627e-ce93-4719-9222-aa6ec0ecd9e4","text":"## Summary\n\nAdded a **Board** section to the `?` keyboard help overlay in `KeyboardHelp.tsx`, documenting all existing Board shortcuts: J/K navigation, arrow column switching, Enter to open, S/L/E quick-set, 1–7 column status, and `.` to copy ID.\n\n## Rationale\n\nThe Board view already had full keyboard support — `S`/`L`/`E` handlers and `1`–`7` column shortcuts were implemented in `Board.tsx` but never documented in the help overlay. No handler changes needed; this is purely a documentation fix.\n\n## Decisions made\n\n- Placed the Board section between Backlog and Issue Detail in the group order — matches the nav order\n- Used \"1–7\" (en-dash range) matching the existing \"1–5\" style in the Issue Detail section\n\n## Status\n\n`make test` passes (lint + Go tests). Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-09-08T13:54:46.744971Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
