{"id":"xpo-0b193b","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-73c48c6c-9ad8-42f6-9278-e56faf4cc12f","text":"## Implementation complete\n\n### Summary\nAdded a `useEffect` in `IssueDetail.tsx` that clears the `artifactContent` cache when `issue.updated_at` changes. This is the only change — the SSE pipeline already works correctly.\n\n### Root cause\nThe artifact fetch effect at line 108 had `if (artifactContent[filename] !== undefined) return;` which prevented re-fetching once content was cached. The cache was only cleared on `issue.id` change (navigating to a different issue), never on `issue.updated_at` change.\n\n### Fix\n```tsx\nuseEffect(() =\u003e {\n  setArtifactContent({});\n}, [issue.updated_at]);\n```\n\nPlaced before the fetch effect. When `updated_at` changes (triggered by the SSE → re-fetch chain), the cache is cleared, then the fetch effect runs and sees `artifactContent[filename] === undefined`, triggering a fresh fetch.\n\n### Why a separate effect\nThe existing `issue.id` reset (line 80-88) also resets UI state (active tab, editing fields, comments). An `updated_at` change should only invalidate cached content, not reset the user's UI context.\n\n### Status\n- `make test` passes\n- Ready for review"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T14:36:35.197723Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
