{"id":"xpo-958474","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-b85db1b1-6237-4a58-8f16-f9cbd9ef6002","text":"## Implementation complete\n\n### Summary\nTwo CSS changes in `web/src/index.css`:\n\n1. **Checkbox border**: `--color-border-default` (`#282828`) → `--color-border-control` (`#404040`) — uses the design system's dedicated control border token, nearly doubling contrast against the `#0f0f0f` background\n2. **Task list padding**: `padding-left: 0.25em` → `0` on `ul.contains-task-list` — checkboxes now align flush-left with surrounding content\n3. **Checkbox margin-right**: `0.25em` → `0.5em` — slightly more breathing room between checkbox and label text\n\n### Status\n- Lint passes\n- Ready for review"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T14:40:22.323829Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-0b193b","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"When an artifact file (spec.md or walkthrough.md) is modified on disk (e.g. by an agent writing a spec), the issue detail panel does not re-render to show the updated content. The user must navigate away and back.\n\n### Expected\n\nSSE events for artifact changes should trigger a re-fetch of the artifact content in the detail panel.\n\n### Found during\n\nTophatting xpo-c08d52 lint fixes"},"created_at":"2026-09-08T14:45:14.135047Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"web"}
