{"id":"xpo-db1b0a","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-27d10816-aeed-4bad-b8ff-6305c36b255b","text":"## Summary\n\nFixed the crash in `MergeView.tsx` when `branch_stats` becomes `undefined` after a merge completes.\n\n**Changes in `web/src/components/IssueDetail/MergeView.tsx`:**\n- Removed the non-null assertion (`issue.branch_stats!`) at line 91, replaced with a plain assignment\n- Changed the `useEffect` dependency from `bs.head_sha` to `bs?.head_sha` (optional chaining)\n- Guarded `defaultCommitMessage` to use `issue.branch_stats?.branch` with a fallback to `issue.id`\n- Added an early return rendering a \"Branch merged\" state when `branch_stats` is `undefined`, placed after the loading/error guards so all hooks remain unconditional\n\n## Rationale\n\nThe early-return pattern is the cleanest fix here — once `branch_stats` is gone, the merge view's diff/stats content is meaningless (the merge already happened). Showing a brief \"branch merged\" indicator with a close button lets the user dismiss the stale view gracefully rather than seeing a crash.\n\n## Status\n\n`make test` passes (lint + Go tests), `tsc` passes with no type errors. Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-09-08T14:52:47.821542Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-46c418","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Add vitest for frontend unit tests","description":"## Feature\n\nAdd vitest as the frontend test framework and write initial tests for the pure utility functions that are easiest to cover and most likely to catch regressions.\n\n### Why\n\nThe frontend has no test coverage. Components like `MergeView` have pure utility functions (`parseDiffByFile`, `addLineNumbers`, `buildFileTree`, `flattenSingleChildDirs`, `buildSplitLines`) that are straightforward to test and have caused bugs in the past (e.g. xpo-db1b0a). vitest is the natural choice since it shares Vite's transform pipeline — near-zero config.\n\n### Scope\n\n1. Install `vitest` and add a `test` script to `web/package.json`\n2. Wire vitest into `make test` alongside the Go tests\n3. Write initial tests for the pure utility functions in the codebase:\n   - `parseDiffByFile` (MergeView)\n   - `addLineNumbers` (MergeView)\n   - `buildFileTree` / `flattenSingleChildDirs` (MergeView)\n   - `buildSplitLines` (MergeView)\n   - `formatRelativeTime` (utils/format)\n4. Optionally add `@testing-library/react` for component-level smoke tests later","status":"BACKLOG","parent_id":"xpo-f539b6","estimate":3,"sort_order":"bYg","dependencies":[{"source_id":"xpo-46c418","target_id":"xpo-db1b0a","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["feature","frontend","testing"]},"created_at":"2026-09-08T14:53:56.614139Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
