{"id":"xpo-e1acfd","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-88218754-a178-4c9c-a32d-2f2d28cd51e6","text":"## Summary\n\nChanged the global scrollbar thumb color from `--color-border-default` (#282828) to `--color-text-muted` in `web/src/index.css` — both the webkit and standards-track scrollbar declarations.\n\nThe root cause: in dark mode, `--color-border-default` (#282828) is nearly indistinguishable from `--color-surface-3` (#222222), making scrollbar thumbs invisible inside menus and popovers. This made it look like item hover backgrounds didn't extend to the full menu width — the scrollbar gutter was taking up 6px of space but the thumb was invisible.\n\n**Scoped to this issue:** global scrollbar contrast fix (2 lines in `index.css`).\n\n**Deferred to xpo-5d1c38 / xpo-de8d06:** the `scrollbar-gutter: stable` fix for consistent item widths in scrollable menus — belongs in the Popover/Menu component extraction where it can be applied once to all menus.\n\nLinked this issue to both for tracking.\n\n## Status\n\n`make lint` passes. Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-09-08T15:17:08.876779Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
