{"id":"xpo-ceb434","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-4715c5f9-7426-430b-bdaf-75bf806ee49d","text":"## Implementation Complete\n\n### Summary\n\nSplit `xpo init` into three focused subcommands and refactored `xpo doctor` into a three-section universal health check.\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `internal/exponential/agents.go` — added `MCPConfigSpec` struct, `GlobalSkillDir` field on `AgentConfig`, trimmed `AgentRegistry` to 6 harnesses (Generic Agent, Claude Code, GitHub Copilot, Cursor, Codex, OpenCode), added `EnsureMCPConfigFor()`/`DetectMCPConfigFor()` supporting JSON and TOML formats, `LookupAgent()`, `DetectSkillInstall()`, `WriteAgentSkill()` with global install + symlink support\n- `internal/exponential/agents_test.go` — 20 new tests for TOML/JSON MCP config, agent lookup, skill install detection, registry validation\n- `cmd/exponential/init.go` — stripped Phase 2 (MCP/agents/skills), now config-only + hints for next steps\n- `cmd/exponential/init_mcp.go` — new subcommand with `--harness` and `--force` flags, per-harness MCP config\n- `cmd/exponential/init_skill.go` — new interactive subcommand with `--harness`, `--global`, `--local`, `--force` flags, handles agent instruction file edge cases (create/append/replace)\n- `cmd/exponential/doctor.go` — reorganized into three sections: Project Configuration, MCP Configuration, Agent Integration\n- `cmd/exponential/main.go` — `PersistentPreRunE` now uses parent-chain check so `init mcp`/`init skill` work without config\n\n### Rationale\n\nThree-way split mirrors the actual concerns: project data, transport (MCP), and content (skills). Each subcommand is independently runnable and idempotent.\n\n### Decisions made\n\n- TOML MCP config (Codex) uses string-based append rather than a TOML library — simpler, preserves existing content, avoids a new dependency\n- `PersistentPreRunE` uses `commandOrAncestorAllowed()` to walk the parent chain instead of adding \"mcp\"/\"skill\" to the flat allowlist — avoids collision with the existing `xpo mcp` server command\n- `resolveAgents()` helper shared between `init_mcp.go` and `init_skill.go` for `--harness` flag handling\n\n### Status\n\n`make test` passes (go vet + eslint + 255 frontend tests + Go tests). Ready for review.\n"},"created_at":"2026-09-09T13:51:54.572639Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.266 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
