{"id":"xpo-dd97a5","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-f52a7034-3754-4446-89a0-9e98f3edfcd2","text":"## Implementation Complete\n\n### Summary\n\nUpdated `GenerateSkillMD()`, `generateWorkflowBody()`, and `generateMCPToolsBody()` in `internal/exponential/agents.go` to match the v3.1 reference skill.\n\n### Changes\n\n- **Frontmatter**: `name: xpo` (was `xpo-workflow`), `version: \"3.1\"` (was `\"1.0\"`)\n- **Workflow steps**: renamed and restructured (Discover→\"Check existing work\", Completion Comment→\"Handoff\", Review \u0026 Spec Update→\"Revisions\"), added explicit gates, self-review before handoff, `rationale` tool usage in spec step\n- **Reference section**: added Issue Labels (primary/secondary system with `bug`/`feature`/`task`/`epic`), Backlog Review, status table with CANCELED/DUPLICATE\n- **MCP tools**: added `rationale` row\n- **`GenerateAgentDocs()`**: updated intro to match v3 style\n- Fixed one test assertion that checked for old skill name in content\n\n### Status\n\n`make test` passes. Ready for review.\n"},"created_at":"2026-09-09T14:47:38.206437Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.266 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-76e2a1","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Polish first-run CLI UX for init, init mcp, init skill","description":"## Summary\n\nThe `xpo init` / `xpo init mcp` / `xpo init skill` flow works correctly but the CLI output needs UX polish. The first-run experience is the first impression users have of the tool and it should feel intentional and guided, not like raw debug output.\n\n## Areas to address\n\n- **Guided first-run flow**: consider whether `xpo init` should walk the user through MCP + skill setup in one shot (wizard-style) rather than requiring three separate commands\n- **Output formatting**: review spacing, alignment, and visual hierarchy across all three commands\n- **Interactive prompts**: the prefix prompt is a good start — extend the pattern to harness selection and scope choice so the flow feels cohesive\n- **Non-interactive mode**: ensure headless/piped usage produces clean, parseable output\n- **Error states**: what happens when the user runs `xpo init mcp` before `xpo init`? The error message should be helpful, not just \"not found\"\n- **`xpo doctor` output**: the three-section layout works but could be tighter — consider whether the fix hints are actionable enough\n\n## Context\n\nThis follows xpo-ceb434 (init subcommand split) and xpo-dd97a5 (v3 skill + CLI polish). The structural work is done — this issue is purely about making the experience feel polished.","status":"BACKLOG","sort_order":"bc2","dependencies":[{"source_id":"xpo-76e2a1","target_id":"xpo-ceb434","kind":"relates_to"},{"source_id":"xpo-76e2a1","target_id":"xpo-dd97a5","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["task","ux"]},"created_at":"2026-09-09T15:31:34.917951Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.266 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
