{"id":"xpo-fad57f","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-587c029a-016a-4627-8800-8293e27c9699","text":"## Implementation complete\n\n### Summary\n\nReplaced the working-directory-based mergeability check with a proper committed-ref comparison using `git merge-tree --write-tree`.\n\n**`internal/exponential/merge.go`:**\n- Added `CheckMergeConflicts(branch)` — uses `git merge-tree --write-tree` to test whether committed refs merge cleanly, ignoring working-directory state entirely\n- Added `HubRequireCleanTree()` — simple guard for dirty tracked files with clear \"uncommitted changes — commit or discard before merging\" message\n- Added `HubDirtyTrackedFiles()` — returns dirty tracked files for warning purposes\n- Refactored `HubCleanForMerge(branch)` to delegate to `CheckMergeConflicts` + `HubRequireCleanTree` (preserves existing callers in CLI and MCP)\n\n**`internal/server/handlers.go`:**\n- `handleMergeability` now uses `CheckMergeConflicts` for blockers and `HubDirtyTrackedFiles` for warnings — uncommitted changes no longer block the read-only check\n- `handleMergeIssue` checks merge conflicts and clean tree separately with distinct error messages\n- Response now includes `warnings` array alongside `blockers`\n\n**`web/src/api/client.ts`:** Added `warnings` field to `Mergeability` interface\n\n**`web/src/components/IssueDetail/MergeView.tsx`:** Displays warnings (amber text) below the merge status\n\n### Rationale\n\n`git merge-tree --write-tree` performs an in-memory merge between committed refs without touching the working tree. This is the correct tool for answering \"can this branch merge?\" — the old approach conflated working-directory overlap with merge conflicts.\n\n### Decisions made\n\n- `HubRequireCleanTree` blocks on *any* dirty tracked file, not just those overlapping with the branch. Simpler and safer for the pre-merge guard.\n- Kept `HubCleanForMerge` as a convenience that delegates to both new functions — avoids changing CLI and MCP callers unnecessarily.\n\n### Status\n\n`make test` passes — lint, 255 frontend tests, Go tests all green. Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-09-09T15:57:00.311614Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.266 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-110b09","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Highlight uncommitted files in MergeView file tree","description":"## Feature\n\nIn the MergeView file tree, highlight files that have uncommitted or untracked changes in the worktree with an amber color indicator. This gives the user immediate visibility into which files are blocking the merge without needing to open the blocker detail modal.\n\n### Approach\n\n- Wire the `warnings` or a new `dirty_files` field from the mergeability response into the file tree component\n- Files that appear in the dirty list get an amber highlight or badge\n- Pairs with the worktree cleanliness check added in xpo-fad57f","status":"BACKLOG","sort_order":"bd4","dependencies":[{"source_id":"xpo-110b09","target_id":"xpo-fad57f","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["feature","Frontend"]},"created_at":"2026-09-09T16:54:46.493519Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.266 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
