{"id":"xpo-110b09","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-b9ce4251-2aad-47c5-8855-874194ec64da","text":"## Implementation complete\n\n### Summary\n\nAdded amber highlighting for uncommitted/untracked files in the MergeView file tree.\n\n**`internal/server/handlers.go`:** Added `dirty_files` top-level array to the mergeability response, surfacing the worktree dirty file paths directly (previously only available inside blocker internals). Always returns `[]` when clean, never null.\n\n**`web/src/api/client.ts`:** Added `dirty_files: string[]` to the `Mergeability` interface.\n\n**`web/src/components/IssueDetail/diff-utils.ts`:** Added `hasDirtyDescendant(dirPath, dirtyFiles)` utility that checks if any file in the dirty set is a descendant of a directory path (uses prefix matching with trailing `/` to avoid false matches on similarly-named directories).\n\n**`web/src/components/IssueDetail/MergeView.tsx`:**\n- `MergeView`: builds `dirtyFilesSet` from `mergeability.dirty_files` and passes it to `FilesTab`\n- `FilesTab`: accepts and threads `dirtyFiles: Set\u003cstring\u003e` to `FileTreeView`\n- `FileTreeView`: accepts `dirtyFiles` prop. Files in the dirty set get `text-amber-500` icon color with \"Uncommitted changes\" tooltip. Directories with dirty descendants get amber coloring with \"Contains uncommitted changes\" tooltip. Amber takes priority over green/red diff coloring.\n\n### Rationale\n\nKept the dirty files as a top-level field rather than requiring frontend parsing of blocker internals — cleaner API contract and no coupling to the blocker message format.\n\n### Status\n\n`make test` passes — lint, 260 frontend tests (including 5 new `hasDirtyDescendant` tests), and all Go tests green. Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-09-09T17:07:37.386539Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.266 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-6211f5","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"MergeView: uncommitted vs committed diff toggle","description":"## Feature\n\nAdd a view toggle to the MergeView Files tab that lets the user switch between:\n\n1. **All changes** (default) — the full branch diff against main, as it works today\n2. **Uncommitted** — only uncommitted/untracked changes in the worktree (working tree vs HEAD)\n\n### Motivation\n\nWhen an agent is actively making changes to a branch or worktree, the user wants to follow along in real time. The current \"all changes\" view mixes committed work with the agent's in-progress edits, making it hard to see what just changed. An \"uncommitted\" view isolates the live delta so the user can review incremental work as it happens.\n\n### Approach\n\n- **Backend**: Add a new endpoint (or query parameter on the existing diff endpoint) that returns `git diff HEAD` from the worktree instead of the branch-vs-main diff\n- **Frontend**: Add a segmented toggle (e.g. \"All changes\" / \"Uncommitted\") above the file tree in the Files tab. When \"Uncommitted\" is selected, fetch and display the uncommitted diff instead, and filter the file tree to only show dirty files\n- The uncommitted view should also show untracked files (via `git diff HEAD` + `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard`)\n\n### Notes\n\n- The `dirty_files` list from the mergeability response (xpo-110b09) can seed the file tree filter, but the actual diff content needs a separate fetch\n- Consider auto-refreshing or polling when the uncommitted view is active, since the working tree is changing in real time","status":"BACKLOG","sort_order":"be6","dependencies":[{"source_id":"xpo-6211f5","target_id":"xpo-110b09","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["feature","Frontend","Backend"]},"created_at":"2026-09-09T19:03:23.025204Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.266 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
