{"id":"xpo-3b2ec1","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Tests fail when git init.defaultBranch != main","description":"## Problem\n\nThe test suite assumes `git init` creates a `main` branch, but this depends on the machine's\n`init.defaultBranch` git config. On machines configured with `master` (or any other name),\ndozens of tests fail across `internal/exponential` and `internal/mcpserver`.\n\n## Failing test categories\n\n1. **Default branch detection** — `TestDefaultBranch_*` expects `main` as the git fallback\n2. **Merge tests** — test repos land on `master`, then code tries to merge into `main`\n3. **Start/worktree tests** — worktree creation fails because the base branch name is wrong\n4. **MCP start/merge tests** — same root cause via the MCP layer\n\n## Root cause\n\nTest helpers call `git init` without `-b main`, inheriting whatever the system default is.\n\n## Fix\n\nEnsure all test git-init calls explicitly use `-b main` so tests are deterministic regardless\nof the machine's git configuration.","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"bUg","labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-09-09T19:13:03.163308057Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.263 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
