{"id":"xpo-6211f5","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-68727ab2-bf66-434f-8980-fc3599571459","text":"## Implementation complete\n\n### Summary\n\nAdded a scope toggle to the MergeView Files tab that lets users switch between \"All changes\" (branch vs main) and \"Uncommitted\" (working tree vs HEAD), with 3-second auto-refresh polling for live follow-along during agent sessions.\n\n**`internal/exponential/review.go`:** Added three helpers — `listUntrackedFiles(dir)` lists untracked files via `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard` (filtering `.xpo/`), `buildSyntheticDiff(path, content)` generates a unified diff entry for untracked files (new file mode, `/dev/null` origin, all lines as additions), and `isBinary(data)` detects binary files via null byte check. Two new public functions: `GetWorkingTreeFullDiffText(dir)` combines `git diff HEAD` with synthetic diffs for untracked files (skipping binary and \u003e1 MB files), and `ListWorkingTreeAllFilesChanged(dir)` merges `ListWorkingTreeFilesChanged` with untracked files as status `A` entries with line-counted insertions.\n\n**`internal/server/handlers.go`:** Added `resolveWorkingDir(branch)` helper that returns the worktree path if one exists, or `\"\"` if the branch is the current branch, enabling both worktree and branch-mode support. Updated `handleGetIssueDiff` and `handleGetIssueFiles` to accept a `?scope=uncommitted` query parameter — when set, they use the new full-diff/all-files functions via the resolved working directory; returns 404 if neither worktree nor current branch applies.\n\n**`web/src/api/client.ts`:** Added optional `scope` parameter to `fetchIssueDiff` and `fetchIssueFiles`, appending `?scope=uncommitted` when set.\n\n**`web/src/components/IssueDetail/MergeView.tsx`:**\n- `MergeView`: added `diffScope`, `uncommittedDiff`, `uncommittedLoading` state. Added `refreshUncommitted()` with in-flight guard via `refreshingRef`. A `useEffect` sets up 3-second polling when `diffScope === \"uncommitted\"` AND `activeTab === \"files\"`, clearing on scope/tab change. `handleScopeChange` clears `selectedFile` on switch. Passes `activeFileDiffs` (scope-dependent) to `FilesTab`.\n- `FilesTab`: accepts `diffScope`, `onScopeChange`, `uncommittedLoading` props. Renders a segmented toggle (\"All changes\" / \"Uncommitted\") above the file filter, using the same button group pattern as the Unified/Split toggle. When uncommitted scope is active and the diff is empty (and not loading), shows a centered \"No uncommitted changes\" empty state.\n\n### Rationale\n\n- Query parameter on existing endpoints (not new endpoints) keeps the API surface small.\n- Synthetic diffs for untracked files are read-only and safe — no index modification via `git add -N`.\n- `resolveWorkingDir` handles both worktree and branch-mode transparently — toggle is always available when the issue has a branch.\n- Polling with in-flight guard prevents overlapping requests during slow diffs.\n\n### Status\n\n`make test` passes — lint (`go vet` + eslint), 263 frontend tests (including 3 new synthetic diff parsing tests), and all Go tests (including 4 new `GetWorkingTreeFullDiffText`/`ListWorkingTreeAllFilesChanged` tests) green. Ready for review."},"created_at":"2026-09-09T19:38:47.093655Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.266 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
