{"id":"xpo-d47781","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-1557e07a-ba00-4dde-806c-020777ba1b39","text":"## Review revision complete\n\nRemoved the duplicated per-consumer `TAB_ITEMS` adapters identified in review. `Tabs` now accepts each view's existing keyed `TAB_CONFIGS` directly and owns the single `Object.entries` normalization used for rendering and keyboard order. The spec was updated first to record this API decision.\n\nVerification remains green: `make test` (267 frontend tests plus Go suite), production build, ESLint, and `git diff --check`. Ready for another review."},"created_at":"2026-09-10T12:47:35.386842Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.154.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-54a423","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"MergeView \"Files changed\" count ignores uncommitted changes","description":"When a worktree has no commits but has uncommitted changes, the Review pane's \"Files changed\" tab always shows **0** because its count is derived solely from `fetchIssueFiles()` (committed changes).\n\nTwo symptoms:\n\n1. **Tab badge shows 0** — The `files.length` count on the \"Files changed\" tab only reflects committed files. When there are only uncommitted changes, it stays at 0 even when the \"Uncommitted\" toggle shows a full file list with diffs.\n\n2. **\"All Changes\" is empty** — With no commits, the \"All Changes\" view shows nothing. The intent of \"All Changes\" should be the union of committed + uncommitted changes, but it currently only shows committed diffs.\n\n**Root cause:** `MergeView.tsx` line 511 uses `files.length` (from `fetchIssueFiles`) for the tab count. This endpoint only returns files from committed changes. The uncommitted file diffs (`uncommittedFileDiffs`) are never factored into the count. Additionally, the \"All Changes\" scope shows only `fileDiffs` (committed diff) without merging in uncommitted changes.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":2,"sort_order":"bUg","labels":["bug","frontend"]},"created_at":"2026-09-10T12:49:44.788827Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.267 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
