{"id":"xpo-54a423","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","sort_order":"a1","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-09-10T12:50:34.59319Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.267 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-54a423","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-1eec47ad-06e0-44d8-876f-b5216473dc46","text":"Fix implemented in `MergeView.tsx`. Three changes:\n\n1. **Eagerly fetch uncommitted diff on mount** — added `fetchIssueDiff(issue.id, \"uncommitted\")` to the initial `Promise.all` in `refreshData`, so uncommitted diffs are always available (not only when the user toggles to \"Uncommitted\").\n\n2. **\"All Changes\" falls back to uncommitted diffs** — when `diffScope === \"all\"` and there are no committed diffs (`fileDiffs.size === 0`), `activeFileDiffs` now falls back to `uncommittedFileDiffs`. This means worktrees with only uncommitted changes show those changes in the default view.\n\n3. **Tab count uses active diffs** — changed `count: files.length` to `count: activeFileDiffs.size` so the badge dynamically reflects whichever scope is active. This also allowed removing the `files` state, the `fetchIssueFiles` call, and the `FileInfo` import — they were only used for that count.\n\nAll tests pass (`make test`: 263 frontend tests, lint clean, all Go tests green)."},"created_at":"2026-09-10T12:53:18.224909Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.267 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-caf557","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"title":"Centralize keyboard navigation with provider and shortcut registry","description":"## What\n\nReplace the application's scattered document-level keyboard listeners with a central `KeyboardNavProvider` and shortcut registry. The provider owns the single `document.keydown` listener; global features, active views, overlays, and reusable controls declare bindings through a registration hook.\n\n## Current problem\n\n`App` and multiple views independently install `document.addEventListener(\"keydown\", ...)` handlers. This duplicates guards and cleanup, makes collision behavior depend on listener order, scatters popover suppression, and encourages visual primitives such as `Tabs` to install more global listeners.\n\nThe originally proposed `useViewKeyboard` hook would remove boilerplate but would still install one document listener per caller, so it does not address the architectural problem.\n\n## Target API\n\n```tsx\n\u003cKeyboardNavProvider\u003e\n  \u003cApp /\u003e\n\u003c/KeyboardNavProvider\u003e\n\nuseKeyboardShortcuts({\n  scope: \"tabs\",\n  priority: \"control\",\n  enabled: !popoverOpen,\n  shortcuts: [\n    {\n      id: \"tabs.previous\",\n      key: \"[\",\n      label: \"Previous tab\",\n      run: selectPreviousTab,\n    },\n  ],\n});\n```\n\n## Responsibilities\n\n- Exactly one document-level keyboard listener\n- Central editable-target, composition, modifier, repeat, and `preventDefault` policy\n- Scoped registrations with explicit priority\n- Stable callbacks without repeated listener installation\n- Deterministic collision handling with development warnings\n- Single-key, modified-key, and multi-key sequence support\n- Registration metadata suitable for future view-aware keyboard help\n\n## Migration scope\n\nMigrate the global shortcuts in `App` and the existing view-level handlers in Backlog, Board, My Issues, Inbox, and Dependencies. Reusable controls may register their own semantic shortcuts without directly accessing `document`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Exactly one application-owned `document.keydown` listener remains\n- [ ] All current global and migrated view shortcuts retain their behavior\n- [ ] Editable fields, modifier keys, composition, repeats, and open overlays follow explicit central policy\n- [ ] Active higher-priority scopes take precedence deterministically\n- [ ] Conflicting active bindings are surfaced during development\n- [ ] Shortcut callbacks always see current component state\n- [ ] Shortcut metadata can be consumed by the future keyboard-help redesign\n- [ ] Unit tests cover dispatch, precedence, guards, conflicts, cleanup, and sequences\n- [ ] Build, lint, frontend tests, and repository tests pass","estimate":5,"dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-09-10T13:01:16.285192Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.154.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
