{"id":"xpo-54a423","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-09b925f0-1ca6-4391-9a30-a22e7aeec87f","text":"Updated: moved the scope selector into the tab bar row (right-aligned, before the refresh button) instead of a separate secondary toolbar. No vertical space wasted — the toggle only renders when the \"Files changed\" tab is active.\n\nLayout: `[Commits 0] [Files changed N] [Conversation 3]  ···  [All changes | Uncommitted] [↻]`"},"created_at":"2026-09-10T13:07:06.059387Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.267 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-caf557","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## What\n\nReplace all scattered document-level keyboard listeners with a central `KeyboardNavProvider` and shortcut registry. The provider owns the sole `document.keydown` listener; global features, active views, overlays, and reusable controls declare semantic bindings through `useKeyboardShortcuts`.\n\n## Why\n\nIndependent listeners duplicate guards and cleanup, allow collisions to depend on mount/listener order, scatter overlay suppression, and encourage visual primitives to install global handlers. The original `useViewKeyboard` proposal would only hide that duplication while retaining one document listener per caller.\n\n## Core API\n\n- `KeyboardNavProvider` — owns event dispatch and the registry\n- `useKeyboardShortcuts(registration)` — registers bindings without installing a listener\n- `useActiveShortcuts()` — exposes help-ready metadata for currently active global, view, control, and overlay registrations\n\nBindings include a stable ID, key or sequence, label, group, scope/priority, callback, enabled state, modifier/repeat/default-prevention policy, and `showInHelp`.\n\n## Responsibilities\n\n- Exactly one application-owned document keydown listener\n- Central editable-target, composition, modifier, repeat, sequence, and default-prevention policy\n- Explicit priority: overlay \u003e control \u003e view \u003e global\n- Stable current callbacks and deterministic collision handling\n- Single-key, modified-key, and multi-key sequence support\n- Active registration metadata as the canonical shortcut-help source\n\n## Migration scope\n\nMigrate global shortcuts in `App` and view handlers in Backlog, Board, My Issues, Inbox, and Dependencies. Reusable controls may register semantic shortcuts without touching `document`.\n\n`KeyboardHelp` is a normal registry client: it registers its always-mounted `?` toggle and its enabled-only-while-open Escape binding, then `xpo-4ded6b` will render `useActiveShortcuts()`. The provider remains UI-agnostic and does not render help.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Exactly one application-owned document keydown listener remains\n- [ ] Existing global and migrated view shortcuts retain behavior\n- [ ] Priority, guards, conflicts, sequences, enabled state, callback freshness, and cleanup are tested\n- [ ] `KeyboardHelp` can register `?`/Escape without a direct listener\n- [ ] Active help metadata includes global plus current view/control bindings\n- [ ] Build, lint, frontend tests, and repository tests pass","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-09-10T13:11:11.55758Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.154.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-4ded6b","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"title":"Make keyboard help registry-driven and view-aware","description":"## What\n\nMake `KeyboardHelp` a registry-driven, view-aware consumer of the keyboard infrastructure from `xpo-caf557`. The component remains mounted while closed, registers its own toggle/close shortcuts, and renders only shortcuts relevant to the current UI context.\n\n## Why\n\nThe current overlay duplicates shortcut definitions in a static list that can drift from real behavior. Showing shortcuts for unmounted views would require a second catalog and undermine the registry as the canonical source of truth.\n\n## Behavior\n\n- Register `?` through `useKeyboardShortcuts` to toggle the help overlay\n- Register Escape at overlay priority only while help is open\n- Read shortcut metadata through `useActiveShortcuts()`\n- Show global shortcuts plus the current view's and active controls' shortcuts\n- Exclude inactive/unmounted views\n- Exclude bindings marked `showInHelp: false`\n- Preserve a clear grouped layout and keyboard-key badges\n- Keep the search/filter interaction only if it remains useful for the active shortcut set\n\n## Dependency\n\nDepends on `xpo-caf557`, which supplies the provider, registration API, active-scope metadata, and sole document listener.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] No hardcoded duplicate shortcut catalog remains in `KeyboardHelp`\n- [ ] `?` opens and closes help through the registry\n- [ ] Escape closes help through an overlay-priority registration\n- [ ] Displayed shortcuts are limited to global plus current view/control context\n- [ ] Shortcut labels, keys, and groups come from live registrations\n- [ ] Help-only control bindings can be hidden from the list\n- [ ] Overlay remains usable by keyboard and pointer\n- [ ] Tests, build, and lint pass","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-09-10T13:11:11.615005Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.154.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-d47781","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## What\n\nExtract the shared underlined tab selector used by Backlog and My Issues into a generic controlled `Tabs\u003cT\u003e` component. `Tabs` renders selectors in `TopBar.left`; each parent continues to own active state and render tab content separately below `TopBar`.\n\nTimeline is excluded because `xpo-eb76cd` replaced its former tabs with a multi-select event filter.\n\n## API\n\n```tsx\ninterface TabsProps\u003cT extends string\u003e {\n  items: Readonly\u003cRecord\u003cT, { label: string }\u003e\u003e;\n  activeId: T;\n  onChange: (id: T) =\u003e void;\n  keyboardNavigationEnabled?: boolean;\n}\n```\n\nConsumers may attach additional metadata to each keyed configuration entry; `Tabs` reads only `label`. Key insertion order defines display and keyboard order.\n\n## Behavior\n\n- Preserve the existing underlined selector styling\n- Register `[` and `]` at control priority through the keyboard registry from `xpo-caf557`\n- Cycle with wrapping\n- Disable registration while relevant view overlays are open\n- Never install a document-level listener\n- Publish shortcut metadata consumed by the registry-driven help overlay from `xpo-4ded6b`\n\n## Consumers\n\n- Backlog: All Issues, Active, Backlog, Completed\n- My Issues: Assigned to Me, Created by Me\n\n## Dependencies\n\nDepends on `xpo-caf557` for keyboard registration and `xpo-4ded6b` for the registry-driven help consumer.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Shared selector renders identically in both views\n- [ ] Parents retain ownership of state and content\n- [ ] No per-consumer tab-config adapter is required\n- [ ] `[`/`]` cycles and wraps through registered shortcuts\n- [ ] No direct document listener exists in `Tabs`\n- [ ] Active tab shortcuts appear automatically in keyboard help\n- [ ] Tests, build, and lint pass","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-09-10T13:11:11.669592Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.154.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
