{"id":"xpo-caf557","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"## What\n\nReplace every application-owned document-level keyboard listener with a central `KeyboardNavProvider` and shortcut registry. The provider owns the sole `document.keydown` listener; global features, active views, overlays, reusable controls, and shared primitives declare semantic bindings through `useKeyboardShortcuts`.\n\n## Why\n\nIndependent listeners duplicate guards and cleanup, allow collisions to depend on mount/listener order, scatter overlay suppression, and encourage visual primitives to install global handlers. The original `useViewKeyboard` proposal would only hide that duplication while retaining one listener per caller.\n\n## Core API\n\n- `KeyboardNavProvider` — sole document listener, dispatch, sequences, priority, and registry\n- `useKeyboardShortcuts(registration)` — declarative registration without document access\n- `useActiveShortcuts()` — help-ready metadata for enabled global and current view/control bindings\n\nPriority is `overlay \u003e control \u003e view \u003e global`. Bindings include ID, key or sequence, label/group, enabled state, modifiers, repeat/default-prevention policy, and `showInHelp`.\n\n## Complete migration scope\n\nMigrate document keydown ownership from:\n\n- `App`\n- `KeyboardHelp`\n- `Layout/ProjectSelector`\n- `Modal`, `Popover`, and `ContextMenu`\n- `NewIssueModal`\n- Backlog and `Backlog/FilterMenu`\n- Board\n- My Issues\n- Inbox\n- Dependencies and `DepGraph`\n- Timeline overlays\n- Issue Detail\n\nBacklog's window-level keydown/keyup listener used only to track drag modifier state is explicitly excluded: it is input-state tracking, requires keyup, and does not dispatch shortcuts.\n\n## KeyboardHelp contract\n\n`KeyboardHelp` is a normal registry client: it remains mounted, registers its own `?` toggle and conditional Escape close binding, and later renders `useActiveShortcuts()` in `xpo-4ded6b`. The provider remains UI-agnostic.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The provider is the only application-owned `document.keydown` listener\n- [ ] Every listed global, view, overlay, and primitive listener is migrated\n- [ ] Existing shortcut, dismissal, focus-trap, and sequence behavior is preserved\n- [ ] Priority, guards, conflicts, sequences, enabled state, callback freshness, Strict Mode, and cleanup are tested\n- [ ] Active metadata is the canonical keyboard-help source\n- [ ] Repository search confirms no direct document keydown registration outside the provider\n- [ ] Build, lint, frontend tests, and repository tests pass","estimate":8,"dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-09-10T13:21:53.826002Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.154.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
