{"id":"xpo-caf557","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-423b2be6-221e-4038-aa90-d927ced27831","text":"## Implementation complete\n\n### Central keyboard infrastructure\n- Added a root `KeyboardNavProvider` with the sole application-owned `document.keydown` listener.\n- Added `useKeyboardShortcuts`, `useKeyboardHandler`, and `useActiveShortcuts`.\n- Added structured bindings for IDs, keys/sequences, labels/groups, scope priority, enabled state, modifiers, editable targets, repeat/default prevention, and help visibility.\n- Added deterministic priority dispatch (`overlay \u003e control \u003e view \u003e global`), conflict warnings, 1-second sequences, stable callback refs, and overlay blocking of lower scopes.\n\n### Complete migration\nMigrated App, KeyboardHelp, Layout/ProjectSelector, Modal, Popover, ContextMenu, NewIssueModal, Backlog, FilterMenu, Board, My Issues, Inbox, Dependencies, DepGraph, Timeline overlays, and Issue Detail away from direct document listeners.\n\n`KeyboardHelp` now registers its own always-mounted `?` toggle and open-only Escape/`?` close bindings. Its registry-driven display remains scoped to `xpo-4ded6b`.\n\n### Compatibility decisions\n- Invalid `g` sequence continuations are consumed, matching the prior App handler.\n- Active overlays block unmatched keys from leaking to background scopes.\n- Backlog's window keydown/keyup drag modifier tracker remains intentionally excluded because it tracks input state and requires keyup; it does not dispatch shortcuts.\n\n### Verification\n- `make test`: 269 frontend tests plus Go suite pass\n- Production TypeScript/Vite build passes\n- ESLint and `git diff --check` pass\n- Listener audit finds only `KeyboardNavProvider` on `document.keydown`\n\nReady for review."},"created_at":"2026-09-10T13:34:58.242047Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.154.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"xpo-863802","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Remove branch mode from xpo start/merge","description":"## What\n\nRemove the `mode: \"branch\"` option from `xpo start` and the non-worktree merge path from `xpo merge`. Worktree mode becomes the only way to work on issues.\n\n## Why\n\nBranch mode is fundamentally incompatible with the hub model. `.xpo/` is hub state — a shared, append-only event log plus artifacts that all concurrent work reads and writes. In worktree mode this works because the hub checkout stays on main and `.xpo/` lives there. In branch mode there's only one checkout, so `.xpo/` travels with the branch:\n\n1. **Merge breaks**: `xpo merge` needs to `git checkout main`, but MCP operations (specs, walkthroughs, comments, status transitions) continuously modify `.xpo/issues.db` on the feature branch. Git refuses the checkout because `issues.db` is dirty and differs between branches. The pre-check (`HubRequireCleanTree`) intentionally skips `.xpo/` paths, but the actual `git checkout` still sees them.\n\n2. **Data loss risk**: When the checkout does succeed (e.g. after manually committing `.xpo/`), `git merge --squash` overwrites main's `issues.db` with the branch's version. The `unionLines` helper exists to mitigate this, but it's fragile — if another worktree wrote events to main's `issues.db` after the branch forked, squash merge clobbers them. We got lucky in the xpo-54a423 merge (the branch was a strict superset of main), but this is a ticking time bomb.\n\n3. **Conceptual mismatch**: branch mode pretends `.xpo/` is per-branch state, but the entire system (MCP server, merge tool, worktree layout) treats it as hub state. Every fix for branch mode is a patch over this model mismatch — auto-committing `.xpo/` before checkout, union-merging after, stashing around switches. Each adds complexity and fragility.\n\n## What to remove\n\n- `mode` parameter from `xpo start` (and any config that sets default mode to \"branch\")\n- The `!useWorktrees` / `else` branch in `MergeIssue` (merge.go ~line 74) — the `CheckoutBranch(base)` path, the `mainIssuesDB` union-merge logic, and the non-worktree cleanup\n- `CheckoutBranch` function in git.go if unused after removal\n- Frontend `mode` option in the start MCP tool schema\n- Any tests that specifically cover branch-mode merging\n\n## What to keep\n\n- The worktree path in `MergeIssue` — it's the correct implementation\n- `HubRequireCleanTree`, `HubBranch`, `WorktreeRequireClean` — these are hub-aware and correct\n- The `.gitattributes` merge=union driver for `issues.db` — still useful for regular merge strategy in worktree mode\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `xpo start` always creates a worktree, `mode` parameter removed\n- [ ] `xpo merge` only supports the worktree path\n- [ ] No branch-mode-specific code remains in merge.go or git.go\n- [ ] Tests updated to remove branch-mode coverage\n- [ ] `make test` passes","status":"PLANNED","estimate":3,"sort_order":"bUg","labels":["task","Backend"]},"created_at":"2026-09-10T13:39:17.98143Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.267 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
